window.READOUT = {"seal":{"name":"live-2026-11-22","root":"03bee5ef2bef4699cdfff74c78cd6eba55bfddbcb690ffe378da4e2b8e5d6b3c","count":539,"sealedAt":"2026-11-22T16:31:23.237Z","timestamped":true,"stamp":{"state":"pending","date":"2026-11-24"}},"scored":0,"learned":{"trainedOn":9432,"seal":"live-2026-11-27-ml","root":"6b2ec665a62bb55af0bf110939387f3dee04b9dce3787b926527cfe195aef34e","count":505},"log":[{"date":"2026-11-22","kind":"finding","text":"Tests on past trials cannot prove a forecaster. On 207 trials that had already reported, the model said it remembered the real result for 131. Scores from the past are set aside; only forecasts sealed before a result count."},{"date":"2026-11-22","kind":"sealed","text":"539 forecasts sealed across 505 trials that have not reported. Fingerprint 03bee5ef2bef…"},{"date":"2026-11-22","kind":"finding","text":"6 of the first 40 trials we researched had already announced results, and the model flagged 13 more by itself. All are excluded. Trials not yet researched are marked \"not yet screened\" and do not count until they are."},{"date":"2026-11-22","kind":"finding","text":"Gathering evidence moved a forecast by 5 points on average. Whether those moves make forecasts better is unknown until the trials report."},{"date":"2026-11-23","kind":"negative","text":"We tried blending the model's forecast with a plain statistical model. On past trials it did not improve the forecast, so the published number stays the model's own."},{"date":"2026-11-23","kind":"sealed","text":"The statistical model's own forecasts for all 505 trials are sealed too, so the comparison is fair when results arrive. Fingerprint 5a7c6aef66f4…"},{"date":"2026-11-24","kind":"sealed","text":"The fingerprint of the first record was submitted to OpenTimestamps, an outside timestamping service. It is waiting to be written into a Bitcoin block."},{"date":"2026-11-27","kind":"finding","text":"We built a second forecaster that learns from results: boosted decision trees trained on 9,248 past trials from the public registry. On 180 recent trials it never saw, it removed 23% of the error of always guessing the average, against 17% for our earlier statistical model. It does not use the fields the registry rewrites after a trial ends, such as the final headcount. Other text in a record can still be edited, so expect less on live trials."},{"date":"2026-11-27","kind":"finding","text":"More data helps it. Trained on 250 past trials, the same model scored about 13% on the same kind of test; on 9,248, about 21%. Retraining on newly posted results is a manual step today, and each retrain is sealed as a new version."},{"date":"2026-11-27","kind":"sealed","text":"The learned model's forecasts for all 505 open trials are sealed, so it is scored on the same trials as the published forecast. Fingerprint 6b2ec665a62b… It has no outside timestamp yet."},{"date":"2026-11-25","kind":"finding","text":"We scored the learned model's method on TOP, the public test set that published trial-outcome models report on. ROC-AUC, where 0.5 is a coin flip and 1 is perfect: Phase I 0.677, Phase II 0.698, Phase III 0.761. That is level with the best published results we found (0.653, 0.701, 0.772) and ahead of the earlier published models, but the test cannot separate us from the top one, so we do not claim first place. The full table is in MODEL.md in the public repo."},{"date":"Open","kind":"open","text":"Not done yet: the step that checks each trial's real result and scores it."}],"trials":[{"nct":"NCT06839066","title":"A Phase II Study to Evaluate HLX43 in Subjects With Recurrent/Metastatic Nasopharyngeal Carcinoma Failed or Intolerance to Second-line Therapy","sponsor":"Shanghai Henlius Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-22","enrollment":70,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.38820721911112427,"rationale":"This is an open-label, dose-randomized phase II study of three HLX43 doses with no comparator, so 'success' amounts to an encouraging ORR in heavily pretreated NPC. That outcome is fairly plausible: topoisomerase-I ADCs have shown 30–50% ORRs in later-line NPC, and HLX43 showed meaningful phase 1 activity in NSCLC. The main uncertainty is that, without a formal hypothesis test against a control, there is no clear pass/fail criterion. Its novel anti-PD-L1 ADC mechanism is also unproven in NPC, and no results appear to be public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"da59532e4ec2ee5f747123c0a22e290734a714d2fe20c63dc726bea74067038b"},{"nct":"NCT07533786","title":"A Clinical Trial Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of HSK55718 in Patients for Postoperative Pain Treatment in Abdominal Surgery","sponsor":"Haisco Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-22","enrollment":200,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.8165843774691643,"rationale":"HSK55718 is an undisclosed Haisco injectable analgesic, and the morphine active comparator suggests an opioid-like or opioid-alternative mechanism. Chinese postoperative pain trials of potent IV analgesics against placebo on SPID usually succeed, and here any of three doses (about 40 patients per arm) beating placebo counts. The main risks are a novel non-opioid mechanism with limited efficacy in visceral abdominal pain, and rescue medication shrinking the separation from placebo. I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"33c0dd504d55e889e3be7179e01a587a226315f44564e4e38a5e118516d1e08e"},{"nct":"NCT06567782","title":"A Study of Neoadjuvant Dostarlimab Plus Capecitabine Plus Oxaliplatin (CAPEOX) Vs CAPEOX With Previously Untreated T4N0 or Stage III Mismatch Repair Proficient (MMRp)/Microsatellite Stable (MSS) Colon Cancer","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-23","enrollment":120,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.27663072684768764,"rationale":"This is an exploratory randomized phase 2 (about 60 per arm) adding PD-1 blockade to neoadjuvant CAPEOX in MMRp/MSS colon cancer, a setting where PD-1 monotherapy is largely inactive. Chemotherapy alone yields low major pathological response rates (FOxTROT-type data), so a large relative gain is conceivable, and some single-arm Chinese studies of PD-1 plus chemotherapy report higher regression. Still, the incremental benefit of PD-1 in MSS disease has generally been modest, and the trial is framed as looking for 'early signs of effectiveness' rather than powered for a formal significance test. Results have not been released, so I estimate a moderate-low probability of a statistically significant mPR difference.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5cb56da77a2af0abd43ce34913ad65e4bdc379cc8955e76555c759852b6fc547"},{"nct":"NCT06693895","title":"A Study on the Safety of an Investigational Chickenpox Vaccine, When Given to Healthy Children, 12 to 15 Months of Age","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-23","enrollment":750,"base":0.8,"researched":0.85,"learned":0.8201988804169299,"rationale":"This is a descriptive phase 3a safety study of GSK's VNS varicella vaccine against Varivax, with no prespecified hypothesis test, so 'meeting the endpoint' in practice means the sponsor reports an acceptable, comparable safety profile. In phase 2, adverse event rates were similar to Varivax and seroresponse was high, and GSK has a long track record with Oka-strain vaccines. Descriptive safety trials almost always end with a 'well tolerated, comparable to control' topline. The remaining risk is an unexpected rash or fever signal, or ambiguity in how such a descriptive trial is scored.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"adba9c6b6a92e0ac193ef90b6fec2cefcdfad05f3a3b5adce76a6e200eb4da96"},{"nct":"NCT06585787","title":"A Study to Evaluate KarXT as a Treatment for Psychosis Associated With Alzheimer's Disease (ADEPT-4)","sponsor":"Karuna Therapeutics, Inc., a Bristol Myers Squibb company","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-24","enrollment":406,"base":0.5,"researched":0.45,"learned":0.5145508030762452,"rationale":"KarXT is proven in schizophrenia, and xanomeline monotherapy showed dose-dependent reductions in hallucinations and delusions in Alzheimer's disease, so the mechanism is plausible here, but no randomized data on this endpoint exist yet. Psychosis trials in Alzheimer's disease have a poor record: placebo responses on NPI-type scales are high, pimavanserin missed in an AD-only trial and in its AD subgroup, and atypical antipsychotics show only small effects. The add-on schizophrenia trial missed, and slow enrollment amid eligibility stringency plus site irregularities at a sister trial add execution risk. With about 400 patients, the trial is adequately powered for a modest effect, so a forecast near 45% balances the drug's mechanistic promise against the field's high failure rate.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"3505aa4abc9dfb84021464dd402db93940b1f2c01c1a0f32b42fd29be858a937"},{"nct":"NCT06616974","title":"A Study of TX000045 in Patients With Pulmonary Hypertension Secondary to Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (the APEX Study)","sponsor":"Tectonic Therapeutic","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-24","enrollment":191,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.31984458805241506,"rationale":"TX000045 is a long-acting relaxin-Fc agonist. Tectonic's Phase 1b reported acute reductions in PVR and PCWP and increases in cardiac output in PH-HFpEF patients, and in CADENCE sotatercept lowered PVR significantly in CpcPH, so PVR is a plausible and fairly responsive hemodynamic endpoint. Against that, the primary analysis is restricted to the CpcPH subgroup, likely about 100–130 patients across three arms, and right-heart-catheterization PVR is noisy. Durability of relaxin's effect over 24 weeks of chronic dosing is also unproven, and Phase 2 cardiovascular proof-of-concept trials frequently miss.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6671a8b81178a356d1cecd4fbd5b2b4f078cc861b7132a1c35a9e36bc4425b4a"},{"nct":"NCT07057622","title":"A Phase III Clinical Study to Compare the Safety and Efficacy of 177Lu-DOTATATE Injection and Long-acting Oxytrexine in Adult Patients With NETs","sponsor":"HTA Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-24","enrollment":184,"base":0.88,"researched":0.9,"learned":0.5329820700842461,"rationale":"177Lu-DOTATATE has repeatedly and strongly beaten octreotide LAR 60 mg on PFS in this population (NETTER-1 HR 0.21, 20-month PFS 65% vs 11%; NETTER-2 HR 0.28), and a Chinese monotherapy analogue (XT-XTR008) also met its PFS endpoint against the same comparator. With n=184 and a weak control arm, even a much smaller effect than NETTER-1's, such as an 18-month PFS gap of about 25 points, should be readily detectable. The main risks are execution and operational: a single site, an open-label design with no DMC, a likely slipping timeline, an unclear powering and analysis plan, and possible product or quality differences for this generic-style radioligand.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"a7d57e8c3a8459d07e1a22aecc2acd30b0e504876d07b94cde9fce6b321d0ceb"},{"nct":"NCT07600983","title":"Clinical Trial of the 24-valent Pneumococcal Polysaccharide Conjugate Vaccine (CRM197/Tetanus Toxoid)","sponsor":"CanSino Biologics Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-11-24","enrollment":854,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.7117864298629972,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is Phase I adverse reaction incidence, a descriptive safety endpoint with no formal superiority or non-inferiority test. Success therefore effectively means acceptable safety and a decision to advance the vaccine. CanSino already markets a PCV13i, and multivalent CRM197/TT conjugates generally show tolerable reactogenicity in phase 1/2, so the safety signal is likely acceptable and the sponsor will likely report a positive outcome. Some risk remains from the ambiguity of 'meeting' a descriptive endpoint, possible immune interference with 24 valents, and timeline slippage.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e5dbaabfcbbaad584533a829ec760b883c0e0396c0820a77b0daec3b57920b63"},{"nct":"NCT06775860","title":"ICP-332 in Subjects With Moderate to Severe Atopic Dermatitis","sponsor":"Beijing InnoCare Pharma Tech Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-25","enrollment":552,"base":0.95,"researched":null,"learned":0.8751060105682661,"rationale":"ICP-332 (soficitinib) is an oral TYK2/JAK1 inhibitor. In its Phase 2 atopic dermatitis study it produced large, dose-dependent EASI-75 responses with placebo-adjusted gains well above what this trial needs. Oral JAK1-class drugs (upadacitinib, abrocitinib, ivarmacitinib) have consistently beaten placebo on EASI-75 and vIGA-AD at week 16 in Phase 3, and this trial has about 550 patients, ample power for a likely effect size of 30 percentage points or more. The main residual risks are execution issues or an unusually high placebo response, so I put success at about 95%.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"66bf234c9dbea16bb3f6b26ed4468308f93c917d750cad6d7546334ae5ff2923"},{"nct":"NCT03981796","title":"A Study to Evaluate Dostarlimab Plus Carboplatin-paclitaxel Versus Placebo Plus Carboplatin-paclitaxel in Participants With Recurrent or Primary Advanced Endometrial Cancer","sponsor":"Tesaro, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-26","enrollment":785,"base":0.97,"researched":null,"learned":0.6769026229623303,"rationale":"This is the RUBY trial. The Part 1 results (Mirza et al., NEJM 2023) showed that dostarlimab plus carboplatin-paclitaxel significantly improved investigator-assessed PFS, in both the dMMR/MSI-H population (HR ~0.28) and the overall population (HR ~0.64). Overall survival was later also significantly improved, and Part 2 (dostarlimab plus niraparib) likewise met its PFS primary endpoint. The first-listed primary endpoint has therefore already been met and publicly reported.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"08818aaad39600296051bbb44fa3637868689d86d0a26de50959e24e6e4d1ada"},{"nct":"NCT07122401","title":"Study of MT1013 for the Treatment of Patients With Secondary Hyperparathyroidism","sponsor":"Shaanxi Micot Pharmaceutical Technology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-26","enrollment":424,"base":0.75,"researched":0.75,"learned":0.8204423586427884,"rationale":"MT1013 is an IV calcimimetic-type agent whose Phase II iPTH response rates (about 74–77% reaching >50% reduction) roughly matched etelcalcetide. Etelcalcetide itself beat oral cinacalcet head-to-head on both >30% and >50% iPTH reduction, partly because in-clinic IV dosing removes adherence problems, and this trial (n≈435) is well sized for a similar effect. The design is unstated; if it tests non-inferiority, success is very likely, while superiority on the >50% endpoint is plausible but less certain. No results have been reported and the trial remains blinded, so I put the probability at about 0.75.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"dd4ae60e7068ac394c44c47a0147e9f2a7b49820dfaabcdba6ce8e121336e9ac"},{"nct":"NCT06660992","title":"A Study to Assess the Efficacy and Safety of HSK31858 in Participants With Non-Cystic Fibrosis Bronchiectasis","sponsor":"Haisco Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-28","enrollment":669,"base":0.72,"researched":0.83,"learned":0.711692122583824,"rationale":"The DPP1 mechanism is validated in bronchiectasis: brensocatib's large ASPEN phase 3 succeeded, with roughly a 20% reduction in exacerbation rate, and HSK31858's own phase 2 showed a strong, highly significant reduction (IRR 0.41 at 40 mg) in a Chinese population similar to this one. The phase 2 effect is likely inflated, but with about 700 patients, 52 weeks of follow-up, 2:1 randomization and a requirement of at least 2 prior exacerbations, the trial should still be reasonably powered for a 25–30% reduction. The main risks are regression of the effect toward brensocatib-like sizes, a high placebo response, and an assumed effect size that is not disclosed; even so, phase 3 success after strong phase 2 data with a validated mechanism is likely.","sources":11,"state":"screened","leaf":"6fdc7580e3915905e55965659c7377dfc5c6d7296d8c97ca78645ce69cf340ac"},{"nct":"NCT06773962","title":"A Phase 2a Multicenter Clinical Trial of TB006 in Participants With Parkinson's Disease","sponsor":"TrueBinding, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-28","enrollment":62,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.26412758996067814,"rationale":"TB006 is an anti-galectin-3 monoclonal antibody whose Alzheimer's phase 1/2 study missed its efficacy endpoints. Disease-modifying antibodies in early Parkinson's (prasinezumab, cinpanemab) have not shown significant MDS-UPDRS benefit even in much larger, longer trials. With about 62 participants, 28 weeks of follow-up and a noisy motor score, a significant win against placebo is unlikely unless there is a symptomatic effect, and a small sponsor's prior claims don't change that much. I put the chance of a significant primary result at roughly 10–15%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e1b1884c251df3b4ed8a208e73024b3c070dad32607b425e4b62212575c69021"},{"nct":"NCT07103148","title":"A Phase III Control Study of the Safety and Immunogenicity of vYF in Pediatric Population","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-28","enrollment":2440,"base":0.85,"researched":0.86,"learned":0.8831034360833555,"rationale":"vYF is a Vero-cell-derived 17D vaccine that showed near-identical day-29 seroconversion to YF-VAX in adults (99.7% vs 99.4%), so non-inferiority against licensed 17D comparators should be likely, and the same vYF arm is compared with both Stamaril and YF-VAX. Pediatric seroconversion is lower and more variable, which shrinks the margin of safety. There are four co-primary comparisons across two age groups, and if all must pass, joint risk rises, though the large sample (about 600 per vYF age group) gives good power. Sanofi runs this trial as a regulatory-grade effort, and non-inferiority trials of near-copy live vaccines usually succeed.","sources":6,"state":"screened","leaf":"c24c0bd8f845bb7383527d81cd88a18f12b21df167feb0b9c5a9ba332224f8a9"},{"nct":"NCT06641466","title":"A Study to Learn About the Study Medicine Called Rimegepant in Women When Used for Intermittent Prevention of Menstrual Migraine","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-29","enrollment":723,"base":0.65,"researched":0.78,"learned":0.9154715958041609,"rationale":"Rimegepant is a proven oral gepant with demonstrated preventive efficacy in episodic migraine, and the same-class atogepant LUNA trial, using an identical 7-day perimenstrual regimen, met its primary endpoint with a highly significant 0.8-day placebo-adjusted reduction. The roughly 723 participants across four arms give about 180 per arm, adequate power for a similar effect. Risks are rimegepant's weaker preventive potency than atogepant (its plasma half-life of about 11 h makes once-daily dosing modest), the small absolute benefit in a 5-day window, high placebo responses, and unclear multiplicity handling across two rimegepant arms. The status and timeline inconsistency suggests the trial may still be ongoing.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"fed0526a406f0d98b7dd72aa97e4769236f69ed42e01ad3dbaa20b3eebfb8640"},{"nct":"NCT05462587","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of AVTX-803 in Patients With Leukocyte Adhesion Deficiency Type II","sponsor":"AUG Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":4,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.7500789439088593,"rationale":"Oral L-fucose has a clear mechanistic rationale in LAD II (SLC35C1-CDG). Case reports show restored sialyl-Lewis X expression on neutrophils in responders, and this trial excludes known non-responders, so the biomarker effect is likely large and consistent. However, with only about 4 patients in a crossover, formal significance is fragile: nonparametric tests cannot reach p<0.05 at n=4, and results may be reported descriptively. The trial has also been recruiting since 2022 at a single site under a small sponsor, so it may not complete with an interpretable topline.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2249a69810f663e5c512ac5754951c470a8630d09065850797a6772bbf982f2e"},{"nct":"NCT05682443","title":"ONC-392 Plus Lutetium Lu 177 Vipivotide Tetraxetan in Patients With mCRPC","sponsor":"OncoC4, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":148,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.38051920704099834,"rationale":"The first primary efficacy endpoint is the phase 2 PSA50 comparison, with roughly 45–50 patients per arm against an active Lu-PSMA-617 control that already gives PSA50 near 46–50%. A statistically significant gain would need a very large added effect, roughly 25–30 percentage points. Anti-CTLA4 therapy has a poor record in mCRPC (ipilimumab failed in phase 3), and immunotherapy combined with Lu-PSMA has shown only modest, uncontrolled signals. Gotistobart's improved safety profile may help tolerability, but this small open-label phase 2 is unlikely to show significance on PSA50 or rPFS, and I don't recall any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"39606f9aaea0b4a17510f88c8d7cc8e85a60debb01ad82aa2cdd487e89fb68d2"},{"nct":"NCT05890729","title":"Study of Multiple-Ascending-Dose Study of XTMAB-16 in Patients With Pulmonary Sarcoidosis With or Without Extrapulmonary Manifestations","sponsor":"Xentria, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":32,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.39382127088777524,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is safety and tolerability (AE, SAE, DLT and AESI rates) in a small Phase 1/2 multiple-ascending-dose study, with no formal efficacy comparison against placebo. XTMAB-16 is an anti-TNFα monoclonal antibody, a well-characterized mechanism with a known safety profile, so serious unexpected toxicity at these doses seems unlikely. Sponsors usually describe such trials as having met the primary endpoint when the drug is generally well tolerated. The main risks are the ambiguity of scoring a non-comparative safety endpoint, plus possible infection signals or slow enrollment at a small sponsor.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cac782bca041d27470642f015f09ab616b73f746a4754469a3bef3be3a3490ac"},{"nct":"NCT06129175","title":"UCMSCs as Treatment for Patients With Acute Ischemic Stroke (Stroke Neuroncell-EX)","sponsor":"Cytopeutics Sdn. Bhd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":80,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.443527606973123,"rationale":"Large well-designed trials of intravenous MSCs in ischemic stroke (MASTERS, MASTERS-2, TREASURE, and the larger Chinese and Korean studies) have generally missed functional primary endpoints such as mRS, so the prior for a cell therapy in stroke is low. This trial is small (80 patients, single center) and is powered only for a large effect on Barthel Index or mRS, which are noisy endpoints in a heterogeneous moderate-to-severe stroke population. Small, company-sponsored, single-site studies sometimes report positive results on loosely defined endpoints, and the multiple timepoints give some room for that, but the trial was still recruiting and results may be delayed. Overall I put the chance of a clearly significant primary result at about 20%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"142fadda81c6419eb4b58b757e1020edc4f2b5fd2fd3e2904b57be660766a2c4"},{"nct":"NCT06812078","title":"A Study of TAK-360 in Adults With Idiopathic Hypersomnia","sponsor":"Takeda","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":96,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.33290973972656407,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety count (participants with TEAEs), not an efficacy comparison, so whether this trial 'meets its primary endpoint' will likely depend on how the sponsor frames its topline efficacy readouts, such as ESS change at Week 4. Orexin-2 agonists have shown wake-promoting effects in NT2 and IH, with early ORX750 and ALKS 2680 data supporting some benefit even without orexin deficiency. However, effect sizes outside NT1 are smaller, and this is a 96-patient, 4-week dose-finding study. The trial is still recruiting, with primary completion around end of November 2026, so no result is public, and the ambiguous safety endpoint keeps the estimate close to a coin flip with a slight lean positive.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3fb672bcb9abac5ae34ed9b5c4b00772b0162f438b4e6f73ef13783e5e246163"},{"nct":"NCT06952699","title":"A Study of TAK-360 in Adults With Narcolepsy Without Cataplexy (NT2)","sponsor":"Takeda","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":88,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.39041079547059654,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a descriptive safety measure (participants with at least one TEAE), with no prespecified superiority test, so 'success' will likely be judged on whether Takeda calls the topline positive on tolerability and efficacy. Orexin-2 agonists have shown robust wakefulness effects in NT1. In NT2 the effects are more modest but still significant, for example alixorexton in Vibrance-2, and TAK-360 was designed for orexin-intact populations. Against this, the trial is small (n=88), still recruiting, and orexin agonists tend to produce more adverse events than placebo (insomnia, urinary frequency), which makes a strict 'favorable comparison' reading ambiguous.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9becc2d4cf5246bd967d34e8149e5683dfeb063a63bed4c14960130159ab97f5"},{"nct":"NCT06954961","title":"A Study to Evaluate D-0502 in Subjects With ER+ Her2- Locally Advanced or Metastatic Breast Cancer","sponsor":"InventisBio Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":640,"base":0.45,"researched":0.35,"learned":0.6944254903313705,"rationale":"This trial tests an oral SERD as monotherapy against fulvestrant in an all-comer population that was not selected for ESR1 mutation. In that setting the class record is mixed: EMERALD and the phase 2 SERENA-2 were positive, while EMBER-3 (imlunestrant), acelERA (giredestrant) and AMEERA-3 were negative overall, and a pooled HR of 0.80 had a confidence interval crossing 1. Patients here have had only 1–2 prior endocrine lines and many Chinese patients may not have had a CDK4/6 inhibitor, so ESR1 mutations will be less common and fulvestrant 500 mg should perform relatively well, shrinking the expected benefit. Working in D-0502's favour are the large 640-patient sample and the sponsor's choice to run a registrational trial, but there are no randomized data for the drug and its single-agent activity is uncertain.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"f98987e6602a7bfd2df100d2cbff8d7fd4774a163ce3af878e61ee22bc0b846c"},{"nct":"NCT06968585","title":"A Study of A166 Versus Trastuzumab Emtansine (T-DM1) in Patients With HER2-Positive Unresectable or Metastatic Breast Cancer Previously Treated With Trastuzumab and Taxane Therapy","sponsor":"Sichuan Kelun-Biotech Biopharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":365,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.6207843850451361,"rationale":"A166 (trastuzumab botidotin) is Kelun's HER2 ADC with a duostatin/MMAF-type payload. To my recollection, Kelun announced in 2024 that this China phase 3 against T-DM1 met its BICR-assessed PFS primary endpoint at a prespecified interim analysis, and an NMPA NDA based on it was accepted and later approved. Independently of that, next-generation HER2 ADCs have generally beaten T-DM1 on PFS in this second-line setting, so the prior was already favorable.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"99d901c3afc735051fe5f3fec949f2b172ff5cea3e99a05848d8de201682fa55"},{"nct":"NCT07122687","title":"IBI363 Combined With Chemotherapy or Pembrolizumab Combined With Chemotherapy as Neoadjuvant Therapy in Resectable Stage IB-III Non-Squamous Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":170,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.3208541577793146,"rationale":"IBI363 is Innovent's PD-1/IL-2α-bias bispecific fusion protein, and here it is tested head-to-head against an active standard, pembrolizumab plus chemotherapy, whose pCR rate in non-squamous NSCLC is roughly 18–25%. With about 85 patients per arm, a statistically significant pCR gain would need an absolute improvement near 15–20 points, a large effect that no next-generation IO agent has yet shown in the neoadjuvant setting. The trial is also a single-site, open-label phase 2 that may be primarily descriptive, and IBI363's strongest signals so far have come in IO-resistant squamous disease rather than non-squamous. Promising early data and the IL-2 mechanism leave some room for a large effect, but superiority over an active comparator is more likely to fail than succeed.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3606a2f4c1434699da3a80ec0d8b40839ab3389e09b1ac328904aea46e6676f8"},{"nct":"NCT07199569","title":"Comparability Trial of the MVA-BN Vaccine Manufactured in Different Production Cells","sponsor":"Bavarian Nordic","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":970,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5542693340021551,"rationale":"This is a non-inferiority comparability trial of the same MVA-BN virus, given in the same infectious-unit dose range, with only the production cell substrate changed from CEF to the CCX.E10 quail line. The sponsor is very experienced, with prior lot-consistency and freeze-dried versus liquid comparability trials of MVA-BN that met their margins. With about 485 per arm, the study is well powered for a GMT-ratio margin, assuming the usual 0.67 or 0.5. The main risk is that a substrate change alters immunogenicity per infectious unit, causing a GMT shortfall, but that seems unlikely given the sponsor's process development.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8df4e8dfaa170ba953c1e14ecc7764f8c985af2da3770f305546397e3ef5297f"},{"nct":"NCT07226258","title":"Phase III Study to Assess the Safety and Efficacy of SL1002 for Osteoarthritis Knee Pain","sponsor":"Saol Therapeutics Inc","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":150,"base":0.55,"researched":0.42,"learned":0.5851750758056722,"rationale":"This is a small (150-patient) single-dose Phase III of an undisclosed chemoneurolytic injection against intra-articular/perineural saline in US knee OA, a setting with very high placebo response and frequent late-stage failures. The Phase II COMPASS results were never published with effect sizes. Still, the sponsor advanced to Phase III with the same investigators, and enrollment uses a diagnostic nerve-block responder enrichment, which plausibly raises the effect size. Given the modest sample, the shifted endpoint (pain while walking) and the base rate for OA pain injectables, success is somewhat less likely than not.","sources":10,"state":"screened","leaf":"9eb6e56f9e062ff5ce1f824d160beb84b5324cbc99f5bb52d312980357f92384"},{"nct":"NCT07365904","title":"Investigating Ovulation Inhibition for Use as a Contraceptive","sponsor":"Mylan Pharmaceuticals Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":60,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.41773241465425315,"rationale":"This is a descriptive, open-label ovulation-inhibition study of a norelgestromin patch, which may be progestin-only, with planned application errors. Success would likely mean showing low ovulation incidence, as judged by Hoogland-Skouby score and the Landgren criterion, rather than a formal significance test. Norelgestromin patches such as Evra have generally kept ovulation suppressed despite extended patch-free intervals, and the sponsor presumably moved this to error testing after a successful earlier study. Still, a possibly estrogen-free formulation, the deliberate stress-testing of errors, and the ambiguity of 'success' for a descriptive endpoint warrant moderate rather than high confidence.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0862954fc985025af7a545f9827a3a7fc7a15bcdedfe9bfdc5de67e230952f6f"},{"nct":"NCT07656727","title":"A Phase 2 Study to Evaluate the Pharmacodynamics, Safety and Tolerability of BGE-102 in Participants With Obesity and Cardiovascular Risk Factors","sponsor":"BioAge Labs, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":160,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.6998749192969609,"rationale":"BGE-102 is an oral NLRP3 inhibitor, and hsCRP is a proximal pharmacodynamic marker that this class reliably suppresses. BioAge's Phase 1 MAD cohorts in obese participants with elevated hsCRP reportedly showed large reductions (around 80%+), and Ventyx's VTX3232 showed a similar effect in a comparable population. With roughly 40 per arm, high-hsCRP enrollment and three doses, any one dose beating placebo on percent change is very likely despite hsCRP variability. The main risks are safety or tolerability problems and an unexpectedly high placebo response, and primary completion is late November 2026, so I don't believe results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b2427821eb92dffa806001580cff9c240e98a7f87f8d0e64cf8a0f7f475bae1e"},{"nct":"NCT07672561","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Phase Ⅲ Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of WD-890 Tablets for the Treatment of Moderate to Severe Plaque Psoriasis","sponsor":"Zhejiang Wenda Pharma Technology LTD.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-11-30","enrollment":375,"base":0.92,"researched":0.88,"learned":0.8944382287249509,"rationale":"WD-890 appears to be an oral TYK2-type inhibitor (it suppressed IL-17 and IFN-γ in an IL-23 mouse model), a mechanism already validated against placebo in psoriasis by deucravacitinib and zasocitinib. The sponsor's move to Phase 3 suggests its Phase 2 dose-ranging data were encouraging. Against placebo with sPGA 0/1 and PASI 75 at week 16 and about 375 patients, the trial has ample power even for a modest effect. The main risks are a weak small Chinese sponsor with an undisclosed Phase 2, possible underdosing, and execution or record issues such as a single site and stale dates.","sources":6,"state":"screened","leaf":"39b4019fc621320142f7580b3a8b700be7d49eae132eab3a587b73981ec54566"},{"nct":"NCT03789552","title":"Outcome Research to Confirm the Anti-anginal Effect of T89 in Patients With Stable Angina","sponsor":"Tasly Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":765,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.8092101999157694,"rationale":"T89 (Dantonic, a Danshen/Sanqi botanical extract) showed only modest, inconsistent improvement in exercise duration in its US Phase 2 trial. The benefit was mainly at the high dose and was not robust across timepoints. Treadmill exercise-duration endpoints in chronic stable angina carry large placebo and training effects, so many antianginal agents fail them, and botanical drugs especially lack a strong track record in FDA-style Phase 3 trials. Recruitment has run since 2019 with no public results. Two doses give a modest boost to the chance of success, but the overall likelihood stays below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8979d74dd23f4f8442b97465ef53e1ca9bca6c3106cc635500735ba5af875539"},{"nct":"NCT03994874","title":"Peritoneal Ultrafiltration in Cardio Renal Syndrome.","sponsor":"Iperboreal Pharma Srl","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":84,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.2735623225588102,"rationale":"This is a small (n=84), open-label, three-site Italian phase 1/2 trial run by a small sponsor, testing nightly peritoneal ultrafiltration against no intervention in diuretic-resistant congestive HFrEF; no result from it is public. The composite primary endpoint is dominated by soft, partly investigator-driven components (a ≥50% diuretic dose increase, or escalation to IV diuretics or ultrafiltration), and control-arm event rates should be high in this population, so a large effect is plausible. Observational peritoneal ultrafiltration data in refractory heart failure also look favorable. Against that, the small sample, recruitment and feasibility problems that are likely to delay the trial, the adaptive re-sizing, and the low base rate for phase 2 heart-failure trials keep my estimate below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c7f8514d14d5505cb0b41fbf75cf4992d160424ce8fbb076b9a2ef37f29f5533"},{"nct":"NCT04042844","title":"A Single Dose of BRTX 100 for Patients With Chronic Lumbar Disc Disease (cLDD)","sponsor":"BioRestorative Therapies","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":99,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3336374728150045,"rationale":"Intradiscal cell therapies for discogenic back pain have a poor record against controls; for example, Mesoblast's Phase 3 rexlemestrocel-L trial missed its primary endpoint, and sham/placebo responder rates in chronic low back pain are high. BioRestorative has released encouraging blinded interim responder data, but with 2:1 randomization a high pooled responder rate is uninformative about separation from sham. With only about 99 patients, a composite responder endpoint and a trial framed as 'preliminary efficacy', a statistically significant win is possible but less likely than not, though a sham that is not injected intradiscally may modestly help separation.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"22384549a0bef4eaa896e226a4a4b638fea4eed3ded946cd3f2130d0ef16d1be"},{"nct":"NCT04344158","title":"A Phase III Clinical Trial of AK105 Injection Combined With Anlotinib Hydrochloride Capsules Versus Sorafenib in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":648,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.5307178089787123,"rationale":"AK105 is penpulimab, and this is the APOLLO first-line HCC trial of penpulimab plus anlotinib versus sorafenib. PD-1/PD-L1 plus anti-angiogenic combinations have repeatedly beaten sorafenib on overall survival, as in IMbrave150, ORIENT-32 and CARES-310, which gives a high base rate. I recall APOLLO being reported around 2024 with a significant OS benefit (median roughly 16.5 vs 13.2 months, HR about 0.69), followed by NMPA approval of the combination in China. That recollection is not certain, so the probability is high but short of certainty.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"b7dbcef4150407ff1397edf99e9125cd476730835f3cb0ada82a9a3a0dd1e646"},{"nct":"NCT04435990","title":"Efficacy and Safety Evaluation for the Treatment of Allergy Against Mites","sponsor":"Inmunotek S.L.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":150,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.780570555576207,"rationale":"House dust mite SCIT has an established mechanism, but phase 3 allergen immunotherapy trials using combined symptom-medication scores often fail to reach significance because of large placebo responses and perennial, variable exposure. This trial is small (about 50 per arm), runs only 12 months, and has recruited slowly since 2020, all of which reduce power. Inmunotek's MM09 allergoid has supportive earlier data, and having two dose arms gives two chances at success, which partly offsets these weaknesses. No results appear to be public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4436596f186a19b6f5e716b7da2b3304a0f88c8968df11c6623838ef8865602c"},{"nct":"NCT04442022","title":"A Study of Rituximab-Gemcitabine-Dexamethasone-Platinum (R-GDP) With or Without Selinexor in Patients With Relapsed/Refractory Diffuse Large B-cell Lymphoma","sponsor":"Karyopharm Therapeutics Inc","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":501,"base":0.12,"researched":0.05,"learned":0.740427131159354,"rationale":"The FDA asked Karyopharm to withdraw the DLBCL indication in March 2026 because the company could not complete this confirmatory trial, and the company has said it will stop DLBCL development costs. That makes a completed, positive Phase 3 PFS readout very unlikely. The underlying efficacy case was also modest: SADAL showed 29% ORR single-arm, there are no randomized data for adding selinexor to R-GDP, and the related endometrial Phase 3 narrowly missed on PFS. The remaining probability mainly covers the chance that some prespecified analysis, such as the Phase 2 ORR, comes out positive, or that a truncated analysis is reported favorably.","sources":10,"state":"screened","leaf":"a07784b9cbe9228ddb8d7a89f8070d93a6e56172df665ea155a6c6084fe0bdf1"},{"nct":"NCT04639986","title":"Asian Study of Sacituzumab Govitecan (IMMU-132) in HR+/HER2- Metastatic Breast Cancer (MBC)","sponsor":"Gilead Sciences","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":331,"base":0.95,"researched":null,"learned":0.6943806621660464,"rationale":"This is EVER-132-002, the Asian Phase 3 trial of sacituzumab govitecan versus physician's-choice chemotherapy in HR+/HER2- metastatic breast cancer. I recall it was reported (around ESMO 2024) as meeting its primary endpoint, IRC-assessed PFS (HR about 0.67), with an overall survival benefit as well. That is consistent with TROPiCS-02, where the same drug improved PFS in the same setting. The registry's primary completion date likely reflects a final analysis, so I place high confidence in success with some allowance for imperfect recall.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"32d0d2275a38729aad0dd95ef3a707fec18f8b15db78d61d61bfa4bb896548da"},{"nct":"NCT04704921","title":"Pivotal 1 Study of ABBV-RGX-314 (Also Known as RGX-314) Gene Therapy Administered Via Subretinal Delivery One Time in Participants With nAMD","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":671,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.8292598460131608,"rationale":"ATMOSPHERE is a pivotal test of whether one subretinal dose of ABBV-RGX-314, with supplemental anti-VEGF rescue allowed, is non-inferior to monthly ranibizumab on mean BCVA change at week 54 in previously treated nAMD patients. Phase 1/2a data at the higher doses showed roughly stable BCVA with large cuts in injection burden, and rescue injections plus a likely ~4–5 letter non-inferiority margin make success plausible. Risks remain: monthly ranibizumab is a strong control, the vitrectomy and subretinal procedure can cost vision, and dose-dependent variability and inflammation could erode mean BCVA. Primary completion is December 2026, so topline results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"83a2b87bf7fb2e61b750e68aa3c1bfeaa00ff15714d21d461e0a121370149ca8"},{"nct":"NCT04853342","title":"To Assess the Efficacy and Safety of Furmonertinib Versus Placebo, in Patients With Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor Mutation Positive Stage II-IIIA Non-small Cell Lung Carcinoma, Following Complete Tumour Resection With or Without Adjuvant Chemotherapy","sponsor":"Allist Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":318,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.5027912758769146,"rationale":"Furmonertinib is a third-generation EGFR TKI with the same mechanism as osimertinib, which cut DFS risk dramatically against placebo in resected EGFR-mutant stage IB-IIIA NSCLC in ADAURA (HR about 0.2). Other adjuvant EGFR TKIs (icotinib, gefitinib) have also consistently improved DFS, and furmonertinib has proven efficacy in advanced disease. With about 318 patients and a placebo control, power for DFS should be ample. The main risks are operational: slow single-site recruitment, a possibly early or underpowered analysis, or the trial never reporting, and I do not recall any published result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"af3cab94c7c3e5d6667a1c0ba8e5c80d13e54a9efdf54b24c39d2d0ff2f1b77a"},{"nct":"NCT04969731","title":"Safety and Efficacy of Immuncell-LC With Gemcitabine in Resectable Pancreatic Cancer","sponsor":"GC Cell Corporation","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":408,"base":0.22,"researched":0.2,"learned":0.5408657030575039,"rationale":"Adjuvant immunotherapy add-ons to gemcitabine in resected pancreatic cancer have a poor record (GI-4000, algenpantucel-L, erlotinib/sorafenib in CONKO-005/006), and this trial has no randomized pancreatic data behind it, only preclinical and retrospective signals. The HCC adjuvant RFS success shows Immuncell-LC can reduce recurrence, and the open-label design against a weak gemcitabine-only control helps somewhat. Still, pancreatic cancer's immunosuppressive biology and early systemic relapse make a meaningful RFS benefit unlikely, and with 408 patients only a moderate hazard ratio would reach significance. The record has not been updated since 2021 and no result is public, so recruitment may be slow and the readout delayed.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"cfa28681ba7e22dafb09d142552e4e0ea24b469469b61b4b65a5da5238d1c10e"},{"nct":"NCT04986423","title":"ZEN003694 and Enzalutamide Versus Enzalutamide Monotherapy in Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer","sponsor":"Zenith Epigenetics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":200,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.4082457102235719,"rationale":"ZEN-3694 plus enzalutamide showed encouraging but uncontrolled rPFS (about 9 months) in the post-abiraterone phase 1b/2a study, and enzalutamide after abiraterone is a weak control, especially in poor abiraterone responders. Against that, BET inhibitors have a poor track record, dose-limiting toxicities such as thrombocytopenia may limit exposure, and the Cohort A comparison is modestly sized. Enrollment by a small sponsor appears slow, with the trial still recruiting close to its planned primary completion. Base rates for randomized phase 2 oncology combinations of a novel mechanism suggest roughly a one-in-three chance of a significant rPFS benefit.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"76c5dcd46fc9fe7111943569bf8ba56a758993ed699e8a3d32324d80fb9a1e91"},{"nct":"NCT05065216","title":"Treatment of Acute Ischemic Stroke (ReMEDy2 Trial)","sponsor":"DiaMedica Therapeutics Inc","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":728,"base":0.1,"researched":null,"learned":0.45759756840103283,"rationale":"Acute ischemic stroke neuroprotection and recovery trials have a very poor track record. DiaMedica's own Phase 2 ReMEDy1 missed its primary endpoint, with only post-hoc subgroup signals, and the dichotomized mRS 0–1 endpoint in a moderate-severity, non-thrombectomy population needs a sizable effect to reach significance. The trial has a futility interim at 200 patients, has had slow enrollment and a prior clinical hold for hypotension, and is still recruiting, so a success at the final analysis looks unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"84ca6e06fbb3b629740c04f7934b15f76cb53c971ebafa4d4060f17dd35d7304"},{"nct":"NCT05139719","title":"A Study to Explore the Therapeutic Effect of HEC585 on Delaying Forced Vital Capacity (FVC) Decline and Tolerance in Progressive Fibrosing Interstitial Lung Disease (PF-ILD) Patients","sponsor":"Sunshine Lake Pharma Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":110,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3827881675012074,"rationale":"HEC585 (yinfenidone) is a pirfenidone-derived antifibrotic, and the mechanism has supportive but modest evidence in non-IPF progressive fibrosis (uILD, RELIEF). With about 37 patients per arm and only 24 weeks of follow-up, the expected FVC difference of roughly 50–80 mL against a between-patient SD near 200 mL leaves the trial clearly underpowered for p<0.05. The study is still recruiting at a single site close to its planned primary completion, which adds execution risk, though having two doses gives it two chances to succeed. No results are public, so I forecast moderately below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5a33b890ac02d3712a5342bbd8b141996a87bc195379e3bebd8e071059ef8ed6"},{"nct":"NCT05262023","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics, and Pharmacodynamics of DNL593 in Healthy Participants and Participants With Frontotemporal Dementia (FTD-GRN)","sponsor":"Denali Therapeutics Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":85,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.40079352150230846,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are purely safety and tolerability measures (TEAEs, labs, vitals, ECG, C-SSRS), with no efficacy comparison, so 'success' here amounts to the sponsor reporting DNL593 as generally well tolerated. Denali's previously disclosed Part A single-ascending-dose data in healthy volunteers were described as generally well tolerated, and the transport-vehicle platform has a reasonably established safety profile. The main risks are platform-related adverse events (e.g., infusion reactions or anemia-type effects seen with TfR-targeting molecules), or deprioritization or ambiguous reporting by Denali. I have not seen the Part B topline results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e74879e565f9bbf0b0db316e47491b211927990b5ceed037c9845743493a0ee4"},{"nct":"NCT05281471","title":"Efficacy & Safety of Olvi-Vec and Platinum-doublet + Bevacizumab Compared to Physician's Choice of Chemotherapy and Bevacizumab in Platinum-Resistant/Refractory Ovarian Cancer (PRROC) (OnPrime, GOG-3076)","sponsor":"Genelux Corporation","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":186,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.6377716741120973,"rationale":"The single-arm Phase 2 VIRO-15 trial reported striking ORR (~54%) and PFS (~11 months) in heavily pretreated PRROC, but single-arm results in selected patients often shrink in randomized testing. Here the control arm gets active bevacizumab plus chemotherapy, which can include a platinum doublet, so the comparator is strong. Oncolytic viruses have a poor Phase 3 track record, ovarian cancer Phase 3 success rates are low, and a 186-patient open-label trial from a small sponsor adds risk. Blinded independent central review of PFS and the plausible platinum-resensitization mechanism give some upside, but failure remains more likely than success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0cbee2d1bb85ecadf6d64ce5273e4080bb7b4fd42766680684adc8ae9fdb7728"},{"nct":"NCT05365672","title":"Clinical Trial With Donor Modified Immune Cells in Living Donor Kidney Transplantation","sponsor":"TolerogenixX GmbH","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":126,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.4451191834670022,"rationale":"The composite 'operational tolerance-like' endpoint favors the MIC arms by design: criterion 4 requires steroid-free therapy with ≤720 mg EC-MPS, which the protocol mandates for MIC patients, while ELITE-Symphony controls typically stay on steroids and full-dose MPS, so very few controls should qualify. The TOL-1 pilot suggested MIC induces regulatory B cells and is safe, supporting the Breg and no-DSA criteria, so even a modest responder rate in the 42 MIC patients could beat the 21 controls. The main risks are rejection or DSA after aggressive immunosuppression minimization, failure to reach the Breg threshold, and slow recruitment or early stopping in a small investigator-driven ATMP trial. No results are public, as the trial was still recruiting at the last update.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8b91e5c8bc0a34662ca0bffb7fbf89214c43d873daa4a64df3fa715a95bc521e"},{"nct":"NCT05397639","title":"Masupirdine for the Treatment of Agitation in Dementia of the Alzheimer's Type","sponsor":"Suven Life Sciences Limited","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":375,"base":0.18,"researched":0.25,"learned":0.6237019655960073,"rationale":"The efficacy signal comes only from a post hoc subgroup of a failed Phase 2a cognition trial, measured on the NPI rather than the CMAI. Every other 5-HT6 antagonist has failed in Alzheimer's, and CMAI agitation trials show large placebo responses, with even approved or promising drugs such as brexpiprazole and AXS-05 producing mixed results. The DSMB's decision not to raise the sample size and the over-enrollment add little information. Two dose arms give the trial two chances to hit significance, which lifts the estimate slightly, but a probability of roughly 25% seems appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"2beebe8aef2645e7e56e20d528b544d4d33a13f626d9353d70988dd132bfcc8e"},{"nct":"NCT05456256","title":"A Study of LP-300 With Carboplatin and Pemetrexed in Never Smokers With Advanced Lung Adenocarcinoma","sponsor":"Lantern Pharma Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":90,"base":0.1,"researched":null,"learned":0.34939391323172214,"rationale":"LP-300 (dimesna/Tavocept) already failed its earlier Phase 3 trials in NSCLC. The never-smoker hypothesis rests on a post-hoc subgroup signal, and this trial's only supporting data are small, uncontrolled lead-in response rates. With about 90 patients randomized 2:1, the trial is underpowered to show a statistically significant PFS or OS gain over carboplatin-pemetrexed in post-TKI patients, especially since chemotherapy is reasonably active in this setting. Slow enrollment, limited sponsor resources and an open-label phase 2 design make a formal statistically significant win unlikely, though not impossible.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5f84611765a8614b56ca00655bc8725aeba39da2fdf3bd300e919dadc3ddaad2"},{"nct":"NCT05477576","title":"Study of RYZ101 Compared With SOC in Pts w Inoperable SSTR+ Well-differentiated GEP-NET That Has Progressed Following 177Lu-SSA Therapy","sponsor":"RayzeBio, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":343,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.8049520229803133,"rationale":"RYZ101 (225Ac-DOTATATE) showed encouraging activity in the ACTION-1 Phase 1b part, with an objective response rate of roughly 29% in patients who had progressed after 177Lu-PRRT. Targeted alpha therapy (including 212Pb-DOTAMTATE) has repeatedly shown meaningful efficacy in this setting. The comparator, investigator's choice of everolimus, sunitinib or high-dose SSA, gives modest PFS in post-PRRT patients, and BICR-assessed PFS with 143 events gives reasonable power. Risks include patient selection (enrolment required at least 6 months of prior disease control on Lu-177), possible toxicity or dose-reduction effects, and the general phase 3 failure rate in oncology, so I settle around 0.68.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"76c906053811cad917b1eaedaf6598f27f367733b6e94b6cdd045ab950e1854d"},{"nct":"NCT05500222","title":"A Phase 3 Study to Evaluate the Effect of Resmetirom on Clinical Outcomes in Patients With Well-compensated NASH Cirrhosis (MAESTRO-NASH-OUTCOMES)","sponsor":"Madrigal Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":845,"base":0.4,"researched":0.37,"learned":0.5497636319236858,"rationale":"No drug has yet shown a benefit on hard clinical outcomes in compensated NASH cirrhosis, and event-driven trials in this population struggle with low placebo event rates (about 2–3% per year), long timelines and dilution from dropout and background therapy. Resmetirom is a proven antifibrotic in F2–F3 NASH, and open-label F4 data show liver-stiffness reductions and some regression, which gives it a better rationale than most entrants. However, histologic and stiffness gains in cirrhosis have not reliably translated into fewer decompensation events, and the 3:1 randomization limits placebo events. Weighing a credible mechanism against a historically very hard endpoint, I put success somewhat below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"608614acec3f43f8f88a53e5b9ecb349d2d706bbb672d92fb73e22cbd9ac399c"},{"nct":"NCT05557448","title":"To Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of TYNADOTE® in the Treatment of Acetaminophen Overdose","sponsor":"Sinew Pharma Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":24,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.2966290647493517,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n=24), single-site exploratory Phase 2 study of an add-on agent (TYNADOTE, likely a sucralose/mannitol-based CYP2E1-inhibiting excipient combination from Sinew Pharma) on top of standard IV NAC. Most NAC-treated overdose patients have modest ALT changes, and the ALT response is highly variable, so percentage change at Day 3 with 12 per arm is badly underpowered. Adjunct therapies to NAC have generally not shown clear benefit, and the record looks stale (last updated January 2024, still recruiting), which suggests slow enrollment. The chance of a statistically significant favorable result on the primary endpoint is low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"32c72129c6bb713b7370d8f3c76a1ee16307b7395d1e56b110c14623af08cb90"},{"nct":"NCT05608681","title":"A Trial to Evaluate EP-104GI in Adults With Eosinophilic Esophagitis (EoE).","sponsor":"Eupraxia Pharmaceuticals Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":117,"base":0.77,"researched":null,"learned":0.7326007188694531,"rationale":"The first-listed primary efficacy outcome is the randomized phase 2 comparison of EP-104GI 120 or 160 mg against vehicle on change in EoEHSS at week 24, measured within the injection area. Locally delivered corticosteroids produce large histologic effects over placebo in EoE, and placebo histologic response is minimal. Eupraxia's open-label dose-escalation cohorts reportedly showed meaningful EoEHSS and eosinophil reductions, and roughly 40 patients per arm should give good power for a continuous histology score. The main risks are whether a single depot dose lasts to week 24, injection-related variability, and the general uncertainty of small-company phase 2 trials; no topline result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5129fb340afcce46de7c4e45cab3c60c99aff96ce5eba747b9a56123e4df837d"},{"nct":"NCT05654454","title":"A Safety and Efficacy Study of Bevacizumab, Paclitaxel, Carboplatin Compared to Avastin® in Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","sponsor":"Mabscale, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":620,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.6110183006651009,"rationale":"This is a biosimilar equivalence trial of bevacizumab against Avastin, using an ORR endpoint with chemotherapy backbones in non-squamous NSCLC. Nearly all such trials have met their equivalence margins, including Russia's earlier BCD-021 and many global bevacizumab biosimilars. With 620 patients, power for a typical ORR risk-ratio or difference margin should be adequate. The remaining risk comes from a smaller, newer sponsor, a margin the record does not state, possible manufacturing or quality differences, and an unknown recruitment status, since the record was last updated in 2024 while the trial was still recruiting.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c7cf037f315c5b74235d96030e591f2f834f9a169c9b344cb74afb92e65080fd"},{"nct":"NCT05727176","title":"Study of Futibatinib in Patients With Advanced Cholangiocarcinoma With FGFR2 Fusion or Rearrangement","sponsor":"Taiho Oncology, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":120,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.37378554156161,"rationale":"This appears to be the FOENIX-CCA4 confirmatory and dose-optimization trial. Its primary endpoint is ICR-assessed ORR, most likely judged as each arm's response rate clearing a prespecified threshold rather than a head-to-head superiority test. Futibatinib 20 mg gave a 42% ORR in FOENIX-CCA2 in FGFR inhibitor-naive, previously treated FGFR2-fusion cholangiocarcinoma, so with about 60 patients per arm the 20 mg arm should comfortably exceed a plausible null rate of 15–20%. The main risks are ambiguity over how success is defined, lower response rates with broader real-world enrollment, and slow recruitment; the result does not appear to be public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6bf626c189f930f0bb24d48c52f08edd0d4ad2fbeb8bbef7dda8fe206a0e7cc3"},{"nct":"NCT05762107","title":"A Study of the Effect of ZT-01 on Night-time Hypoglycemia in Type 1 Diabetes","sponsor":"Zucara Therapeutics Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":186,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.6989818424963227,"rationale":"ZT-01 is a somatostatin receptor-2 antagonist meant to restore the glucagon counter-regulatory response. Phase 1 clamp data reportedly showed a higher glucagon response, but this is the first test of a new mechanism on a clinical endpoint, nocturnal hypoglycemia events below 54 mg/dL. The crossover design, the enrollment of patients with frequent hypoglycemia, and three doses each compared with placebo help power, and one dose succeeding counts. Against that, hypoglycemia event counts are highly variable, the sponsor is small, and enrollment has been slow (still recruiting more than three years after start), so I am somewhat below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7880fef8a59bd66c282afc86cc5c70cb95e9dfcbad6b258067ce949f7bbb7ab4"},{"nct":"NCT05776277","title":"Iltamiocel Compared to Placebo for Chronic Fecal Incontinence in Females With Obstetric Injury","sponsor":"Cook MyoSite","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":200,"base":0.3,"researched":0.25,"learned":0.6279957960199611,"rationale":"Iltamiocel's FI evidence is uncontrolled (Phase 1/2, roughly 54% with ≥50% reduction), and FI episode-frequency endpoints are known for large placebo and regression-to-the-mean responses, as seen with bulking agents and sham-controlled trials. The same autologous muscle-derived cell product failed its randomized placebo-controlled Phase 3 in stress urinary incontinence (52% vs 53.6%), a close mechanistic analogue. Enrollment of about 100–200 with a continuous frequency endpoint gives some power, but the base rate for a cell therapy beating vehicle placebo here is low.","sources":7,"state":"screened","leaf":"62a64d418cfe8be89c69415048ffda61ef8e595d46252046f02c3ca866c6b766"},{"nct":"NCT05778188","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics, and Efficacy of RLS-0071 in Newborns With Moderate or Severe Hypoxic-Ischemic Encephalopathy Undergoing Therapeutic Hypothermia","sponsor":"ReAlta Life Sciences, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":173,"base":0.13,"researched":0.2,"learned":0.6229264445628478,"rationale":"No neonatal HIE adjunct to cooling has yet shown a significant benefit on MRI injury scores; erythropoietin's small phase 2 MRI signal did not hold up in HEAL. RLS-0071 is a novel anti-inflammatory peptide with only preclinical and PK support, and the phase 2 portion now targets about 70 infants split across moderate and severe HIE and two dose levels, so it is likely underpowered for a continuous Weeke score. The shifting endpoints and slipping timelines add uncertainty, though a continuous MRI score and a possible favorable sponsor analysis leave some chance of a nominal win.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"fdfd08bf892ff9873d848a9d84997cf4ddec74756c613693a37d04f4185d20fa"},{"nct":"NCT05780567","title":"Clinical Study on Adjuvant Therapy of TQB3616 Combined With Endocrine Therapy Compared With Placebo Combined With Endocrine Therapy in Patients With Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":1946,"base":0.5,"researched":0.55,"learned":0.6146368165174905,"rationale":"TQB3616 (culmerciclib) is a CDK4-biased inhibitor with strong PFS benefit in advanced HR+/HER2− disease, and the two CDK4/6 inhibitors with similar profiles (abemaciclib, ribociclib) met iDFS in adjuvant phase 3 trials, while palbociclib failed twice. This trial is double-blind and reasonably sized (n≈1946, 2:1), but the eligibility criteria do not clearly restrict to high-risk patients, and follow-up is short (start 2023, primary completion 2026-12), so a low event count could leave it underpowered. Chinese sponsors often have favorable topline readouts, but the adjuvant CDK4/6 track record is roughly 50/50, so I put the probability slightly above even.","sources":1,"state":"screened","leaf":"7ceaae825f59c602afaec7d00a33a5691dd19ec88e89fddbaaeafadaaee24701"},{"nct":"NCT05884255","title":"An Open-label Phase 3 Study of Lutetium (177Lu) Oxodotreotide Injection in Subjects With Advanced Gastrointestinal Pancreatic Neuroendocrine Tumors.","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":220,"base":0.9,"researched":0.93,"learned":0.6621669907960052,"rationale":"This is essentially a NETTER-1-style design (177Lu-SSA plus standard octreotide LAR vs high-dose octreotide LAR) in SSTR-positive G1–G2 GEP-NETs. Every comparable randomized trial of this mechanism gave very large PFS effects: NETTER-1 HR 0.18, the Chinese XT-XTR008 trial HR 0.06, and NETTER-2 in pNET HR 0.34. With about 220 patients and a weak control arm, power is very high even if the effect is attenuated. The main risks are operational: only two sites, still recruiting near the planned completion date, and a possible delay or early termination, which leaves a residual chance of failure.","sources":8,"state":"screened","leaf":"a8808d57d896a66d438f02e0ce161ab9158fa0647c291c9601bf64777160051c"},{"nct":"NCT05922878","title":"Study of ALTO-300 in MDD","sponsor":"Alto Neuroscience","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":325,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.24858290974006755,"rationale":"ALTO-300 is agomelatine, which has modest monotherapy efficacy, but it is being tested here as adjunctive therapy at 25 mg, a weakly supported use, in an EEG-biomarker-defined subgroup. That subgroup is likely only part of the roughly 325 enrolled, which limits power against the high placebo response typical of adjunctive MDD trials. Alto's similar biomarker-guided strategy failed in the ALTO-100 phase 2b in 2024, lowering confidence in the approach. The trial is still recruiting with primary completion planned for December 2026, so no result is public; the estimate starts from a base rate of roughly 25–30% for phase 2 psychiatry trials.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7360eb9dab191cb8737c0097fc6d28364664aa746f75b367ad1ba4e09e914fb4"},{"nct":"NCT05948475","title":"Study of Tinengotinib VS. Physician's Choice a Treatment of Subjects With FGFR-altered in Cholangiocarcinoma","sponsor":"TransThera Sciences (Nanjing), Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":200,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.7592367054464105,"rationale":"Tinengotinib is a multi-kinase inhibitor that also hits FGFR resistance mutations. Phase 2 data in FGFR-inhibitor-refractory FGFR2-fusion cholangiocarcinoma showed meaningful responses and a median PFS of roughly 6–7 months, against an expected 2–4 months for FOLFOX/FOLFIRI in later lines. The efficacy primary, Part B PFS by blinded independent review, favors success, and open-label bias is limited by the independent review. Risks include a small sample, a phase 2 signal that may not hold up in a randomized trial, and a small sponsor, so I place the probability modestly above the oncology phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b36174d03b926987a8ccf605085445486af6053144c5984b2fdf5fc134be60cf"},{"nct":"NCT05987358","title":"A Clinical Study of TQB3454 Tablets in the Treatment of Advanced Biliary Carcinoma.","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":165,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.5703711435027782,"rationale":"IDH1 inhibition has been validated in previously treated IDH1-mutant cholangiocarcinoma: ivosidenib in ClarIDHy clearly improved PFS. Its intention-to-treat OS benefit (HR ~0.79) was not significant, largely because of crossover, while crossover-adjusted OS suggested an HR near 0.5. This trial uses OS as primary with about 165 patients randomized 2:1 and no stated crossover, so a true HR of about 0.6 would give reasonable power. However, the small sample, OS as a demanding endpoint, uncertain potency of this new Chinese IDH1 inhibitor, and possible post-progression access to other therapies leave substantial risk, so I put the chance at about even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c190237dc599b68da3c14f224f21979ca8470850ee95f6bad93d24b7adb5d8de"},{"nct":"NCT06046222","title":"Trial of Efficacy and Safety of NS-229 Versus Placebo in Patients With Eosinophilic Granulomatosis With Polyangiitis","sponsor":"NS Pharma, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":45,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.3381714750201592,"rationale":"NS-229 is a selective JAK1 inhibitor being tested in a small (n≈45) phase 2 EGPA trial. The primary endpoint is remission (BVAS 0 plus prednisone ≤4 mg/day at week 28), and patients enter on background steroids, many already on anti-IL-5 therapy. Placebo remission rates on endpoints like this are typically very low (single digits in MIRRA), so a moderate drug effect could reach significance even with this sample size, and case series of JAK inhibitors in refractory EGPA have shown steroid-sparing benefit. Against that, this is a first randomized test of the mechanism in a rare, heterogeneous disease, with a stringent steroid threshold and a short taper window, so the outcome is roughly a coin flip, slightly below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9878db142807091c156f3ec930bbedfdc17feb4ffe4816d86d1df12fe6732cfd"},{"nct":"NCT06075264","title":"Phase II Study of Artesunate Ointment for the Treatment of Vulvar High Grade Squamous Intraepithelial Lesions (Vulvar HSIL, VIN2/3)","sponsor":"Frantz Viral Therapeutics, LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":27,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.34282106911601407,"rationale":"This is a very small (n≈27, 2:1) phase II placebo-controlled trial of topical artesunate, and its primary outcome is a strict endpoint: complete histologic response at 18 weeks. Earlier artesunate work in cervical HSIL suggested regression, but complete responses with topical therapy for vulvar HSIL are modest (imiquimod reached about 35%). With only about 9 placebo patients, even a 0% placebo rate needs roughly 8/18 responders for p<0.05, so the trial is underpowered. The primary outcome is also framed descriptively, which may mean no formal significant comparison is reported, further lowering the chance of a clear win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a1ba4e54cb411ae50237848d2e6f3b756f66ad63f28818e160c90d72b588efcc"},{"nct":"NCT06080789","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of a Single Dose of RABI-767 in Participants With Acute Pancreatitis","sponsor":"Panafina, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":36,"base":0.42,"researched":null,"learned":0.33025532870218544,"rationale":"This small open-label Phase 2a trial (n=36) has only safety primary endpoints, counts of AEs and SAEs, with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so a statistically significant result favoring RABI-767 is very unlikely. Whether it counts as success therefore depends mostly on whether the sponsor reports the drug as 'safe and well tolerated, meeting the primary endpoint.' Small sponsors often frame safety-primary results that way, but an invasive EUS-guided peripancreatic injection in predicted severe pancreatitis could add adverse events relative to standard care alone. The trial is still recruiting, so delays and limited disclosure are also plausible.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fa4ccdd8fa2af31ed42d2dbe2f95278a99a094c51c73fbb32e002c3c2f496d2c"},{"nct":"NCT06107413","title":"Study to Assess Adverse Events and Change in Disease Activity in Previously Treated Adult Participants Receiving Intravenous (IV) ABBV-400 With Unresectable Metastatic Colorectal Cancer in Combination With IV Fluorouracil, Folinic Acid, and Bevacizumab","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":280,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.45565212945381683,"rationale":"This is a randomized phase 2 dose-optimization study of the c-Met ADC telisotuzumab adizutecan (ABBV-400) plus 5-FU/leucovorin/bevacizumab against FOLFIRI-bevacizumab in second-line mCRC, with ORR as the first primary endpoint. FOLFIRI-bevacizumab gives modest second-line response rates (about 5-20%), and a topoisomerase-I-payload ADC combined with FFB could plausibly reach 30-50%, which would be significant even with roughly 40 patients per arm. However, the stage 2 comparator cohort may be descriptive rather than powered for a formal test, and c-Met expression was not required for enrollment, which may dilute efficacy. Together these leave the outcome close to a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8a6c9eb34142ccceaea583341be88c31597b0ea30b56c78346bf9ce77439a859"},{"nct":"NCT06132893","title":"A Study to Determine if BHV-7000 is Effective and Safe in Adults With Refractory Focal Onset Epilepsy","sponsor":"Biohaven Therapeutics Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":390,"base":0.57,"researched":0.62,"learned":0.7832643896743651,"rationale":"Kv7.2/7.3 opening is a validated mechanism in focal epilepsy: ezogabine was approved, and azetukalner was clearly positive in both Phase 2b and Phase 3. Adjunctive focal-seizure trials of mechanistically sound drugs against placebo succeed fairly often, and the 75 mg open-label responder data are encouraging. Against that, BHV-7000 has no controlled focal efficacy data, it failed its primary endpoints in MDD and bipolar mania, and its selective low-sedation profile may mean weaker target engagement than azetukalner. Biohaven's late-stage track record is spotty and Part B's sample size is modest, so I land moderately above even odds.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"f28e0e2df14eb53ed7732eaac84579518d8a26c2b295b6bc31ce17c1ebd1d491"},{"nct":"NCT06220773","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of BR1019A and BR1019B Combination Therapy","sponsor":"Boryung Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":276,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.9013121828458606,"rationale":"This is a factorial fixed-dose-combination study from Boryung, likely pairing an already-approved antihypertensive (possibly fimasartan) with an approved antidiabetic. The first primary endpoint compares the full combination against the same regimen with a placebo in place of the antihypertensive component (A-1). An approved antihypertensive against placebo typically lowers sitting systolic pressure by 6 to 10 mmHg more over 12 weeks, and about 69 patients per arm gives ample power. The main risks are operational, such as slow enrollment at 3 sites and a large placebo response, so success is highly likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7ae35e912be477bfc5016bb929299e8be3e75ab0406c34558a09a088ba8fe07c"},{"nct":"NCT06221748","title":"DV Combined With Cadonilimab in Subjects With HER2-expressing Gastric Cancer and Gastroesophageal Junction Adenocarcinoma After Progression on First-line Therapy","sponsor":"RemeGen Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":90,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.6725957869760402,"rationale":"The first-listed primary endpoint is phase II ORR across three arms of roughly 30 patients each, likely an exploratory comparison rather than one formally powered for significance. Disitamab vedotin combined with a PD-1 inhibitor has shown ORRs of about 40% or higher in HER2-expressing gastric cancer, against roughly 15–20% for second-line paclitaxel. A gap that size could reach significance even with ~30 per arm. Against that, including HER2 IHC 1+ patients may dilute the effect, the small arms make the result noisy, and the sponsor may report ORR only descriptively, so I put the chance of a clearly significant win near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0f28e95bc33f5a9b31307231719fa2a1a7f6a8723ab82472f216e1ad0380d605"},{"nct":"NCT06269705","title":"ZILRETTA in Subjects With Shoulder Osteoarthritis","sponsor":"Pacira Pharmaceuticals, Inc","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":150,"base":0.58,"researched":0.5,"learned":0.5220185775399496,"rationale":"ZILRETTA clearly beat saline at Week 12 in the large knee pivotal (p<0.0001), but that trial had about 160 patients per arm. This trial has about 100 versus 50, so if the knee effect (roughly 1 point on the NRS, effect size about 0.4) carries over, power is only around 60–70%. Shoulder OA is untested for efficacy and intra-articular steroid evidence in the shoulder is thin. The looser pain entry criterion (≥4) and typically large saline placebo responses add risk, partly offset by placebo-response-reduction training. Signs of trouble include a dropped TCA-IR arm, a timeline-related impairment and the vague interim analysis, so I put this near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"2661b041919f06e8836ec3893b85ddbf717f4595643dcddd366bcd6fcc44a9fd"},{"nct":"NCT06302491","title":"A Study of Safety and Efficiency of AND017 in Patients With β-thalassemia","sponsor":"Kind Pharmaceuticals LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":64,"base":0.57,"researched":null,"learned":0.5111671750447468,"rationale":"The only primary outcome is safety and tolerability (CTCAE AE rate), so there is no prespecified efficacy comparison that could clearly succeed or fail. Such endpoints are usually reported as 'met' when the sponsor describes the drug as safe and well tolerated, but a statistically significant advantage over placebo on AE rate is implausible, which makes the outcome ambiguous. AND017 is an oral HIF-PH inhibitor, and the class (e.g., roxadustat) has shown erythropoietic activity and acceptable tolerability in thalassemia, so a favorable safety readout is likely if the trial is judged that way. Because the scoring convention is uncertain and the small single-country study is still recruiting, I stay only modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3521737ac74514f252dcf5b9e74b8f25100ced11e2c3cdbacee37173c776d41e"},{"nct":"NCT06304103","title":"A Study of Efficacy and Safety of AND017 in Patients With Myelodysplastic Syndrome","sponsor":"Kind Pharmaceuticals LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":63,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.4073764340338867,"rationale":"This is an open-label, single-site, dose-ranging Phase 2 of an oral HIF-PHI with no control arm, so its 'primary endpoint' is a descriptive HI-E/transfusion-independence response rate with no stated threshold, which makes a topline 'success' a judgment call. HIF-PHIs have shown modest erythroid responses in lower-risk, low-transfusion-burden MDS: open-label roxadustat cohorts reported roughly 30–40% transfusion independence, which a sponsor would likely frame as positive. However, roxadustat's placebo-controlled MATTERHORN trial failed, and this small Chinese sponsor's trial is still recruiting, so results may be unimpressive or slow to appear. I land slightly above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"188ff2a208f8abd18dcf208956bc1a411e82424d8f4d60fdc18c1a59bc8cf477"},{"nct":"NCT06309485","title":"Phase 2 Study of WGI-0301 for Advanced HCC","sponsor":"Zhejiang Haichang Biotech Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":60,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3048969495052822,"rationale":"This is a small (60 patients total, including dose escalation), open-label phase 1/2 trial of an LNP-formulated Akt-1 antisense oligonucleotide plus sorafenib. The predecessor, Archexin/RX-0201, showed only modest activity in earlier trials. Sorafenib's ORR after checkpoint-inhibitor failure is low (about 5–10%), so a randomized ORR comparison with roughly 15–20 patients per arm has little power to reach p<0.05 unless the effect is very large, and the study is likely not powered for formal significance at all. A new mechanism in second-line HCC, a weak antisense track record, and an underpowered comparison together make a statistically significant win unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fae5ed13c1ba6e845f833e169e026c3ef71ed494778accf4bc7143a7ca071814"},{"nct":"NCT06340633","title":"SPI-1005 in Adults Receiving Cochlear Implant","sponsor":"Sound Pharmaceuticals, Incorporated","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":40,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.23968507398407377,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety measure, the number of treatment-emergent adverse events. It has no prespecified efficacy comparison, and a 40-patient trial is very unlikely to show a significant difference favoring ebselen over placebo. The sponsor would probably describe the drug as 'safe and well tolerated', which could be scored as a success. But the trial is small, appears delayed (start date listed as 2026-12 while recruiting), and no results are public, so the probability stays low to moderate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1d038e6fe9f6264451fb2651af101edaa5134b40c909227459f0f5e0264f11fb"},{"nct":"NCT06361537","title":"Study of IV Human Plasma-derived C1 Esterase Inhibitor Concentrate in Patients With Congenital C1-INH Deficiency for Treatment and Pre-procedure Preventing of Acute Hereditary Angioedema Attacks","sponsor":"Octapharma","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":124,"base":0.85,"researched":0.8,"learned":0.7908840090725574,"rationale":"Plasma-derived C1-INH at 20 IU/kg against placebo is a well-proven approach: IMPACT-1 (Berinert) with the same n≈124 and dose met its time-to-relief endpoint, and Cinryze and Ruconest also succeeded. OCTA-C1-INH is essentially a biosimilar-like plasma concentrate, so its efficacy should be similar. Risks include the stricter three-consecutive-rating relief definition, a sizable placebo response, heterogeneous multinational sites that may add noise, and recruitment slippage that could shrink the blinded sample. A high but not near-certain probability seems appropriate.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"24f6fa1ba588944f15c4ff8fecccc7c3765fd0ffaaf53287a57b071b5f1ce25a"},{"nct":"NCT06382129","title":"A Study Comparing BL-B01D1 With Docetaxel in Patients With Unresectable Locally Advanced or Metastatic EGFR Wild-type Non-small Cell Lung Cancer(PANKU-Lung02)","sponsor":"Sichuan Baili Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":698,"base":0.6,"researched":0.55,"learned":0.5181533176895365,"rationale":"Iza-bren has already beaten chemotherapy on OS in randomized Chinese Phase 3 trials in TNBC and ESCC, and it met PFS at interim in EGFR-mutant NSCLC. Its single-arm ORR of roughly 30–45% in EGFR-wild-type disease is well above docetaxel's ~13%, and 698 patients should give good power for a modest OS hazard ratio. Against that, OS versus docetaxel after immunotherapy and platinum has defeated similar ADCs (Dato-DXd in TROPION-Lung01, HER3-DXd in HERTHENA-Lung02). Toxicity and the heterogeneous wild-type population (including squamous) could also dilute the survival gain. Balancing the drug's track record and a China-only setting with limited crossover against this historically hard endpoint, I put success slightly above even.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"a1accda8d73a798835e3410c5e685963ff198fc98c2939a923b0865c61188085"},{"nct":"NCT06403267","title":"NoNO-42 Trial in Acute Ischemic Stroke Patients Selected for Thrombolysis With or Without Endovascular Thrombectomy","sponsor":"NoNO Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":600,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3044189293951194,"rationale":"NoNO-42 is a next-generation PSD-95-targeting neuroprotectant, likely engineered to resist the alteplase/plasmin cleavage that undermined nerinetide. Nerinetide itself failed in ESCAPE-NA1 overall and in ESCAPE-NEXT, and acute stroke neuroprotection has a long history of near-universal phase 2/3 failure. A 600-patient open-label, blinded-endpoint trial with an mRS shift primary endpoint has only modest power for the small effects plausible in a thrombolysed population. The trial is still recruiting at only 9 Canadian sites, so no result is public, and the base rate points to a low probability of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3b5e998fd5aac3681b0312a30309301bc3226afe29b63365c5cba584622b587d"},{"nct":"NCT06413433","title":"Elucidating TAAR-1, Dopamine, and Norepinephrine in Binge Eating Disorder Using Solriamfetol","sponsor":"Axsome Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":450,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.7154592510323271,"rationale":"Dopamine/norepinephrine-enhancing drugs have a good track record in binge eating disorder: lisdexamfetamine succeeded in its phase 3 program and dasotraline was positive in at least one trial. A small investigator-initiated study of solriamfetol in BED reportedly suggested benefit, and two doses at 150 per arm give reasonable power. Against that, placebo response in BED is high, a count-of-episodes endpoint is noisy, and Axsome's solriamfetol program outside sleep disorders has been mixed (positive in ADHD, failed in MDD). Overall this lands slightly above a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8524080a14cb1c8fefc08028eb42c99023a29a3cf8aab9c80dda348d9679ba90"},{"nct":"NCT06414954","title":"Safety and Efficacy of 3 Dose Levels of NMD670 in Adult Patients With Myasthenia Gravis","sponsor":"NMD Pharma A/S","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":84,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.5826947138592854,"rationale":"NMD670 is a first-in-class ClC-1 chloride channel inhibitor; its single-dose Phase 1/2a study showed numerical QMG improvements, which gives proof of mechanism but no robust multi-dose efficacy data. This Phase 2b trial is small (about 21 per arm) and short (21 days), with placebo-controlled QMG change on top of background therapy. A symptomatic agent may give only modest effects of 1–3 points against placebo responses of a similar size, so power is marginal. Having three dose arms helps, but multiplicity adjustments and the historical failure rate of first-in-class Phase 2 trials in neuromuscular disease keep the probability below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cfef27213f0ba7b9c565872245a798debad35e48df2af62969aa98404731e6c2"},{"nct":"NCT06456593","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Obefazimod in Subjects With Moderately to Severely Active Crohn's Disease","sponsor":"Abivax S.A.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":212,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.437580408776215,"rationale":"Obefazimod, which upregulates miR-124, has positive Phase 2b and Phase 3 (ABTECT) induction results in ulcerative colitis, so the drug has real anti-inflammatory activity in IBD. However, many agents that work in UC have failed or underperformed in Crohn's disease, and CD has high and noisy placebo responses on CDAI. The primary endpoint, change from baseline in CDAI at week 12, is continuous, there are three doses with about 53 patients per arm, and one dose succeeding counts, all of which help power. Balancing the mechanism's UC validation against the CD translation risk, the chance of success is roughly a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d910d82b2fbad0cdf8e45ca3c9ba1aa11928c1f082bcf6d20c0c6eac0b33bd8b"},{"nct":"NCT06468228","title":"A Study to Assess Disease Activity and Safety of Lutikizumab in Adult and Adolescent Participants With Moderate to Severe Hidradenitis Suppurativa","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":1400,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.8248830915285854,"rationale":"Lutikizumab, an anti-IL-1α/β antibody, showed a clear signal in its Phase 2 study of anti-TNF-experienced HS patients (HiSCR50 roughly 59% vs 35% for placebo at week 16), and IL-17 agents have repeatedly succeeded in HS Phase 3. Each arm has about 640 participants, so the trial is heavily powered, though HiSCR75 is a stricter endpoint and placebo responses in HS can be high. Recent HS programs (e.g., sonelokimab's VELA-2) show that misses happen even after strong Phase 2 data. Primary completion is December 2026 and I don't believe results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7d4a0d120428b14ba9b993b40ecf114da32dd8466e1c6453f0bddedee6e23173"},{"nct":"NCT06500026","title":"A Study Comparing BL-B01D1 With Topotecan in Patients With Recurrent Small Cell Lung Cancer(PANKU-Lung03)","sponsor":"Sichuan Baili Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":722,"base":0.77,"researched":null,"learned":0.6011489929145966,"rationale":"Iza-bren (BL-B01D1), an EGFR×HER3 bispecific ADC with a topoisomerase I payload, showed high response rates (about 50–60%) and encouraging survival in second-line SCLC in early-phase Chinese studies. Baili has already reported positive Chinese phase 3 readouts for this drug in other tumors. Topotecan is a weak comparator, and tarlatamab beat chemotherapy on OS in DeLLphi-304, so a meaningful OS advantage is plausible in this large 722-patient trial. OS in relapsed SCLC is still a hard endpoint (lurbinectedin's ATLANTIS failed against topotecan), and I don't recall a public topline for this trial, so I stay below 80%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7110e7bdb1134a4d9028d77fb5e2681f7697df4af6d8abca060082f7c50585f8"},{"nct":"NCT06501066","title":"Mesenchymal Stem Cells for Frailty Syndrome","sponsor":"Meribank Biotech Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":66,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.3246147573462952,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a Phase I safety measure (incidence of TEAEs/SAEs) with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so success most plausibly means the sponsor reports acceptable safety and tolerability. Single-dose IV umbilical cord MSCs have repeatedly looked well tolerated in older and frail adults, including prior allogeneic MSC frailty trials, and sponsors of such small studies usually announce that the safety endpoint was met. The main risks are that serious adverse events in a 65+ population over 12 months get attributed to treatment, or that the outcome is judged on the secondary frailty efficacy endpoints, which are underpowered at n=66. I know of no published result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9b2517cf043afbe66f7c0406513c4158309550a1ee6ff87daaff58c4a375008b"},{"nct":"NCT06534437","title":"MEN1703 (SEL24) to Treat Relapsed or Refractory Aggressive B-cell Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (JASPIS-01)","sponsor":"Ryvu Therapeutics SA","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":178,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.31122668328479147,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is Part 1 safety, and the efficacy endpoints are complete response and overall response rate, largely in single-arm cohorts. The randomized Part 3 comparison against glofitamab alone is optional and would be underpowered to show a significant gain in complete response over an already active bispecific. PIM/FLT3 inhibition has a weak track record in lymphoma, and early MEN1703 monotherapy activity appears modest, so a clearly positive topline is uncertain. Some chance remains that the sponsor reports encouraging combination complete-response rates that would read as a success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"431181e93294776d29abca44b82564d58ff56b777ad4b4fffe3ecc57640ec93e"},{"nct":"NCT06537999","title":"A Clinical Study to Evaluate DNTH103 in Adults With Multifocal Motor Neuropathy","sponsor":"Dianthus Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":46,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.3574118703937438,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety (TEAE and SAE incidence), not an efficacy comparison, so a sponsor topline would most likely describe it as met if claseprubart is well tolerated. That seems likely, given clean safety in prior claseprubart studies and in other complement C1s antibodies. The mechanism is also supported in this disease: argenx's empasiprubart (anti-C2) Phase 2 ARDA trial in MMN reduced the need for Ig retreatment, so the time-to-Ig-retreatment secondary endpoint could plausibly favor drug even with only 46 patients. The main risks are how a safety-only endpoint gets adjudicated and a small chance of an imbalance in adverse events or infections.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4b83b2df51d694b0d9ef19ec9d87aab29dc3208afc0c9ab32ece556e2a73bffa"},{"nct":"NCT06568367","title":"Studying Solriamfetol Modulation of TAAR-1, Dopamine, and Norepinephrine in Shift Work Disorder (SUSTAIN)","sponsor":"Axsome Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":520,"base":0.85,"researched":0.8,"learned":0.8080406428211165,"rationale":"Solriamfetol has consistently produced large MWT gains versus placebo in narcolepsy and OSA, and a small 4-week SWD RCT showed a 9.4-minute MWT benefit (P<0.001), so the first-listed MWT endpoint is very likely to succeed with roughly 150 per arm. The main risks are the co-primary CGI-S endpoint, a heterogeneous real-world SWD population, the 12-week duration, and higher placebo response in subjective measures. Modafinil and armodafinil did succeed on similar endpoints in SWD. The unexplained timeline slip adds slight uncertainty, but overall success is likely.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"bde181f89b2be70a6e1ac40e78e43bd5d9861ecbb04579de33efe74666f10ae1"},{"nct":"NCT06568627","title":"A Double Blind Study Performed to Evaluate the Efficacy and the Safety of EscharEx in Debridement of VLU (VALUE)","sponsor":"MediWound Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":216,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.5896456731425812,"rationale":"EscharEx (a bromelain-based enzymatic debrider) has repeatedly beaten gel vehicle on complete debridement in earlier phase 2 VLU trials, including ChronEx, so the first-listed endpoint plays to the drug's established mechanism. The adaptive design with a DMC and interim sample-size reassessment further lowers the risk of an underpowered result. The main risks are a strong vehicle response from autolytic debridement under hydrogel, variability in visual assessment across 60 sites, and a possible gatekeeping link to the harder wound-closure co-primary, which would shape how success is reported. I have not seen this trial's topline result made public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5c5b91af530681dd14a1cf20a20ca24fd4e21a61a14f384d1e3f08f5a48b8e63"},{"nct":"NCT06569524","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Recombinant Human FGF21-Fc Fusion Protein for Injection (TQA2225/AP025) in Adult Subjects With Non-alcoholic Steatohepatitis (NASH)","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Nanjing Shunxin Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":120,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.410022174728113,"rationale":"The FGF21 class is well validated in MASH: efruxifermin (an Fc-fusion like AP025), pegozafermin and efimosfermin all hit biopsy endpoints in phase 2 with large effects on NASH resolution and fibrosis. The primary endpoint here is a lenient composite (NASH resolution OR fibrosis improvement), which helps, but with about 40 patients per arm, variable placebo rates in Chinese biopsy trials, and unknown potency for this specific molecule, the trial could be underpowered. The record still shows recruiting and no results appear to be public, so I estimate a moderate-to-favorable chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8386aacb88519290832d621340ba3f5081597303e28cc58f85860c947685b92f"},{"nct":"NCT06570291","title":"Allogenic Adipose-Derived Mesenchymal Stem Cells for the Treatment of Knee Osteoarthritis","sponsor":"Wuxi Cellular Biopharmaceutical Group Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":520,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.5317038604812296,"rationale":"Phase III trials of intra-articular MSC products for knee OA have mixed results: Korea's JointStem reported positive WOMAC results, but many MSC trials show large placebo responses and modest separation, and this trial uses an active hyaluronate comparator, which raises the bar. CBMG/Wuxi Cellular's earlier ReJoin and AlloJoin studies reported favorable WOMAC trends versus HA, and Chinese industry-sponsored trials tend to report positively. The 520-patient sample gives reasonable power for a moderate effect. Still, a 48-week WOMAC difference against an active comparator is uncertain, and results are not yet public (primary completion is planned for December 2026 and enrollment was still ongoing).","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"764c5b7dc5818d142a12c49006db7f7ea6f6740acdea715d21635b859ee1ee23"},{"nct":"NCT06577935","title":"A Trial Evaluating Efficacy of AGA2118 in PostMenopausal Women wIth Low Bone MasS (ARTEMIS)","sponsor":"Angitia Biopharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":379,"base":0.94,"researched":null,"learned":0.8989293506910816,"rationale":"AGA2118 is a bispecific antibody against sclerostin and DKK1, a validated anabolic pathway. Romosozumab's phase 2 showed lumbar spine BMD gains of about 11% versus placebo at 12 months, and early AGA2118 studies reported bone-formation marker increases and BMD gains. With about 54 women per arm, six dose arms and a sensitive BMD endpoint against placebo, at least one arm reaching significance is highly likely. The main residual risk is execution or safety problems; I am not aware of any public topline result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4198961cff94b302d7f60196b82a28f638373fa4dd4c889e4e868497d58521a6"},{"nct":"NCT06579287","title":"A Study of SHJ002 Sterile Ophthalmic Solution for Myopia Control","sponsor":"Sunhawk Vision Biotech, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":140,"base":0.13,"researched":null,"learned":0.47325661024104354,"rationale":"SHJ002 is a first-in-class topical antisense oligonucleotide against a microRNA, tested here in a small (n=140) exploratory Phase II trial against an active atropine comparator rather than placebo. No margin is stated, so success means significant superiority over atropine on change in cycloplegic spherical equivalent, which is a high bar for a novel mechanism with no published efficacy data in myopia. Atropine, even at low dose, has a real effect, and this study is likely underpowered to show a difference against it. A positive head-to-head result is therefore unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"48a327e8da606a886fbe304d0a757174fdad21622eb10de4eba28589d2b1fc9f"},{"nct":"NCT06596252","title":"Once Daily Versus Twice Daily Budesonide Orodispersible Tablets for Induction of Remission in EoE","sponsor":"Dr. Falk Pharma GmbH","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":308,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.8650006678102097,"rationale":"Budesonide orodispersible tablet 1 mg BID is well proven in EoE, with histological remission around 90% at 6 weeks in EOS-1 and higher in EOS-2, and this trial compares the same total daily dose given once daily. With roughly 150 patients per arm and high expected remission rates, the confidence interval should be narrow enough to meet a typical 10–15% non-inferiority margin, unless once-daily dosing truly loses efficacy through shorter mucosal contact time. That pharmacological risk, plus the unknown margin and slow enrollment since 2021, keeps the estimate below 90%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8eff90e8b5134071b8a099e2e9d8900d10c8d25dc5e93e6b788fd8035ccb7ff0"},{"nct":"NCT06607458","title":"Evaluation of the Safety and Efficacy of Treatment w/High Dose Melphalan Given Directly Into the Liver Followed by Treatment w/Approved Cancer Treatment or Approved Cancer Treatment Alone in Patients w/ Metastatic Colorectal Cancer w/Liver Dominant Disease","sponsor":"Delcath Systems Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":90,"base":0.38,"researched":null,"learned":0.34934640289267793,"rationale":"Liver-directed therapies often improve hepatic-specific PFS over systemic therapy alone, and the open-label, investigator-assessed hPFS endpoint favors the experimental arm. Against that, melphalan/HDS has only modest, uncontrolled activity in heavily pretreated colorectal liver metastases. The trial is small (90 patients, 2:1), and Arm A delays systemic FTD-TPI plus bevacizumab by roughly 12 weeks. The study only began in August 2025, is still recruiting, and may never be fully enrolled or adequately powered, which further lowers the chance of a clean positive readout.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"749f16c8ea0fc34c845401b55046cf7a5909494c7ddb2a31314e3aab66457bae"},{"nct":"NCT06671379","title":"A Study of SHR-A2009 Versus Platinum-based Chemotherapy in EGFR-mutated, Advanced or Metastatic NSCLC","sponsor":"Suzhou Suncadia Biopharmaceuticals Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":498,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.6315357338913398,"rationale":"SHR-A2009 is Hengrui's HER3-directed topoisomerase-I ADC, which showed encouraging response rates in early-phase data in EGFR-mutant NSCLC after TKI failure. Same-class or similar ADCs have beaten platinum-pemetrexed on PFS in this setting: patritumab deruxtecan in HERTHENA-Lung02 (HR about 0.77) and sacituzumab tirumotecan in OptiTROP-Lung04 (a large PFS benefit). With about 500 patients and BICR-assessed PFS against an active but modest comparator, a PFS win is likely. The main risks are a modest effect size and ADC toxicity, such as interstitial lung disease, cutting treatment duration. Primary completion is not until December 2026 and I am not aware of any topline result.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"4e850f64e71f25402ffe4b6e1a0e15b6fc78788b0aa16ccd14ba6caec8e0f9bc"},{"nct":"NCT06677229","title":"Phase 1b/2a Clinical Trial to Determine the Safety, Tolerability and Efficacy of TZ-161 in Spinal Cord Injury","sponsor":"Technophage, SA","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":28,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.3103384300138542,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is the incidence of treatment-emergent AEs and SAEs, comparing eletriptan plus standard of care with standard of care alone, in an open-label trial of 28 patients that is still recruiting. A statistically significant difference favoring the drug on AE incidence is very unlikely, because acute SCI patients have frequent AEs in both arms and the trial is tiny. Eletriptan's well-known safety profile, though, makes a sponsor topline of 'safe and well tolerated' quite likely, which might be scored as success. Given that ambiguity, plus possible delays from a small two-site Spanish trial, I place this near even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"49fedf41fc8e748dafad3142c55e0ef01aeeaa3f5ff2005a8fa585487c9af62a"},{"nct":"NCT06707103","title":"Tissue Repair Gel in Venous Leg Ulcers in AU/US","sponsor":"TR Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":312,"base":0.3,"researched":0.2,"learned":0.6720467817217896,"rationale":"Topical add-on drugs for venous leg ulcers have a poor Phase 3 track record (HP802-247, LL-37 and others failed), and TR987's earlier evidence is weak: the Phase 2b primary result was never clearly reported, and the support is a post hoc pooled wound-area analysis with p=0.03 rather than complete closure. Compression standard of care produces substantial closure rates, so a modest add-on effect is hard to show on a binary closure endpoint. The small sponsor reports slow recruitment (~100 of 312 randomized by mid-2026), has de-prioritised one of its two studies, and is talking about a device pathway that may affect the drug trial, all of which make an adequately powered positive result less likely. Counting the real chance that the trial stops or finishes underpowered, the probability of a significant primary result is low.","sources":9,"state":"screened","leaf":"185b74644afa918e7de50fa5fc24a41a6a0534caa3d57838158b1ea0708a11dd"},{"nct":"NCT06707883","title":"A Clinical Study of TQC2731 Injection in Patients With Moderate to Severe Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease","sponsor":"Shanghai Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Technology Development Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":258,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.3621952262333014,"rationale":"TQC2731 is an anti-TSLP antibody, and the closest precedent is tezepelumab's phase 2a COURSE trial in COPD, which missed its primary exacerbation endpoint overall (about 17% reduction) and showed benefit mainly in patients with eosinophils of 150 or more. This trial has no apparent eosinophil enrichment, and with roughly 258 patients and a 24-week exacerbation window it is underpowered for a modest effect. A sponsor-favorable analysis or a lenient alpha could help, but the base rate for a phase 2 trial of a new biologic in COPD exacerbations is low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"85061d99ac3302d36cc6c0e94bc59c2a4e38a0e2d26b73d919b6de3dbd64340f"},{"nct":"NCT06711900","title":"A Study of SKB264 in Combination With Pembrolizumab Versus Chemotherapy in Combination With Pembrolizumab as First-Line Treatment for PD-L1 Negative Patients With Locally Advanced or Metastatic Non-Squamous Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","sponsor":"Sichuan Kelun-Biotech Biopharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":432,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.7055627423146179,"rationale":"Sacituzumab tirumotecan (sac-TMT) is a TROP2 ADC whose Kelun-run Chinese phase 3 trials (e.g., OptiTROP-Lung03/04 in EGFR-mutant NSCLC) have been positive, and its phase 2 first-line combinations with a PD-(L)1 agent showed encouraging response rates and PFS, including in PD-L1-negative patients. The bar here is harder than in those trials: the ADC replaces the platinum-pemetrexed doublet against pembrolizumab-chemotherapy in PD-L1 <1% disease, and TROP2 ADCs have given only modest PFS gains in other NSCLC settings. Single-country Chinese sponsor-run trials with a BICR-assessed PFS endpoint and about 432 patients have historically had relatively high success rates. I have no knowledge of the topline result, so this is a moderately favorable estimate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1be29dc6f921c644a544164aee811c0a8781c0883b710e7b84d85cb8279d35a5"},{"nct":"NCT06721871","title":"Ascending Doses of Crofelemer Powder for Oral Solution in Pediatric Microvillus Inclusion Disease (MVID)","sponsor":"Napo Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":6,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.6751599857307898,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n=6), crossover, dose-escalation study in ultra-rare MVID. Its primary outcomes are safety and tolerability (AEs, physical exam, labs), summarized descriptively with no formal hypothesis test, so 'success' would most likely mean the sponsor declaring crofelemer safe and well tolerated. Crofelemer is minimally absorbed, has a long safety record, and Jaguar/Napo has already promoted positive investigator-initiated MVID data, so a favorable topline framing is likely. Uncertainty remains because a strict statistical reading cannot be satisfied, and with six patients any efficacy signal will be noisy; primary completion is December 2026, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f238648036fe7d75a97af5721687f173d7fd4c89d696ab0859102bb9d2368a33"},{"nct":"NCT06752668","title":"A Study of ORX750 in Participants With Narcolepsy and Idiopathic Hypersomnia","sponsor":"Centessa Pharmaceuticals (UK) Limited","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":248,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.3771091172959487,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are safety and tolerability counts with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so 'success' here means acceptable safety and positive sponsor framing. Centessa has publicly reported interim CRYSTAL-1 data (2025) showing ORX750 was generally well tolerated, with large, statistically significant MWT improvements versus placebo in NT1, NT2 and IH. That supports advancing to registrational studies. The residual risk is that final data show safety signals seen with other orexin agonists, such as visual disturbances, insomnia, urinary effects or hepatotoxicity as with TAK-994, or that a safety-only primary is scored ambiguously.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"fb97ed4da17c0432cacad8f0f62ffaac338d9ee552a310d22f3ab8e442b3d0a8"},{"nct":"NCT06754644","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy, and Safety of QL2107 Plus Chemo and Compare With Keytruda in Participants With IV nqNSCLC","sponsor":"Qilu Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":808,"base":0.86,"researched":0.85,"learned":0.649734642755335,"rationale":"This is an equivalence trial of a pembrolizumab biosimilar against Keytruda, and biosimilar equivalence trials on ORR usually succeed. The closest analogue, Samsung Bioepis SB27 in the same setting, met its margin with 555 patients, and this trial is larger at 808, which narrows the confidence interval. The main risks are that Qilu's margin may be tighter than SB27's, that random ORR variation could push the interval outside it (SB27's point estimate was 0.91), and that some uncertainty about execution and possible delays remains. Overall the probability of meeting the equivalence margin is high but not certain.","sources":8,"state":"screened","leaf":"ea4cef96f73101a71acd39703215779594800b6c9f7c8a65f6c2a1035f00964a"},{"nct":"NCT06767527","title":"AK112 or Placebo Plus Nab-Paclitaxel as First-line Treatment in Inoperable Locally Advanced/ Metastatic Triple-negative Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Akeso","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":416,"base":0.82,"researched":0.77,"learned":0.6976582937662359,"rationale":"Ivonescimab adds a VEGF-blocking component, and bevacizumab plus paclitaxel reliably improved PFS in metastatic breast cancer (E2100). That makes a PFS gain over nab-paclitaxel alone plausible even in a largely PD-L1-negative population, where PD-1 agents alone have failed. Phase 2 TNBC data (ORR 80%, median PFS about 9.3 months, including CPS <10) look strong against an expected control median of about 5 months, and Akeso's China-only placebo-controlled phase 3s have a strong record of hitting PFS, with 416 patients adequate for a hazard ratio around 0.65. Risks are the small uncontrolled phase 2, the PD-L1-negative biology, and possible attenuation under independent central review; no result is public yet.","sources":1,"state":"screened","leaf":"cd6f4a8c1f8c725a7a29c1c6a7bf7d51c4b8a343e8eb67dbb0c076d666aaab09"},{"nct":"NCT06820099","title":"Study on the Efficacy and Safety of HRS-7535 in Patients With Mild Decrease in Ejection Fraction/Preserved Ejection Fraction Heart Failure and Obesity","sponsor":"Shandong Suncadia Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":225,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.44172716477888174,"rationale":"HRS-7535 is Hengrui's oral small-molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist, and earlier phase 2 obesity and diabetes trials showed clear, dose-dependent weight loss over placebo. The primary endpoint here is percent change in body weight at 36 weeks against placebo, with about 225 patients, so even a modest effect in obese HFpEF patients should be highly significant. The main risks are operational: high discontinuation from GI intolerance, or enrollment and completion problems at what is listed as a single site that is still recruiting. I have not seen this trial's result reported.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"384beb1657d3112d3af45e1818be224e5c26056bcdaf629b3ed4ea5cb2de4a88"},{"nct":"NCT06842823","title":"A Study of Navenibart in Participants With Hereditary Angioedema","sponsor":"Astria Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":157,"base":0.95,"researched":0.95,"learned":0.9155661831533041,"rationale":"Navenibart is a long-acting anti-plasma-kallikrein antibody, the same validated mechanism as lanadelumab, and its open-label data showed 84–95% attack reductions. Every placebo-controlled HAE prophylaxis trial on attack rate has succeeded, usually with p<0.001. With about 145 adults across three active arms and placebo, and placebo attack rates near 2 per month, the trial is well powered even for modest effects. The main risks are operational or dosing problems, especially with the every-6-month regimen, but only one arm needs to win.","sources":10,"state":"screened","leaf":"97f61f14795939e87e592165b89364ac575f4d36a1d0b3653c76252bd3cc7c6d"},{"nct":"NCT06848348","title":"Efficacy and Safety Study of Halneuron in the Treatment of Chemotherapy-Induced Neuropathic Pain","sponsor":"Dogwood Therapeutics Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":240,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.38816387855174084,"rationale":"Halneuron is subcutaneous tetrodotoxin, and its earlier Phase 2 trial in chemotherapy-induced neuropathic pain missed its primary endpoint, showing only trends. CINP is a notoriously hard indication with high placebo responses, where even duloxetine shows only modest benefit, so a 4-week responder endpoint in roughly 240 patients is unlikely to show a significant difference. The sponsor is a small, financially constrained company, and I am not aware that topline results have been released.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9f014f606d7df03189a6ae0cfa3c3a72d7a5d5271a34c099810d55c11f3d0a6c"},{"nct":"NCT06852768","title":"Study of d-MAPPS™ Ophthalmic Solution, Safety, Tolerability, and Efficacy in the Treatment of Chronic Ocular Graft-Versus-Host Disease (oGVHD)","sponsor":"Regenerative Ocular Immunobiologics LLC","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":15,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.4792477102015805,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n≈15) phase 1/2 placebo-controlled trial run by a small company testing an amniotic-derived biologic eye drop (d-MAPPS) in ocular GVHD, with a subjective symptom primary endpoint (UNC DEMS change). Placebo/sterile water drops tend to produce substantial symptom improvement in dry eye, and with roughly 7 patients per arm, statistical power to show a significant between-group difference is very low, even if the drug has some effect. Prior d-MAPPS data are open-label and uncontrolled. Success by formal statistical criteria is unlikely, though small sponsors sometimes report favorable trends.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8aa6d303393630e7d1c89f39d4697e487d1a7934e9abc6461a3f256676732350"},{"nct":"NCT06912633","title":"Safety of a Single, Intravitreal Injection of 6.0M jCell (Famzeretcel) in Retinitis Pigmentosa (RP)","sponsor":"jCyte, Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":31,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.29803333224983536,"rationale":"The primary outcome is safety (TEAEs, immunogenicity, safety visual assessments) at 6 months, not a prespecified efficacy comparison, so success would most plausibly be judged as acceptable tolerability. Earlier jCell (famzeretcel) trials, including the Phase 2b at doses up to 8.8M cells, showed a generally benign safety profile with no major signals, though the Phase 2b missed its efficacy primary. The main risks are ambiguity in how a safety-only primary is scored and the possibility of unexpected inflammatory or immunogenic events. Primary completion is planned for December 2026, and I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5a0e11786d3b65852c5afbf4df826a0bd845b53d96738a911aced1217f31db6a"},{"nct":"NCT06943820","title":"AK129 Combination Therapy for Advanced Solid Tumors","sponsor":"Akeso","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":230,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.4585104588692841,"rationale":"This is an open-label Phase Ib/II basket study whose first-listed primary endpoint is safety; most cohorts are single-arm and report ORR descriptively, so any 'success' would come down to how the sponsor frames the results. The one randomized comparison (AK129 plus chemotherapy vs penpulimab plus chemotherapy in first-line NSCLC) is small and probably not powered to show a significant ORR difference. Adding LAG-3 blockade to PD-1 inhibition has largely disappointed in NSCLC, though Akeso tends to report its bispecific data positively. I have no knowledge of results, so I land at a moderately low probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a68cd239470d8afb0348eb5bb6abf29231f69c190302488e0ee2c1608bc22fd6"},{"nct":"NCT06972264","title":"Safety and Efficacy of VDPHL01 in Males With AGA","sponsor":"Veradermics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":480,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.7868683734606944,"rationale":"VDPHL01 is an extended-release oral minoxidil, a mechanism with well-established efficacy in androgenetic alopecia, and earlier Veradermics data in men reportedly showed robust hair-count gains over placebo. The primary endpoint is change in non-vellus target-area hair count at Month 6 versus placebo, in roughly 480 subjects. That design is well powered for the effect sizes minoxidil typically produces, and two active doses give two chances to win. The main risks are execution problems or a weaker showing on the co-primary patient-reported benefit measure, and primary completion is planned for 2026-12, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b950ada41716eff58defdbd5ecf220913008110a43ddd7d0f5931e9577466747"},{"nct":"NCT06974851","title":"A Phase III Study Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of HRS9531 Injection in Subjects With Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA) and Obesity","sponsor":"Fujian Shengdi Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":140,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.7799341588813439,"rationale":"HRS9531 is Hengrui's GLP-1/GIP dual agonist, and its earlier trials in Chinese obese patients produced substantial weight loss (roughly 17–20% in phase 2/3). The closest precedent, tirzepatide in SURMOUNT-OSA, cut AHI by about 50–60% versus roughly 5% with placebo, a very large effect. Even with 140 patients in a placebo-controlled design, the trial should have ample power on percentage change in AHI. The main risks are operational (it is still recruiting with a single site listed, and the 52-week endpoint may make the stated timeline slip), not efficacy, and I know of no public result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"44359cfce6f771c0e5735da17d334f8d520ed807f366389500694b8610411084"},{"nct":"NCT06989918","title":"MHB018A Treatment in Patients With Active Thyroid Eye Disease","sponsor":"Minghui Pharmaceutical (Hangzhou) Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":108,"base":0.85,"researched":0.93,"learned":0.7565064139853694,"rationale":"Every placebo-controlled IGF-1R antibody trial in active TED I know of has met the proptosis responder endpoint by wide margins, with placebo responses of roughly 4–18% against active responses of 50–85%. MHB018A's Phase 1/2 showed an 81% proptosis response at Week 12 at the chosen 450 mg dose, and with 108 patients the trial has ample power for even a modest class effect. The remaining risk comes from a novel subcutaneous antibody whose Week 24 durability and placebo-controlled effect have not been shown, plus the single-site design and no DMC. No topline result for this trial has been found, although the sponsor's press release title mentioning 'Phase III results' is somewhat ambiguous.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"b798ec273d06cee5e3f0b1143eda3af1e1893b63b8e423ba3e76ff1ec3faa891"},{"nct":"NCT06994650","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Phase III Clinical Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of HRS9531 Injection in Subjects With Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA) and Obesity Who Are on Positive Airway Pressure Ventilation (PAP) Therapy","sponsor":"Fujian Shengdi Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":144,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.727005863047655,"rationale":"HRS9531 is Hengrui's GLP-1/GIP dual agonist, and its Chinese phase 3 obesity trials have shown large weight loss, comparable to tirzepatide. In SURMOUNT-OSA, tirzepatide cut AHI by about 25–29 events/h versus about 5 with placebo in both the PAP and non-PAP trials, with very small p-values. With 144 patients over 52 weeks and a placebo comparator, this trial is well powered for an effect of that size, so the main risks are dropout or an operational problem. The trial's primary completion is planned for December 2026, and I am not aware of any public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d75f442a9f6d947cfde2932a7f3c474984338b0dbf42b0d5027c19e3427a6600"},{"nct":"NCT06999733","title":"A Study Comparing KB801 Verse Placebo in Patients With Stage 2 or 3 Neurotrophic Keratitis","sponsor":"Krystal Biotech, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":60,"base":0.47,"researched":null,"learned":0.43495879830942263,"rationale":"The first-listed efficacy primary is complete PCED closure at week 8 versus vehicle. The NGF mechanism is validated: cenegermin (Oxervate) showed about 65–72% versus 17–30% closure, an effect large enough to reach significance even with about 30 patients per arm. Krystal's HSV-1 vector platform has worked topically (B-VEC), but corneal transduction and NGF expression from a vector are untested for efficacy. Vehicle healing rates in recent NK trials have sometimes been high, and this small phase 1/2 may not be powered for formal significance, so the forecast sits near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6da48390130618d0856c118ab5dc7493c393583b6f7ec782115c5803f8dafd79"},{"nct":"NCT07010471","title":"A Clinical Trial for Participants With DEE to Assess Efficacy, Safety, Tolerability, and PK of Relutrigine","sponsor":"Praxis Precision Medicines","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":160,"base":0.6,"researched":0.6,"learned":0.823417532046061,"rationale":"Relutrigine showed large, highly significant placebo-adjusted seizure reductions in EMBOLD (53%, p<0.0002), but only in SCN2A/SCN8A gain-of-function patients, whose disease biology suits a sodium-channel blocker. EMERALD enrolls a broad, heterogeneous DEE population, where the effect is likely diluted and some genotypes may respond poorly. Its sample size of about 160–200 still gives reasonable power for a moderate effect on motor seizure frequency. Praxis's recent misses with vormatrigine and ulixacaltamide, plus the lack of precedent for sodium-channel drugs in broad DEE, temper my confidence, so I put success moderately above even.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"3958334dd15a699a02ae2f11a2a45e5b2187e900c99d63fc544a96af119e5f59"},{"nct":"NCT07016750","title":"A Study Comparing KB803 and Matched Placebo in Patients With Dystrophic Epidermolysis Bullosa","sponsor":"Krystal Biotech, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":16,"base":0.52,"researched":null,"learned":0.7214193864371733,"rationale":"KB803 is an eye-drop form of B-VEC (Vyjuvek), which is already proven on DEB skin wounds, and compassionate-use ocular cases have been encouraging, so the mechanism is plausible. But this trial has only 16 patients, and the efficacy endpoint is a subjective count of symptom days per month from episodic corneal abrasions. Collagen VII expression may persist into the placebo period and dilute the crossover comparison, and statistical power is limited. Krystal is an experienced sponsor with a validated platform, but the small, noisy design keeps this near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f8763f0336247c6822a743fa50bb981c89e8a2ec65f3fdc484485cbf9e0860dd"},{"nct":"NCT07023614","title":"A Trial to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Ninerafaxstat in Patients With Symptomatic Non-obstructive Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy","sponsor":"Imbria Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":165,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3502872569974253,"rationale":"Ninerafaxstat, a cardiac metabolic modulator that partially inhibits fatty acid oxidation, was safe in the small Phase 2 IMPROVE-HCM trial in non-obstructive HCM. Its efficacy signals there were exploratory, notably better VE/VCO2 slope and KCCQ gains in more symptomatic patients, not a robust primary-endpoint win. Non-obstructive HCM has been a hard indication: mavacamten failed ODYSSEY-HCM on KCCQ-CSS, and KCCQ endpoints carry large placebo responses, which makes a 12-week trial of about 165 patients underpowered for modest effects. The Phase 2b base rate and a plausible but unproven mechanism support a below-even probability, and the trial is still recruiting, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"18df7781edb623092fbbc378fb1cda7a29e1120c1e2b9d861d4c1d7c3c27faf5"},{"nct":"NCT07037277","title":"C-Forward: Efficacy and Safety of BEM/RZR vs SOF/VEL in Subjects With Chronic HCV","sponsor":"Atea Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":880,"base":0.85,"researched":0.87,"learned":0.6830573852314162,"rationale":"This is a non-inferiority trial with a 5-point margin and about 440 patients per arm, so the lower confidence bound sits roughly 2.5 points below the observed difference. The sister trial C-BEYOND, with the same design and comparator, met non-inferiority in mITT (93.9% vs 94.8%), and C-FORWARD's per-protocol primary analysis should push both arms higher and reduce discontinuation noise. The main risks are a genotype mix richer in GT3 and GT4 (Pakistan, India, Egypt), where BEM/RZR's 8-week regimen and its small Phase 2 GT3 dataset are less proven, and a modest timeline slip. Overall success looks likely but not certain.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"65df1e950ae3b1fedc35dc392331c6f9c83fe94b6dff1a3a37d6ad8032814151"},{"nct":"NCT07074977","title":"Proof of Concept Study to Assess the Pharmacokinetics/Pharmacodynamics of Nemolizumab in Adults With Chronic Pruritus of Unknown Origin (CPUO)","sponsor":"Galderma R&D","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":50,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.3009143015050703,"rationale":"The primary endpoints are descriptive PopPK and PK/PD parameter estimates (CL/F, Vd/F, Ka, IC50 for pruritus inhibition), with no prespecified hypothesis test, so 'success' mostly means getting usable model estimates. That is likely, since nemolizumab PK is well characterized. The IC50 component depends on a real exposure-response signal for itch, which is plausible given nemolizumab's strong anti-pruritic effects in prurigo nodularis and atopic dermatitis. However, CPUO is heterogeneous, and with roughly 10 placebo patients any efficacy comparison is underpowered. Because it is unclear how a descriptive endpoint will be scored as a win, I land moderately above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dfec23dd24ad442627f4e57d526f7fc1e49fe2e6af7407f278a4f1bb8f2c7c3e"},{"nct":"NCT07089186","title":"Study to Assess the Efficacy and Safety of Meropenem and Pralurbactam in Carbapenem-Resistant Enterobacteriaceae Infections","sponsor":"Qilu Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":80,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.7172053414050357,"rationale":"This is a small (n=80), single-site, open-label pathogen-focused CRE trial against best available therapy, similar in design to TANGO II and CREDIBLE-CR, which are usually descriptive rather than powered for formal hypothesis testing. The first-listed primary endpoint covers only the cUTI subgroup, probably a fraction of the 80 patients, so a statistically significant difference is unlikely. Best available therapy in China often includes ceftazidime-avibactam, which works well against KPC-producing strains, further narrowing any plausible advantage. The drug may well look numerically favorable, but a formal significant win on this endpoint seems improbable.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"bce6b4c57b17b09bbecf710a2eaf59d811d0ff7a9f9378b3ef6c8ddd268395f2"},{"nct":"NCT07093476","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Add-On Therapy With Empagliflozin in Patients With Type 2 Diabetes on a Background of Alogliptin and Metformin","sponsor":"Celltrion","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":171,"base":0.96,"researched":0.96,"learned":0.942258643392272,"rationale":"Empagliflozin is a proven SGLT2 inhibitor that has consistently lowered HbA1c by about 0.6–0.8% versus placebo as add-on therapy, including Korean triple-therapy trials on metformin plus a DPP-4 inhibitor with similar sample sizes (~170). With roughly 57 patients per arm, the trial has very high power for an effect of this size, and the mechanism works independently of DPP-4 inhibition. The main residual risks are operational: a single site, possible enrollment shortfall or delay, or execution problems.","sources":2,"state":"screened","leaf":"5fc3b02a381afd1f1cbd48847e57009c1ef44fc9e65f5e66cc014fabf8967ad1"},{"nct":"NCT07128550","title":"A Study to Evaluate Tobevibart+Elebsiran in Participants With Chronic HDV Infection Not Virologically Suppressed With Bulevirtide","sponsor":"Vir Biotechnology, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":150,"base":0.85,"researched":0.92,"learned":0.7172884130929196,"rationale":"ECLIPSE 1 showed 79% undetectable HDV RNA with tobevibart+elebsiran versus 0% in untreated controls, and SOLSTICE showed about 41% TND at week 24. The control here is continued bulevirtide in patients who have already failed to suppress on it, so its week-24 TND rate should be near zero. With about 150 patients randomized, even a 25–35% response in the combination arm against roughly 0–5% on bulevirtide would be highly significant. The main risks are lower efficacy in this pretreated population, a different endpoint definition (TND rather than <LLOQ), or a non-standard analysis, but overall success looks very likely.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"be77c3f3951f3269a0368c6bebacd4c8d05c438e3149941977e4a4dcd526424b"},{"nct":"NCT07142044","title":"Safety, Tolerability and Exploratory Efficacy of EC5026 in Parkinson's Disease (STEP Study)","sponsor":"EicOsis Human Health Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":18,"base":0.77,"researched":null,"learned":0.32135953629496794,"rationale":"The primary outcome is the incidence of adverse events in a small Phase 1b MAD study (n=18), with no formal efficacy hypothesis test, so success will most likely mean a topline report that EC5026 was safe and well tolerated. EC5026, an sEH inhibitor, has already completed Phase 1 studies in healthy volunteers without major safety signals. The 2–4 mg doses and 28-day exposure are modest, which favors a benign safety readout. The main risks are an unexpected safety signal (for example endocrine or HPA-axis effects, given the exclusion criteria), enrollment delays at a single recruiting site, or ambiguity about how a safety-only endpoint is scored.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4f2028c2f75e4d6064be114e20c7423f72e68ad8d4b8b3cecbc07c4357270804"},{"nct":"NCT07169851","title":"A Study to Evaluate LY3537021 for the Treatment of Nausea and Vomiting Caused by Chemotherapy in Adults With Cancer","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":204,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.46593721083958556,"rationale":"LY3537021 is a long-acting GIP receptor agonist being tested as an antiemetic. The idea rests mainly on animal data and Lilly's interest in reducing incretin-related nausea, so this is essentially a first efficacy test of a new mechanism in humans. It is added on top of triple antiemetic prophylaxis (5-HT3 antagonist, NK1 antagonist and dexamethasone), which already gives a high delayed-phase complete response rate (about 65–80%). With roughly 100 patients per arm, that ceiling leaves limited room and limited power to reach p<0.05 unless the effect is olanzapine-sized (about 15 percentage points or more).","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4001fd7f1f3398c33459658d7058e507cf3c4d153545996a1cca2b32703069d0"},{"nct":"NCT07194382","title":"AURA-IPF: A Randomized Phase 2 Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of AP02 (Nintedanib Solution) in IPF","sponsor":"Avalyn Pharma Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":160,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.26481680563799287,"rationale":"Oral nintedanib's efficacy in IPF is well established, and inhaled delivery to treatment-naive patients could plausibly match or exceed it, so a real FVC signal is biologically credible. However, the trial is small (~53 per arm) and runs only 12 weeks; with a typical SD of 150–200 mL, it would need roughly a 70 mL placebo-adjusted difference for p<0.05, versus an expected oral-nintedanib-like effect of about 30–60 mL. POC studies like this are often powered with relaxed alpha or analyzed in a Bayesian framework, so a 'positive' sponsor readout may not reach conventional two-sided significance. Two doses give two chances, but overall the odds sit below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5779826dcf3d943875dc681663b2a439a7d93dd954e975e5b539e1624c2b8299"},{"nct":"NCT07215273","title":"Phase 2 EL219 Versus Liposomal Amphotericin B or Voriconazole for Early Antifungal Therapy","sponsor":"Elion Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":60,"base":0.1,"researched":null,"learned":0.3285851777421899,"rationale":"This is a small (n=60) Phase 2 trial with day-21 all-cause mortality as the first primary outcome. Day-21 mortality in early antifungal therapy is low, roughly 5-15%, so the trial has essentially no power to show a statistically significant superiority difference against active LAmB or voriconazole. The design is descriptive, estimating safety and efficacy rather than testing a hypothesis, and no non-inferiority margin is stated. The sponsor may well report favorable numbers, but formal statistical success on mortality is very unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"000807aa923f768fd481a97a095642710bdff880178aaf788a186e5b2c26c925"},{"nct":"NCT07221578","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of VQW-765 for the On-Demand Treatment of Social Anxiety Disorder","sponsor":"Vanda Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":500,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.633226587499483,"rationale":"VQW-765, an alpha7 nicotinic partial agonist, missed significance on SUDS in the overall population of its Phase 2 public-speaking trial. Vanda's case for efficacy rested on post-hoc signals in women and in patients with optimal plasma exposure, yet this Phase 3 enrolls both sexes without exposure enrichment. Single-dose public-speaking challenge trials in social anxiety are noisy and have mixed results; Vistagen's fasedienol, for example, failed PALISADE-1 and PALISADE-3 and succeeded only in PALISADE-2. Vanda also has a track record of trials driven by subgroup findings, so despite the adequate 500-patient sample I put success below the Phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"22f2bc3c9cf40c2f4997d76322dc53136c39051094cabf314332b8e4c2ff378f"},{"nct":"NCT07229950","title":"A Phase 2 Clinical Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety, and Pharmacokinetics of HRS-7085 Tablets in Patients With Inflammatory Bowel Disease","sponsor":"Shandong Suncadia Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":48,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5316375857833537,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety measure, the proportion of patients with at least one adverse event at Week 14, not an efficacy comparison. Under a strict superiority reading, a 48-patient trial is very unlikely to show a significantly lower adverse event rate on HRS-7085 than on placebo. Some weight goes to the chance the outcome is scored as success if the sponsor reports acceptable safety, and early Hengrui/Suncadia oral IBD agents in China have usually been tolerable. Results are not yet public and may never be fully reported, so the forecast stays low but not extreme.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"da4779cbb6bb5a748cd85ac04a9c172b8e2afe81d35694233a95972d2b302231"},{"nct":"NCT07231679","title":"A Study to Investigate IGT-303 in Healthy Volunteers and Participants With Chronic Kidney Disease","sponsor":"Ingenia Therapeutics INC","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":94,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5124107266445788,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human Phase 1/2a SAD/MAD study whose primary endpoint is safety and tolerability (AE counts), with no prespecified efficacy comparison. In practice, sponsors of such trials almost always report a topline of \"safe and well tolerated,\" which is how meeting the endpoint would be judged. IGT-303 appears to be Ingenia's Tie2-activating antibody, a mechanism without known major class-wide safety signals, so dose-limiting toxicity severe enough to stop development is uncommon. I see no public topline yet; the main risks are an unexpected safety signal or no clear public readout.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"34b544371f90be01a829a0af93b4b00345c9674e61b8c1375bfe3c3d2d0e2bad"},{"nct":"NCT07260877","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2a Study With an Open-Label Extension Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of VENT-03 in Adult Participants With Active Cutaneous Lupus Erythematosus With or Without Systemic Lupus Erythematosus","sponsor":"Ventus Therapeutics U.S., Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":24,"base":0.38,"researched":null,"learned":0.35592792163740067,"rationale":"VENT-03 is a first-in-class oral cGAS inhibitor, tested here in a very small (n=24) four-week phase 2a with a mechanistic primary endpoint: percent change in skin interferon gene signature. Biomarker endpoints are easier to move than clinical scores, and IFN-pathway drugs such as anifrolumab and litifilimab clearly suppress the skin IFN signature. However, CLE interferon is driven largely by pDC TLR7/9 signaling, so it is unclear how much of it is cGAS-dependent, and the sample is underpowered for anything short of a large effect. The trial may also be analyzed descriptively, without formal significance testing, which further lowers the chance of a clear statistical win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"52580730c826180b73f23f3f774a907d105d921566023cca23f1f3b8ef26e9bc"},{"nct":"NCT07285070","title":"Tacrolimus Ophthalmic Solution for the Treatment of Non-infectious Anterior Uveitis","sponsor":"Novaliq GmbH","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":20,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.35233190332366904,"rationale":"This is a small (n=20) first-in-human dose-ranging study with no placebo. Its primary endpoint is adverse events, not a statistical efficacy comparison, so 'success' would likely mean the sponsor reports NOV05 as safe and well tolerated. Topical tacrolimus is well characterized, and Novaliq's water-free semifluorinated alkane vehicle has been tolerated in approved products, so a favorable safety readout is likely. The main uncertainty is that a descriptive safety endpoint may not map cleanly onto 'met primary endpoint', and an unexpected ocular tolerability signal remains possible, so I stop short of a very high probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6787d2ebde9d84c06eef36c79c6c0a0e1a1c025ad37101b6995db0556fb46508"},{"nct":"NCT07297797","title":"Phase II Clinical Study of HRS-9563 in Patients With Mild to Moderate Hypertension","sponsor":"Fujian Shengdi Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":238,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.6379542943626416,"rationale":"HRS-9563 appears to be Hengrui's injectable, likely siRNA-based, RAAS-targeting agent (probably angiotensinogen-directed, like zilebesiran), though this identification is not confirmed. That mechanism has already shown large placebo-adjusted reductions in 24-hour ambulatory systolic pressure in KARDIA-1, so the proof of concept is strong. This trial compares four doses with placebo in about 238 untreated mild-to-moderate hypertensives, which gives ample power for ambulatory reductions on the order of 10 mmHg or more, and only one arm needs to succeed. The remaining risks are a weaker-than-expected candidate, durability at month 6, and single-site execution; I do not know of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"73118ce09e2b0135dd131a04dcc5f0c47a136afae719089ab0cdee537f284b0b"},{"nct":"NCT07298395","title":"Study of ENV-294 in Adults With Moderate-to-Severe Atopic Dermatitis","sponsor":"Enveda Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":105,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.5051503635105096,"rationale":"ENV-294 is a first-in-class oral small molecule from Enveda with an undisclosed, non-JAK mechanism and no prior efficacy data in atopic dermatitis. Most novel oral non-JAK mechanisms tested in moderate-to-severe AD have failed or shown only modest effects. The primary endpoint, percent change in EASI against placebo, is continuous and fairly sensitive, but about 52 patients per arm can only detect roughly a 20-point difference given a 25-35% placebo response. Phase 2 base rates in dermatology and this unvalidated mechanism point to a below-even chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"443ec3f21954e549e2328df1198842e09239ecd91cbabd596ed6717d698d878a"},{"nct":"NCT07301255","title":"ENV-294 for Moderate-to-Severe Asthma: A 12-Week Study in Adults","sponsor":"Enveda Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":50,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.34876086088153,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety (incidence of treatment-emergent adverse events), not efficacy, so there is no formal superiority test against placebo. Such trials are usually reported as having 'met' the endpoint when the drug is described as safe and well tolerated. ENV-294 is an oral, first-in-class anti-inflammatory that has already been through Phase 1, which lowers the risk of a disqualifying safety signal over 12 weeks in about 50 patients. Remaining uncertainty comes from how a safety-primary trial gets scored and from the chance of tolerability problems or an underwhelming readout; recruitment was still ongoing and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a4349bedd345e179d8f6904701cfb32486eacf623f5aa698d3cc85142f610211"},{"nct":"NCT07371650","title":"This is an Early-stage Clinical Trial to Determine a Safe and Effective Dose for Tivoxavir Marboxil in Patients With Mild to Moderate Influenza","sponsor":"Traws Pharma, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":105,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.4627136559606034,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are descriptive safety measures (AEs, labs, ECGs, physical exams) in a small open-label Phase 2a with no formal hypothesis test, so 'success' will most likely be judged by whether the sponsor reports TRX-100 as safe and well tolerated. Tivoxavir marboxil is a cap-dependent endonuclease inhibitor in the same class as approved baloxavir, and its Phase 1 data reportedly showed good tolerability, so a clean safety readout is likely. Traws Pharma is a small, financially constrained sponsor that tends to frame results positively. The remaining risk is an unexpected safety signal, a stalled or incomplete study, or ambiguity in how a descriptive endpoint gets graded.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c9541f5c4c585e18c0b6c6127377ab5b480f991866d3f8fa3d5d9756bc217d4c"},{"nct":"NCT07408024","title":"Safety and Efficacy of TollB-001 Tablets in Moderate to Severe Rheumatoid Arthritis","sponsor":"Toll Biotech Co. Ltd. (Beijing)","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":24,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.6500627724697083,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n=24), single-site, sequential dose-escalation Phase IIa trial in China whose first-listed primary outcome is safety (AE incidence), not an efficacy comparison. With only about 6 patients per arm, any formal superiority test against placebo would almost certainly be underpowered. Success will therefore likely be judged as acceptable safety and tolerability over 8 weeks, which early oral RA drugs often show, though such small Chinese biotech trials often go unreported. I know of no public results, so I set a moderate probability that reflects both the likely 'safe and well tolerated' framing and the ambiguity of scoring a safety-only endpoint.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"33c9b5ecbbe6fb9ccfa6799aba3dc822a823231b10fcbe89a3655d14b5b72486"},{"nct":"NCT07413094","title":"Efficacy and Safety of YD0743 Treatment for Sepsis-Associated ARDS","sponsor":"Shanghai Yidian Pharmaceutical Technology Development Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":309,"base":0.13,"researched":null,"learned":0.20237016957541215,"rationale":"Pharmacotherapy for sepsis-associated ARDS has an extremely poor track record: statins, beta-agonists, keratinocyte growth factor, interferon-beta, sivelestat and many others have failed to improve ventilator-free days or mortality in randomized trials. YD0743 is a novel continuous-infusion agent from a small Chinese sponsor, and there is no public phase 1b or efficacy data. Its bleeding-related exclusions hint at an anticoagulant or anti-protease mechanism, a class with a history of failure in sepsis. With about 100 patients per arm, a noisy ventilator-free-days endpoint and two doses offering slight multiplicity, the chance of a significant result is low but not negligible, given possible single-site or homogeneous-population effects in China.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7688c9b6dbe92df3bdfefe325b2fe4cb42f122be3ce1fd9e3ec60f477b08ea16"},{"nct":"NCT07439848","title":"Mesenchymal Stem Cells (MSCs) and Conditioned Medium Mesenchymal Stem Cells as Adjuvant Therapy for Sepsis","sponsor":"PT. Prodia Stem Cell Indonesia","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":15,"base":0.15,"researched":null,"learned":0.38824904038331487,"rationale":"This is a 15-patient (5 per arm), single-site phase 1/2 trial of UC-MSC with or without secretome in severe ARDS. The first-listed primary outcome is the lung injury score, and its first timepoint is \"before therapy,\" so there is no clear prespecified comparison. Larger MSC trials in ARDS (START, REALIST, several COVID-ARDS RCTs) have mostly failed on their primary efficacy endpoints, and with 5 patients per arm only a very large effect could reach p<0.05. The sponsor is a small company and the multiplicity of outcomes could let it claim a positive result on something, but under a strict definition success is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"384c97978b40ef52f4b47773255a457f8dea42cc966c0ba88797c00ab8e24218"},{"nct":"NCT07472725","title":"A Study Comparing Safety and Efficacy of SHR-3167 Fixed-Dose Titration and Individualized-Dose Titration in Adults With Type 2 Diabetes Inadequately Controlled With Oral Antihyperglycemic Agents","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":102,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.8393806189248213,"rationale":"SHR-3167 appears to be HengRui's once-weekly basal insulin, and this small open-label phase II trial (n=102, 2 sites) compares two titration algorithms of the same drug, with no true control arm. The primary endpoint, the proportion of patients with any hypoglycemic event, looks descriptive rather than a powered superiority or non-inferiority test. Even if one algorithm produced fewer hypoglycemic events, a statistically significant difference at this sample size is unlikely. A sponsor-defined success is therefore improbable, and no results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"691e87bf831c795729c59165458d08243ccbf5ff2bd9085326a4c68d10fa6303"},{"nct":"NCT07482657","title":"A Phase 2 Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Zelicapavir in Participants Aged ≥28 Days to ≤36 Months of Age Infected With Respiratory Syncytial Virus","sponsor":"Enanta Pharmaceuticals, Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":150,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3390792885047341,"rationale":"Zelicapavir missed its primary endpoints in the earlier pediatric Phase 2 (RSVPEDs, viral load) and in the adult high-risk Phase 2b (symptom score). Both trials showed only directional or subgroup-level signals of antiviral and clinical benefit. This 150-patient trial in Thailand uses a novel clinical-sign resolution endpoint (RESOLVE-P) that is likely noisy, which limits power, though enrolling within 72 hours of onset helps. Ziresovir's success in China shows RSV antivirals can work in infants, but the base rate for this drug's prior trials and for small Phase 2 symptom-endpoint studies points to a below-even chance.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b3679e177e9ff3a266544105f73ee195a46a1f10ef84e66b2ad9bb064d08e097"},{"nct":"NCT07489612","title":"QLS1410 in Participants With Uncontrolled Hypertension","sponsor":"Qilu Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":260,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.7340410941001766,"rationale":"QLS1410 appears to be an aldosterone synthase inhibitor; the trial design (uncontrolled or resistant hypertension on a diuretic, potassium exclusions) closely mirrors baxdrostat's BrigHTN and lorundrostat's Target-HTN, both of which beat placebo on systolic BP in phase 2. Three doses with about 65 patients per arm give reasonable power for a 7–10 mmHg placebo-adjusted drop, and only one dose needs to succeed. Risks are a fast-follower compound with uncertain potency or selectivity (some earlier inhibitors had cortisol off-target problems), a possibly large placebo response, and a single-site Chinese trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"406fb15117b296301330cd34c7d7cb50f56f2f137f0989d23d431b48d743d9c3"},{"nct":"NCT07499674","title":"Evaluation of the Safety and Efficacy of Abenacianine (VGT-309) to Identify Cancer in Subjects Undergoing Surgery for Cancer in the Lung","sponsor":"Vergent Bioscience, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":132,"base":0.8,"researched":0.88,"learned":0.7014372580665063,"rationale":"The design mirrors pafolacianine's ELUCIDATE: the primary endpoint is a CSE proportion in the NIR arm tested against a fixed low threshold (likely about 10%), and the small randomized control arm exists mainly to preserve blinding. Phase 2b VISUALIZE produced about a 40–45% CSE rate with a lower 95% bound of 34%, far above a 10% null, and pafolacianine succeeded on a near-identical design. The main risks are a stricter prespecified threshold than the 10% used before, a CSE definition narrower than phase 2b's (margins excluded), lower yield at the untested 96-hour dosing window, or a shift to more experienced surgeons. Even so, the bar looks comfortably clearable with about 115 evaluable patients.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"c2ad3321382c84c0672b745a558769398ef0ee079eb395d54efcf196d84e518c"},{"nct":"NCT07511361","title":"Study of Efficacy and Safety of Tonlamarsen in Participants With a Recent Hospitalization and a Concurrent Episode of Acute Severe Hypertension","sponsor":"Kardigan, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":140,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.4602358271324794,"rationale":"Tonlamarsen (ION904) is a GalNAc-conjugated antisense oligonucleotide against hepatic angiotensinogen, and earlier studies showed large, consistent plasma AGT reductions. The first listed primary outcome (Part A variability) is descriptive, so the meaningful test is Part B's placebo-controlled percent change in AGT at Week 4, a pharmacodynamic endpoint the mechanism almost always hits. The main risks are operational: Part B may be delayed or not run, or results may be reported only descriptively, rather than any doubt about efficacy.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9e08d913e2a33138d6a2789d803a1573de6ae7cd8c154648d8b40b9f6b826b85"},{"nct":"NCT07548632","title":"A Clinical Study Evaluating Licaminlimab for Dry Eye Disease","sponsor":"Oculis","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":160,"base":0.37,"researched":null,"learned":0.6969506596426053,"rationale":"Licaminlimab (OCS-02), a topical anti-TNFα antibody fragment, appears to have shown only modest or mixed results in Oculis's earlier Phase 2b RELIEF trial, as best I recall. The TNFR1 genotype enrichment hypothesis seems to come from exploratory or post hoc analyses, which often fail to replicate prospectively. Dry eye symptom endpoints such as ocular discomfort score are notoriously noisy with large vehicle responses. A 160-patient trial, in which the genotype-positive primary population may be only a subset, gives limited power, though the targeted enrichment and the sponsor's belief in the signal give it some chance.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"91d6487bbc54ef0201db342b8dbd906e84a585a296a6d0cd5e9af87d8b183e6b"},{"nct":"NCT07576608","title":"A Phase II Study of 9MW3811 in Patients With Pathological Scar","sponsor":"Mabwell (Shanghai) Bioscience Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":30,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.42206684549975904,"rationale":"This is a small (n=30, roughly 7 per arm) exploratory phase II trial of a first-in-class anti-IL-11 antibody in pathological scar, a new mechanism in an indication where systemic biologics are unproven. The trial is not powered for formal significance testing, and a 12-week window is short for measurable change on mVSS, so a statistically significant win over placebo is unlikely even if the drug has some activity. Three dose arms raise the chance that one arm reaches nominal significance somewhat, but sponsor-reported results will more likely describe numerical trends.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6d8e9da54bbf6c624271133a562718dab955341ceabcd6103dc3fed838598060"},{"nct":"NCT07678931","title":"Study on the Treatment of Adolescent Patients With Seasonal Allergic Rhinitis","sponsor":"Chengdu Kangnuoxing Biopharma,Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":136,"base":0.72,"researched":0.7,"learned":0.8242536781740936,"rationale":"Stapokibart already succeeded in an adult phase 3 SAR trial (PHECDA, n=108) on the same 2-week rTNSS primary endpoint, with a clear effect (−1.3, P=0.0008), and this adolescent extension uses a similar design with a slightly larger sample (n=136). Uncertainties remain: the registration lists no eosinophil ≥300 enrichment, and the phase 2 MERAK missed this endpoint in an unselected population. Enrollment is also compressed into a short autumn pollen window, and seasonal symptom trials are vulnerable to variable pollen loads and high placebo response. Extrapolation trials of a proven drug usually succeed, but these risks pull the estimate down to about 70%.","sources":0,"state":"screened","leaf":"196286fc9b882b692421282e5ea8e82e2cb0762f28cdf62472c70342a99221e2"},{"nct":"NCT07688772","title":"A Clinical Study Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of SHR-1819 Injection in Patients With Seasonal Allergic Rhinitis","sponsor":"Guangdong Hengrui Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":220,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8273135928350749,"rationale":"SHR-1819 is Hengrui's anti-IL-4Rα antibody, and a mechanistically similar drug (stapokibart/CM310) already met the identical endpoint, 2-week rTNSS change versus placebo, in a Chinese seasonal allergic rhinitis phase 3 with fewer patients. This trial has 220 patients, enrolls people with a poor response to intranasal steroids during an autumn pollen season, and runs at one experienced site, all of which favor a detectable effect. Residual risks are a high placebo response, variable pollen exposure, and the short 2-week primary window.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"39def169464a9e87ba6068241a1a7121c53a83bbf2b70e0ee07030bb37b5cc4e"},{"nct":"NCT07709897","title":"A Clinical Trial of HRS5580 for Injection Combined With Palonosetron Hydrochloride for the Prevention of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting","sponsor":"Fujian Shengdi Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12","enrollment":260,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.4611531422243452,"rationale":"HRS5580 appears to be an NK-1 receptor antagonist from Hengrui/Shengdi. Adding an NK-1 antagonist to a 5-HT3 antagonist in high-risk PONV patients generally cuts vomiting and improves 72-hour complete response, as Chinese fosaprepitant and aprepitant studies showed. Complete-response endpoints that count rescue use are often diluted, because rescue is driven by nausea, which NK-1 agents affect less, so expected differences of roughly 10–20 points with about 87 patients per arm give only moderate power. Since success needs only one dose to beat palonosetron alone and the mechanism is validated, a modestly favourable probability seems right.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"47f0aaf8c8e600c9f7bfdf5896270737130c342c3c68c176c1b74214dde153da"},{"nct":"NCT07832552","title":"A Phase 3 Study Evaluating the Safety and Efficacy of TRIESENCE® (Injectable Suspension) for the Treatment of Ocular Inflammation and Pain After Ophthalmic Surgery","sponsor":"Harrow Inc","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":250,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.8226053327374682,"rationale":"A corticosteroid against sham after cataract surgery, with rescue use counted as failure, is a format where nearly every prior product has won on both anterior chamber cell clearing and pain-free endpoints (Dexycu, Dextenza, loteprednol and difluprednate gels). Subconjunctival triamcinolone is a well-established, potent periocular steroid, and 250 patients randomized 2:1 gives ample power for the usual 25–35 point differences. The main risks are the co-primary requirement, possible slower anterior chamber clearing from a depot suspension, and execution quality at a small sponsor whose protocol is sloppy. Results are not yet public, as primary completion is planned for December 2026.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3df522ed1b096f83b36de50c411b92744d21d742c4ac2a9c0dc596f3ad4c2762"},{"nct":"NCT07937462","title":"The Efficacy and Safety of DLBS1442 in Patients With Primary Dysmenorrhea","sponsor":"Dexa Medica Group","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12","enrollment":210,"base":0.57,"researched":null,"learned":0.785270638632884,"rationale":"DLBS1442 (Dismeno), a Phaleria macrocarpa fraction from Dexa Medica, is already marketed in Indonesia. Earlier sponsor-run studies in dysmenorrhea and endometriosis reportedly showed benefit, and sponsor-run single-site Indonesian trials tend to report favorable results. Two doses (one success counts) and a quadruple-masked design with about 70 per arm give reasonable power for a moderate effect. However, the acute 6-hour VAS endpoint is demanding for an herbal anti-inflammatory, placebo response in dysmenorrhea pain is large, and rescue paracetamol may dilute differences, so the outlook is only modestly better than even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1d5ee8a042130cedb5a07a4c4c1671c64d5d1c31681d25280af93fa538429f73"},{"nct":"NCT03767244","title":"A Study of Apalutamide in Participants With High-Risk, Localized or Locally Advanced Prostate Cancer Who Are Candidates for Radical Prostatectomy","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":2517,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.7462387234756344,"rationale":"This is PROTEUS, the phase 3 trial of neoadjuvant and adjuvant apalutamide plus ADT around prostatectomy; I do not recall its pCR or MFS readout being public. In phase 2 work (ARNEO, enzalutamide and abiraterone neoadjuvant studies), adding an AR inhibitor to ADT consistently deepened pathologic response, though true pCR stayed low (about 3-10% versus 0-3% with ADT alone). With about 2,500 patients, even a 2-3 percentage-point absolute pCR difference would likely be significant at a split alpha. The main risks are that pCR rates are extremely low in both arms or that a stringent alpha allocation is missed, so I place success somewhat above the oncology phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6b44d69ae6d54e2309b8a7030bd103f20cd7bd628df5cde1e0d80e5ee0cec001"},{"nct":"NCT05128825","title":"A Study of Azenosertib (ZN-c3) in Subjects With Platinum-Resistant High-Grade Serous Ovarian, Fallopian Tube or Primary Peritoneal Cancer","sponsor":"K-Group, Beta, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of Zentalis Pharmaceuticals, Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":310,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.49341344103895635,"rationale":"DENALI Part 2 is a single-arm, registration-intent ORR study of azenosertib in Cyclin E1-positive platinum-resistant ovarian cancer, so success means the confidence interval for ORR clears a prespecified null rate, likely around the 10-15% that standard chemotherapy achieves. Earlier pooled data at 400 mg 5:2 in Cyclin E1-positive PROC showed ORR around 30-35%, and a cohort of about 100 patients would likely give a lower bound above a modest null. Risks are dilution in more heavily pretreated patients (prior mirvetuximab, bevacizumab and PARP inhibitors), regression to the mean from small early cohorts, and a stricter-than-expected FDA-negotiated threshold. I am not aware of a public topline readout for Part 2.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3babdb9727abb2ec04d069f1ad40e3ac0f4dfa23d287242d8e55c00248640b18"},{"nct":"NCT05860465","title":"Safety and Efficacy of SPH4336 in Combination With Endocrine Therapy in the Treatment of Locally Advanced or Metastatic Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Shanghai Pharmaceuticals Holding Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":254,"base":0.28,"researched":null,"learned":0.6228753779158698,"rationale":"SPH4336 appears to be a CDK4/6 inhibitor from Shanghai Pharmaceuticals. It is being tested here as CDK4/6 rechallenge plus endocrine therapy after progression on a prior CDK4/6 inhibitor, a setting with mixed precedent: postMONARCH and MAINTAIN were positive on PFS, while PACE and PALMIRA were negative. The first-listed primary endpoint is objective response rate, which in this setting differed only modestly and non-significantly even in positive trials (e.g., 17% vs 13% in postMONARCH), so a significant ORR difference at about 254 patients is hard to achieve. The trial is still recruiting, has no public results, and the sponsor has limited global track record, so I put the probability modestly below the base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a20686e77be8f46dd87489bbfa70b89923f1e315e196001063029f818f3f813f"},{"nct":"NCT06000956","title":"A Study of Comparing Overall Improvement of Patients With Spondyloarthritis Treated With Jitongning Tablets and Placebo","sponsor":"Tasly Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":408,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.8350555232303164,"rationale":"Chinese TCM phase III trials run by large sponsors such as Tasly against placebo usually report success, likely because of patient selection, a subjective PRO-based endpoint and publication patterns. ASAS20 at 8 weeks in an NSAID-free, active, HLA-B27+/CRP-elevated population leaves room for a separation from placebo, and n=408 gives decent power. Still, placebo ASAS20 response in axSpA is often 30-40%, and Jitongning, a TCM formula, has no rigorous prior evidence in axSpA. The trial is still recruiting with an estimated primary completion of December 2026, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3bda5879aa7f0d1c5ae7106ab7f3aee8f7984549a85deaf06be87956a10faa00"},{"nct":"NCT06685757","title":"A Study to Learn More About the Effects and Safety of Felzartamab Infusions in Adults With Kidney Transplants Who Have Antibody-Mediated Rejection (AMR)","sponsor":"Biogen","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":132,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.5950782408481118,"rationale":"In the phase 2 placebo-controlled trial (Mayer et al., NEJM 2024), felzartamab produced morphologic AMR resolution at week 24 in about 82% of patients versus 20% on placebo, with consistent reductions in MVI, molecular scores and dd-cfDNA. TRANSCEND uses a similar week-24 biopsy endpoint against placebo, and 132 patients give high power even if the true effect is well below the phase 2 estimate. The main risks are regression from a very small phase 2, heterogeneity in a broader multinational population including chronic active AMR, and stricter central Banff 2022 reading. Primary completion is December 2026, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9c0a667fe67278f0880a3d038c7af3909d24ad5216a74a8fbcfab389c88290f4"},{"nct":"NCT06699108","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of VGR-R01 Gene Therapy in Patients With Bietti Crystalline Dystrophy","sponsor":"Shanghai Vitalgen BioPharma Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":45,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.635857713607875,"rationale":"VGR-R01 (AAV-CYP4V2) showed meaningful BCVA gains in its earlier open-label study, and a similar Chinese CYP4V2 gene therapy (ZVS101e) reported comparable signals, so the biology looks credible. The comparator is an untreated control in a slowly progressive disease, which makes a between-group BCVA responder difference fairly easy to show, and the assessor-masked, open-label design favors the treatment arm. The risks are the small sample (30 vs 15), BCVA measurement noise, possible surgery-related acuity loss, and the fact that single-arm phase 1/2 gains often shrink in controlled trials. Primary completion is December 2026, and I am not aware of any public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1bd7c39d1788c8ec29271c7951ac13bd1da45d3107993132755d06bc693b849c"},{"nct":"NCT06838000","title":"Study of the Safety and Immunogenicity of Catch-up Vaccination With a 21-valent Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccine (PCV21) in Healthy Infants, Toddlers, Children, and Adolescents","sponsor":"Sanofi Pasteur, a Sanofi Company","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":1268,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8015548648346451,"rationale":"This Phase 3 catch-up study of Sanofi/SK bioscience's PCV21 (SP0202) against Prevnar 20 has descriptive primary endpoints: the first-listed outcome is immediate adverse events, followed by immunogenicity counts with no stated non-inferiority margin or hypothesis test. Catch-up studies like this usually just describe safety and immune responses, and an outcome would likely be judged successful if the vaccine's safety is comparable and immune responses are robust. Phase 2 infant data for SP0202 showed immunogenicity comparable to PCV13 and an acceptable safety profile, and catch-up regimens in older children are generally highly immunogenic. The main risk is ambiguity about how a descriptive result gets scored, plus a small chance of an unexpected safety signal.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"57b6e954590d9bb625aa836a1f5060dc9a6b324edd3b9fd82d91d6012a4e1d65"},{"nct":"NCT06907511","title":"Study to Evaluate the Safety and the Immunogenicity of a Second Generation Structurally Designed mRNA Vaccine Candidate Against Pandemic Influenza H5 HA Strain in Healthy Adult Participants Aged 18 Years and Older","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":720,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.5624070929379437,"rationale":"The primary endpoints are descriptive safety counts (reactogenicity, AEs, SAEs) with no formal hypothesis test, so 'success' amounts to an acceptable safety and tolerability profile that supports further development. Mid-study, Sanofi added a 480-participant extension at the low dose, which suggests the initial dose-ranging data were reassuring. mRNA H5 vaccines from other sponsors have generally been tolerable, with expected reactogenicity, though H5 immunogenicity can be modest. I am not aware of a public topline result, and how a purely descriptive safety endpoint will be scored is uncertain, so I keep the forecast well short of certainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7987c27c49910ed89745c355d22e7c3d51da545072cd679a8e0749594d1817fe"},{"nct":"NCT07090759","title":"To Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety and Population Pharmacokinetics of GST-HG141 in Patients With Chronic Hepatitis B (CHB) Who Have an Inadequate Response to Antiviral Drug Treatment","sponsor":"Fujian Akeylink Biotechnology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":526,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.7748171216026198,"rationale":"GST-HG141 (neracorvir) is a capsid assembly modulator, and in phase 2 add-on studies in NA-treated patients with low-level viremia it markedly increased the proportion with HBV DNA below LLOQ versus placebo. CAMs as a class potently suppress residual HBV DNA when added to nucleos(t)ide analogues, and the comparator here is continued NA monotherapy, which gives modest rates of undetectability in HBeAg-positive partial responders. With 263 patients per arm, the trial is well powered for the expected large difference, and this primary endpoint is the class's most reliable effect; the main risks are resistance emergence and lower-than-expected effect in HBeAg-positive patients.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ce0570da6f59ab1f4e2cfe0a054a1a003d4edb4bfbdfd429431084181e4c9de4"},{"nct":"NCT07446439","title":"A Study to Evaluate Tradipitant on Treating Nausea and Vomiting Induced by GLP-1R Agonist Use","sponsor":"Vanda Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-01","enrollment":280,"base":0.76,"researched":null,"learned":0.7377593890089633,"rationale":"Vanda's earlier Phase 2 semaglutide-challenge study, as I recall it, showed tradipitant roughly halving vomiting versus placebo with strong significance. Tradipitant has also shown positive vomiting results in motion sickness, where I believe it may now be approved as Nereus. This Phase 3 repeats essentially the same acute GLP-1 challenge model with a larger sample (280) and a binary vomiting endpoint, which the area-postrema NK-1 mechanism plausibly addresses. The main risks are a lower-than-expected placebo vomiting rate, Vanda's variable trial execution, and the gastroparesis failure, but replicating a positive challenge model generally succeeds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"52f98d5a23f1f9b615d4f6b9dbabf5c18b9b7fd4732b2178b47b2ac883351d6c"},{"nct":"NCT07029711","title":"A Study to Learn About Medicine Called Ritlecitinib in Children Aged Between 6 to 12 Years With Severe Alopecia Areata","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-02","enrollment":208,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.8412700634755766,"rationale":"Ritlecitinib is already approved for severe alopecia areata in patients aged 12 and older. In ALLEGRO-2b/3, SALT≤20 response at Week 24 was about 23% on 50 mg versus about 2% on placebo, and adolescents responded at least as well as adults, so extrapolation to children aged 6 to under 12 is reasonable. With roughly 70 children per arm, a placebo response rate near zero, and success needed in only one of two doses, power on the first-listed SALT≤20 endpoint should be high. The main risks are pediatric dosing or exposure miscalibration and a smaller-than-planned enrollment (208 versus at least 225), which matter more for the stricter EU SALT≤10 endpoint.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b2be8aa48dbdf1d54a9c513cc34224a068ebe7ecff78b9d9b1de4656edb13deb"},{"nct":"NCT06421636","title":"A Study to Test the Safety, Tolerability, and Efficacy of an Antibody, REGN7999, Injected Under the Skin for the Treatment of Iron Overload in Adult Participants With Non-Transfusion Dependent β-thalassemia, Using MRI Scans to Measure Iron Levels in the Body","sponsor":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-03","enrollment":19,"base":0.17,"researched":null,"learned":0.5051758714087686,"rationale":"REGN7999 is an anti-TMPRSS6 antibody that raises hepcidin and so cuts dietary iron absorption. That mechanism removes stored liver iron slowly, and any LIC reduction within 24 weeks is likely modest; it could even be offset by iron shifting into hepatic macrophages. Actual enrollment of only 19 across two parts with 2:2:1 randomization leaves very few placebo patients, so a formal placebo comparison has little power. The small enrollment may also signal early truncation or deprioritization. No prior TMPRSS6 agent has shown robust LIC reduction in NTDT, so I put the chance of a statistically significant primary result at low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"56d11d72423fe40d132bae60eb8342a457d1c496e34aa0ff425db94d4c08f4d6"},{"nct":"NCT06602258","title":"A Study of E2814 With Concurrent Lecanemab Treatment in Participants With Early Alzheimer's Disease","sponsor":"Eisai Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-03","enrollment":105,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.3574605096690897,"rationale":"E2814 (etalanetug) is an anti-MTBR tau antibody, and the primary endpoint, change in CSF MTBR-tau-243, is close to a direct target-engagement readout for its epitope. Eisai's Phase 1b/2 and DIAN-TU data showed robust, dose-dependent reductions in CSF MTBR-tau-243, so a positive dose-response signal against placebo plus lecanemab at 6 months is highly plausible even with about 21 participants per arm. The main risks are assay or analysis quirks, an attenuated incremental effect on top of lecanemab, and how the dose-response test is defined. Primary completion is December 2026, and I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"858027ecaeeb1dc4e6a11b174a32641f32ebdf437fa2c0f7a36503634aa3e13b"},{"nct":"NCT06991556","title":"An Open-label Study of JSB462 (Luxdegalutamide) in Combination With Abiraterone in Adult Male Patients With Metastatic Hormone-sensitive Prostate Cancer (mHSPC)","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-03","enrollment":168,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.2780220933969977,"rationale":"Luxdegalutamide (JSB462/ARV-766, an AR PROTAC degrader) plus abiraterone is being compared with abiraterone or enzalutamide alone on confirmed PSA90 rate, in a roughly 56-per-arm Phase II whose main purpose is dose selection for Phase III. Control-arm PSA90 rates in high-volume mHSPC are already high (about 60–75%), so the ceiling effect and small arms make a statistically significant difference hard even if the combination is genuinely better. The design pairs efficacy with safety endpoints and judges dose on the 'totality' of data, which suggests estimation rather than a powered hypothesis test. Earlier trials adding a second AR-pathway agent to an existing one were mostly disappointing, though PSA endpoints are more sensitive than survival endpoints, so I put modest odds on a significant result in favour of either dose.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"76588684e6e37b494510bfebbdc3ff87961512ccfbf80538756f8e6a51a72ea9"},{"nct":"NCT07500506","title":"A Study to Learn About the Safety, Tolerability, and Immunogenicity of a Fifth Dose of 6-Valent OspA-Based Lyme Disease Vaccine","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-04","enrollment":1712,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.7870205229842614,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcomes are descriptive safety measures, so success turns on the immunogenicity non-inferiority comparison: Dose 5 versus Dose 4 anti-OspA IgG GMR and seroresponse across serotypes ST1–ST6, one year apart. Valneva's phase 2 booster studies reported strong anamnestic responses after a second annual booster, broadly comparable to the first, which supports meeting standard NI margins. The main risks are blunted boosting from residual antibody one year after Dose 4 and the need to pass NI on all six serotypes and two metrics. No results are public yet; primary completion is planned for December 2026.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dc6ed60aa18d626a87f17c04662734ef617393ed8fdc9481c24111d7da99a16f"},{"nct":"NCT05757869","title":"A Study of Milvexian Versus Apixaban in Participants With Atrial Fibrillation","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-08","enrollment":20284,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.8303183730395821,"rationale":"LIBREXIA-AF is a large non-inferiority trial of milvexian 100 mg twice daily against apixaban for stroke and systemic embolism, a strong active comparator that sets a high bar. The closest precedent is OCEANIC-AF, where asundexian, another factor XIa inhibitor, was clearly inferior to apixaban and stopped early; that raises real doubt about whether this mechanism matches factor Xa inhibition for stroke prevention in AF. Offsetting this, milvexian is dosed for more complete factor XIa suppression, and the monitoring committee has let the trial continue through interim looks that would likely have caught an asundexian-sized efficacy gap. With LIBREXIA-ACS stopped for futility adding mechanism uncertainty, I put the chance of meeting the non-inferiority margin near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cc721e6aadbfab5cebc5a078c9fd295f23b0d09b2a180a9cff1432c6eec882e3"},{"nct":"NCT07228390","title":"A 16-Week Study to Learn About the Study Medicine Called Ritlecitinib in Adults With Long Lasting Painful Red Skin Lumps, Known by the Medical Term, Hidradenitis Suppurativa, or HS.","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-08","enrollment":128,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.46297828845183525,"rationale":"Ritlecitinib 30 mg beat placebo on HiSCR50 at week 16 in Pfizer's earlier phase 2a HS study (about 64% vs 42%), and other JAK inhibitors (povorcitinib, upadacitinib) have shown activity in HS. This trial uses a loading dose, which suggests a higher exposure that could enlarge the effect. However, HiSCR50 placebo responses are high and variable (roughly 30–45%), and with about 128 patients a 20-point difference gives only modest power, so a miss is quite possible. Primary completion is December 2026, so no result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6d274a25455173d7a894b11aa39169c2e1bdc61df9a99fb2f0b93b68ffaa163e"},{"nct":"NCT06126224","title":"A Study to Assess Efficacy and Safety of KarXT for the Treatment of Psychosis Associated With Alzheimer's Disease (ADEPT-2)","sponsor":"Karuna Therapeutics, Inc., a Bristol Myers Squibb company","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-09","enrollment":500,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.4539040510037962,"rationale":"KarXT (xanomeline-trospium) is proven in acute schizophrenia, and xanomeline alone reduced hallucinations and delusions in Alzheimer's patients in 1990s trials, which gives real mechanistic support. Against that, Alzheimer's psychosis trials have high placebo response and a poor track record (pimavanserin's acute results were mixed), the adjunctive schizophrenia trial ARISE failed, and cholinergic tolerability may limit dosing in elderly patients. BMS reportedly enlarged and extended this trial, which may signal concern about variability. I do not know of any topline result, so a roughly even probability seems appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5d906866809324461d88f3be6d3a49de2ae15337b01e629b8a7c4268295a885b"},{"nct":"NCT07280858","title":"A Phase I/II, Dose-finding Study to Assess the Safety, Reactogenicity, and Immunogenicity of a Broadly Protective Sarbecovirus Vaccine (GBP511) in Healthy Adults.","sponsor":"SK Bioscience Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-09","enrollment":368,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8314378865071801,"rationale":"This is a Phase I/II dose-finding safety and immunogenicity study of SK Bioscience's mosaic RBD nanoparticle pan-sarbecovirus vaccine (built on the SKYCovione/GBP510 platform, with Gates/CEPI backing). Its first-listed primary outcome is a descriptive safety measure (immediate reactions), not a superiority comparison against Comirnaty. Such trials are usually reported as having \"met\" their primary endpoint when safety is acceptable, and this platform has a good safety and immunogenicity record. The main risks are an unfavorable safety signal or the outcome being judged ambiguous because no formal hypothesis test is prespecified, which limits confidence somewhat.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2ffe64c86d9e52e0ab674c2c74deb7e8f1ad4417e46fe3df4c8149a4c4e3bec0"},{"nct":"NCT05686642","title":"Efficacy and Safety of LT3001 on Treating the Acute Ischemic Stroke","sponsor":"Shanghai Pharmaceuticals Holding Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-10","enrollment":300,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.249663939100359,"rationale":"The only primary outcome is adverse-event incidence, a descriptive safety measure with no stated statistical comparison, so whether this trial 'meets its primary endpoint' depends on how the sponsor frames a topline result. LT3001 (odatroltide) has looked safe in earlier phase 2 work, including Lumosa's US trial, which reported acceptable symptomatic intracranial hemorrhage rates, so a 'safe and well tolerated' announcement is plausible. A strict reading that requires a significant favorable difference in AEs versus placebo would almost certainly fail, and efficacy signals in an unthrombolysed population treated up to 24 hours after onset are uncertain. Balancing these readings gives a near-coin-flip estimate leaning slightly positive.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"15c249ea7961372f37d3c24876b1c036c6bb6f26314db12f34c7df25945ac9a0"},{"nct":"NCT06151574","title":"Beamion LUNG-2: A Study to Test Whether Zongertinib (BI 1810631) Helps People With Advanced Non-small Cell Lung Cancer With HER2 Mutations Compared With Standard Treatment","sponsor":"Boehringer Ingelheim","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-10","enrollment":428,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7343409257854298,"rationale":"Zongertinib is a potent, HER2-selective, EGFR-sparing TKI. In the Beamion LUNG-1 treatment-naive cohort it produced an objective response rate around 75% with durable responses, which led to accelerated approval. Pembrolizumab plus platinum-pemetrexed works relatively poorly in HER2-mutant NSCLC, with median PFS of roughly 6–8 months, and first-line targeted agents in oncogene-driven NSCLC have usually beaten chemotherapy-based controls on PFS. Remaining risks are an open-label design, possible crossover or durability surprises, and a large sample, but a central-review PFS benefit appears likely and no topline result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"08e894834e4db28a93019e50a7cbb7780f9c2cfed9fd15063f60110a9be3bd2b"},{"nct":"NCT07222917","title":"A Phase IIb Study to Evaluate the Effect of Dapagliflozin in Combination With Baxdrostat Compared With Baxdrostat on Albuminuria in Participants With Chronic Kidney Disease and High Blood Pressure.","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-10","enrollment":222,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5004487550355098,"rationale":"Dapagliflozin reliably lowers UACR by about 30% in CKD, and the CONFIDENCE trial showed an SGLT2 inhibitor added substantial further albuminuria reduction on top of mineralocorticoid-pathway blockade with finerenone. With about 111 patients per arm and typical log-UACR variability, a 25–30% between-arm difference would give high power, and the hemodynamic UACR effect appears within weeks, well inside the 12-week window. The main risks are that baxdrostat's mechanism overlaps with the SGLT2 inhibitor's, which could shrink the incremental effect, and the modest sample size, so I set the probability high but below certainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7592112ab20f1b85cf5328b50c69ff317576e0deb4b79d75fce68c8d7c9b693d"},{"nct":"NCT04879329","title":"A Study of Disitamab Vedotin Alone or With Pembrolizumab in Urothelial Cancer That Expresses HER2","sponsor":"Seagen, a wholly owned subsidiary of Pfizer","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-11","enrollment":372,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.47363273302041814,"rationale":"This is a multi-cohort phase 2 trial whose primary efficacy endpoint is BICR-confirmed ORR, mostly in single-arm cohorts, so success likely means beating a historical response threshold rather than winning a head-to-head comparison. Disitamab vedotin has produced roughly 50% ORR in HER2-expressing urothelial cancer in Chinese trials, and early Cohort C data with pembrolizumab in first-line disease reportedly showed high response rates; Pfizer has advanced the combination to a phase 3 trial. Risks include weaker activity in HER2-low and post-enfortumab-vedotin cohorts, and ambiguity in how the randomized part of Cohort C would be judged.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"391290a33671c75bdec4d3a9a1e213e48392676f7a2bf0b3e115b45aea30279f"},{"nct":"NCT07230132","title":"Efficacy and Safety of ZT006 in Overweight and Obese Participants","sponsor":"Beijing QL Biopharmaceutical Co.,Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-12","enrollment":184,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.8337034260265198,"rationale":"ZT006 appears to be an oral GLP-1 receptor agonist tablet. Oral small-molecule GLP-1 agonists such as orforglipron have consistently produced large, highly significant placebo-adjusted weight loss in Phase 2 trials at 26–36 weeks. Even with only about 30 participants per arm, a placebo-adjusted difference of 5% or more at week 28 in at least one of five active arms would very likely reach significance. The main risks are an unusually weak molecule or tolerability-driven dropout, and primary completion (December 2026) has not yet passed, so results are not public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"aabce6df6156893133c449a9c21242003d669f60a8f046a31681363e35849e07"},{"nct":"NCT04957550","title":"To Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of SHR0302 Tablet in Subjects of Active Psoriatic Arthritis","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-13","enrollment":418,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.8983754529620877,"rationale":"SHR0302 (ivarmacitinib) is a selective JAK1 inhibitor that has already succeeded in phase 3 trials in rheumatoid arthritis and ankylosing spondylitis. In psoriatic arthritis, the same mechanism has consistently beaten placebo on ACR20 (tofacitinib, upadacitinib, filgotinib). With about 140 patients per arm, a largely biologic-naive population, a placebo comparator and the sensitive ACR20 endpoint, the trial is well powered for the typical 20-30 point treatment difference. Primary completion is not until December 2026, so I am not aware of any public result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"34b1a90fcb9b33b12dc76d89a2dd7346bb989b7dd86f41bf902dda9b06cf111e"},{"nct":"NCT06122779","title":"Study to Evaluate Safety, Tolerability and Drug Levels of BMS-986435/MYK-224 in Participants With Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (HFpEF)","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-14","enrollment":227,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.30963135511204,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are descriptive safety measures (incidence of TEAEs, SAEs and discontinuations) in a Phase 2a exposure-response study, so there is no prespecified efficacy comparison that could come out significant for the drug. Success therefore depends on how 'met' is judged: a sponsor might call acceptable tolerability a success, but a significant between-arm safety benefit is implausible. Cardiac myosin inhibition also carries an LVEF-lowering risk, and mavacamten failed in non-obstructive HCM (ODYSSEY-HCM), which adds uncertainty about whether BMS will describe the safety profile favorably in HFpEF. Given the ambiguity, a near-coin-flip estimate is appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"33f9557377ff6ea2b2dce86a1b06dced9b1ea9e6ca4b1fdb2cd0481c8e451afc"},{"nct":"NCT06430866","title":"Pharmacokinetic Similarity Between ABP 234 and Keytruda® (Pembrolizumab)","sponsor":"Amgen","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-14","enrollment":163,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.6369011718666431,"rationale":"This is a PK equivalence trial of a biosimilar (ABP 234) against Keytruda, run by Amgen, which has a strong biosimilar track record; the success bar is AUC ratio 90% CIs falling within standard bioequivalence margins (typically 80–125%). Biosimilar PK similarity studies almost always succeed when the analytical similarity work was solid, though variability in a patient population (n=163) and the co-primary steady-state AUC requirement add some risk. Other pembrolizumab biosimilars (e.g., Samsung Bioepis, Sandoz, Amgen's own) have generally shown PK equivalence. I am not aware of any public topline result for this trial, and primary completion is planned for December 2026.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a077f12f3536eb610ef4987ebbc1277b420950757200d10c009462741e6e5f99"},{"nct":"NCT06806137","title":"A Study on the Immune Response and Safety of the Second Dose of an Investigational Chickenpox Vaccine When Given to Healthy Children 3 Months After a First Dose at 12 to 15 Months of Age","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-14","enrollment":600,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8822359500115616,"rationale":"This is a non-inferiority immunogenicity trial of GSK's reformulated live-attenuated varicella vaccine (VNS, Oka-strain lineage like Varilrix) against Varivax. After a second dose, seroresponse rates (gE IgG ≥300 mIU/mL) approach 100% with either vaccine, which makes the seroresponse margin relatively easy to meet. The main risk is the GMC co-primary, since earlier VNS studies hinted at somewhat lower anti-gE concentrations than Varivax, and running this extra study may reflect regulatory concerns from first-dose data. Non-inferiority trials of near-equivalent live vaccines usually succeed, so I put the probability at about 0.8.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4c274e11f9c563c5e2fc06e3ec944c2af77783ef63e78f903ede2a37252d8cca"},{"nct":"NCT07184632","title":"A Research Study on How Well Different Doses of the Medicine NNC0662-0419 Help People Living With Overweight or Obesity","sponsor":"Novo Nordisk A/S","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-14","enrollment":224,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.607473736868616,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome (Part A TEAE count) is a safety measure, so the relevant efficacy comparison is Part B: percent body-weight change versus placebo at 36 weeks. NNC0662-0419 appears to be a potent incretin- or amylin-class agent, given the exclusions for prior GLP-1, GIP and amylin agonists and the requirement that participants be willing to lose more than 25% of body weight. Drugs in this class reliably beat placebo on weight loss, even in modestly sized phase 2 dose-ranging arms. The main uncertainties are how this multi-part, safety-led design gets scored, and the small chance of tolerability or development problems.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a9b7b189e0b65cb99718fd3a3acacbd50e8332f699db8bf868273cb92d95e3a1"},{"nct":"NCT07543796","title":"Efficacy and Safety of TRD205 Tablets for Postoperative Analgesia in Unilateral Total Hip Arthroplasty (Phase IIb)","sponsor":"Beijing Tide Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-14","enrollment":200,"base":0.57,"researched":null,"learned":0.7874633576085592,"rationale":"TRD205 is a novel oral non-opioid analgesic from Tide Pharmaceutical, and the move to Phase IIb suggests the earlier Phase IIa in this setting was encouraging. Hip arthroplasty is a harder acute pain model than bunionectomy or abdominoplasty, because baseline multimodal analgesia and rescue opioids compress drug-placebo differences in resting pain. With about 40 patients per arm, a single site, and three doses (any one beating placebo counts), the trial has a reasonable but not high chance of reaching significance on resting-pain NRS AUC0-48h. I start near the Phase 2 base rate and adjust modestly upward for the multiple doses and the presumed positive prior signal.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"02a233569244b564529fcd83614d56bae305e8d2e9447babd2fee4570b1d55f1"},{"nct":"NCT03817502","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Cariprazine in the Treatment of Adolescent Participants (13 to 17 Years of Age) With Schizophrenia","sponsor":"Gedeon Richter Plc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-15","enrollment":330,"base":0.57,"researched":null,"learned":0.6595696041062178,"rationale":"Cariprazine is a proven antipsychotic in adult schizophrenia, and most atypicals (aripiprazole, risperidone, olanzapine, quetiapine, lurasidone) succeeded in adolescent placebo-controlled trials. However, several adolescent trials failed or were mixed (asenapine, ziprasidone, paliperidone at some doses, brexpiprazole not reaching significance) because of high placebo response and heterogeneous enrollment. This trial has two doses, which raises the chance that at least one arm succeeds. It has also enrolled very slowly over about seven years, partly at Eastern European sites disrupted by the war, which adds noise and dropout risk, so I put it modestly above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"96994055f57c863fab1e19a4ec5fcf70fd460770b8637ec63c256cc9827a9f89"},{"nct":"NCT05327114","title":"Efficacy and Safety Study of Nipocalimab for Adults With Chronic Inflammatory Demyelinating Polyneuropathy (CIDP)","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-15","enrollment":201,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.7509227545823048,"rationale":"FcRn inhibition is already validated in CIDP: efgartigimod's ADHERE trial used nearly the same responder-enriched randomized-withdrawal design and showed a strong reduction in relapse risk (HR ~0.39, p<0.0001). Nipocalimab produces deep IgG lowering and is approved in gMG, so the class effect should carry over. Withdrawal designs that enrich for open-label responders and use time to relapse as the endpoint tend to succeed when the drug works. Remaining risks are a fairly modest sample size, a slow trial still recruiting near its planned primary completion, and possible differences in dosing or relapse adjudication, so I place this somewhat below the near-certain level.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"07438785eba532330a79253232b688406a2f792c3a101b1c516f5dbed69d162d"},{"nct":"NCT05678673","title":"Study of XL092 + Nivolumab vs Sunitinib in Subjects With Advanced or Metastatic Non-Clear Cell Renal Cell Carcinoma","sponsor":"Exelixis","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-15","enrollment":317,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.6100809040403019,"rationale":"This is STELLAR-304, testing zanzalintinib (a cabozantinib-like VEGFR/MET/TAM TKI) plus nivolumab against sunitinib, a weak comparator in papillary and other non-clear cell RCC. PAPMET already showed cabozantinib significantly beat sunitinib on PFS, and cabozantinib plus nivolumab produced high response rates in phase 2 nccRCC cohorts, so a similar combination should beat sunitinib. With 317 patients randomized 2:1, there is reasonable power for a sizeable PFS effect, though histologic heterogeneity and the uncertain size of zanzalintinib's effect leave some risk. I do not recall a topline result being public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c6bfdf0724b15b70eda09e5fbf14cdb74c79c628cfb8c9e344d904c15341aba4"},{"nct":"NCT05503264","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacokinetics (PK), and Pharmacodynamics (PD) of Satralizumab in Participants With Anti-N-methyl-D-aspartic Acid Receptor (NMDAR) or Anti-leucine-rich Glioma-inactivated 1 (LGI1) Encephalitis","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-16","enrollment":122,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.7076814705539743,"rationale":"CIELO is the first randomized placebo-controlled test of IL-6 receptor blockade in NMDAR and LGI1 encephalitis, supported only by small open-label tocilizumab series. The primary endpoint, a 1-point or greater mRS improvement without rescue therapy, likely has a high placebo response, because many patients improve with first-line immunotherapy and the natural course of these diseases. The NMDAR cohort is also small (roughly 60–80 patients), which leaves limited power. Roche's protocol amendments to the cohort design add some uncertainty, and a new mechanism in a rare neurological disease suggests a below-base-rate chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"53cd40540980495a8fae251e3f9b1562d6fe2a7259c0f3e3c4d26fc5fc9a330d"},{"nct":"NCT06747338","title":"A Phase III Study of KN026 in Combination With HB1801 ± Carboplatin as Neoadjuvant Treatment for Early or Locally Advanced HER2-Positive Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Shanghai JMT-Bio Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-16","enrollment":520,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.707866926247132,"rationale":"KN026 (anbenitamab), a HER2 biparatopic antibody, has shown strong activity, including positive phase 3 data in HER2+ gastric cancer and high response rates with docetaxel in HER2+ breast cancer; HB1801 is likely CSPC's albumin-bound docetaxel. The record does not say whether the design is superiority or non-inferiority against an active TH-P ± carboplatin comparator, which already achieves roughly 55-65% tpCR in Chinese patients. With 520 patients, a superiority trial could detect only about a 12-point gain in tpCR, which would be ambitious, while a non-inferiority trial would likely succeed. Weighing those two scenarios gives a near-coin-flip estimate tilted slightly toward success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"31c7a077c630a0588e41efd222882e720f8e8c1d4e3a72c9e724dde86a9c1e4a"},{"nct":"NCT06268886","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of an Anti-MTBR Tau Monoclonal Antibody (BMS-986446) in Participants With Early Alzheimer's Disease","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-17","enrollment":310,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.2166571480391926,"rationale":"BMS-986446 (PRX005) is an anti-MTBR tau antibody, and this Phase 2 proof-of-concept trial uses slowing of tau PET accumulation at week 76 as its primary endpoint, a biomarker target that is easier to hit than a clinical one. N-terminal tau antibodies (gosuranemab, tilavonemab, semorinemab) showed no tau PET benefit. More encouragingly, UCB's mid-region antibody bepranemab showed slowing of tau PET accumulation despite missing its clinical primary, and MTBR-directed antibodies are mechanistically favored. With about 310 patients, two dose arms and a noisy longitudinal tau PET endpoint, success is plausible but far from assured, so I estimate somewhat below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d33a491783e95ae9d1b1cdd598549d1a044165350f35d4fd21d0a04bdbbb4876"},{"nct":"NCT06958536","title":"A Study to Investigate Efficacy and Safety of Brivekimig in Participants With Crohn's Disease","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-17","enrollment":99,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.4768384377541843,"rationale":"Brivekimig is a bispecific nanobody against TNF and OX40L. TNF inhibition is a validated mechanism in Crohn's disease, and the drug showed positive phase 2 signals in hidradenitis suppurativa. Against that, the trial is small (about 33 per arm), enrolls many patients who have already failed advanced therapies (possibly including anti-TNFs), and uses centrally read endoscopic response at Week 16, so power for a 20–25 point placebo-adjusted difference is only moderate. Dose-ranging phase 2 studies also sometimes lack strict formal significance testing, so I put the chance of a statistically significant win for at least one dose slightly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"bb7863987b89c073cffcd871caa7bbaa9e9fa4c3df58e2e32dbff978ee6ac2e9"},{"nct":"NCT06975722","title":"A Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Brivekimig in Adult Participants With Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-17","enrollment":105,"base":0.52,"researched":null,"learned":0.49937217930137295,"rationale":"Brivekimig is a TNF/OX40L bispecific nanobody, and its TNF arm is a mechanism already validated in UC, which supports some efficacy. It also showed positive phase 2a signals in hidradenitis suppurativa. However, with only about 35 patients per arm, a stringent centrally read week-16 remission endpoint, and a mixed population that includes advanced-therapy-experienced patients, a modest anti-TNF-like effect (for example 15–20% vs 5–10%) could miss significance at two-sided p<0.05. Weighing the validated mechanism against limited power, I put success near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"669d13d0540258142ddafa269e725e291c472524ef43c03df4b0da787a1099b3"},{"nct":"NCT07363720","title":"A Trial of TAK-861 for the Treatment of Narcolepsy With Cataplexy","sponsor":"Takeda","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-17","enrollment":98,"base":0.94,"researched":null,"learned":0.7628630482672408,"rationale":"TAK-861 (oveporexton), an OX2R agonist, showed very large, highly significant ESS improvements over placebo in NT1 in the phase 2b trial and the phase 3 FirstLight and RadiantLight trials, and phase 2 data showed symptoms return soon after stopping the drug. This randomized withdrawal design enrolls open-label responders and switches half to placebo, so placebo patients should relapse quickly on ESS while those continuing the drug stay stable. That makes time-to-loss-of-response a sensitive endpoint even with roughly 70–90 randomized. The main risks are a small sample, the relapse definition, or the short 4-week window, but the effect size should easily overcome them.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1508df279f544d4f4ad9360ff68afe05de1f6f9dec3318e2ce642d1cc85f1926"},{"nct":"NCT06062810","title":"Bioequivalence ANDA SNP Clinical Study - Raloxifene and Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms","sponsor":"Han Xu, M.D., Ph.D., FAPCR, Sponsor-Investigator, IRB Chair","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-18","enrollment":600,"base":0.15,"researched":null,"learned":0.6127733080180378,"rationale":"This is one of many near-identical registrations from a single sponsor-investigator. It compares two generic raloxifene products, and its primary outcome only measures and reports SNP genotypes, with no prespecified hypothesis test, superiority comparison, or non-inferiority margin. The design is internally incoherent (an off-label 120 mg dose called 'chemotherapy', 'measurable disease' in LCIS, one site, 600 patients), which makes it doubtful the trial will produce interpretable or publicly reported results. With no testable comparison and a low chance of credible results, a positive topline on the primary endpoint is unlikely, though a purely descriptive endpoint could be claimed as met.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8119770a5d385471aaa51839ea493ccbf25c8297cfec578def0f637a0c61fc8b"},{"nct":"NCT07145333","title":"Pharmacogenomics ANDA SNP Clinical Study - Topotecan and Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms","sponsor":"Han Xu, M.D., Ph.D., FAPCR, Medical Director, IRB Chair","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-18","enrollment":600,"base":0.05,"researched":null,"learned":0.6222693656676437,"rationale":"This is one of a series of near-identical registrations from a single individual sponsor, the 'Pharmacogenomics ANDA SNP' studies. They have implausible designs (600 patients at one site, start-to-completion in about 10 weeks) and a descriptive primary outcome with no prespecified comparison or hypothesis test. These studies are not known to have run or reported any results, so a topline announcement of a statistically significant primary endpoint is very unlikely. Even if data emerged, the outcome is not a superiority or non-inferiority comparison that could be judged met.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3e01596d943501bc89466367809935c03460a099775a03f96e9f8db89bc8a18d"},{"nct":"NCT07246889","title":"Study of AHB-137 in Participants With Chronic Hepatitis B (CHB) Treated With Nucleos(t)Ide Analogues (NAs)(AUSHINE)","sponsor":"Ausper Biopharma Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-18","enrollment":577,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.7894191018551611,"rationale":"AHB-137 is an antisense oligonucleotide. Phase 2 data in NA-suppressed, HBeAg-negative patients with low baseline HBsAg (≤3000 IU/mL) showed high on-treatment HBsAg loss and meaningful functional-cure rates off treatment. The placebo-plus-NA arm should give near-zero rates of HBsAg clearance sustained 24 weeks off all therapy, so the ~577-patient trial is powered to detect even a modest absolute difference. The same mechanism appears validated by bepirovirsen's positive phase 3 results; the main risks are durability off NA therapy and Phase 2 effects shrinking at scale.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fb95e53ed8014e463a9b86497cf5028413a453dd883277e25fb8234a5d027790"},{"nct":"NCT05468697","title":"A Study of Belzutifan (MK-6482) in Combination With Palbociclib Versus Belzutifan Monotherapy in Participants With Advanced Renal Cell Carcinoma (MK-6482-024/LITESPARK-024)","sponsor":"Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-22","enrollment":60,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.4991268018378456,"rationale":"The registered primary outcomes are now only descriptive safety measures (DLT counts, any AE, discontinuations due to AE), with no prespecified comparison against belzutifan monotherapy. Such endpoints have no significance test, so 'success' depends on whether a tolerable recommended palbociclib dose is established. The record looks amended: only combination arms remain and enrollment is just 60, which suggests the randomized efficacy comparison was dropped or deprioritized, a weak signal for the program. Belzutifan plus a CDK4/6 inhibitor is likely tolerable at some dose, but because a descriptive-safety trial is ambiguous to score, I stay near even with a slight lean toward 'met'.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"438f62cded428c0742addfe8c5fede20b3f78e3f5662c2fa262cd71b9b70a472"},{"nct":"NCT06544616","title":"A Study of JNJ-64042056 in Participants With Preclinical Alzheimer's Disease","sponsor":"Janssen Pharmaceutica N.V., Belgium","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-22","enrollment":55,"base":0.13,"researched":null,"learned":0.21216024128302913,"rationale":"JNJ-64042056 (ACI-35.030) is an anti-phospho-tau active vaccine, and anti-tau antibodies such as semorinemab, gosuranemab and tilavonemab have consistently failed to slow tau PET accumulation, so the mechanism's track record on this biomarker is poor. This small companion study enrolled only 55 participants, which is badly underpowered to detect a modest difference in tau PET change. Tau accumulation in preclinical AD is slow and variable even over about two years, adding noise. Some chance of a nominal signal in one ROI remains, but the probability of a significant primary result is low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3ba19ecbcba1e312203530f8f272bde644ab8fe09b150d5f9229004b6471407e"},{"nct":"NCT06769048","title":"A Study to Test Different Doses of BI 1584862 in People With a Distinct Form of Age-related Macular Degeneration (AMD) Called Geographic Atrophy","sponsor":"Boehringer Ingelheim","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-22","enrollment":150,"base":0.22,"researched":null,"learned":0.35447993864070204,"rationale":"BI 1584862 appears to be a first-in-class or novel-mechanism agent being tested for the first time for efficacy in geographic atrophy, a disease where most phase 2 programs have failed. The exceptions, the complement C3 and C5 inhibitors, needed larger trials or showed only modest effects of roughly 15–30% slowing in lesion growth. With about 150 patients split across three doses and placebo (the staged design suggests uneven allocation), the trial has limited power to show a statistically significant difference in GA growth slope over 50 weeks. A Boehringer exploratory dose-finding study may also have been powered at a lenient alpha, which does not map onto the two-sided p<0.05 criterion, so I put the chance of a clearly positive primary result at roughly one in five.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0d75b748fb15a9b13ed4a1ae28970b907608d3e9c10caa7ca59a4b51df4b58b6"},{"nct":"NCT06856577","title":"Efficacy and Safety Study of Ixoberogene Soroparvovec (Ixo-vec) in Participants With Neovascular Age-Related Macular Degeneration","sponsor":"Adverum Biotechnologies, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-22","enrollment":311,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.7181417481351402,"rationale":"ARTEMIS is a non-inferiority trial of BCVA change versus aflibercept 2 mg q8w, and Ixo-vec patients can receive aflibercept rescue. Rescue-allowed anti-VEGF NI designs (e.g., the port delivery system's Archway, newer anti-VEGF agents) usually meet a standard ~4–5 letter margin. Phase 2 LUNA and OPTIC data showed stable BCVA with large injection-burden reductions, and Lilly's 2025 acquisition of Adverum suggests outside confidence. The main risks are gene-therapy inflammation or hypotony eroding vision in a subset, variable rescue adherence, and modest sample size, so this sits somewhat below the typical NI success rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8ce3139110bf54e560bedef0c1c2d47529f1bf0151cf403f816683e69350e861"},{"nct":"NCT07285291","title":"A Phase 3 Study of TS-172 in Hyperphosphatemia Patients on Hemodialysis With Phosphate Binders","sponsor":"Taisho Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-22","enrollment":100,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7035965534934517,"rationale":"TS-172 is Taisho's oral intestinal phosphate-absorption inhibitor, and Japanese phase 2 data in hemodialysis patients reportedly showed dose-dependent serum phosphorus lowering. Add-on, placebo-controlled designs with phosphorus endpoints have generally succeeded in Japan, for example tenapanor added to binders, and placebo response in serum phosphorus is small. With about 100 patients and a titratable dose, a responder-rate primary endpoint at week 8 should be adequately powered. The main risks are a modest effect size on a binary endpoint and tolerability-limited titration, so I forecast a high but not certain probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b5b530695c712de89ba3f37679912f2e9faff777c762a6238cbf1e91e32d7c8a"},{"nct":"NCT05692180","title":"A Multicentre, Randomised, Double-blind, Parallel Group, Placebo-controlled, Time-to-first Asthma Exacerbation Phase III Efficacy and Safety Study of Benralizumab in Paediatric Patients With Severe Eosinophilic Asthma","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":94,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.5581293018764389,"rationale":"Benralizumab consistently cut exacerbations by roughly 30-50% in adult eosinophilic asthma, and other type-2 biologics (dupilumab in VOYAGE, mepolizumab in MUPPITS-2) succeeded in children, which supports a real effect here. Against that, only 94 patients are enrolled in an event-driven time-to-first-exacerbation design, so the study has few events and modest power. Pediatric trials also tend to see large placebo responses, and the adolescent subgroups in SIROCCO/CALIMA showed weaker benralizumab effects. I put success somewhat above a coin flip, and I don't know of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"658e4d7f0b7c6546bb9ca142341ae930cda967c4bf29c8f306f9730e11fdd9c5"},{"nct":"NCT05849298","title":"A Phase II Study of AAA617 Alone and AAA617 in Combination With ARPI in Patients With PSMA PET Scan Positive CRPC","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":49,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.39282271257901413,"rationale":"This is a small, randomized but explicitly non-comparative phase II trial (49 enrolled, likely fewer than planned) with no prespecified between-arm test, so 'success' would hinge on an undisclosed response-rate threshold or a descriptive readout. Lu-PSMA-617 has proven activity in mCRPC, and in a low-burden, PSMA-PET-positive nmCRPC population, particularly combined with an ARPI, confirmed PSA ≤0.2 ng/mL rates could plausibly be substantial. Still, the reduced enrollment, the lack of a formal hypothesis, and the likelihood that Novartis reports the results descriptively rather than as a positive topline make a clear 'met primary endpoint' outcome uncertain. I know of no public result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a1ea6574da5f8c54dbaab56265738ec8d1bf87b0dcc10abad6d9818c6ee0accd"},{"nct":"NCT06402331","title":"FPI-2265 (225Ac-PSMA-I&T) for Patients With PSMA-Positive Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer (mCRPC)","sponsor":"Fusion Pharmaceuticals Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":110,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.3801871080805824,"rationale":"This is an uncontrolled, randomized dose-optimization phase 2 with no comparator. The first primary endpoint is TEAE frequency, so there is no formal superiority test, and 'success' depends on the sponsor reporting acceptable safety and meaningful PSA50 activity. Prior TATCIST data for 225Ac-PSMA-I&T in post-177Lu-PSMA patients showed PSA50 rates of roughly 40-50% with manageable xerostomia and hematologic toxicity. AstraZeneca's acquisition of Fusion suggests continued development and a likely favorable framing, but the descriptive endpoint and the hard post-Lu population leave substantial uncertainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9ea0c09001b6a981ed2c4244c626288eaf7ffc8024cb74e044bb5a1b363b144d"},{"nct":"NCT06500702","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Frexalimab, Brivekimig, or Rilzabrutinib in Participants Aged 16 to 75 Years With Primary Focal Segmental Glomerulosclerosis or Minimal Change Disease","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":84,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5901075742051985,"rationale":"This is a small Phase 2a umbrella study, with roughly 84 participants split across three investigational drugs and placebo, so each arm has only about 14–21 patients. None of the three mechanisms (CD40L blockade, TNF/OX40L nanobody, BTK inhibition) has proven efficacy in primary FSGS or MCD, so detecting a statistically significant UPCR reduction at 12 weeks would need a large effect. Selecting for steroid- or immunosuppression-responsive disease and having three shots at success raise the chance somewhat, and the recent anti-nephrin autoantibody findings in MCD and FSGS lend some biological rationale to the B-cell-related agents. Even so, the historical record for new mechanisms in FSGS is poor, and exploratory Phase 2a trials are often not powered for formal significance.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"454f9cb0693b00d89a017f1d963a46d9dcd319a4e723e0b955b38ad54edf240e"},{"nct":"NCT07260500","title":"A Phase II Study of PEG-rhGH Injection for Short Children Born Small for Gestational Age: Efficacy, Safety, and Pharmacokinetics","sponsor":"Changchun GeneScience Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":72,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.5242157539672503,"rationale":"Jintrolong, a PEG-rhGH already approved in China, has shown height velocity comparable to daily GH in prior Chinese pediatric trials, including SGA populations, so the weekly arms will probably grow similarly to the Jintropin control. This small open-label Phase II (24 per arm) looks dose-finding and descriptive, with no stated non-inferiority margin or superiority hypothesis. Statistically significant superiority over daily GH is unlikely, while a sponsor-claimed 'comparable' or non-inferior result is plausible. Because it is unclear how success would be judged, I put the probability near the middle.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"bbb81275c8331157ae00335ce96a3f91dd1393de54cd7962482bdf0101be121e"},{"nct":"NCT07672236","title":"A Clinical Study to Compare BupiZenge With Lidocaine for Pain Due to Oral Mucositis in Patients With Head and Neck Cancer.","sponsor":"OncoZenge AB","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-23","enrollment":150,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.675784394144107,"rationale":"In earlier Danish trials, including a randomized phase 2 against standard care such as viscous lidocaine, the bupivacaine lozenge gave larger and longer oral pain relief in head and neck cancer patients during radiotherapy. The primary endpoint, pain reduction summed over 3 hours, favors a long-acting agent over short-acting lidocaine, and the open-label, patient-reported design adds further bias toward the novel product. The main risks are small-company execution, missing data on the last day of radiotherapy, and a modest sample of 150 if the true effect is smaller than in phase 2. The planned primary completion date looks unrealistic given the July 2026 start, and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2784db706a2691f5b023077a8fb26bb6a455ab773483312a7758ad7a893115a4"},{"nct":"NCT06008119","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Tunlametinib Plus Vemurafenib in Patients With BRAF V600E-mutant Metastatic Colorectal Cancer","sponsor":"Shanghai Kechow Pharma, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-24","enrollment":165,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.5299687566782408,"rationale":"Tunlametinib, a MEK inhibitor already approved in China, plus vemurafenib showed encouraging early-phase activity in BRAF V600E colorectal cancer, reportedly with response rates and PFS above historical chemotherapy benchmarks. The control, doublet chemotherapy with or without bevacizumab or cetuximab, gives short PFS in BRAF-mutant disease (about 2–4 months, as BEACON showed). An open-label PFS endpoint further favors the experimental arm. Against that, BRAF+MEK without EGFR blockade has historically been weak in CRC, and the trial is modest in size (165) and still recruiting, so meaningful uncertainty remains.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"56f35f465e6a543b7d43a9ee1cb9012e8a47119bd6c164b565f72047ebbfe82b"},{"nct":"NCT06783647","title":"A Clinical Trial of LBL-024 Combination Drug in Patients With Advanced Solid Tumours[Substudy 01(NSCLC)]","sponsor":"Nanjing Leads Biolabs Co.,Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-24","enrollment":250,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.4424670606911942,"rationale":"LBL-024 is Leads Biolabs' PD-L1/4-1BB bispecific, which has shown encouraging activity in extrapulmonary neuroendocrine carcinoma. This NSCLC substudy has only experimental arms; the one randomization in Cohort 1A compares LBL-024+docetaxel with or without bevacizumab, so the ORR primary endpoint is likely descriptive, with no powered comparison against a true control. A sponsor would probably call reported ORRs positive, but a formal significant between-arm difference is unlikely, so resolution is ambiguous. I have no knowledge of results, and primary completion is not until late 2026.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5c36179a49d38fca054d3fc650f9595043db3a47e193f0747d99c07210b4966a"},{"nct":"NCT05653453","title":"Clinical Study of Tumor Treating Fields Combined with Gemcitabine and Albumin-bound Paclitaxel in the First-line Treatment of Locally Advanced Pancreatic Cancer","sponsor":"Jiangsu Healthy Life Innovation Medical Technology Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-25","enrollment":512,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.489239976441554,"rationale":"Novocure's PANOVA-3 showed that adding tumor treating fields to gemcitabine/nab-paclitaxel in locally advanced pancreatic cancer improved overall survival (HR ~0.82, p≈0.04), so the mechanism has precedent in this exact setting. That effect was modest and only just significant, though, and this Chinese copy-device trial is of similar size (512), unblinded, run at only five sites, and depends on device compliance that may differ. With a true HR near 0.82, power to reach p<0.05 on OS is roughly 50%, offset slightly by the tendency of sponsor-run Chinese device trials to report positively. I know of no public result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"625e65b02f9471b7843a94486f195a7163d47b9ce7f8e73b552797b9e4161604"},{"nct":"NCT06740630","title":"A Study on the Immune Response and Safety of an Investigational Chickenpox Vaccine When Given to Healthy Children 12 to 15 Months of Age","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-25","enrollment":1840,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.9082090771410047,"rationale":"This Phase 3a trial tests lot-to-lot consistency and non-inferiority of GSK's refined Oka-strain varicella vaccine (VNS) against Varivax, a well-established live-attenuated platform where lot consistency and immunogenicity non-inferiority usually succeed. There is some uncertainty: GSK appears to be running additional Phase 3 immunogenicity studies, and the secondary 'adaptive seroresponse threshold' outcome hints that seroresponse margins on the new gE assay may be tight. Enrollment of about 1,840 gives ample power for the usual margins, but meeting several co-primary comparisons adds risk. The trial is still recruiting and its results are not public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ca57d9327f427c1bcbb0af4d5cd57f448473cc4eb69252b073431f1a3cb26065"},{"nct":"NCT07219615","title":"A Study to Learn About Ritlecitinib for the Potential Treatment of Chronic Spontaneous Urticaria in Adults.","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-25","enrollment":200,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.4995817652273639,"rationale":"Ritlecitinib is an approved oral JAK3/TEC-family inhibitor, and its TEC-family coverage includes BTK. BTK inhibition is clinically validated in CSU, with remibrutinib positive in phase 3 and rilzabrutinib positive in phase 2, so the mechanistic rationale is strong and Pfizer likely moved forward on supportive signals. With about 65 patients per arm, two doses and a continuous UAS7 change endpoint at week 12, the trial has reasonable power to detect the typical 5–10 point separation from placebo. Remaining risks are a high placebo response, and that ritlecitinib's BTK occupancy in mast cells may be weaker than that of dedicated BTK inhibitors.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4a3b4d8ad0468165a5f31cd9c774301d648105993ff1c91a25533f679d263296"},{"nct":"NCT04498117","title":"Oregovomab Plus Chemo in Newly Diagnosed Patients With Advanced Epithelial Ovarian Cancer Following Optimal Debulking Surgery","sponsor":"CanariaBio Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-26","enrollment":615,"base":0.18,"researched":null,"learned":0.7198985715791385,"rationale":"Oregovomab monotherapy maintenance already failed in earlier phase 3 trials (IMPACT), and front-line ovarian cancer add-on immunotherapy has repeatedly failed, including checkpoint inhibitors. The randomized phase 2 chemo-combination signal (PFS ~42 vs ~12 months) came from a small, open-label study, and effects that large usually shrink in a confirmatory phase 3. The trial appears to have continued past an interim analysis without an early efficacy stop, and the sponsor is a small biotech, which slightly lowers confidence. I put the probability of a significant PFS benefit well below the phase 3 oncology base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"eb4567a31f5a04b9ce97c994dacbc8c92d04b129996aa369a305c10b103dcebf"},{"nct":"NCT06212999","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Long-Term Safety and Efficacy of Povorcitinib in Participants With Moderate to Severe Hidradenitis Suppurativa","sponsor":"Incyte Corporation","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-26","enrollment":617,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.799183469012337,"rationale":"This is a long-term extension whose primary endpoint is the descriptive proportion of participants with TEAEs, with no prespecified superiority comparison, so 'success' most plausibly means a safety readout the sponsor reports as consistent with the known profile. The parent Phase 3 STOP-HS1 and STOP-HS2 trials reportedly met their primary endpoints, and povorcitinib's safety profile in HS and vitiligo looked consistent with the JAK1 class, with no major new signals. Incyte is pursuing regulatory filings and has every incentive to describe the LTE as supportive. The main risks are ambiguity in how a non-comparative endpoint gets scored and any emerging JAK-class safety signal over longer exposure.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2a3db937bc10cc7ff427ec15984f4804476e33d09e05cd343dad542af40419ea"},{"nct":"NCT07503886","title":"An Exploratory Efficacy and Safety Study of DFL24498 Topical Ophthalmic Solution Compared With Vehicle in Participants With Dry Eye Disease","sponsor":"Dompé Farmaceutici S.p.A","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-27","enrollment":417,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.30800857367524787,"rationale":"DFL24498 is an early-stage Dompé compound, apparently a lyophilized formulation in the vein of its NGF-pathway ocular surface work, with little public efficacy data. Vehicle-controlled dry eye trials using corneal fluorescein staining at week 12 as the primary endpoint fail often because of high vehicle response and variability, though 417 participants gives reasonable power. Phase 2 dry eye trials have a low historical success rate, and the 'exploratory' label suggests modest expectations, so I estimate about 30%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0d7d58c30188f42fecb35f07201c3ccc64174d8fb3e0fd9a87741cdc0927ac86"},{"nct":"NCT07572396","title":"Phase II Study of Dysplasix™ Intravaginal Suppositories in Patients Patients With High-Risk HPV and Mild Cervical Cytologic Abnormalities","sponsor":"Amplexd Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-27","enrollment":45,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.3524127717645995,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety (SAEs/DLTs) and involves no formal comparison, so success likely hinges on the cytologic regression endpoint versus placebo. With only about 45 participants, 30-day follow-up, and high spontaneous regression of ASC-US/LSIL in placebo arms, a statistically significant difference is hard to reach. Prior EGCG (Polyphenon E) trials in cervical lesions were largely negative, and this is a small sponsor's first proof-of-concept study at a single site. Some chance of a nominally positive result or a safety-only 'success' claim keeps this above the floor.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a3c371cc0e2d7df322b88c9018c4f52e31bb806055dc7bd47018e30e7c42945a"},{"nct":"NCT04077723","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Safety, Pharmacokinetics and Preliminary Anti-Tumor Activity of Englumafusp Alfa in Combination With Obinutuzumab and in Combination With Glofitamab Following a Pre-Treatment Dose of Obinutuzumab in Participants With Relapsed/Refractory B-Cell Non-Hodgkin's Lymphoma","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-28","enrollment":498,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.4136051828214668,"rationale":"This is an open-label Phase I/II dose-escalation and expansion study whose first-listed primary outcomes are DLTs and adverse events, with no formal efficacy comparison, so 'meeting the primary endpoint' mostly means identifying a tolerable dose with encouraging activity. Earlier data presented at ASH showed englumafusp alfa plus glofitamab giving high ORR and CR rates in heavily pretreated DLBCL with manageable CRS, and Roche went on to a large Part III expansion in second-line patients. Against that, there is uncertainty about Roche's continued commitment to the CD19-4-1BBL program, and it is unclear how a safety-primary, single-arm study would be judged. I put the probability modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a96ec26b6370dc19133bd6fe444d0d5994f7bc2b9b0a66d6c4c5e0943885b4d3"},{"nct":"NCT05555862","title":"Artesunate Suppositories for the Treatment of HIV-negative Patients With Intra-anal HSIL","sponsor":"Frantz Viral Therapeutics, LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-28","enrollment":17,"base":0.18,"researched":null,"learned":0.3398370689864592,"rationale":"This is a tiny phase II trial (17 enrolled, 2:1 randomization, roughly 11 artesunate vs 6 placebo) from a small sponsor, and it appears designed for descriptive estimation rather than a powered hypothesis test. Earlier open-label artesunate studies in cervical and anal HSIL reported regression rates of about 60%, but spontaneous regression of HSIL in HIV-negative patients can reach 20–30%. Reaching a two-sided p<0.05 with six controls would need a near-total contrast, such as 9/11 vs 0/6. Even if the drug works, a formally significant result on the primary endpoint is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"634bcc63c910406314bdf66760a69f5dade1f666dd33503196083994cf6cd2e5"},{"nct":"NCT06157827","title":"A Clinical Trial of LBL-024 Combined With Etoposide and Platinum in Patients With Advanced Neuroendocrine Carcinoma","sponsor":"Nanjing Leads Biolabs Co.,Ltd","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-28","enrollment":178,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.37810679933170765,"rationale":"LBL-024 is a PD-L1/4-1BB bispecific that has shown encouraging single-arm activity in extrapulmonary neuroendocrine carcinoma. Early combination data with etoposide-platinum in first-line NEC reportedly gave high response rates, and the sponsor has moved toward pivotal development. However, this is an open-label phase Ib/II whose first-listed efficacy endpoint (ORR) may be analysed only descriptively, and any formal comparison against an active atezolizumab-plus-EP control would be underpowered in a small randomized subset. The probability of a statistically significant ORR advantage being reported is therefore uncertain, near even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8e6387eb6c8b8f74db486b08ab734530a24af3c0dcacc9378dd78574f1f44e99"},{"nct":"NCT07645248","title":"A Study to Compare Safety of 4 Weeks Exposure to Propellants Hydrofluoroalkane 1,1-difluoroethane (HFA-152a) and HFA-1,1,1,2-tetrafluoroethane (134a)","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-28","enrollment":110,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.7831020256037491,"rationale":"This is a descriptive safety crossover study of the low-global-warming propellant HFA-152a against the HFA-134a it replaces, likely in a salbutamol MDI. The primary outcome is AE counts, with no stated hypothesis test, so a statistically significant result in favor of HFA-152a is very unlikely; success depends on whether 'comparable safety' would be read as meeting the endpoint. Earlier GSK and AstraZeneca HFA-152a programs showed safety and tolerability similar to HFA-134a, so a reassuring topline is likely. Ambiguity about how a descriptive endpoint resolves keeps the probability moderate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"204be4c3451e7cf87fd492a03a6ac4f9ce468b26d12d0d30a579b88061647f1b"},{"nct":"NCT07477704","title":"A Study to See How Safe and Effective Alirocumab is When Given Weekly to Adult Participants Who Have Hypercholesterolemia","sponsor":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-29","enrollment":438,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.9289376216663463,"rationale":"Alirocumab is an approved PCSK9 antibody that reliably lowers LDL-C by about 45-60%, so weekly dosing of an adequate dose will almost certainly produce large LDL-C reductions from baseline. However, the control arm is itself alirocumab (likely the approved regimen), and the open-label dose-ranging design suggests the goal is dose selection or showing comparability, possibly for co-formulation with obesity drugs, rather than superiority. If success is judged as within-arm LDL-C reduction or comparable efficacy, it is near-certain. Formal superiority over an active alirocumab control is unlikely, so I discount for how the outcome will be adjudicated.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a7e745bea258cb9595268d8cc9677ad412f7819a48815294593164f252bd9026"},{"nct":"NCT03592472","title":"A Study of Pazopanib With or Without Abexinostat in Patients With Locally Advanced or Metastatic Renal Cell Carcinoma (RENAVIV)","sponsor":"Xynomic Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":413,"base":0.18,"researched":null,"learned":0.6047225724416481,"rationale":"HDAC inhibitors added to standard therapy have almost always failed in solid-tumor phase 3 trials, and the support here is only a small single-arm phase 1b showing durable responses with pazopanib. The sponsor, Xynomic, is small and financially strained, and the trial has recruited slowly since 2018. It is still recruiting with a projected 2026 completion, so it may be underpowered or never finish. The PFS endpoint against a pazopanib control gives some chance of a modest positive effect, but added toxicity and dose reductions could erode the benefit.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"53c10c170f0ad95dc3a148cbd6c27d9b49ef5a733fab9676615bcf449acaaae5"},{"nct":"NCT04588922","title":"Study of SLS009 (Formerly GFH009) a Potent Highly Selective CDK9 Inhibitor in Patients With Hematologic Malignancies and High-Risk Newly Diagnosed AML","sponsor":"Sellas Life Sciences Group","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":160,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.5363821537520609,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is DLT incidence in a Phase I/IIa trial with no formal hypothesis test, so 'success' will likely be judged by whether the sponsor reports tolerability and encouraging activity. Sellas has already publicized favorable interim data for SLS009 plus venetoclax/azacitidine in venetoclax-refractory AML, including ORRs of roughly 30–40% and higher in ASXL1/MR cohorts, with manageable safety. The randomized newly diagnosed Group 4 is small and unlikely to show a statistically significant ORR difference over active ven/aza, which adds downside if the result is judged on that comparison. Balancing a likely positive sponsor framing against the ambiguous endpoint and the small randomized cohort, I estimate a moderate probability of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f240e74d70b6b1157bfff4cd7a4acdcf5ff9552d152796b24d1e01a0217039f4"},{"nct":"NCT04658862","title":"A Study of TAR-200 in Combination With Cetrelimab Versus Concurrent Chemoradiotherapy in Participants With Muscle-invasive Bladder Cancer (MIBC) of the Bladder","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":518,"base":0.03,"researched":null,"learned":0.6726702817770486,"rationale":"This is SunRISe-2. As I recall, in 2024 Johnson & Johnson stopped the trial after a planned interim analysis, when the independent data monitoring committee concluded that TAR-200 plus cetrelimab was unlikely to beat concurrent chemoradiotherapy on bladder-intact event-free survival. Even without that, beating chemoradiotherapy, an established bladder-sparing standard, with an open-label superiority design would have been a hard bar. Because the futility stop appears to be public, the probability of meeting the primary endpoint is very low.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"c8c03b9b0fe840a9754fb4469ae1d79f252163fc22ca6d992d8f8324a0252b0c"},{"nct":"NCT05486104","title":"Phase II Study of Hemay005 in Patients With Active Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Ganzhou Hemay Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":92,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.5105279765321327,"rationale":"Hemay005 (mufemilast) is an oral PDE4 inhibitor similar to apremilast, which met its Phase 2 UC remission endpoint (about 32% vs 12% placebo at week 12 in roughly 170 patients), so the mechanism has proof of concept. This trial is much smaller, with about 30 patients per arm. Significance would need something like a 30–35% vs 10% remission gap, which is plausible but well short of assured power. Base rates for Phase 2 UC and the unreplicated efficacy of this specific compound in UC argue for a below-even estimate, offset somewhat by two dose arms giving two chances.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b6d8c9b0ce11ba8506e8a3915d85b35241df2dbde2c3c925a2cf7dcf472ed61b"},{"nct":"NCT05563844","title":"Study of Purinostat Mesylate for Injection in the Treatment of Relapsed or Refractory Diffuse Large B-cell Lymphoma (R/R DLBCL)","sponsor":"Chengdu Zenitar Biomedical Technology Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":74,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.32281674051080816,"rationale":"This is a small open-label phase II in China that randomizes patients between two doses of a new class I/IIb HDAC inhibitor, with no control arm. Success therefore depends on ORR clearing a prespecified historical threshold, which tends to favour sponsor-declared success. Purinostat has reportedly shown encouraging early activity in R/R DLBCL and received Chinese breakthrough designation. However, HDAC inhibitors have historically produced only modest single-agent response rates in DLBCL, and the sample per arm is small, so the probability is set moderately above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6c08dcaa9a7a22cdd6e1e8017aeaacf9192373da9dc8293e9ec5fe44dac42ff9"},{"nct":"NCT05631262","title":"SKB264 Monotherapy in Selected Subjects With Advanced Solid Tumors","sponsor":"Sichuan Kelun-Biotech Biopharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":321,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.39756160765932164,"rationale":"Part II of this study appears to match OptiTROP-Lung03: sacituzumab tirumotecan (SKB264) versus docetaxel in EGFR-mutant NSCLC after failure of EGFR-TKI and platinum chemotherapy. As I recall, the reported ORR was about 45% versus 16%, with significantly longer PFS, and it supported Chinese approval in this setting. Even without that, TROP2 ADCs consistently give much higher response rates than docetaxel (roughly 10–15% ORR) in pretreated EGFR-mutant disease, so an ORR comparison is a low bar. The main residual uncertainties are whether my match of this registration to that trial is correct and how the multi-cohort primary endpoint is formally scored.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"f65e75a66aec3585818bd490c20eb911e30d4814952bf0531e8b296f894284b0"},{"nct":"NCT05909397","title":"Vepdegestrant (ARV-471/PF-07850327) + Palbociclib vs Letrozole + Palbociclib in ER(+)/HER2(-) Advanced Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":59,"base":0.04,"researched":null,"learned":0.7053716601434127,"rationale":"Enrollment is actual at 59, which matches only the ~50-patient study lead-in. Pfizer and Arvinas deprioritized the first-line palbociclib combination and did not proceed with the 1,130-patient randomized Phase 3 portion, so the PFS superiority comparison against letrozole plus palbociclib will never be run. The first-listed primary outcome (SLI Grade 4 neutropenia incidence across two palbociclib doses) is descriptive and has no prespecified efficacy comparison favoring an investigational arm. A topline 'met primary endpoint' result is therefore very unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9b7cc6711b26939745f565a7cb65c4116cc345392790d7356bf8d0ec9f38fe75"},{"nct":"NCT06194734","title":"A Study of KC1036 Versus Investigator's Choice of Chemotherapy in Patients With Advanced Esophageal Cancer","sponsor":"Beijing Konruns Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":490,"base":0.38,"researched":null,"learned":0.6379110383131771,"rationale":"KC1036 is a multi-target oral TKI (VEGFR/AXL-type) with encouraging phase 2 single-arm activity in pretreated ESCC, but it is being tested against active chemotherapy, not placebo, with an overall survival primary endpoint. Antiangiogenic TKIs in ESCC have a mixed record: anlotinib improved PFS but not OS versus placebo (ALTER1102). Beating irinotecan, docetaxel or S-1 on OS is a harder bar. Chinese single-sponsor phase 3s with ~490 patients do succeed fairly often, and no results appear to be public, so I put the chance somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"84d65854022a89e8a458e99e11109a4c492a3404ad11aff211ae6f2c0ec4a574"},{"nct":"NCT06206733","title":"ASKB589 in Combination With CAPOX and PD-1 Inhibitor in Patients With Advanced or Metastatic GC/GEJ Adenocarcinoma","sponsor":"AskGene Pharma, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":780,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.6061511268922946,"rationale":"ASKB589 is an anti-CLDN18.2 monoclonal antibody, a mechanism validated by zolbetuximab, which significantly improved PFS when added to chemotherapy in SPOTLIGHT and GLOW (HR ~0.69–0.75). ASKB589's own phase 2 data with CAPOX plus a PD-1 inhibitor showed high response rates. The added benefit on top of chemo-immunotherapy is unproven and may be smaller, and a possibly broader CLDN18.2 positivity cutoff could dilute the effect. Still, a large 780-patient trial with an IRC-assessed PFS endpoint gives reasonable power, so the odds of success are modestly better than even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0356e6a092e3d5bdbf7a4bb61944828134181bbf47b7a92bfa4cc4a8785c3e58"},{"nct":"NCT06238843","title":"A Multicenter, Phase 3 Study of IBI343 Monotherapy Versus Treatment of Investigator's Choice in Subjects With Previously Treated, Claudin (CLDN) 18.2-positive, HER2-negative, Gastric or Gastroesophageal Junction Adenocarcinoma (G-HOPE-001)","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":464,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.6184031095980356,"rationale":"IBI343 is a CLDN18.2-directed exatecan ADC. In phase 1 it showed roughly 28% ORR and about 5.5 months median PFS in heavily pretreated CLDN18.2-positive gastric cancer, versus roughly 2–3 months PFS expected with irinotecan, paclitaxel or FTD/TPI in third line. With PFS as the first primary endpoint, an open-label design, 464 patients and a weak chemotherapy comparator, success is likely; similar topoisomerase-ADC trials (e.g., T-DXd in DESTINY-Gastric) have beaten chemo in later lines. The main risks are a small or overstated effect from early single-arm data, toxicity, and variability in CLDN18.2 selection, so I stay below 85%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cf9d52a56c67f7183f242279b461eca6f1241450b987171a624fc27dd2c6b4f7"},{"nct":"NCT06388941","title":"Iptacopan in Patients With ANCA Associated Vasculitis","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":84,"base":0.22,"researched":null,"learned":0.4149781933401549,"rationale":"Complement factor B inhibition is mechanistically plausible in AAV, given the alternative pathway and C5a axis that avacopan validated. However, in ADVOCATE (n=331) avacopan improved week-52 sustained remission by only about 11 percentage points (65.7% vs 54.9%). This 84-patient phase 2 trial adds iptacopan on top of rituximab-based standard of care, and with about 42 per arm it is underpowered to show a modest sustained-remission difference at conventional significance. Unless the effect is much larger than avacopan's or the trial uses a lenient alpha, a statistically significant primary result looks unlikely, though positive trends are possible.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0d2cdf2818fae318922d755086b74453f71693350c0b3947f92f3d9680b5a266"},{"nct":"NCT06447597","title":"A Clinical Study of B007 in the Treatment of Generalized Myasthenia Gravis.","sponsor":"Shanghai Jiaolian Drug Research and Development Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":104,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.7676568212341944,"rationale":"B007 appears to be a subcutaneous B-cell–targeting antibody given on days 1 and 15. That class has mixed results in gMG: BeatMG with rituximab failed, while RINOMAX and inebilizumab's MINT trial succeeded, though only modestly and with slow onset. The primary endpoint is an MG-ADL ≥2-point responder rate at about 16 weeks, where placebo responses are often 30–40%; with about 104 patients possibly split across two doses, power to detect a modest early B-cell-depletion effect is limited. Chinese industry-run phase II/III trials in MG often report positive results, which partly offsets this, so I put the chance of success near even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0881026b8efb3b8871496047ca26fcc590b27e6d6498039736e4264ca928bc8b"},{"nct":"NCT06465563","title":"SHR-8068 in Combination With Adebrelimab, Bevacizumab, and Platinum-Based Chemotherapy as First-line Treatment in Patients With Advanced Biliary Tract Cancer","sponsor":"Suzhou Suncadia Biopharmaceuticals Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":93,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.33326096006577943,"rationale":"SHR-8068 is Hengrui's anti-CTLA-4 antibody, and here it is added to adebrelimab plus gemcitabine-cisplatin in a small open-label Chinese phase II with about 30 patients per randomized arm, ORR as the primary endpoint and cohort C single-arm. Earlier data from adding a CTLA-4 antibody to PD-L1 plus chemotherapy in biliary cancer showed at most modest ORR gains (durvalumab with or without tremelimumab plus gem-cis gave broadly similar results), and the comparator ORR is already about 25-30%. With arms this small, a statistically significant ORR difference is unlikely unless the effect is very large, and the trial may not even be powered for a formal comparison. I'm not aware of any reported results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ea36b713f393575663f2776c09d85c0c1ae92cac0bb006faa09d0c16be59ef20"},{"nct":"NCT06547151","title":"Evaluating the Safety and Efficacy of AMOR-1 as a Treatment for Hypocalcemia Associated With Hypoparathyroidism in Adults","sponsor":"Amorphical Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":62,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.5674374590471859,"rationale":"The composite endpoint requires at least a 50% cut in calcium dose, which the control arm keeps at its full dose by design, so the control response rate should be near zero. Even a modest AMOR-1 response rate of about 25–30% in roughly 41 patients would likely reach significance. The main risk is that amorphous calcium carbonate's claimed doubling of bioavailability (from animal and small pilot human data) does not hold up. In that case many patients would fall below 8.0 mg/dL or need more active vitamin D, and the sponsor's analysis might not be a straightforward comparison against control.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2a9a9db24f151cc9a2b7913c2b4ca8b451a59515bddbcdb05f46fd32eefefa92"},{"nct":"NCT06559306","title":"Phase 3 Study of Adjunctive Treatment With Seltorexant in Adult and Elderly Participants With Major Depressive Disorder and Insomnia Symptoms","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":752,"base":0.58,"researched":null,"learned":0.5979631388732048,"rationale":"Seltorexant 20 mg adjunctive to SSRI/SNRI in MDD with insomnia symptoms already succeeded in a phase 2b trial and in the phase 3 MDD3001 study. MDD3001 used the same 6-week MADRS primary endpoint, met it with a roughly 2.5-point drug–placebo difference, and enrolled a similar population. With about 750 participants in Part 1 this trial is reasonably powered for that effect, but adjunctive depression trials often fail because of high placebo response, multinational site variability and small effect sizes. I therefore put it moderately above a coin flip; I do not recall the topline result being public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f12e492df1b209705ff215ed843fc819ab21f83ea2f459758183e578e6f157ec"},{"nct":"NCT06577519","title":"Efficacy and Safety Study of Vicagrel in Patients With Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS) Undergoing Percutaneous Coronary Intervention (PCI)","sponsor":"Jiangsu vcare pharmaceutical technology co., LTD","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":1000,"base":0.77,"researched":null,"learned":0.5743407612015337,"rationale":"Vicagrel is a close structural analog of clopidogrel that needs less CYP2C19-dependent activation, and earlier PK/PD work showed comparable or better platelet inhibition. With 1,000 patients and a 6-month MACE endpoint, the trial cannot be powered for superiority, so it is almost certainly a non-inferiority registration study for Chinese approval. Near-copy non-inferiority trials with low event rates usually meet their margin. Remaining risks are execution problems (a single listed site, still recruiting near the planned completion date), an unknown margin, and possible ambiguity in how success is defined.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"292f810f25a2a0f8ebb8293e5b7ffc28a421797b7b599cb4acf2ba42b8185c12"},{"nct":"NCT06646055","title":"AK112 and Cadonilimab Combined With Chemotherapy for 1L Treatment of Metastatic Pancreatic Cancer","sponsor":"Akeso","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":110,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.457935135084592,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is phase Ib safety, and the efficacy primary is ORR in a small, open-label randomized phase II of roughly 25–35 patients per arm against gemcitabine/nab-paclitaxel, whose ORR is typically about 25–35%. Early Akeso data for ivonescimab plus cadonilimab plus chemotherapy in PDAC reportedly showed high response rates, and a sponsor-run open-label trial with an ORR endpoint favors a positive-looking readout. However, the design looks descriptive rather than powered for a formal comparison, and with small arms even a 20-point ORR gain may not reach p<0.05. PD-1/VEGF and CTLA-4 strategies also have a poor record in pancreatic cancer.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"777ff46025a9bae67ea9b183a231c51a8a5364d54dbc1353e60910f91a2f7f7b"},{"nct":"NCT06799247","title":"Investigating an mRNA CAR T-cell Therapy, Known as Descartes-08, as a Potential Approach to Treat Myasthenia Gravis","sponsor":"Cartesian Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":128,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.6108364471007932,"rationale":"In its small Phase 2b, Descartes-08 gave higher MG composite and MG-ADL responder rates than placebo (roughly 71% vs 25% on MGC in the efficacy population). That trial was small, with uncertain effect size, wide confidence intervals and heterogeneity. AURORA is larger (n=128), restricted to AChR+ patients, and uses MG-ADL responders at Month 4, where placebo responses in gMG trials are often 30–45%. A shrunken but real effect (e.g., 55–60% vs 35–40%) would give only moderate power, so I put the odds slightly better than a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e3d3ad2eb096a8080f766ae8738ce5418e792dda523916c889042aea7e1cac9d"},{"nct":"NCT06832722","title":"A Phase 1b/2a Trial to Evaluate Invobenitug Also Known as Procizumab (PCZ; AK1967) in Critical Cardiovascular Care.","sponsor":"4TEEN4 Pharmaceuticals GmbH","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":90,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.38499868842483864,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is the number of treatment-emergent adverse events, a descriptive safety endpoint with no prespecified efficacy comparison. 'Success' therefore most likely means the sponsor declaring invobenitug safe and well tolerated, which is plausible given earlier experience with DPP3 antibodies. Against that, adverse events are near-universal in cardiogenic shock, so a significant difference favoring the drug is very unlikely. The trial is still recruiting, no results are public, and the scoring interpretation is ambiguous, so I place the forecast near 50%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c106699a5509c900e5b4fe48c34fecc916c6782664d6d2fd6a8af24af2a1352d"},{"nct":"NCT07106892","title":"Phase II, Open-label, Multicenter Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of HLX43 (an Anti-PD-L1 ADC) in Subjects With Advanced Colorectal Cancer","sponsor":"Shanghai Henlius Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":60,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.43506313158444704,"rationale":"This is a small, open-label, dose-finding Phase II with three HLX43 dose arms, no control arm and no prespecified hypothesis test, so 'success' would rest on whether IRRC-assessed ORR looks clinically meaningful. HLX43 has shown encouraging responses in NSCLC, particularly squamous, but previously treated microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer responds poorly to both PD-L1-directed and non-HER2-targeted topo-I ADC approaches, with ORRs often in the single digits to low teens. A modest ORR that the sponsor may not frame as positive seems the most likely outcome, and I am not aware of any published result from this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0ef91ee6d4dc9ef9b3ff7d4809df6091f876e1ffdff0af9db17b5780a9793bdc"},{"nct":"NCT07118241","title":"A PHASE II PROSPECTIVE RANDOMIZED DOUBLE-MASKED CONTROLLED STUDY ASSESSING THE SAFETY & EFFICACY OF RHPRG4 (450 µG/ML RECOMBINANT HUMAN PROTEOGLYCAN 4) COMPARED TO VEHICLE FOR THE TREATMENT OF SJÖGREN'S RELATED DRY EYE DISEASE","sponsor":"Lubris Bio Pty Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":80,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.28727680035736586,"rationale":"rhPRG4 (lubricin) showed signal-level benefits in earlier small dry eye studies, and the endpoint of complete clearance of corneal staining from a mild baseline (Oxford 1–2) was likely chosen from prior data, which modestly helps. Still, this is a small trial (about 40 per arm) with a binary responder endpoint at only 28 days. A PBS vehicle often produces substantial staining improvement on its own, and dry eye trials frequently fail on sign endpoints. Given the low base rate for phase 2 dry eye trials and limited power, success is less likely than not.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a6579ee4e9ff592cfd691508e50e015ce40231befeba48b7806262f1fc48b20b"},{"nct":"NCT07214571","title":"A Study of S-337395 in Symptomatic Nonhospitalized Adults With Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) Who Are at High Risk of Progression to Severe Disease","sponsor":"Shionogi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":192,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.41236164480113346,"rationale":"S-337395 is Shionogi's oral RSV L-polymerase inhibitor, and in a human challenge study it cut viral load AUC substantially. That supports a real antiviral effect, and the primary endpoint is virologic rather than clinical, which is easier to hit. However, outpatient adults treated up to 72 hours after symptom onset often have falling viral loads, which dilutes drug–placebo differences. For example, Enanta's zelicapavir showed only modest virologic effects in high-risk adults. The first-listed Day 2 timepoint may also show a smaller separation than later days, so with about 64 patients per arm and two doses, I estimate a moderately better-than-even chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d6fdb5a90c90207087caf306a9b6dd3b427965b71870240e8f8031ac51532ca5"},{"nct":"NCT07388680","title":"Pirfenidone Capsules in the Treatment of Radiation-induced Lung Injury With or Without Immune Pneumonia","sponsor":"Beijing Continent Pharmaceutical Co, Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-30","enrollment":298,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.7654862600637752,"rationale":"Pirfenidone is an established antifibrotic, and small Chinese studies suggest benefit in radiation pneumonitis, so the mechanism is plausible. The sponsor makes the pirfenidone product being tested, and Chinese industry trials often report positive results. However, the phase II stage randomizes only about 30 patients per arm, and 24-week DLCO change is noisy in a population that often partly recovers on steroids alone, so power to show a significant difference is limited. Overall this sits near the phase II/III base rate, slightly below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"54708a05b35d6c46c764114f78e8ef264b7fd9689ddfb86663381b9804acc293"},{"nct":"NCT01297400","title":"Phase 2 Pilot Study of the Safety and Efficacy of Topical MW-III in Thermal Burns","sponsor":"Skingenix, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":60,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3332081561496967,"rationale":"This is a small (n=60), open-label phase 2 pilot from a tiny sponsor (Skingenix, registered in 2011 and still recruiting in 2026), comparing an uncharacterized topical agent against active silver sulfadiazine on time to healing. Pilot studies of this size are rarely powered to show a statistically significant superiority difference, and the long, troubled history suggests recruitment and operational difficulties. Silver sulfadiazine is known to slow re-epithelialization somewhat, which gives a modest chance of a favorable signal, but formal significance on the primary endpoint is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"442772e796618c0d03fd13014ab5d96ae46568a0d701c3dcdf4876681b97ff3c"},{"nct":"NCT03383081","title":"The Safety/Efficacy of hUC Mesenchymal Stem Cells（19#iSCLife®-OA） Therapy for Patients With Osteoarthritis","sponsor":"Sclnow Biotechnology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":60,"base":0.1,"researched":null,"learned":0.28636983219549783,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is change in Kellgren-Lawrence grade at 12 months. KL is a coarse 0–4 ordinal structural scale that rarely improves in any OA trial, so a significant between-arm difference with about 20 patients per arm is very unlikely, even open-label. Prior UC-MSC knee OA trials have sometimes shown symptomatic (VAS/WOMAC) benefit but almost never radiographic KL improvement. The trial is a small single-site study by a small Chinese company, still 'recruiting' with completion pushed to end-2026 after starting in 2018, which suggests operational trouble and makes a clean positive readout on this endpoint improbable.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6c92515f693610adb7143d071091826f27b6741e543370b148ee39fa43893248"},{"nct":"NCT03887455","title":"A Study to Confirm Safety and Efficacy of Lecanemab in Participants With Early Alzheimer's Disease","sponsor":"Eisai Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":1906,"base":0.99,"researched":null,"learned":0.6733341300613136,"rationale":"This is Clarity AD, the Phase 3 trial of lecanemab in early Alzheimer's disease. Topline results were announced in September 2022 and published in NEJM (van Dyck et al., 2023). The core study met its primary endpoint, with a 27% slowing of CDR-SB decline at 18 months (difference -0.45, p<0.001), and these data supported full FDA approval. The registered primary completion date reflects the ongoing extension phase, but the first-listed core-study primary endpoint was clearly met.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"23b468a8a51733646b76fc8e7a9864f2df6d97fed7a7669622717ad6e8539a26"},{"nct":"NCT03994471","title":"Efficacy and Safety of XyloCore Peritoneal Dialysis Solution.","sponsor":"Iperboreal Pharma Srl","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":170,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.7417455218584058,"rationale":"This is the ELIXIR trial, and its primary endpoint of total weekly Kt/V is almost certainly a non-inferiority comparison against standard glucose solutions; Kt/V depends mainly on dwell volume and residual renal function, not the osmotic agent. A pilot study of XyloCore reported comparable small-solute clearance and ultrafiltration, and investigators can adjust prescriptions in both arms to hold Kt/V above 1.7, which makes non-inferiority easier to show. The main risks are slow recruitment (still recruiting near the planned primary completion date), which could leave the study underpowered, and possible differences in ultrafiltration or residual function affecting total Kt/V.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dd9dd1474478c0a620381540ae08296b9ff11f0127293d41edf0213c68314f6a"},{"nct":"NCT04318041","title":"Evaluation of the Structural Modification Effect of Diacerein (Artrodar®) in Knee Osteoarthritic Patients","sponsor":"TRB Chemedica","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":128,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.5413596262783787,"rationale":"Disease-modifying drug trials in knee osteoarthritis almost always fail on structural endpoints. Diacerein's structural evidence is weak: it slowed joint-space narrowing in the hip (ECHODIAH), but knee data are inconsistent and modest. With about 64 patients per arm at a single site, detecting a between-group difference in two-year MRI cartilage volume loss, which is small and variable, is underpowered unless the effect is large. Small, sponsor-run single-country trials sometimes report positive results, which nudges the estimate slightly above a pure base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9881bcbffc1f039c136df80795727eb82d96ed3e01d9818bd472e98ff820009e"},{"nct":"NCT04691804","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Phase III Study of Fuzuloparib Combined With Abiraterone Acetate and Prednisone (AA-P) Versus Placebo Combined With AA-P as First-Line Treatment in Patients With Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":496,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6741937523165041,"rationale":"Two PARP inhibitor-plus-ARPI combinations met rPFS in unselected first-line mCRPC: PROpel (olaparib + abiraterone, HR ~0.66) and TALAPRO-2 (talazoparib + enzalutamide). MAGNITUDE (niraparib + abiraterone) succeeded only in HRR-positive patients and was futile in the HRR-negative cohort. This trial, with about 496 patients, a BICR-assessed rPFS endpoint and DRD-positive patients enriching the all-comer cohort, should be adequately powered for an effect like PROpel's. The remaining risks are the MAGNITUDE-like negative signal in non-DRD patients, the dose limits of combining with fuzuloparib, and uncertainty in the global execution. I am not aware of a topline announcement.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"52b3b6ace7bd672244f2752ac7f6cc8d5b595c323fe424c92cba87e567adb769"},{"nct":"NCT04977024","title":"SARS-CoV-2 Vaccine (GEO-CM04S1) Versus mRNA SARS-COV-2 Vaccine in Patients With Blood Cancer","sponsor":"GeoVax, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":63,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.3916808378590719,"rationale":"This is a small (n=63) randomized phase 2 comparing GeoVax's synthetic MVA vaccine against an active, effective comparator, mRNA vaccine, in post-HCT/CAR-T patients. The composite responder endpoint (≥3-fold rise in neutralizing antibodies or IFN-γ) will likely be met by a high fraction of both arms, which makes a statistically significant superiority difference hard to show even with a one-sided test. GeoVax's public interim updates have described robust or comparable responses, especially T-cell responses, rather than clear superiority on the primary composite. Given the active control and small sample, success on the formal comparison looks unlikely, though a sponsor-favorable framing is possible.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ed4220de8282cd184d229160a883dd1807742ec8869b8709c16511104aef45e0"},{"nct":"NCT05198323","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of LT3001 Drug Product in Subjects AIS Undergoing EVT","sponsor":"Lumosa Therapeutics Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":66,"base":0.52,"researched":null,"learned":0.2599724319470188,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety endpoint (sICH within 24 hours), and in a 66-patient trial a statistically significant reduction versus placebo is essentially unachievable. Whether this counts as \"met\" therefore depends on whether a low or zero sICH rate is framed as success, which Lumosa did with its earlier LT3001 Phase 2a stroke trial. This small two-site study is still not recruiting toward a late-2026 completion, and I am not aware of any public topline. Balancing a likely favorable safety readout against the strict-significance interpretation, I land near even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9673638ea3b4e89ef15e7c6d3c5f2193cc4a3ece8946b9729baf1de2a1ff4cbf"},{"nct":"NCT05302284","title":"A Study of RC48-ADC Combined With Toripalimab For First-line Treatment of Urothelial Carcinoma","sponsor":"RemeGen Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":452,"base":0.96,"researched":null,"learned":0.6895257640526679,"rationale":"This is RC48-C016, a Chinese phase 3 of disitamab vedotin plus toripalimab versus gemcitabine-platinum in HER2-expressing first-line metastatic urothelial carcinoma. My recollection is that RemeGen announced in 2025 that the trial met both PFS and OS at interim analysis, with data presented at ESMO 2025 (PFS HR about 0.36, OS HR about 0.54). The analogous EV-302 result (ADC plus PD-1 versus chemotherapy) and strong phase 2 activity of this combination make success highly plausible even without that memory. Residual uncertainty reflects possible errors in my recall.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"7c79bef0a8d27d43ad6b4e4c5442ca669d1f0442170cec81089dc4885f13ebe8"},{"nct":"NCT05413655","title":"A Study of Oral EX039 in Subjects with Mild Alzheimer's Disease","sponsor":"Excelsior","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":120,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.1606688131132463,"rationale":"EX039 is a little-known oral compound from a small Taiwanese sponsor, tested as an add-on to acetylcholinesterase inhibitors in a single-site, roughly 40-per-arm phase 2 with a 28-week ADAS-Cog primary endpoint. Phase 2 Alzheimer's symptomatic add-on trials have a very low success rate. Over 28 weeks placebo decline on ADAS-Cog is small, so this sample size is underpowered for plausible effects. The trial is still recruiting late into its planned timeline, results may not be reported cleanly, and a chance positive in one dose arm is the main route to success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"376e1cf34a21f1b36920449e28982a54a4aa079c0e07753f53b7435cdc8036d7"},{"nct":"NCT05424835","title":"A Trial of SHR-A1811versus Pyrotinib in Combination With Capecitabine in HER2-Positive, Unresectable and/or Metastatic Breast Cancer Subjects Previously Treated With Trastuzumab and Taxane","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":381,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.6843171803636152,"rationale":"SHR-A1811 (trastuzumab rezetecan) is a HER2-targeted topoisomerase-I ADC closely analogous to T-DXd, which beat T-DM1 by a large margin in second-line HER2+ MBC (DESTINY-Breast03). Pyrotinib plus capecitabine is a strong comparator (PHOEBE median PFS ~12.5 months), but early-phase SHR-A1811 data showed high ORR and long PFS in pretreated HER2+ disease. An open-label design with a BIRC-assessed PFS primary endpoint and ~381 patients gives ample power for a T-DXd-like effect. I believe Hengrui has publicly reported that this trial met its PFS endpoint, supporting a regulatory filing, though I hold that recollection with only moderate confidence.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"cdc1b4b4f5f48394d4c3f3ff33c2f3a989c17e1cd3ab318ec8e8b089eca7541a"},{"nct":"NCT05456425","title":"A Clinical Trial on Safety and Efficacy of CBT-001 in Patients With Pterygium","sponsor":"Cloudbreak Therapeutics, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":660,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.7495271599430403,"rationale":"CBT-001 is a topical nintedanib-type multikinase inhibitor, and its Phase 2 trial reportedly showed significant reductions in both conjunctival hyperemia and pterygium lesion vascularity/length versus vehicle. The first-listed primary endpoint, change in hyperemia at 3 months, is a short-term, pharmacologically plausible anti-angiogenic effect. With two doses and about 220 per arm, the trial is reasonably powered. Risks include a high vehicle response on a subjective grading scale, heterogeneity across multinational sites, and the generally modest Phase 3 success rates in ophthalmology; I am not aware of a public topline result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e0ecd0643190ff17a40482d4bc1c94f92190c62aebf7b5c1e1da6dd3be62f730"},{"nct":"NCT05464784","title":"MN-001 in Non-alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease, Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, and Hypertriglyceridemia","sponsor":"MediciNova","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":40,"base":0.18,"researched":null,"learned":0.690483071513679,"rationale":"MN-001 (tipelukast) earlier showed triglyceride reductions only in small open-label, uncontrolled studies, and its effect on liver fat has not been validated in a controlled trial. The first-listed primary endpoint, change in CAP score, is noisy and responds to placebo and lifestyle effects. With about 20 patients per arm across 2 sites, the trial is likely underpowered for anything short of a large effect. The base rate for small phase 2 trials of a modestly active repurposed compound in NAFLD is low, so a statistically significant win on CAP versus placebo appears unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8467447e59b6f50d0c6c51cbdde037bde13813d56f09c15ed4fbfe48b79445ad"},{"nct":"NCT05645692","title":"A Study Evaluating Different Immunotherapies (LAG-3 and PD-1 With or Without TIGIT, Compared to PD-L1 Alone) in Participants With Untreated Locally Advanced Metastatic Urothelial Cancer","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":204,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.24605789795662256,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is incidence and severity of adverse events, a descriptive safety measure with no prespecified superiority test, so a statistically significant result favoring the investigational arms is unlikely. Tobemstomig (PD-1/LAG-3 bispecific) plus tiragolumab is expected to cause at least as many adverse events as atezolizumab alone. Tiragolumab failed across several Phase 3 trials and Roche has deprioritized both drugs, so there is little reason to expect a favorable efficacy or safety signal either. The only meaningful upside is that a sponsor might describe an acceptable safety profile as having met the endpoint, so I put the probability at about 20%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5b0521f5dce8dd987a87df4109ed14ee1eb2c3349252de48d9fb98c17225a869"},{"nct":"NCT05658575","title":"Study of Dapansutrile Tablets in Subjects With an Acute Gout Flare","sponsor":"Olatec Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":300,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.7527928880380158,"rationale":"IL-1β blockade is validated in acute gout (canakinumab, anakinra), and dapansutrile's small open-label phase 2a showed meaningful pain reduction, so the NLRP3 mechanism is biologically plausible. Rescue medication is barred until after the Day 4 (72-hour) assessment, which should widen any drug–placebo gap, and 300 patients randomized 2:1 gives reasonable power for a roughly 10 mm VAS difference. Against that, placebo response in self-limiting gout flares is large, there are no prior randomized controlled data for this drug, and slow enrollment by a small sponsor adds uncertainty about dose, exposure and trial execution. I put the chance of success near a coin flip, slightly favoring success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"588c9954f2d8c279df6901058803c581e82fb6dce58996f6c75c042a89a02b3a"},{"nct":"NCT05672576","title":"A Research Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Cenerimod in Subjects Suffering From Systemic Lupus Erythematosus","sponsor":"Viatris Innovation GmbH","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":451,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.640488002644543,"rationale":"Cenerimod's phase 2b CARE study missed its primary endpoint for the 4 mg dose after multiplicity adjustment, and the efficacy signals came mainly from post hoc subgroups such as high interferon signature and mucocutaneous/musculoskeletal disease. This phase 3 enriches for those features, but that rationale is post hoc. SLE phase 3 programs fail often, and SRI-4 at 12 months on top of background therapy usually carries a high placebo response. No other S1P modulator has proven efficacy in SLE. With about 420 patients the trial is reasonably powered, so I place success modestly below a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"623b40fbedb1271ebcb3386be2a3e258dbfc005adc7877a236c257a9a1ef61f0"},{"nct":"NCT05910528","title":"Afimkibart (RO7790121) for the Treatment of Moderate to Severe Active Crohn's Disease","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":21,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.3041117375412345,"rationale":"This is a small (n=21), two-dose, single-drug Phase 2 study whose first-listed primary outcome is descriptive safety (TEAE/SAE incidence), with no placebo comparator and no prespecified hypothesis test, so 'meeting the endpoint' most plausibly means reporting an acceptable safety profile. Anti-TL1A agents, including afimkibart in the TUSCANY trials and tulisokibart/duvakitug in IBD, have so far shown benign safety, and Roche has moved afimkibart into Phase 3 in IBD, which suggests no safety red flags. The main uncertainty is how an endpoint with no formal comparison will be adjudicated, which keeps the forecast well away from certainty. I am not aware of any published primary result from this specific study.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fbb9dd723a16b082cf54380adf84be26def63d890da19a250f17941eacd659ef"},{"nct":"NCT05913752","title":"A First in Human Study of CMND-100 in Healthy and Alcohol Use Disorder (AUD) Subjects","sponsor":"Clearmind Medicine Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":84,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.42985902774872675,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are safety, tolerability and PK, with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so 'meeting the primary endpoint' amounts to finding a tolerable dose and characterizing PK without prohibitive toxicity. Small first-in-human studies of this kind almost always report as successful, and Clearmind has a habit of announcing favorable interim safety updates. The main risks are unexpected toxicity from MEAI, a psychoactive aminoindane, or the study stalling or not completing, given a small sponsor and a planned completion of December 2026. I don't know of any topline result for the full study yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"07313fdfd4244a75d83f41fd1cd8b228cf880238c793191f74b702f08fef19ea"},{"nct":"NCT05944224","title":"A Study to Efficacy and Safety of SPH4336 Monotherapy or in Combination With Cadonilimab in Patients With Advanced Solid Tumors.","sponsor":"Shanghai Pharmaceuticals Holding Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":63,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.4686303832705163,"rationale":"This is a small (n=63) open-label phase Ib/IIa study randomizing among three experimental arms with no true control: the CDK4/6 inhibitor SPH4336 alone, cadonilimab alone, and the combination. PFS is likely to be analyzed descriptively rather than through a powered comparison. With about 21 patients per arm in liposarcoma, a statistically significant PFS advantage for the combination over monotherapy is unlikely, even though earlier single-arm data for SPH4336 in WD/DD liposarcoma looked encouraging. The uncertainty is mainly about whether a descriptively 'positive' readout would count as success, so I put the probability somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"628d98589f4a87ab6ca190a534602ee6aa1c37db8e3005661484fcffc81999fc"},{"nct":"NCT06052267","title":"A Study to Test if a Fixed-Dose Combination of Fluticasone Propionate/Albuterol Sulfate is Effective in Preventing Asthma Exacerbations","sponsor":"Teva Branded Pharmaceutical Products R&D LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":2769,"base":0.76,"researched":null,"learned":0.679204679358224,"rationale":"This trial tests as-needed ICS/SABA rescue, a concept already validated. In AstraZeneca's MANDALA trial, as-needed budesonide/albuterol at 160/180 cut time to first severe exacerbation by about 27% versus albuterol alone (p<0.001), while the lower dose missed significance. Here the primary comparison is the higher fluticasone propionate dose (110 mcg per use) versus albuterol, in an event-driven design of about 2,800 exacerbation-prone patients, which should give good power for a similar effect. Remaining risks are that a dry-powder inhaler used in children as young as 4 could dilute the effect, the event-driven design could under-accrue events, and fluticasone propionate may have a less favourable dose-response than budesonide, so I sit somewhat below near-certainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"750b48308771f621fe72883a38e2e60487f341e17a17850505e08db538617d04"},{"nct":"NCT06081959","title":"Study of SKB264 for Locally Advanced, Recurrent or Metastatic HR+/HER2- Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Sichuan Kelun-Biotech Biopharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":376,"base":0.97,"researched":null,"learned":0.6630792100392087,"rationale":"SKB264 (sacituzumab tirumotecan) is a TROP2 ADC, and drugs of this class have already beaten chemotherapy on PFS in pretreated HR+/HER2- breast cancer (TROPiCS-02, TROPION-Breast01). I recall that Kelun reported OptiTROP-Breast02 met its BICR-assessed PFS primary endpoint at interim analysis, with a large benefit (HR around 0.35), presented around ESMO 2025. Chinese regulatory filing or approval followed. Given the strong class precedent and the reported result, success is very likely.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"2079cf1bc4fb720b087e9f090cbaaa64da5e9bcefe4564d5f5740f4d8d7d8e61"},{"nct":"NCT06094179","title":"Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability of BAT6026","sponsor":"Bio-Thera Solutions","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":33,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.6362902462896161,"rationale":"BAT6026 is Bio-Thera's anti-OX40 antibody. Its mechanism is validated in atopic dermatitis by rocatinlimab and amlitelimab, so an efficacy signal and acceptable tolerability are plausible. However, the registered primary outcomes are purely descriptive safety measures (AEs, vital signs, ECG, labs) in a 33-patient Phase Ib with 9:3 randomization per cohort, so no powered superiority comparison exists and 'success' depends on how the safety readout is framed. Such trials are usually reported as 'well tolerated', but with no formal statistical test and a small placebo group, any efficacy comparison could easily miss significance, so I stay moderately above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8296469729427c39713ce1b7d43807dd89b93bf8fbe5997b1050ce095b4691f3"},{"nct":"NCT06104566","title":"Global Trial in APG2575 for Patients With CLL/SLL","sponsor":"Ascentage Pharma Group Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":400,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.651042444983366,"rationale":"Adding a BCL-2 inhibitor to a BTK inhibitor is biologically well validated: ibrutinib plus venetoclax deepened responses and improved PFS over ibrutinib alone in FLAIR, and lisaftoclax has shown activity and gained approval in China. The main risks are a low PFS event rate in patients already controlled on BTKi for at least 12 months, an open-label design, and a still-recruiting trial that may need long follow-up to collect enough events. The sponsor is small, but the combination-versus-backbone design generally favors success, so I place the probability moderately above the phase 3 oncology base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"23ed7e0cc26ace91ff7556dd6f1f9bc4cb83f800c309c3dda51fd451192a0641"},{"nct":"NCT06125327","title":"SC1011 Twice Daily vs Placebo in Patients Diagnosed With Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis (IPF)","sponsor":"Guangzhou JOYO Pharma Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":210,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.49923462910531624,"rationale":"Sufenidone (SC1011) appears to be a pirfenidone-like antifibrotic, and that class has validated efficacy on annual FVC decline against placebo in IPF, which supports a reasonable prior. However, roughly 100 patients per arm is modest for this noisy endpoint: pirfenidone's CAPACITY 006 failed, and nintedanib's TOMORROW (about 85 per arm) narrowly missed on FVC decline rate. The small Chinese sponsor, single listed site, seamless phase 2/3 design and stale registration add execution risk, and no results are public, so I put the chance near even, slightly below.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ed710c8dddc2223dc37f6fbe5a69ad2ca78c3aa5172c19984f8240e20cd51230"},{"nct":"NCT06138743","title":"Study of SRP-1003 in Participants With Type 1 Myotonic Dystrophy","sponsor":"Sarepta Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":78,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.555158819479962,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is a descriptive safety measure (number of participants with TEAEs) with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so 'success' will most likely be judged on whether SRP-1003 shows acceptable tolerability and the program moves forward. Phase 1/2 trials of GalNAc-like or receptor-targeted siRNA platforms (Arrowhead's TRiM, here muscle-targeted via an integrin ligand) have generally shown acceptable safety, and Sarepta kept this program after its 2025 pipeline restructuring. Residual risks are muscle-delivery toxicity at higher doses, program deprioritization, and the ambiguity of scoring a safety-only endpoint. I am not aware of a public topline readout of this trial's primary result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"242591ced95d4f4a4b58aa3e8f7c562ba040f2b390fb9d35f8720a6b50917f2b"},{"nct":"NCT06197568","title":"Proof of Concept Study of Vaginal AZU-101 in Vulvovaginal Atrophy in Postmenopausal Women","sponsor":"Azure Biotech Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":90,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.35112752118816654,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety count (SAEs or severe TEAEs) plus PK, not an efficacy comparison, so 'success' here mostly means the drug proved acceptably safe. Microgram-level vaginal lasofoxifene, an approved-elsewhere oral SERM with known vaginal benefits, is very likely to be safe over 14 days. The risk is that a safety-primary trial is scored on a placebo comparison, which would show no significant difference, or that this small sponsor's single-site trial, already delayed since 2023, never reports. That ambiguity keeps the estimate near the middle.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f37ecd21d6b4edfe8b4dd54e663033a2c854e1d60c57709269f79266b42f2e68"},{"nct":"NCT06206564","title":"Artesunate Ointment for the Treatment of Anal HSIL in HIV-negative Participants","sponsor":"Frantz Viral Therapeutics, LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":48,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.35219225894039685,"rationale":"Topical artesunate has shown encouraging histologic regression of HPV-associated HSIL in earlier work, including cervical HSIL studies and small anal HSIL phase 1 studies from the same sponsor. Even so, this is a tiny (n=48, 2:1) single-sponsor phase 2. Its primary endpoint includes partial response, which also captures spontaneous regression in the placebo arm, limiting power to detect a significant difference. The trial is still recruiting, and no results are public, so I estimate a modestly below-even chance of a statistically significant win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"24cafbff3984c6c79efbdaef29e76ade455b81f621308ae794b65ca4f9902f6c"},{"nct":"NCT06281119","title":"Clinical Study to Evaluate SIIPL qHPV Vaccine (CERVAVAC®) in Women Living With HIV Aged 15-25 Years","sponsor":"Serum Institute of India Pvt. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":450,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8729995163911437,"rationale":"The primary comparison is almost certainly a non-inferiority test of HPV16/18 GMTs one month after three doses of Cervavac versus Gardasil, the same mechanism and antigen types. Serum Institute's earlier Indian phase 2/3 trial showed Cervavac non-inferior to Gardasil, with numerically higher GMTs. Women in this trial have well-controlled HIV (CD4 above 350) and receive the same three-dose schedule as the comparator, so immune blunting should hit both arms equally. The main risks are the modest sample of 150 per arm, assay or site variability across three African countries, and some uncertainty about how success is defined, so I keep the forecast below 0.9.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d9dd1e9aa6b5848669141c7f0cda74caf69375c4b35bc44ef97ef5ca0cbfd626"},{"nct":"NCT06284265","title":"Clinical Trial of the Efficacy and Safety of Raphamin in Prevention of Recurrences of Chronic Bacterial Cystitis","sponsor":"Materia Medica Holding","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":415,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.7153225773611979,"rationale":"Raphamin is a Materia Medica Holding 'release-active' (ultra-high-dilution antibody) product with no plausible pharmacological mechanism, so a true drug effect on time to recurrence over 6 months would be unlikely. Against that, this sponsor's Russian multicenter placebo-controlled trials have fairly often reported statistically significant primary results, though several have also failed or gone unreported. Time to first recurrence in 415 women is a moderately powered, subjective symptom-based endpoint, which leaves room for either outcome. Balancing the weak biological prior against the sponsor's track record gives a probability somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9701bfc0ec89736e0b022b05b390b56f58a175cd3c4ebb04f4198d515224dc85"},{"nct":"NCT06328712","title":"Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of EN001 in Patients With Charcot-Marie-Tooth Disease Type 1A(CMT1A) (Phase 1b: Open-label, Dose-escalation, Single-center; Phase 2a: Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled, Multicenter)","sponsor":"ENCell","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":27,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.5906461996334648,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is Phase 1b safety (DLT), so the relevant efficacy test is the Phase 2a comparison of CMTNSv2 change at week 24 against placebo. With 27 total participants split across a 3+3 escalation and a 1:1:1 Phase 2a, each Phase 2a arm likely has only about 5–7 patients. CMTNSv2 changes over 24 weeks in CMT1A are small and noisy, and the analysis plan is largely descriptive. Allogeneic MSC therapy for an inherited demyelinating neuropathy is an unproven mechanism, and the supportive open-label signals were uncontrolled, so a statistically significant win over placebo is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"caad7c11cf31c0c933625ab9bcaa1e38f314edf8d1aca3b3a2fc280f22f0a37f"},{"nct":"NCT06434610","title":"A Study of B013 in Combination With Paclitaxel in Patients With Platinum-resistant Recurrent Ovarian Cancer.","sponsor":"Shanghai Jiaolian Drug Research and Development Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":90,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.2518666890818655,"rationale":"B013 is a little-characterized investigational biologic from a Chinese sponsor, tested against a placebo-plus-weekly-paclitaxel control. In platinum-resistant ovarian cancer, add-ons to weekly paclitaxel have mostly failed (immune checkpoint inhibitors, several novel agents); anti-angiogenics are the main exception. With about 90 patients, PFS is reasonably sensitive to a moderate effect, and phase 2 trials sometimes use lenient alpha, but power is limited. The trial was still recruiting in mid-2026, and no results are known, so I stay slightly below a neutral phase 2 oncology base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f817f5421f2fb47072b915478e92a086763388424a60ca72ddcb11b33747f932"},{"nct":"NCT06470191","title":"A Clinical Study of B007 in the Treatment of Primary Membranous Nephropathy.","sponsor":"Shanghai Jiaolian Drug Research and Development Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":216,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6424106628570821,"rationale":"B007 appears to be a humanized subcutaneous anti-CD20 antibody, a mechanism already validated in primary membranous nephropathy: in MENTOR, rituximab was superior to cyclosporine at 24 months (about 60% vs 20% remission), largely because patients relapse after cyclosporine is stopped. A 2-year overall remission endpoint therefore favors the anti-CD20 arm, and with 216 patients there is adequate power for an effect anywhere near MENTOR's size. The main uncertainties are the unknown potency of subcutaneous B007 dosed only twice, an unclear statistical hypothesis (non-inferiority or superiority), and a Phase II/III trial that is still recruiting and run by a smaller sponsor. No results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0e14d6d1776af9e1ee097ed1876cbfc991beda3c116f481fb004cdce7df7c29b"},{"nct":"NCT06479135","title":"Study of Navtemadlin add-on to Ruxolitinib in JAK Inhibitor-Naïve Patients With Myelofibrosis Who Have a Suboptimal Response to Ruxolitinib","sponsor":"Kartos Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":600,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.816299473234208,"rationale":"Navtemadlin showed real spleen activity in the phase 1b/2 add-on cohort in ruxolitinib suboptimal responders. In BOREAS, as monotherapy in relapsed/refractory MF, it gave numerically about three times the SVR35 rate of best available therapy. Here the placebo-plus-ruxolitinib arm should have a low SVR35 rate because these patients have already responded suboptimally after run-in, and a 2:1 randomization of a few hundred patients gives reasonable power on the first-listed SVR35 endpoint. The main risks are MDM2-inhibitor GI and hematologic toxicity limiting exposure, the modest effect sizes seen earlier, and some ongoing placebo-arm response from continued ruxolitinib; I recall no topline results yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2998a77cf62d8a3a63d53e7fe85ba30dd3d420c4ad6bed108992fbaca77c3e1a"},{"nct":"NCT06496971","title":"A Prospective Pivotal Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Avastin® Bevacizumab (BEV) With or Without Microbubble-mediated Focused Ultrasound (FUS-MB) Using NaviFUS System in Recurrent Glioblastoma Multiforme Patients","sponsor":"NaviFUS Corporation","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":32,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.6659391947571095,"rationale":"This is a small (32-patient), open-label, two-site Taiwanese trial comparing bevacizumab with or without NaviFUS blood-brain-barrier opening in recurrent GBM, with PFS-6 as the primary endpoint. With about 16 patients per arm and a bevacizumab control PFS-6 of roughly 40%, only a very large effect (well over 35 percentage points) would reach two-sided significance. Bevacizumab is a large antibody whose antiangiogenic action does not clearly depend on crossing the BBB, and the phase 1 NaviFUS data are encouraging but uncontrolled. The 'pivotal' label and sponsor-driven design may mean a lenient or one-sided analysis, but this is still a likely miss on a strict significance criterion.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8e09d5b19eac812e890a24523928108ce03c3e57d77bc2c283546fb9f1ac53f5"},{"nct":"NCT06531824","title":"EASi-KIDNEY™ (The Studies of Heart & Kidney Protection With BI 690517 in Combination With Empagliflozin)","sponsor":"Boehringer Ingelheim","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":8371,"base":0.64,"researched":null,"learned":0.7642741353566762,"rationale":"Vicadrostat, an aldosterone synthase inhibitor, cut albuminuria substantially on top of empagliflozin in phase 2, and steroidal MRA biology is validated by finerenone's positive outcome trials in diabetic CKD (FIDELIO/FIGARO). This is a large, event-driven trial (about 8,400 patients) run by the experienced Oxford/BI team behind EMPA-KIDNEY. Its broad composite, including heart-failure hospitalization and CV death, should give adequate power for a roughly 15–20% risk reduction. The main risks are the non-diabetic subgroup, where finerenone's FIND-CKD missed, the incremental benefit over a background SGLT2 inhibitor, and hyperkalemia-driven discontinuations diluting the effect.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dce534055a56f8516fb4d8fd11ddddb0fd4b4fc1e65e163d28b8a567d460d02f"},{"nct":"NCT06660394","title":"A Phase 3, Placebo-Controlled Study to Investigate LP352 in Children and Adults With Dravet Syndrome (DS)","sponsor":"Longboard Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":108,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.7128522097273143,"rationale":"Bexicaserin is a selective 5-HT2C agonist, and in the Phase 1b/2a PACIFIC study in developmental and epileptic encephalopathies it produced roughly a 50%+ median reduction in countable motor seizures. Serotonergic therapy has strong validation in Dravet through fenfluramine, and Dravet Phase 3 trials of active drugs (fenfluramine, cannabidiol, stiripentol) have generally succeeded with modest placebo responses. However, the more selective 5-HT2C agonist lorcaserin reportedly missed its Phase 3 Dravet primary endpoint, and a roughly 108-patient trial leaves limited margin. This trial's results are not yet public, so I land somewhat above the Phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"53f3cf94d88241786e74fcc3784743c3d1ca26011d44b543d9441753bc27086d"},{"nct":"NCT06664775","title":"A Study to Compare the Efficacy and Safety of TachoSil and Surgicel Original as an Adjunct to Control Mild to Moderate Soft Tissue Bleeding During Surgery","sponsor":"Corza Medical GmbH","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":116,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.7469048897498974,"rationale":"TachoSil is an established fibrin sealant patch. In head-to-head hemostasis trials, fibrinogen/thrombin patches have repeatedly beaten oxidized regenerated cellulose at early time points; EVARREST, for example, roughly doubled success rates versus Surgicel in soft tissue bleeding. The open-label design with surgeon-assessed hemostasis also tends to favor the experimental arm. The main risks are that Surgicel performs relatively well in mild (VIBe grade 1–2) bleeding, which narrows the gap, and that roughly 58 patients per arm gives only modest power if the difference is under about 20 percentage points.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"208539e623181c6ac8f537643ed644a0ae93f5bf27043864a73072d707fd4f01"},{"nct":"NCT06696261","title":"A Study of Lianxiaxiaopi Granules in the Treatment of Postprandial Distress Syndrome","sponsor":"Tasly Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":342,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.6702134386262947,"rationale":"Chinese TCM Phase III trials in functional dyspepsia sponsored by industry against placebo report success at high rates; Lianxiaxiaopi (likely a Banxia Xiexin-type formula) presumably had a positive Phase II supporting this confirmatory study, and 342 patients gives reasonable power on a responder endpoint. Placebo response in FD is high, though, and the strict weekly-responder definition (≥50% of weeks with ≥50% reduction in both PDS symptoms) can shrink the between-arm difference. Publication and reporting bias in Chinese TCM trials inflates apparent success rates, so I temper the estimate somewhat. No results are public yet, as the trial is still recruiting with primary completion planned for end of 2026.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a3639cc8aff0c963563f9296016af4fef436f5fe4ecf3e574787571b429bc1ee"},{"nct":"NCT06769152","title":"A Phase II Clinical Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of HLX43 (Anti-PD-L1 ADC) in Patients With Advanced Gynecological Malignant Tumors","sponsor":"Shanghai Henlius Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":190,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.4055836543684731,"rationale":"This trial randomizes patients only between HLX43 doses and has no control arm, so 'success' depends on whether the reported ORR and PFS look clinically meaningful rather than on a formal superiority test. Early HLX43 phase 1 data showed antitumor activity across solid tumors, including some gynecologic responses. Topo-I ADCs often reach roughly 25-40% ORR in platinum-resistant ovarian and post-ICI cervical cancer, so an encouraging topline readout is plausible. Uncertainty remains high because there is no prespecified comparator or hypothesis, the PD-L1-targeted ADC approach is unproven, and the trial runs at a single center.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4b6b63a75d291c6062870eaa578f3cdff31f3cffad6dc94ffa44a1c457ac5b42"},{"nct":"NCT06776432","title":"Safety and Efficacy Study of Sivopixant, Acetazolamide and SASS-001 in Sleep Apnea","sponsor":"Shionogi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":60,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.4396242223691684,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is the within-subject change in AHI from baseline on SASS-001, which appears to be a sivopixant plus acetazolamide combination from the Shionogi-Apnimed joint venture. That is an easy bar to clear statistically, even if the comparison is made against placebo. Acetazolamide alone reliably cuts AHI substantially in patients with central or high-loop-gain sleep apnea, and enrollment was enriched for exactly those patients, so a significant reduction is likely even if sivopixant adds little. The main risks are a small sample (n=60), dropout, and uncertainty about how the primary comparison is formally defined.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d8e24e03499c23caf9b594bf44a374efdb8a922d3bd811551cf19b566e97f51b"},{"nct":"NCT06797297","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of IBI363 Monotherapy Compared to Pembrolizumab in Patients With Unresectable Locally Advanced or Metastatic Mucosal or Acral Melanoma Who Had Not Previously Received Systemic Therapy","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":203,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.37767921818178085,"rationale":"IBI363, a PD-1/IL-2 fusion, showed encouraging phase 1 activity in acral and mucosal melanoma, including IO-pretreated patients, and these subtypes respond poorly to pembrolizumab alone (ORR roughly 15-20%, median PFS about 3 months). A randomized phase 2 of about 200 patients with IRRC-assessed PFS is reasonably powered for the hazard ratio near 0.6 that the early data suggest. Risks include the high base-rate failure of novel IL-2 agents against active controls, overestimated effects from single-arm data, and possible toxicity-driven dose limits. I am not aware of any topline result being public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4ce4c0a72bef22dc2627ac649a025fffeceec3d083ce8c33009f70f3eafd1978"},{"nct":"NCT06803823","title":"A Study of ONO-2020 in Patients With Agitation Associated With Alzheimer's Disease Dementia","sponsor":"Ono Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":90,"base":0.22,"researched":null,"learned":0.21641812296475407,"rationale":"ONO-2020 is a novel-mechanism compound (reportedly an epigenetic regulator) in an exploratory Phase 2a with only about 90 hospitalized Japanese patients, randomized 1:1 against placebo, with change in CMAI at week 12 as the primary efficacy endpoint. Agitation trials in Alzheimer's disease are known for large placebo responses and frequent failures, even for drugs with stronger prior validation such as brexpiprazole and AVP-786. A small Phase 2a sample gives limited power to detect a modest effect, and there is little public efficacy data for this mechanism. The trial is still recruiting, with primary completion planned for end of 2026, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"43f98878386ef3b7d357fd11a0c0eb4364a36b96eaef92859de782a9d86a9df0"},{"nct":"NCT06819826","title":"A Study of SC0062 Capsule for the Treatment of IgA Nephropathy with Proteinuria","sponsor":"Biocity Biopharmaceutics Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":360,"base":0.91,"researched":null,"learned":0.7068624428707259,"rationale":"Endothelin-A antagonism has reliably lowered proteinuria in IgA nephropathy: atrasentan (ALIGN) and sparsentan (PROTECT) both met 36-week UPCR endpoints with large effects, and SC0062's phase 2 (2-SUCCEED) showed significant dose-dependent proteinuria reduction versus placebo. This trial uses a placebo comparator, a surrogate endpoint that is well suited to the mechanism, and 360 patients, which gives ample power for an expected roughly 30-40% relative reduction. The main risks are operational (dropouts, edema-related discontinuations, or growing SGLT2i use shrinking the treatment effect), but these rarely erase an effect this robust. Primary completion is planned for December 2026, and I do not recall any topline result being public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"54cd7798355b6ab202f6f66f5e80a766aa883ad3f182a5984529a7b1f2efccfe"},{"nct":"NCT06842966","title":"Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of 4-MUST Tablets in Chronic Cholecystitis and Biliary Dyskinesia","sponsor":"Valenta Pharm JSC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":300,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.6699961178873248,"rationale":"4-MUST is a new salt of trimebutine, an established spasmolytic, combined with hymecromone (4-methylumbelliferone), a choleretic used for biliary dyskinesia, so both components are already in clinical use in Russia. Valenta has a track record of Russian placebo-controlled trials of its own products that report positive results. Against that, the primary endpoint is a subjective VAS pain score with a large placebo response in functional biliary disorders, the per-arm size is modest (about 75), and the trial is still recruiting with no public results. Three dose arms give multiple chances to hit significance, so I put the probability moderately above the Phase 2 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7c9acfc5409dbcfd84b47757e8b1567521f679e77a69847ee6ef72a53105b4f3"},{"nct":"NCT06843018","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Different Doses of Graminidin With Anesthetic, a Metered Dose Topical Spray, in the Treatment of Acute Infectious and Inflammatory Pharyngeal Diseases Compared With Drug Septolete Total, Lozenges","sponsor":"Valenta Pharm JSC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":300,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.6175055765261145,"rationale":"This is an open-label, sponsor-run Russian registration study of a reformulated, long-marketed local antiseptic/anesthetic combination (gramicidin C + oxybuprocaine + cetylpyridinium) against Septolete Total. Although the record does not say so, the design is most likely non-inferiority, and such comparisons of similar topical sore-throat products usually meet their margins, especially with subjective endpoints in unblinded trials. The main risks are the two-component co-primary endpoint, both of which may need to succeed, and uncertainty about the margins or statistical framework. The trial is still recruiting and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"23fdc10671a5ca024feb7f47b0293d58fa687fe25013abc0ec3b6dc1ec0abd2f"},{"nct":"NCT06863701","title":"Efficacy Anda Safety of Etoricoxib With Betamethasone for the Treatment of Acute Gout Arthritis","sponsor":"Laboratorios Silanes S.A. de C.V.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":72,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.6754519906575686,"rationale":"This small (n=72), single-site Mexican trial compares an etoricoxib/low-dose betamethasone (0.25 mg) fixed-dose combination against etoricoxib alone, which is already highly effective for acute gout. Detecting an add-on benefit between arms on a crude 4-point Likert pain scale is hard. The primary outcome is framed as within-group change from baseline, so the sponsor may report 'success' on that basis, but a significant between-arm difference is less likely. Local sponsor-run fixed-dose-combination trials do sometimes report favorable results, which nudges the estimate up slightly.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2bf620978b0b579774b1c67c9faaa60e154f8e18a087205fd688e74e1b3d32c7"},{"nct":"NCT06884293","title":"A Study Comparing IBI362 vs Semaglutide in Chinese Overweight or Obese Adults With Metabolic Dysfunction-associated Fatty Liver Disease （MAFLD）","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":479,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.881122409275325,"rationale":"IBI362 (mazdutide) is a GLP-1/glucagon dual agonist. At 9 mg in Chinese adults with obesity it produced roughly 18–19% weight loss at 48 weeks in GLORY-1 and phase 2 studies. Semaglutide 2.4 mg produced about 12–13% in STEP 7, and mazdutide has already beaten semaglutide head-to-head in DREAMS-3 in type 2 diabetes with obesity. With about 480 patients, a likely 4–6 percentage-point difference in weight loss gives very high power, and glucagon agonism makes superiority on liver fat also likely. The remaining risk is a shortfall in tolerability or adherence, or semaglutide performing unexpectedly well in an open-label setting.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9214c3cb5b69ba11a04b4ae524a1943650a330d4e289f5075ecbe14edbc5d51f"},{"nct":"NCT06908876","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of IBI302 inSubjects With Diabetic Macular Edema（DME）","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics Technology Limited (Shanghai R&D Center)","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":150,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.5445357317071647,"rationale":"IBI302 (efdamrofusp alfa), a VEGF/complement bispecific, is compared head-to-head with faricimab in a small Phase 2 DME study (~50 per arm), with BCVA change at week 16 as the primary endpoint. Beating an effective anti-VEGF/Ang-2 comparator on BCVA by a statistically significant margin at this sample size is unlikely, especially since faricimab gets four monthly loading doses against IBI302's three plus PRN. The trial looks exploratory or non-inferiority in spirit, so even a favorable 'comparable efficacy' readout would probably not count as significant superiority. I am not aware of any public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"05c069adbdc2579fbc10ab8df59b55cff7224d081e0ed7ce9a0543501470c983"},{"nct":"NCT07005180","title":"Low-dose Carbon Monoxide (HBI-002) Trial to Evaluate Safety, Tolerability, PK, and Biomarkers in Parkinson's Disease","sponsor":"Hillhurst Biopharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":36,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.5016654679809701,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is safety and tolerability (treatment-emergent adverse events versus placebo) in a small 36-patient, 14-day Phase 2a study, so 'success' in practice means the sponsor reports HBI-002 as safe and well tolerated. Phase 1 data with low-dose oral carbon monoxide in healthy volunteers were reportedly benign at controlled COHb levels, and the strict exclusion criteria further reduce the risk of a safety signal. The main risks are an unexpected tolerability signal, enrollment delays (the trial started in mid-2026 with an ambitious completion date), or the result being judged ambiguous because no efficacy comparison exists. I put the probability moderately high rather than near-certain.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4616625b1a26fd1ba770f731d84c587cd07b770e666e3ee5dbc9e6fcc6de15b5"},{"nct":"NCT07087158","title":"A Study of IBR854 Combined With Pazopanib Versus Pazopanib in Advanced Renal Cell Carcinoma","sponsor":"Imbioray (Hangzhou) Biomedicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":30,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3320376718431154,"rationale":"IBR854 is an early-stage cell therapy from a small Chinese biotech, tested here in a tiny 30-patient, 2:1 randomized, open-label phase II against pazopanib, which has a median PFS of about 8–11 months in first-line ccRCC. With roughly 10 control patients and a planned primary completion of end-2026, there will be few PFS events, so the trial has very little power to show a statistically significant difference unless the effect is very large. The study looks exploratory and is unlikely to have been powered for formal significance, and no mechanistic precedent strongly supports large benefit, so success is improbable.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"aecaf63a95a83b359b4c200fbcd67115eb7d7e714acf176bca6b5cac091c122b"},{"nct":"NCT07113262","title":"A Clinical Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of IBI311 in Subjects With Inactive Thyroid Eye Disease","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":111,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.6912800797430453,"rationale":"IBI311 is Innovent's teprotumumab-like IGF-1R antibody, and it already met its primary endpoint in active TED in the RESTORE-1 phase 3. Teprotumumab itself beat placebo on proptosis response in chronic/inactive TED (about 62% vs 25%), and a Japanese inactive-TED trial also succeeded, so the mechanism is validated in this population. With 111 patients randomized 2:1, the trial has ample power for an effect of that size on an objective endpoint. The main risks are a smaller effect in long-standing disease (2–10 years) or a high placebo response, and I am not aware of any public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"50062200456a3b10c03f0354dd70458b076eade128954f91b13295ec31e2108a"},{"nct":"NCT07121413","title":"A Clinical Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Immunogenicity of SV001 in Patients With Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis","sponsor":"Shanghai Synvida Biotechnology Co.,Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":48,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.3037173237304461,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is incidence of treatment-emergent adverse events in a small (n=48) placebo-controlled multiple-ascending-dose study of a biologic, SV001, in IPF, so no formal superiority test is planned. Sponsors of such safety-primary trials usually report the result as met when the drug is described as safe and well tolerated, which is the common outcome for early-phase biologics. The probability is held below the high range because a safety endpoint does not map neatly onto statistical success, there may be tolerability signals, and a small Chinese sponsor may report results late or incompletely. I am not aware of any public topline results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c54a6b75add069e1a0e51da6e2578b7f9310fddd204d3cde61838bdf7d6bcda1"},{"nct":"NCT07127042","title":"Study on BT-114143 Reducing Perioperative Bleeding in Total Knee Arthroplasty（TKA）","sponsor":"ScinnoHub Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":270,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5783807398000864,"rationale":"BT-114143 appears to be a novel antifibrinolytic or hemostatic agent, tested in this phase 2 trial against an active tranexamic acid regimen (20 mg/kg pre-incision plus 1 g postoperatively), not placebo. Showing statistically significant superiority in Gross-formula total blood loss over well-dosed TXA with about 90 patients per arm is hard, because TXA already captures most of the achievable antifibrinolytic benefit in TKA. The record specifies neither a non-inferiority margin nor a formal hypothesis, so the trial may be largely dose-finding and estimation, which lowers the chance of a clear 'met primary endpoint' outcome. Some upside remains if the high dose is substantially more potent, or if the sponsor frames the result as a non-inferiority success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"130b8fd1ed822ad3973ca9829136a97e4daf28acca8e82f6508da3f3f0b59f2e"},{"nct":"NCT07136805","title":"A Phase 3 Study of VVN461 Ophthalmic Solution for Noninfectious Anterior Uveitis","sponsor":"VivaVision Biotech, Inc","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":154,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.7284601371304654,"rationale":"VVN461 is a topical JAK1/TYK2 inhibitor, and this Chinese pivotal trial (n=154) is very likely a non-inferiority comparison against Pred Forte on Day 14 change in anterior chamber cell grade. Earlier-phase data reportedly supported anti-inflammatory activity, and non-inferiority on a change-from-baseline endpoint within a modest margin is attainable. However, topical prednisolone is a highly potent comparator, topical JAK inhibition is unproven in uveitis, and the margin and sample size are uncertain. That leaves a moderately favorable but uncertain outlook.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b5f9229229731fc9aa45a3b2649a0312c8858331f9f373b93eef541fa96ee2c4"},{"nct":"NCT07162883","title":"Pharmacokinetic Study of QL2107 Versus Keytruda® for Adjuvant Therapy of Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)","sponsor":"Qilu Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":146,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.6609713690188648,"rationale":"This is a PK equivalence trial of a pembrolizumab biosimilar in resected NSCLC, a design modeled on Amgen's and Samsung Bioepis's PK-similarity studies, and well-developed biosimilar mAbs usually meet the 80–125% GMR bounds for AUC. Qilu has a solid biosimilar track record, and adjuvant patients without tumor burden give relatively homogeneous PK. Risks are the small sample (about 73 per arm) with two co-primary endpoints, including a cycle 7 steady-state AUC prone to dropout and variability, plus possible ADA or manufacturing differences. I estimate a high but not certain chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"faef85f524366106371055b6b333d0e56d7043ced83a0f6af1808493a28c90ec"},{"nct":"NCT07186413","title":"A Study to Compare the Efficacy, Safety and Pharmacokinetics of Trifarotene 50 mcg/g Cream in Chinese Subjects With Acne Vulgaris","sponsor":"Galderma R&D","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":561,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.9110753922212868,"rationale":"Trifarotene 50 mcg/g cream already met all co-primary endpoints against vehicle in the large PERFECT 1 and 2 phase 3 trials (IGA success about 29% vs 20% and 42% vs 26%), so this is a regional bridging study of a proven drug. With about 561 participants, an IGA difference of 10–15 points should give reasonable to good power, though vehicle response in acne trials varies and could narrow the gap. Primary completion is planned for late 2026, and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6200d9285297efdecadec56006cfbf5b0220b464c1892f942cba345915596120"},{"nct":"NCT07223229","title":"Phase 2 Study to Evaluate EI-001 in Non-segmental Vitiligo Patients","sponsor":"Elixiron Immunotherapeutics (Hong Kong) Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":45,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.4735297227591467,"rationale":"This is a small (n=45) first proof-of-concept phase 2 test of a novel immunomodulatory antibody from a small biotech in non-segmental vitiligo, where repigmentation is slow and 24 weeks is a short window. Oral JAK inhibitors have produced significant F-VASI changes at 24 weeks, but non-JAK biologics such as anti-IL-15 have largely disappointed. Placebo response in F-VASI is low, which helps, but the modest sample still needs a large effect to reach significance. Without public efficacy data for EI-001, a below-base-rate estimate seems appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3018f2cdf1db44f05d5452c3c36d9dd06763f62c4a2a95fdf977499ff3968bdc"},{"nct":"NCT07226661","title":"Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study in Adults With Major Depressive Disorder","sponsor":"Supernus Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":230,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.21666691553820755,"rationale":"SPN-821 is a follow-on mTORC1 activator to SPN-820 (NV-5138), whose adjunctive Phase 2 in treatment-resistant depression showed no separation from placebo on MADRS in 2024, so this mechanism already has a negative proof-of-concept. Adjunctive MDD trials face high placebo response, and this one is only 4 weeks long with about 115 patients per arm, so power is modest for the 2–3 point MADRS difference a typical adjunctive drug achieves. Phase 2 psychiatry trials succeed roughly 30% of the time, and the prior failure in this class pulls the estimate below that.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"72e265bc98a9261ff63b88e3dc356302dc3a86dd598bd829623d18fdb829b911"},{"nct":"NCT07249632","title":"A Study of Telitacicept in Patients With Ocular Myasthenia Gravis (OMG)","sponsor":"RemeGen Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":120,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.6563633885954063,"rationale":"Telitacicept (TACI-Fc) produced a large MG-ADL benefit over placebo in RemeGen's Chinese Phase 3 in generalized MG and is approved in China, so the mechanism has supporting evidence and the sponsor-run Chinese trials have tended to succeed. Ocular MG is harder to win in: it has lower antibody positivity, its primary endpoint is patient-reported (MGII PRO ocular) and prone to placebo response, the sample is modest (120 patients), and there are no validated precedents for drug success in this population. Balancing the strong prior efficacy signal against these design and disease uncertainties gives a probability modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3e64410627440a508e361b0f926b80efe6aa3ec16d927ee09dbf3b9d79f5095f"},{"nct":"NCT07265349","title":"A Phase I/II Clinical Trial of Intramyocardial Injection of HucMSCs for the Treatment of Chronic Heart Failure","sponsor":"Tasly Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":51,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.3828624756549421,"rationale":"This is a small (n=51), open-label phase I/II dose-exploration trial of umbilical cord MSCs given with CABG, with roughly 12 patients per arm. The first-listed primary outcome is phase I safety, and the phase II LVEF comparison against CABG alone is likely underpowered or only descriptive. Prior trials of MSCs given alongside CABG, such as PERFECT and the CSCC_ASCII-type studies, have mostly shown no significant LVEF benefit over surgery alone, and CABG by itself improves LVEF substantially, which raises the bar for showing added benefit. Chinese sponsors sometimes report favorable results, but a statistically significant between-arm LVEF difference in a study this size is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"79b9f13883f6ea29ff8e4a0094a49b0908caf47e3c4f7fc13ea250843962c723"},{"nct":"NCT07391241","title":"A Phase 2 Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Pudafensine in Vulvodynia (Provoked Vestibulodynia)","sponsor":"Initiator Pharma","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":24,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.619351461776114,"rationale":"This is a small (n=24), single-site, exploratory 4-way crossover of single doses of pudafensine, a monoamine reuptake inhibitor with positive Phase 2 erectile dysfunction data, in a new indication, provoked vestibulodynia. A single dose of a reuptake inhibitor plausibly changes the vestibular pain threshold, and the crossover design with three doses improves power and offers several chances to win. Still, pain endpoints carry large placebo and variance effects, and first tests of a mechanism in a hard pain condition usually miss formal significance. Small sponsors often announce such studies as 'positive' on trends, but under a strict p<0.05 criterion success is less likely than not.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e69c5b68a2b055feee9093782e91f16a5301e12d75933e2b9331bc82c56dd5ed"},{"nct":"NCT07413549","title":"Clinical Study of Human Umbilical Cord Mesenchymal Stem Cells Injection in Patients With Decompensated Hepatitis B Cirrhosis","sponsor":"Beijing Tuohua Weiye Biotechnology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":76,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.47413258855170404,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are safety and tolerability (AE/SAE incidence within 28 days) and choosing a recommended phase II dose, with no prespecified comparative efficacy test. Umbilical cord MSC infusions in decompensated HBV cirrhosis have repeatedly been well tolerated in Chinese trials, so a topline claim of acceptable safety and an identified RP2D is likely. The main risks are ambiguity about how a safety-only primary is judged, possible SAEs in a fragile decompensated population, and an unclear reporting timeline from a small single-site industry sponsor. I know of no public results for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9cf8f25a3ebdaa8205be56d7eb313722dff5219ce2b5044650c60c762c5cfc51"},{"nct":"NCT07443202","title":"Study of Lotilaner Ophthalmic Gel in Patients With Ocular Rosacea (KORE)","sponsor":"Tarsus Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":155,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.44875950902495915,"rationale":"The only primary outcome is the incidence of treatment-emergent adverse events, with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so a superiority 'success' (significantly fewer adverse events than vehicle) is very unlikely. A sponsor topline, however, would probably call it met if the gel is well tolerated, which is plausible given lotilaner's clean safety record as Xdemvy in Demodex blepharitis. With primary completion planned for end of 2026 and no known public readout, the result depends mostly on how a safety-only endpoint is judged. I therefore settle near the middle.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6e4e8adb0bb4ad90014a59478389f68864fe3d67065c984a01c14043b719f2d6"},{"nct":"NCT07443696","title":"PET Myocardial Fatty-acid Metabolic Imaging With XTR003 Injection and 18F-FDG to Assess Myocardial Viability in Ischemic Cardiomyopathy","sponsor":"Sinotau Pharmaceutical Group","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":40,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3009230632416409,"rationale":"This is a small (40–60 patients, about 20 per arm), exploratory, open-label Phase IIb diagnostic study whose primary outcome is descriptive: sensitivity and specificity of each arm for predicting functional recovery after revascularization, with no stated hypothesis test or margin. If success is judged as a significant between-arm difference, that is very unlikely at this sample size, since glucose-loaded FDG is already a strong reference method. If it is judged as the XTR003 arm showing acceptable diagnostic accuracy, the sponsor could plausibly claim success, given that XTR003 has shown reasonable earlier fatty-acid imaging results. Weighing this ambiguity, and noting the trial is still recruiting so the result is not public, I put the chance of a clear topline 'success' at about 30%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ecd2bab395c0a459b6c9045ce4c8c0d525be1ffbf9af511ad46d58fb09a63876"},{"nct":"NCT07521137","title":"Biweekly Long-term Occidiofungin Study for Suppression of Mycotic Recurrence","sponsor":"Sano Chemicals Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":36,"base":0.22,"researched":null,"learned":0.3753783967895558,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n=36, single-site) phase 2a first-in-patient efficacy test of a novel antifungal, occidiofungin, at a low gel concentration, run by a small sponsor. The primary endpoint is strict: a VSS total score of 0 at Days 4, 8 and 25, so even an active drug may score low (a Day 4 complete cure is rare), although placebo rates should also be low. With roughly 18 per arm, power is limited, and the study may be largely descriptive with no formal hypothesis test. A real antifungal effect versus placebo is plausible, but a statistically significant win on this composite is uncertain.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d1c4271740a37135da29dc396e788b39c916a187f636d2a98415bfc1a3647a20"},{"nct":"NCT07644832","title":"An Open-label, Multicenter Phase I/II Clinical Trial to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Efficacy, and Pharmacokinetic/Pharmacodynamic (PK/PD) Characteristics of SR604 Injection in Patients With Hemophilia A/B and Congenital Factor VII Deficiency","sponsor":"Shanghai RAAS Blood Products Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":76,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6974471018295507,"rationale":"This is an open-label, uncontrolled-style phase I/II dose-escalation study whose first-listed primary outcome is AE incidence, so there is no formal superiority test, and success will in practice mean an acceptable safety profile plus encouraging bleeding-rate reductions. SR604 appears to be a subcutaneous non-factor rebalancing agent, a mechanism already validated by anti-TFPI antibodies (concizumab, marstacimab) and SerpinPC. That makes reduced ABR in on-demand patients with frequent prior bleeds likely. Thrombotic events, a known class risk, or immunogenicity could still derail it, and ambiguity over how success is defined adds uncertainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6f7ae645e24189507fa4a43f9e3e49bb17b2fd7424cd405140d2204ff87b74fb"},{"nct":"NCT07712523","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Parallel-Group, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Phase II Clinical Trial to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of QY201 Tablets in Subjects With Non-Segmental Vitiligo","sponsor":"E-nitiate Biopharmaceuticals (Hangzhou) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":200,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.5439090089796748,"rationale":"QY201 appears to be an oral JAK-pathway inhibitor. That class has consistently beaten placebo on percent change in F-VASI at week 24 in phase 2 vitiligo trials, including ritlecitinib, upadacitinib and povorcitinib. With about 50 patients per arm, three dose arms and a continuous, sensitive endpoint, at least one dose reaching significance is likely. The main risks are uncertainty about the drug's potency at these doses, a single-site trial run by a small sponsor, and the low F-VASI entry threshold, which could add noise.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e8b87409de2ee114c09df8ada0c53276ebde9cb19c9b69a4bb6c26da18184778"},{"nct":"NCT07719530","title":"Phase II Clinical Trial of SHR-1139 Injection in Patients With Psoriasis","sponsor":"Guangdong Hengrui Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":60,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.7650451414017526,"rationale":"SHR-1139 is a Hengrui biologic for psoriasis, a disease area where effective cytokine-targeting agents usually beat placebo easily. However, this 60-patient, single-site trial has two SHR-1139 arms and no placebo-only arm. Placebo appears to be used only to blind dosing regimens, so the primary PASI 100 analysis is likely a descriptive dose comparison rather than a powered superiority test. Any formal comparison between two active regimens on a demanding endpoint with about 30 patients per arm is unlikely to reach significance, though a sponsor may still describe the results as positive.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f8f7ab45785c9db6a9fd030d7ba995f4f9ad29a74c0d07cffe335cbc910de600"},{"nct":"NCT07746726","title":"Safety and Efficacy of HRS-9190 Compared to Rocuronium for Tracheal Intubation and Bolus Maintenance in Adults","sponsor":"Jiangsu HengRui Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2026-12-31","enrollment":320,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.7060841569362851,"rationale":"This is a Hengrui phase III comparing its novel neuromuscular blocker HRS-9190 with rocuronium, with the primary endpoint being the rate of excellent or good Cooper intubation conditions. The trial is almost certainly a non-inferiority design, though the record does not state the margin. Both arms should reach near-ceiling rates (about 95% or more), and Chinese phase III non-inferiority trials of neuromuscular blockers with this endpoint very commonly succeed, especially after a sponsor has picked its dose in phase II. Residual risk comes from an unknown margin, possible slower onset at the chosen bolus dose, and execution at only two sites.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dca10a7294072512a29d955f4df99c340a2fbd3d430c6e00af2f1867c014149d"},{"nct":"NCT04485949","title":"A Phase 2b Clinical Study With a Combination Immunotherapy in Newly Diagnosed Patients With Glioblastoma","sponsor":"Imvax","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":99,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.2675934870102855,"rationale":"Randomized trials of new immunotherapies and vaccines in newly diagnosed glioblastoma have almost uniformly failed (e.g., rindopepimut, nivolumab in CheckMate-498/548, DCVax controversies), so the base rate is very low. IGV-001's evidence comes from a small single-arm Phase 1 at Thomas Jefferson with encouraging PFS in a higher-dose subgroup, which is weak evidence prone to selection bias. This Phase 2b is small (n=99), so it can only detect a large PFS effect, though centrally reviewed PFS is a somewhat more attainable endpoint than OS and a Phase 2b may use a relaxed alpha. I know of no public topline result, and primary completion is planned for 2027-01.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"98842c59409b6e7b2f7c497f7e33864498225780843c4feb5bd222bf6034d905"},{"nct":"NCT05050136","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of an Investigational Drug Named Volixibat in Patients With Itching Caused by Primary Biliary Cholangitis","sponsor":"Mirum Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":333,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6859154649152164,"rationale":"IBAT inhibition is a validated mechanism for cholestatic pruritus in PBC: GSK's linerixibat met its Phase 3 GLISTEN itch endpoint. Mirum's VANTAGE Part 1 interim data showed meaningful itch reductions on volixibat, which supported advancing the 20 mg dose. The main risks are the high placebo response typical of PBC itch trials (linerixibat's Phase 2b missed partly for this reason) and diarrhea-related unblinding or dropout. Powering looks adequate with about 333 patients, and primary completion is listed for 2027-01, so the topline result does not appear to be public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c9d9836e610f4818b0cdb873340a0c700344e4789f7c12ad01fde0ba1753a1dc"},{"nct":"NCT05171894","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of Light Dose in Subjects With PWB Treated With Hemoporfin PDT","sponsor":"Shanghai Fudan-Zhangjiang Bio-Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":84,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.5998708170960523,"rationale":"Hemoporfin PDT is already approved in China for port-wine stains, where a Phase 3 trial showed clear superiority over placebo PDT, so the Stage Two efficacy comparison (PWB-IGA reduction vs vehicle plus green light) has a strong prior of success even in a small US Phase 2. However, the first-listed primary outcome is a Stage One safety endpoint (adverse event incidence), which has no clear success criterion. Small arms (about 84 patients across six arms) and possible differences in US populations and skin types add uncertainty. Balancing a likely positive efficacy signal against how ambiguously this endpoint will be scored, I estimate a moderate-to-favorable probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0e76975400e005187abf5378ef998f01b5564f0c850f58589a69c445cd3a3b54"},{"nct":"NCT05406362","title":"Assess Safety and Efficacy of VAD044 in HHT Patients","sponsor":"Vaderis Therapeutics AG","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":75,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.4269591090424594,"rationale":"The first-listed primary endpoint is safety and tolerability (type and severity of AEs), not a statistical efficacy comparison, so success hinges on the drug being judged well tolerated. As I recall, Vaderis reported Part I topline data in 2024 saying VAD044 (an oral AKT inhibitor) was well tolerated and met its primary safety and tolerability endpoint, with clinically meaningful reductions in nosebleeds at 40 mg. Some uncertainty remains because a descriptive safety endpoint does not map cleanly onto a superiority comparison, and the long Part II extension is still ongoing.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"5ab8e35d8348a2197a9e90643eeb6e66f3c5e1e17a56a3a7c281ff8ff9b690ef"},{"nct":"NCT05540860","title":"A Study of EDG-5506 in Children With Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy (LYNX)","sponsor":"Edgewise Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":76,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.5589621237148176,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are safety measures (number and severity of adverse events) with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so 'success' likely amounts to acceptable tolerability. Edgewise has publicly reported that sevasemten was generally well tolerated in LYNX and related Duchenne and Becker studies, with CK and fsTnI reductions during the 12-week placebo-controlled part. The main risk is scoring ambiguity, since a safety-only endpoint has no clean statistical win, plus some chance of emerging long-term safety signals before the 2027 primary completion.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1096b665a875d203e0a6a33c5a86b3283b08097abfe5a9f7529bcf29870c7b5f"},{"nct":"NCT05751928","title":"A Study of Neoadjuvant Therapy With BCD-217 (Nurulimab + Prolgolimab) in Patients With Resectable Stage III Skin Melanoma","sponsor":"Biocad","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":411,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.5827792874286073,"rationale":"This trial closely replicates NADINA: two cycles of neoadjuvant anti-CTLA-4 plus anti-PD-1 with response-directed surgery, versus surgery plus adjuvant PD-1 therapy. In NADINA, a similar-sized trial (n=423), neoadjuvant ipilimumab plus nivolumab gave a large, highly significant EFS benefit (HR about 0.32), and SWOG S1801 supports the broader neoadjuvant-first principle. The main uncertainties are whether Biocad's nurulimab/prolgolimab combination matches ipi/nivo in potency, open-label conduct, and the timing of the EFS analysis. Primary completion is planned for 2027-01 and no results are public, but the size of the class effect makes success fairly likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"16fc2bd513103c15be84751414f84c99f5231285cf0dd46c5de3a37107e5f610"},{"nct":"NCT06029972","title":"Study of Tilpisertib Fosmecarbil in Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Gilead Sciences","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":176,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.44935084260047997,"rationale":"Tilpisertib fosmecarbil is a prodrug of Gilead's TPL2/MAP3K8 inhibitor, a new mechanism in UC with no validated proof of concept; the parent compound GS-4875 did not produce a public efficacy signal that would raise confidence. The trial enrolls only advanced-therapy-experienced patients, where placebo clinical response is about 25-30% and drug effects tend to be smaller. With roughly 44 patients per arm, a difference of about 20-25 points would be needed for significance, though having three doses gives several chances to succeed. The base rate for novel-mechanism Phase 2 trials in UC is modest, so I put the probability below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a0d3c626ab35eac52c7ced68e07931373f7c0a07ea25588f01ca7a5c8b681248"},{"nct":"NCT06032195","title":"Study of Organ Perfusion in Heart Transplantation in Children","sponsor":"Dr. F. Köhler Chemie GmbH","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":15,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.3046968747379995,"rationale":"This is a tiny (n=15), descriptive phase II safety study whose primary outcome is adverse event reporting, with no prespecified efficacy comparison or non-inferiority margin, so a statistically significant win for Custodiol-N is very unlikely. The sponsor may well call it a success if safety looks comparable, and earlier Custodiol-N studies in adult heart and other transplants suggest a benign safety profile, but that kind of success doesn't clearly fit the definition used here. The trial is still recruiting, primary completion is planned for 2027-01, and enrollment may lag, so results could be delayed or never formally reported. My estimate reflects mostly the chance that a descriptive safety success is scored as meeting the endpoint.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"74bdadfa16e2190e2e5d98e75ac37e6b7877fa76cff37fa1d63048b09938120c"},{"nct":"NCT06109272","title":"A Study to Assess the Dose, Adverse Events, and Change in Disease Activity of Livmoniplimab as an Intravenous (IV) Solution in Combination With Budigalimab as an IV Solution in Adult Participants With Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":89,"base":0.08,"researched":null,"learned":0.7215268916946836,"rationale":"Actual enrollment is 89 against a planned 660, so only the Stage 1 dose-optimization portion appears to have run and the Stage 2 OS comparison likely will not happen, which may reflect a strategic or efficacy-driven decision. The first-listed primary endpoint is investigator-assessed ORR in Stage 1, with roughly 30 patients per arm, which is almost certainly descriptive. Even if formally compared, it is badly underpowered to show a significant gain over active standards like atezolizumab-bevacizumab or STRIDE. Phase 1 activity of anti-GARP/TGF-β livmoniplimab plus PD-1 was encouraging but not clearly superior, so a statistically significant win is unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cd26abdec5b5514576e5f7be0317d82ccc82cda957c26e0eb5a613bc623e3123"},{"nct":"NCT06384261","title":"A Study Comparing Venetoclax and Azacitidine Plus Cusatuzumab to Venetoclax and Azacitidine in Newly Diagnosed AML Ineligible for Intensive Therapy","sponsor":"OncoVerity, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":140,"base":0.13,"researched":null,"learned":0.330618487416746,"rationale":"This is a small randomized phase 2 (about 120 patients, 2:1) testing whether adding the CD70 antibody cusatuzumab to venetoclax/azacitidine prolongs overall survival in unfit AML. Overall survival on that backbone is a demanding endpoint, and a trial this size can only detect a large hazard ratio. Many add-on strategies to ven/aza or aza have failed on survival, including magrolimab, sabatolimab and pevonedistat. Cusatuzumab's earlier single-arm data with aza and with ven/aza were encouraging but not clearly better than historical controls, so a statistically significant OS benefit appears unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1a82b9c15e7eb1f7013e882aabf21650addcc9cb2bcdc16a0f97643ca46f8f3a"},{"nct":"NCT06481891","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Sotagliflozin in Symptomatic Obstructive and Non-obstructive Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy","sponsor":"Lexicon Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":500,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.7637123123089329,"rationale":"SGLT2 inhibitors have improved KCCQ in symptomatic HFpEF (PRESERVED-HF about +5 points, CHIEF-HF about +4), which gives sotagliflozin a plausible mechanistic rationale in HCM with its shared diastolic dysfunction. However, HCM-specific evidence is limited to small or observational data. In nonobstructive HCM, even the potent cardiac myosin inhibitor mavacamten failed on KCCQ in ODYSSEY-HCM, and a likely 2-4 point effect against placebo in a mixed oHCM/nHCM population of about 500 leaves power marginal. Weighing the new-indication base rate and the modest expected effect against a validated but noisy endpoint, I estimate a below-even chance of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3a7bf496ba184833c22a25921915676c2e8320a99f4b9915209590bc37244ba1"},{"nct":"NCT06561607","title":"A Clinical Trial of TQB2102 for Injection in the Treatment of HER2 Low-Expressing Recurrent/Metastatic Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":542,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.6788683309511021,"rationale":"TQB2102 is a biparatopic HER2 ADC with a topoisomerase-I payload, tested against single-agent chemotherapy on IRC-assessed PFS in chemo-naive, endocrine-pretreated HR+/HER2-low metastatic breast cancer. This is close to the DESTINY-Breast06 design, where T-DXd clearly beat chemotherapy on PFS (HR ~0.62). Chinese HER2 ADCs such as SHR-A1811 have also succeeded in similar HER2-low settings. Risks are that this is a less proven ADC, the open-label design, and a single-country trial, but with 542 patients and a mechanism-class effect this large, success is likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"95b8a06cd78a9b8ac1e70e1a7c7f34133f6fb3654c64ceb3bfe71367e3660c28"},{"nct":"NCT06601335","title":"A Phase 3 Study of AK112 Plus AK117 Versus Pembrolizumab in Recurrent or Metastatic Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma (R/M HNSCC)","sponsor":"Akeso","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":510,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.5053612668748151,"rationale":"This trial tests ivonescimab (a PD-1/VEGF bispecific) plus ligufalimab (a CD47 antibody) against pembrolizumab, with overall survival as the primary endpoint. Phase 2 data in first-line HNSCC showed high response rates, and ivonescimab beat pembrolizumab on progression-free survival in China (HARMONi-2); Akeso's China-only phase 3 trials have generally succeeded. Against that, OS against an active PD-1 comparator is a hard bar, VEGF blockade in HNSCC (E1305) did not significantly improve OS, and CD47 agents have repeatedly failed elsewhere. I am not aware of any topline result, so I land near a coin flip, slightly below.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"689b7fd33b1fb4f3bb9469025d792587951d7469505e852bb6d7324b6ec71fd9"},{"nct":"NCT06701331","title":"Safety and Efficacy of Upadacitinib in Combination With Topical Corticosteroids in Children From 2 to Less Than 12 Years of Age in Japan With Moderate to Severe Atopic Dermatitis","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":99,"base":0.93,"researched":null,"learned":0.9482364826902608,"rationale":"Upadacitinib plus TCS has shown large EASI-75 effects in adults and adolescents, including in Japanese patients (about 65-77% vs about 26% on placebo plus TCS in AD Up and Rising Up). Pediatric biologic trials with TCS, such as dupilumab, kept similarly large separations. With about 50 per arm and an expected absolute difference near 40 percentage points, power is very high, so the main risks are an unusually high placebo-plus-TCS response or an underperforming pediatric dose. I am not aware of a public topline result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dbf8489f75a01ce37373d029464f1ebb535366eeaa28605c993f74d55b3e9a80"},{"nct":"NCT06721143","title":"A Study to Investigate the Safety, Tolerability, and Preliminary Efficacy With AION-301 Administered by Intravenous Infusion Compared With Placebo Administered by Intravenous Infusion Investigational Intervention in Participants Aged 35 to 75 Years of Age With Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)","sponsor":"AION Healthspan, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":36,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.4205082697803762,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a safety measure: the proportion of participants with grade ≥3 adverse events versus placebo by day 90, in a small (n=36) phase 1/2 trial of what appears to be an allogeneic biologic or cell-derived product. Under a strict superiority reading, a statistically significant reduction in grade ≥3 adverse events versus placebo is nearly impossible at this size. However, a sponsor would likely announce the primary safety endpoint as 'met' if there is no excess toxicity, which seems plausible. Given that ambiguity in how the result will be scored, and the trial still recruiting with no public results, I put this near the middle, leaning below 50%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"301aec62d6b3ceb87f0a5e973cfaae679885fa626a07adc1f3675294107b2d97"},{"nct":"NCT06860971","title":"A Study of AL2846 Capsule Versus Placebo in the Treatment of Advanced Radioiodine-Refractory Differentiated Thyroid Carcinoma","sponsor":"Chia Tai Tianqing Pharmaceutical Group Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":144,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.6268905837737171,"rationale":"AL2846 is a multi-target TKI (c-MET, VEGFR1, RET, c-KIT) closely related to cabozantinib's mechanism. Cabozantinib's placebo-controlled COSMIC-311 in VEGFR-refractory RAIR-DTC showed a large PFS benefit (HR ~0.22), and placebo PFS in this setting is only about 2 months. A placebo comparator with IRC-assessed PFS in an indolent but progressing population makes success likely even with 144 patients, and CTTQ's TKI programs in China have a strong record in similar designs. The main residual risks are weaker activity after prior multi-kinase VEGFR TKIs and a modest sample size; I am not aware of any reported result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e3125da5ecee13912fc2e995fc99a4a3aa672411d60391f33f6083711ccc4516"},{"nct":"NCT06873035","title":"An Interventional Study of Infigratinib in Children With Hypochondroplasia","sponsor":"QED Therapeutics, a BridgeBio company","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":24,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7315667802562292,"rationale":"As registered, the trial is a small open-label Phase 2 of infigratinib (n≈24, two doses) measuring change from baseline in annualized height velocity at 26 weeks against each child's own observational-study baseline, which is an easy bar for a drug with proven growth-promoting FGFR3-pathway activity. Infigratinib raised height velocity by about 2.5 cm/yr in PROPEL 2 for achondroplasia, and the related CNP-pathway drug vosoritide increased it by about 1.8 cm/yr in hypochondroplasia, so a clinically and statistically meaningful within-patient gain is likely even with about 12 children per arm. The main risks are a smaller effect in hypochondroplasia's milder, more heterogeneous genetics, regression-to-the-mean issues, and some ambiguity over how a single-arm 'success' is judged. I do not recall a public topline for this trial, so this is a forecast rather than a recalled result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3942f6c86ea3c0fbfbc3f313a3f0ce703a66910769e16a20e3f57ce80b7bfffe"},{"nct":"NCT06879717","title":"A Study of Roginolisib (IOA-244) in Combination With Dostarlimab With or Without Docetaxel in Metastatic Non Small-cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) Patients","sponsor":"iOnctura","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":45,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.37056701104884937,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a descriptive safety count, so the closest thing to a testable efficacy endpoint is the comparison of patients with at least a 50% peripheral Treg reduction by Day 42 across arms. PI3Kδ inhibition has a plausible mechanism for strongly depleting Tregs, and roginolisib's earlier studies reported Treg reductions, so a large difference between roginolisib arms and dostarlimab plus docetaxel is biologically plausible. Against that, only about 15 patients per arm, an open-label Phase I/IIa design likely analysed descriptively, possible chemotherapy effects on Tregs in the control arm, and uncertainty over whether a formal significance test will be reported all lower the chance of a clear statistically significant win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"98b794552537e10531c6ad753e4a6cc58ac38b33377729a1dc01d3d4e3cc0b12"},{"nct":"NCT06889701","title":"A Phase 1/2 Study to Evaluate the Safety, PK and Efficacy of TNP-2092 Administered Via IA Injection in PJI Participants","sponsor":"TenNor Therapeutics Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":33,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.6744046641572375,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is safety and tolerability, measured as AE counts, in a small open-label proof-of-concept trial with no powered efficacy comparison, so 'success' most plausibly means the sponsor reports the drug as safe and well tolerated. TNP-2092 (rifaquizinone) has prior phase 1 data and an earlier PJI study, and the 14-day local intra-articular dosing keeps systemic exposure low, so a favorable safety readout is likely. The main uncertainty is how a safety-only primary endpoint gets scored, along with the small chance of local tolerability signals or delays, since the trial is still recruiting with primary completion planned for January 2027. I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3bc40173c770978e8e6e8a9124ea78a96fb82655791701a4635c106f05104851"},{"nct":"NCT07027345","title":"A Phase II, Placebo Controlled, Clinical Trial of Topical TolaSure Targeting Aggregated Mutant Keratin in Epidermolysis Bullosa Simplex","sponsor":"BioMendics, LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":40,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.34110913574215374,"rationale":"This is a small (n=40), two-site Phase II trial from a small company testing a first-in-class topical aimed at mutant keratin aggregation in EBS, with mixed localized, intermediate and severe subtypes. The primary endpoint, change in blister surface area, is highly variable and prone to large placebo responses because flares resolve on their own. Prior topical EBS programs, such as diacerein in a Phase 2/3, have failed to separate from placebo. A small company's sponsor-defined analysis might still report a favorable p-value, but statistical success on the primary comparison looks unlikely, and no results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f199075249af15ea87f8513a8736b9dc42773f7a52ac9a316031a1f70eaecf4d"},{"nct":"NCT07038382","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of Human Sialidase Fusion Protein (HLX79) in Combination With Rituximab Injection Versus Placebo in Patients With Active Glomerulonephritis","sponsor":"Shanghai Henlius Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":24,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.41917814365787365,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is purely a safety and tolerability count (treatment-related AEs and lab abnormalities) in a 24-patient dose-ranging Phase II with no prespecified efficacy hypothesis test. A statistically significant advantage over placebo plus rituximab is essentially impossible on such an endpoint at this sample size. Resolution therefore hinges on interpretation: a sponsor would likely call the trial successful if HLX79 was 'safe and well tolerated', which is plausible for a sialidase fusion protein added to a well-characterized anti-CD20 backbone. Given that ambiguity and no public results (primary completion is 2027-01), a near-midpoint estimate is appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"34011de4766b50b67d66117dcf4896bd0ca1ebb75526c2b12d312640fb39dd15"},{"nct":"NCT07062978","title":"A Comparative Study to Valuating the Efficacy and Safety of QL1206 and Prolia®","sponsor":"Qilu Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":278,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.7582961925723359,"rationale":"This is a randomized, double-blind equivalence trial comparing Qilu's denosumab biosimilar QL1206 with Prolia on percent change in lumbar-spine BMD at 12 months, a sensitive, low-variability endpoint. Comparative trials of denosumab biosimilars against Prolia have almost uniformly met their equivalence margins, and QL1206 is already approved in China against Xgeva, which supports analytical and PK similarity. The main risk is the modest sample size of 278, which leaves less room if the margin is tight or variability is higher than expected. Primary completion is planned for January 2027, so no result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0b3a7ae413749703d6c1ace20a80a69f99ccb9405b4462a6c7650b6354a94eb2"},{"nct":"NCT07080034","title":"Study of the Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics, and Immunogenicity of BCD-261 in Subjects With Moderate to Severe Active Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Biocad","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":198,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.6626619737418208,"rationale":"Anti-TL1A is now a validated mechanism in UC: tulisokibart, duvakitug and afimkibart all beat placebo on week 12–14 clinical remission in phase 2, typically by 15–25 percentage points over placebo rates of roughly 1–12%. With about 40 patients per arm across four BCD-261 dose arms and placebo, any one arm reaching significance would count, so power is reasonable if this Biocad antibody has potency comparable to the class. Remaining risks are uncertain potency and dosing of a new subcutaneous molecule, a possibly higher placebo response in Russian single-country sites, and small arm sizes. Primary completion is planned for 2027-01, and I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d490f766ff986061171c55e358708655d7b65eb326dc36f76df4a6d4373ac4b1"},{"nct":"NCT07144345","title":"Study of Reformulated Levulan Kerastick Plus PDT for Actinic Keratosis on Face and Scalp","sponsor":"Sun Pharmaceutical Industries, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":160,"base":0.94,"researched":null,"learned":0.8947393740422379,"rationale":"Levulan Kerastick (ALA 20%) with blue-light PDT is an approved AK therapy, and prior vehicle-controlled trials showed large effects: complete clearance of roughly 50-70% versus 5-30% for vehicle, including short-incubation (1-3 h) field-directed face/scalp studies. With about 40 patients per arm, 4-8 mild to moderate lesions per patient, and two possible PDT sessions, the trial is well powered even if a reformulation or shorter incubation trims the effect somewhat. The main risks are an unusually high vehicle-plus-light response or underpowered per-incubation-time comparisons, but one arm succeeding is very likely. The trial is still recruiting, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a62600278a578be120a03a0752ee0196a1c281d4509dc0059e978640396eab42"},{"nct":"NCT07144852","title":"Study of Reformulated Levulan Kerastick Plus PDT for Actinic Keratosis on Upper Extremities","sponsor":"Sun Pharmaceutical Industries, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":260,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.8601534715628176,"rationale":"Levulan Kerastick plus BLU-U blue-light PDT is already FDA-approved for AK, including the upper extremities, after a vehicle-controlled phase 3 that showed significantly higher complete clearance than vehicle PDT. This trial tests a reformulated version of the same 20% ALA product against vehicle, with up to two PDT sessions allowed, and about 260 patients is enough power even for a modest absolute difference in complete clearance. The main risks are a lower complete clearance rate on the extremities and the reformulation performing worse than expected, but a vehicle-controlled test of a proven photosensitizer usually succeeds. The primary completion date is in 2027, so no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3dc22aca2ffd06df1237458384b2952120eeb03b23b75aae083bc1a8b4afe291"},{"nct":"NCT07179640","title":"A Study to Assess Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of ALE1 in Healthy Adults and Adults With Hypophosphatasia in Order to Identify Suitable Doses of ALE1","sponsor":"Alesta Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":120,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.7906905511281401,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human Phase 1/2a SAD/MAD study whose primary endpoints are purely descriptive safety measures (TEAEs, labs, ECG, vital signs), with no formal efficacy comparison against placebo. Such trials are usually counted as meeting their primary endpoint when the drug proves acceptably safe and tolerable at the doses studied, which most oral small molecules do in short dosing. The main risks are unexpected toxicity, early termination, or a small sponsor losing funding. I have no knowledge of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"69b37b791d2a131657f0ddc24aa0d52a7a920226a6042f1d2953faaa527909d6"},{"nct":"NCT07205900","title":"Study to Evaluate HM15275 in Obese or Overweight Subjects Without Diabetes Mellitus","sponsor":"Hanmi Pharmaceutical Company Limited","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":267,"base":0.96,"researched":null,"learned":0.7181783925243485,"rationale":"HM15275 is Hanmi's GLP-1/GIP/glucagon triple agonist, a mechanism already validated by retatrutide's large weight-loss effects in phase 2, and early-phase data for HM15275 reportedly showed meaningful weight reduction. The primary endpoint is percent body-weight change versus placebo at 36 weeks, with about 53 participants per arm across four active doses, which gives ample power for the double-digit placebo-adjusted differences typical of incretin agonists. Failure would most likely require unexpected tolerability problems or high dropout, so success is very likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c674f7d05086f16f72f28d0863718e4ddbbac57c0656a0d01948841b80dc5c18"},{"nct":"NCT07323784","title":"A Study of NTX-1472 in Social Anxiety Disorder","sponsor":"Newleos Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":100,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.2759699941920672,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety and tolerability (TEAE incidence), so there is no formal superiority test. Sponsors of such trials usually announce that the drug was 'safe and well tolerated', and V1a antagonists like balovaptan have been well tolerated, which favors a 'met' outcome. However, if the result is judged on efficacy (LSAS change), the odds are lower: V1a antagonism is unproven in anxiety disorders, balovaptan failed in autism, and 100 patients over 8 weeks is modest against a high placebo response in SAD. Weighing the ambiguity between these readings gives a probability modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e409281048a1bca9b058a7b9c21d1ee25a0355df5aeaf3d15c9c9ebafe9a3b65"},{"nct":"NCT07478744","title":"A Phase 2a Efficacy, Safety, Tolerability, and PK Study of SYT-510 in Participants With Generalized Anxiety Disorder","sponsor":"Synendos Therapeutics AG","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":24,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.36320423039850763,"rationale":"SYT-510 is a first-in-class endocannabinoid reuptake inhibitor being tested in a small (n=24), single-dose, single-site experimental-medicine crossover. The first-listed primary endpoint is amygdala BOLD response to fearful faces, which is noisy at this sample size and after only one dose. Related endocannabinoid-enhancing drugs (FAAH inhibitors) have reduced amygdala reactivity in healthy volunteers, but only after repeated dosing and with mixed clinical translation. With many co-primary measures, a sponsor could claim a 'positive' signal on some of them, but a significant result on the first-listed fMRI outcome is less likely than not.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a8340ee52dc7b1b8a225310022abbbdc710f6e178cfcefed8c4e94d1ed028924"},{"nct":"NCT07481604","title":"Safety and Immunogenicity of CVI-VZV-001 in Adults Aged 50 Years and Above","sponsor":"Aribio Lab Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":135,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.7120418783206215,"rationale":"This is a small (n=135, about 45 per arm) dose-finding Phase 2 trial comparing an adjuvanted recombinant gE vaccine (CHA Vaccine Institute's CVI-VZV-001) against Shingrix, the highly immunogenic licensed comparator. The primary GMFR endpoint looks descriptive or exploratory ('explore differences'), and beating Shingrix on anti-gE GMFR with statistical significance would be unlikely for a new adjuvant platform. The sponsor might still frame 'comparable' immunogenicity as success, which adds some upside. Overall, a formal superiority or prespecified win appears unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8b217838d485fa77011d8d7fd99c8f94cb0fba8b215705e24a0d2ce41e9f3d6e"},{"nct":"NCT07505004","title":"Randomized Clinical Trial Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of Vormatrigine in Adults With Focal Seizures","sponsor":"Praxis Precision Medicines","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":300,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.8142471801215408,"rationale":"Vormatrigine is a next-generation sodium channel modulator, and sodium channel drugs (lacosamide, eslicarbazepine, cenobamate) have a strong record in adjunctive focal-seizure trials. The primary endpoint, median percent change in seizure frequency, is a standard and sensitive one. Phase 2 open-label data (RADIANT) showed robust seizure reductions, and with three dose arms including 40 mg, at least one arm succeeding is reasonably likely. The main risks are high placebo response in small US-only cohorts (~75 per arm across 7 sites) and uncertainty from the not-yet-public POWER1 result, which may have prompted adding the higher dose.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"efa53e142f0e2829386b968cd1a08d99ab1b730d7957121937affc5693db74f4"},{"nct":"NCT07505836","title":"Phase Ⅲ Trial of Group ACYW135 Meningococcal Conjugate Vaccine in Children Aged 12-23 Months","sponsor":"Sinovac Biotech Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":1040,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.8363970419243633,"rationale":"This is a Chinese non-inferiority immunogenicity trial of a MenACYW conjugate vaccine against a licensed CRM197 conjugate (CanSinoBIO Menhycia) in baseline-seronegative toddlers, a setting where conjugate vaccines typically produce very high seroconversion rates. Such trials usually meet their margins, and Sinovac has experience with meningococcal vaccines, so the base rate is high. The main risk is that non-inferiority must hold for all four serogroups on both seroconversion and GMT, and differences in carrier protein can produce a serogroup-specific shortfall, usually for Y or W135. Assuming a well-chosen dose, I put the probability of success near 88%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4d38a0e87f839d8b33329ba40a44ad6e0b33c2be0cf29fb68173db8f01ff3222"},{"nct":"NCT07565506","title":"Phase 2a Dose Finding Study of Nu-3 Gel in Subjects With Mild iDFU","sponsor":"Lakewood-Amedex Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":24,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.3603881305436613,"rationale":"This is a small (n=24), uncontrolled, three-dose Phase 2a study from a micro-cap sponsor, with a microbiological primary endpoint: the rate of ≥2-log CFU reduction per pathogen versus baseline. With no placebo arm and about 8 patients per arm, a formal statistically significant between-arm comparison is unlikely, so 'success' would rest mainly on the sponsor describing within-patient bacterial reductions as positive. Topical antimicrobials plus intensive debridement often reduce bacterial load substantially, and the earlier Nu-3 iDFU study reportedly showed microbial effects, which favours a positive-sounding readout. Against that, the absence of a formal hypothesis test, the risk of small or underpowered results, and enrollment or timing uncertainty keep the estimate below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b02d93aee070b41a4e1d454272cf93c9194241eda888a3b914ef92ab9c42a686"},{"nct":"NCT07576868","title":"A Study of CP-COV03 Compared With Placebo in Participants With Dengue (Part 1) and Dengue-like Illness (Part 2)","sponsor":"Hyundai Bioscience Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":210,"base":0.18,"researched":null,"learned":0.6571225786656938,"rationale":"CP-COV03 is Hyundai Bioscience's oral niclosamide formulation, and its earlier COVID-19 trials missed their primary endpoints. Dengue antivirals have a poor record: balapiravir, celgosivir, chloroquine and lovastatin all failed to reduce viremia in patients. Here the first efficacy endpoint is the Day 1–3 viral load AUC, with about 52 patients per arm against viremia that is already falling quickly on its own, which makes a significant result hard to reach. One of three doses beating placebo, plus possible flexible reporting, adds some chance, but the most likely outcome is no significant antiviral effect.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"97319292dcf213a369447c977503bc3ec6abb304879a4ba1c2325e1f56c7c831"},{"nct":"NCT07600736","title":"A Study to Investigate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics, and Clinical Activity of ABS-1230 in Pediatric and Young Adult Participants With KCNT1-related Epilepsy","sponsor":"Actio Biosciences, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":61,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3656980482768791,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is descriptive Part 1 safety, so the meaningful test is the Part 2 placebo-controlled comparison of percent change in motor seizure frequency. ABS-1230 is a first-in-class selective KCNT1 inhibitor in a severe developmental epileptic encephalopathy. Quinidine, an earlier and less selective KCNT1-targeting approach, failed in a controlled setting, though a precision mechanism in a genetically defined population could produce large effects. The randomized portion is very small (likely about 30–45 patients over 12 weeks), seizure counts in this population are highly variable, and novel-mechanism phase 2 epilepsy trials fail more often than they succeed, so I place this somewhat below even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c961b5d9ee9b6c8aa79ce24329473733ee5876e58fb65c09f5e7184fc98843b8"},{"nct":"NCT07614958","title":"Phase 3 Clinical Study Evaluating Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of Obicetrapib Vs Bempedoic Acid to Treat Dyslipidemia in Adults With Primary Non-familial Hypercholesterolemia or Mixed Dyslipidemia at High to Very High Cardiovascular Risk, During a Treatment Period of Approximately 84 Days","sponsor":"A. Menarini International Licensing S.A.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":426,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.8732025020145741,"rationale":"In placebo-controlled Phase 3 trials on top of statins (BROADWAY, BROOKLYN), obicetrapib 10 mg lowered LDL-C by about 30-35%. Bempedoic acid's placebo-adjusted effect on top of statins is about 17-18% (CLEAR Harmony), so obicetrapib should lead by roughly 12-18 percentage points. With about 213 patients per arm and a typical SD of 20-25%, power to show superiority in this short 12-week biomarker trial is very high. The main risks are operational (a single UK site, a still-recruiting trial run by the licensee Menarini) or an unexpectedly weak obicetrapib effect, but the record gives no sign of either.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0f53b1efc0f2572b1af5850a772491f02808e1f7a31a25b5aea3b0aa9984e900"},{"nct":"NCT07641634","title":"A Phase 1/2 Study of PRO-203 in Healthy Volunteers and Participants With Systemic Sclerosis.","sponsor":"Prolium Bioscience, Inc","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":44,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.3496734658973448,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human Phase 1/2 dose-escalation study whose primary endpoint is descriptive safety and tolerability, with no formal efficacy comparison. Such trials are usually reported as having met the endpoint when the drug proves acceptably tolerated and escalation completes. The step-up priming regimen suggests a B-cell-depleting T-cell engager, which carries real risks of cytokine release syndrome and infection. Still, healthy-volunteer Part 1 finished and the study moved on to systemic sclerosis patients, which supports acceptable early safety, and I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"92c2e6157fe162db1473d1f3c632d6adf9723c87d9026cffd8d9fb87342edf62"},{"nct":"NCT07694375","title":"A Study of CA201A Eye Drops to Prevent Corneal Endothelial Cell Loss in Patients Undergoing Cataract Surgery","sponsor":"Caravel Oculus Pty Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01","enrollment":200,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.3200417630510001,"rationale":"Ascorbate as an endothelial free-radical scavenger has some support from small studies: intravenous and intracameral ascorbic acid reduced endothelial cell loss after phacoemulsification of hard nuclei. Robust evidence for topical 5% drops is lacking, though, and aqueous ascorbate is already physiologically high, which may limit any added benefit. With about 100 patients per arm, the most damaging brunescent cataracts excluded, and the high variability of specular microscopy cell counts, the trial is powered only for a moderate effect. Given a roughly 30–40% base rate for phase 2 ophthalmology trials and a small sponsor, a modest probability is appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fcba6f3c6f820ecea994ffb000126b653332f319e6c0ea82c3e4155d83de71c6"},{"nct":"NCT07842991","title":"Clinical Evaluation of a Toothpaste for Dental Plaque Reduction and Prevention of Gum Problems","sponsor":"Colgate Palmolive","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01","enrollment":120,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.4727867398186456,"rationale":"Colgate runs many single-site six-month gingivitis and plaque trials of 0.45% stannous fluoride against a regular fluoride negative control, and these almost always show significant reductions in MGI, bleeding and plaque. The first-listed primary endpoint (MGI) compared against the negative control is a near-certain win given this proven technology and the sponsor's track record. The main uncertainty is whether the prespecified comparison is instead against the 67% bicarbonate (Parodontax-type) positive control, which would be harder to beat, but one arm succeeding against its control is enough here. With roughly 40 subjects per arm, power is adequate for the expected effect against the negative control.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"656303aaac172bc3fbf5fb4f7192ea36f333e5952185e03f7df5b808037b356c"},{"nct":"NCT04957485","title":"Study to Assess the Safety and Immunogenicity of TPOXX® When Administered Orally for 28 Days With JYNNEOS","sponsor":"SIGA Technologies","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-01","enrollment":100,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.595528507423982,"rationale":"This is a drug–vaccine interaction study, so a sponsor would count it a success if TPOXX does not meaningfully reduce JYNNEOS immunogenicity (antibody GMT non-inferiority) and adds no safety signal. Tecovirimat blocks VP37-mediated egress of enveloped virus, while MVA-based JYNNEOS is replication-deficient in human cells, and non-human primate data suggested little interference with MVA immunogenicity. So 'no interference' is mechanistically likely. The main uncertainty is how success is scored: the first-listed outcome is adverse-event counts, no non-inferiority margin is stated, and roughly 50 per arm limits precision, so I land moderately above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"62634143af2884202b05fa248b6cf98f2a7383c0dc0e17e840b60f09e8b0601a"},{"nct":"NCT07402369","title":"Phase II Study of CMS-D002 Capsule for Uterine Fibroids With Menorrhagia","sponsor":"Shenzhen Kangzhe Biotechnology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-03","enrollment":120,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8800694792571989,"rationale":"CMS-D002 from China Medical System's subsidiary is most likely an oral hormonal agent such as a GnRH antagonist or progesterone receptor modulator, though I cannot confirm the mechanism. Drugs in those classes (elagolix, relugolix, linzagolix, SPRMs) routinely achieve responder rates of about 70–90% on the MBL <80 mL with ≥50% reduction endpoint, against roughly 10–20% on placebo. With about 30 patients per arm, three doses, and only one dose needing to win, the trial has ample power if the drug is active. Remaining risk comes from the unconfirmed mechanism, possible underdosing, and single-site execution; results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b42074099dfc2a904aae2974d95b172baee2ac8b8bf79b2132cd230c0e816224"},{"nct":"NCT06641089","title":"Evaluation of Sonelokimab in Patients With Active Psoriatic Arthritis and Anti-TNFα Inadequate Response","sponsor":"MoonLake Immunotherapeutics AG","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-04","enrollment":600,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.9398950056968296,"rationale":"Sonelokimab is an IL-17A/F nanobody, a mechanism already validated in TNF-inadequate-responder psoriatic arthritis: bimekizumab's BE COMPLETE showed ACR50 of about 43% vs 7% for placebo. Sonelokimab's own Phase 2 ARGO trial showed a clear ACR50 separation from placebo. With about 600 patients, a placebo control and an objective-ish ACR50 endpoint, power is ample even allowing for some placebo inflation like that seen in MoonLake's VELA hidradenitis program. Primary completion is expected January 2027, so I do not believe results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"934b3ff42d71372e6148ea39a00b447818aeaa8bfd74848826e69c5877be673d"},{"nct":"NCT07000136","title":"A Phase III Study to Assess the Effect of AZD0780 on LDL-C in Patients With HeFH","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-04","enrollment":473,"base":0.97,"researched":null,"learned":0.8999174400345962,"rationale":"AZD0780 is an oral small-molecule PCSK9 inhibitor that cut LDL-C by about 50% versus placebo on top of statins in the phase IIb PURSUIT trial. Oral PCSK9 inhibitors such as enlicitide have also met LDL-C endpoints in phase III, including in HeFH (CORALreef HeFH). With roughly 470 patients randomised 2:1 and an expected placebo-adjusted LDL-C reduction of 40–50% at 12 weeks, the trial is overpowered, and HeFH patients respond well to PCSK9 inhibition because they are heterozygous. Topline results are not yet public, as primary completion is planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7e35b65cd1078da67295dfca89695d69a3c25396246c5a7b325968fcf50d83d9"},{"nct":"NCT07243171","title":"A Phase Ib/IIa Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of Oral Ecnoglutide Tablets in Chinese Participants With Overweight or Obesity","sponsor":"Hangzhou Sciwind Biosciences Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-05","enrollment":126,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8480935299706375,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is the incidence and severity of adverse events. That is descriptive safety with no prespecified superiority test, so 'success' effectively means the sponsor reports acceptable safety and tolerability, as is typical in Phase Ib/IIa topline announcements. Ecnoglutide is already validated as a subcutaneous GLP-1 agonist in Phase 3, and earlier oral formulation data from Sciwind suggested GI-dominated, manageable tolerability. The main risks are a dose-limiting GI or other safety signal at the higher oral doses, or ambiguity in how a safety-only endpoint gets scored. The trial is still recruiting with primary completion in 2027, so its results are not public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1410794407bdff5f0582859609d7186337cbb915aa96070b3d0343f9d7b89778"},{"nct":"NCT05925803","title":"Determine Effectiveness of Anifrolumab In SYstemic Sclerosis (DAISY)","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-06","enrollment":314,"base":0.28,"researched":null,"learned":0.6436721407341098,"rationale":"Systemic sclerosis has a poor track record in phase 3: tocilizumab (focuSSced), lenabasum (RESOLVE-1) and abatacept (ASSET) all missed their primary endpoints, and composite responder endpoints like CRISS can show high placebo responses, especially with background mycophenolate allowed. Anifrolumab is proven in SLE, and the type I IFN signature is elevated in a subset of SSc patients, but there is no randomized efficacy data in SSc, only small early-phase pharmacodynamic studies. The trial has a reasonable size (~314) and enriches for early, active, anticentromere-negative disease, but the effect of IFN blockade on skin and lung fibrosis is uncertain. Primary completion is January 2027, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2d31cda6fbb18230c6ad250bb784bf918685fb9a943d4ae0ad7effd951faf594"},{"nct":"NCT06401044","title":"A Study of AMG 732 in Healthy Participants and Participants With Thyroid Eye Disease","sponsor":"Amgen","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-06","enrollment":94,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6312966457027639,"rationale":"AMG 732 appears to be a subcutaneous IGF-1R–targeting antibody, a follow-on to teprotumumab; the exclusions for teprotumumab hypersensitivity and prior IGF-1R inhibitor use point to this mechanism. The mechanism is well validated in active TED, with proptosis reductions of roughly 2.5–3 mm versus placebo, and other subcutaneous IGF-1R agents have reported positive results. Part B is small (perhaps ~40–50 patients split across three doses plus placebo), and a phase 2 may be analyzed descriptively rather than with a formal test. Even so, the large expected effect size makes it likely that at least one dose shows a significant improvement over placebo.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c303f944892959ac65c2de72e221490d38d54d04a09730ab442a1a44ee7543c9"},{"nct":"NCT06481306","title":"A Study to Evaluate BMS-986470 in Healthy Volunteers and Participants With Sickle Cell Disease","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-06","enrollment":224,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.4322426316364907,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human Phase 1/2a trial of BMS-986470, an oral degrader of ZBTB7A/WIZ meant to induce fetal hemoglobin, and its first-listed primary endpoints are descriptive safety counts with no formal efficacy hypothesis test. Such trials are usually judged successful if the drug proves tolerable and shows pharmacodynamic activity. Early healthy-volunteer data reportedly showed dose-dependent HbF induction, and the program's progression to sickle cell disease cohorts suggests acceptable safety so far. Remaining risks are safety signals in the patient cohorts, such as myelosuppression from a molecular-glue degrader, and ambiguity over how a descriptive safety endpoint gets scored.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e51bf2da57355cdb640f4cf0a320a0c61f36d499689e370a23bb902119b6f46f"},{"nct":"NCT07218523","title":"A Study to Investigate Bowel Cleansing With PLENVU® Compared to Sodium Picosulfate in Participants Aged 1 to < 18 Years of Age in Preparation for Colonoscopy","sponsor":"Norgine","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-06","enrollment":212,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.7820034561696885,"rationale":"This is a pediatric (likely PIP-driven) Phase 3 comparing PLENVU (1L PEG-ascorbate) with sodium picosulfate, a well-tolerated active comparator. The primary outcome is worded descriptively ('to describe the success rate'), which suggests either no formal superiority test or a non-inferiority framing. Superiority over picosulfate is unlikely, but non-inferiority or numerically comparable cleansing is plausible given PLENVU's adult efficacy. The main risks are pediatric palatability and adherence problems with PLENVU, plus ambiguity about how a descriptive endpoint would be judged.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cededd290390f791a7cba52b4b1cbddd713727c1f417f1c2a8bc994854692a2e"},{"nct":"NCT07247188","title":"Study of a Single Dose of a 21-valent Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccine in Children and Adolescents With Sickle Cell Disease","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-07","enrollment":100,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.5794669141890456,"rationale":"This is a small (n=100), descriptive Phase 3 safety and immunogenicity study of Sanofi/SK bioscience's PCV21 against Prevnar 20 in children with sickle cell disease, and none of the primary outcomes appears to carry a formal superiority or non-inferiority hypothesis. Earlier PCV21 (SP0202) data showed robust immunogenicity and acceptable reactogenicity, and special-population studies like this one are usually reported as favorable or supportive. The main uncertainty is how a descriptive outcome will be scored, plus a small chance of a safety or immunogenicity signal in this population. I estimate a moderately high probability that the result will be read as meeting its primary objectives.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f3ce2f65ee5f5d79db1964d99381d1190b7bf5f062e52e55342eed3814c83874"},{"nct":"NCT05221840","title":"A Global Study to Assess the Effects of Durvalumab With Oleclumab or Durvalumab With Monalizumab Following Concurrent Chemoradiation in Patients With Stage III Unresectable Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-08","enrollment":1051,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.6476365436462839,"rationale":"PACIFIC-9 tests whether adding a CD73 antibody (oleclumab) or an NKG2A antibody (monalizumab) to consolidation durvalumab improves PFS, based on the small, open-label phase 2 COAST trial (PFS HRs about 0.4). Such phase 2 signals for IO add-ons to PD-(L)1 have repeatedly failed to hold up in phase 3: IDO, TIGIT in SKYSCRAPER, and monalizumab's own INTERLINK-1 failure in head and neck cancer. Oleclumab has also been deprioritized elsewhere. Having two arms gives two chances, and the control arm is well characterized, but the base rate for novel IO combinations beating active PD-L1 therapy in phase 3 is low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fb19fe926608530319ae785831a1201e57e76ed8eee31e3a1cff848ea4321583"},{"nct":"NCT06495918","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Intravitreal OTX-TKI (Axitinib Implant) in Subjects With Neovascular Age- Related Macular Degeneration","sponsor":"Ocular Therapeutix, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-08","enrollment":825,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.73701330107262,"rationale":"This appears to be SOL-R, a non-inferiority trial of OTX-TKI (Axpaxli) redosed about every 24 weeks versus aflibercept 2 mg every 8 weeks, with a likely margin of about 4.5 letters on BCVA change and a large sample. Non-inferiority trials of durable anti-VEGF approaches against on-label aflibercept have usually succeeded. Phase 1/2 data for OTX-TKI showed BCVA roughly maintained compared with aflibercept, and a similar TKI implant (EYP-1901) met non-inferiority in phase 2. The main risks are less potent VEGF suppression from a TKI depot causing gradual vision loss before redosing, and the dilution caused by rescue rules, so the forecast sits moderately above the base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"806c92cc66176515a7d59d1579a89e09f18d9f60999167fb0077b7677c6d3300"},{"nct":"NCT07673029","title":"A Trial Comparing GQ1005 and T-DM1 in Patients With HER2-Positive Unresectable or Metastatic Breast Cancer","sponsor":"GeneQuantum Healthcare (Suzhou) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-09","enrollment":228,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.7029632949815687,"rationale":"GQ1005 is a HER2-targeted ADC carrying a DXd-type topoisomerase-I payload, tested here in the setting where DESTINY-Breast03 showed trastuzumab deruxtecan beating T-DM1 with an HR of about 0.28. Several Chinese HER2-ADC analogues have since beaten T-DM1 on PFS in similar second-line trials. Even a much smaller effect (HR about 0.5) should be detectable with 228 patients. The main risks are unproven differences in GQ1005's conjugation, potency or toxicity, and possible underpowering if its effect is modest; no topline result is known.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"85106c5ce9d617bf4620bb2a05cfde1678798f07980df0459f4e7fa3cb5bd0bd"},{"nct":"NCT05519085","title":"A Study to Evaluate Mezigdomide, Bortezomib and Dexamethasone (MEZIVd) Versus Pomalidomide, Bortezomib and Dexamethasone (PVd) in Participants With Relapsed or Refractory Multiple Myeloma (RRMM)","sponsor":"Celgene","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-10","enrollment":810,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.7277646544589863,"rationale":"Mezigdomide is a more potent CELMoD than pomalidomide, with preclinical activity in IMiD-resistant disease and high response rates for MeziVd in phase 1/2 lenalidomide-exposed cohorts. That makes a PFS advantage over PVd (median about 11 months in OPTIMISMM) plausible in this 810-patient trial. Against that, it is an active head-to-head comparison within the same mechanism, neutropenia may limit dose intensity, and phase 3 trials in myeloma fail fairly often even with strong early data. I am not aware of any topline readout, and the trial is still recruiting with primary completion planned for 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0aef3c78900c336e062d1f9f7aa9f9636e62ebc546579c6c466038a69cc3bedd"},{"nct":"NCT06177041","title":"M108 Plus CAPOX Versus Placebo Plus CAPOX as First-line Treatment for Claudin (CLDN) 18.2-Positive, HER2-Negative, PD-L1 CPS<5, Locally Advanced Unresectable or Metastatic Gastric or Gastroesophageal Junction (GEJ) Adenocarcinoma.","sponsor":"FutureGen Biopharmaceutical (Beijing) Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-11","enrollment":486,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.6252894824995398,"rationale":"M108 (FG-M108) is an Fc-enhanced anti-CLDN18.2 antibody, a mechanism already validated in first-line HER2-negative gastric cancer: zolbetuximab met PFS in both SPOTLIGHT and GLOW, and GLOW used this same CAPOX backbone (HR ~0.69). The trial is placebo-controlled, has a PFS primary endpoint and enrolls 486 patients, which should give adequate power for an effect of that size. Restricting to PD-L1 CPS<5 avoids the immunotherapy comparator problem. Risks remain: the CLDN18.2 positivity cutoff may be lower and dilute the benefit, and earlier M108 data are limited to small single-arm studies from a smaller sponsor, so I put this somewhat above the base rate for validated-mechanism follow-ons.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1915d221f3ace3f1dbb8d69e15255792a5f250032935987271706bd1bc6ad3fa"},{"nct":"NCT06417814","title":"A Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Dato-DXd With or Without Osimertinib Compared With Platinum Based Doublet Chemotherapy in Participants With EGFR-Mutated Locally Advanced or Metastatic Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-11","enrollment":768,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.7897443607786236,"rationale":"Dato-DXd showed meaningful activity in EGFR-mutated NSCLC after osimertinib (TROPION-Lung05, ORR around 43%, leading to accelerated approval). Other ADCs have beaten platinum-pemetrexed on PFS in this post-TKI setting (sac-TMT in OptiTROP-Lung04; HER3-DXd modestly in HERTHENA-Lung02). Platinum-pemetrexed has a modest median PFS of about 5 months, and the trial has two shots on goal; the osimertinib combination arm is especially likely to show a PFS benefit. The main risks are that Dato-DXd alone may give PFS similar to chemotherapy and that toxicity in an open-label design could cut into the benefit, but one arm succeeding counts.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dbea20ed99fdc198579541a4fc207551d76a43d435c5b5870b0b36d81eb2918d"},{"nct":"NCT06957080","title":"A Study of 2 Doses of Remigromig (EYE103) Compared With Ranibizumab (0.5 mg) in Participants With DME","sponsor":"EyeBiotech Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-01-11","enrollment":1054,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8448802838470908,"rationale":"Remigromig (EYE103/Restoret, now Merck's MK-3000) is a multispecific antibody that activates the Wnt/Frizzled-4 pathway and also blocks VEGF. The first-listed primary endpoint appears to be non-inferiority in BCVA change at week 52 against monthly ranibizumab, with superiority listed as a secondary outcome. Because both arms are dosed monthly in year 1 and the drug carries its own anti-VEGF activity, matching ranibizumab within a typical ~4-letter margin is likely, and early-phase AMARONE data reportedly showed good visual gains. The main risks are an unexpected safety or immunogenicity problem, a dose-related shortfall, or tight margins in a large trial, though one of two doses succeeding is enough.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c288b31bd663b6a4e0ad1fa461690b01ac08b05b111ef139cc3c84b20d49746d"},{"nct":"NCT07000123","title":"A Phase III Study to Assess the Effect of AZD0780 on LDL-C in Patients With Clinical ASCVD or at Risk for a First ASCVD Event","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-11","enrollment":3103,"base":0.98,"researched":null,"learned":0.863449485873534,"rationale":"AZD0780 is an oral PCSK9 inhibitor that cut LDL-C by about 50% versus placebo on top of statins in the phase 2b PURSUIT trial. This is a large placebo-controlled phase III trial (about 3,100 participants) with a biomarker primary endpoint (percent change in LDL-C at 12 weeks), so statistical success is nearly certain if the drug is active. Merck's oral PCSK9 inhibitor enlicitide recently succeeded in similar phase III trials, which supports the mechanism. The remaining risk is mainly operational or safety-driven, and topline results are not yet public, with primary completion planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ba0d3488641d9b25d266579a345927015e571949f5058e1cbfc6252688547023"},{"nct":"NCT05609968","title":"Study of Pembrolizumab (MK-3475) Monotherapy Versus Sacituzumab Govitecan in Combination With Pembrolizumab for Participants With Metastatic Non-small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) With Programmed Cell Death Ligand 1 (PD-L1) Tumor Proportion Score (TPS) ≥50% (MK-3475-D46)","sponsor":"Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-12","enrollment":614,"base":0.64,"researched":null,"learned":0.7294736333025166,"rationale":"EVOKE-03 tests whether adding sacituzumab govitecan to pembrolizumab beats pembrolizumab alone in first-line PD-L1 ≥50% NSCLC, with BICR PFS as the first-listed primary endpoint. In general, adding a cytotoxic payload to pembrolizumab in PD-L1-high disease tends to improve PFS, and EVOKE-02 showed a high response rate (~67–69%) in this subgroup. Against that, EVOKE-01 failed in second-line NSCLC, TROP-2 ADCs have shown only modest single-agent lung activity, and toxicity and dose reductions could blunt the benefit. With about 614 patients and an open-label design, a PFS win is more likely than not; OS would be harder, but PFS is the endpoint scored here.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f40a5088ed779ba37d8d349be0f2a6039a3942846d866154f73261be1ecfdc9b"},{"nct":"NCT05952206","title":"Ischemic and Bleeding Outcomes After Angiolite Stent Implantation and an Abbreviated Dual Antiplatelet Therapy","sponsor":"iVascular S.L.U.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-13","enrollment":2312,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5946023326993168,"rationale":"The first-listed primary endpoint is non-inferiority on 12-month target lesion failure for Angiolite, a thin-strut cobalt-chromium sirolimus-eluting stent, versus Xience. Contemporary thin-strut drug-eluting stents nearly always meet non-inferiority against Xience in all-comer trials, and Angiolite has already shown comparable outcomes to Xience in earlier randomized and registry studies. With about 1,150 patients per stent arm and expected TLF around 5–6%, a typical absolute margin of about 3% leaves reasonable power, though the margin is not stated and event rates could be higher than planned. No results are public yet; primary completion is planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"aeb516807c4cabf190b6017b2533af1b771fc3b66788a54df98d9fd1e8f17487"},{"nct":"NCT06951503","title":"AK112 and Chemotherapy in First-line Metastatic Colorectal Cancer","sponsor":"Akeso","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-13","enrollment":560,"base":0.47,"researched":null,"learned":0.5857950168317694,"rationale":"AK112 (ivonescimab, a PD-1/VEGF bispecific) has won Akeso-run Chinese phase 3 trials in NSCLC, including head-to-head studies, and early phase 2 data with FOLFOXIRI in first-line mCRC showed high response rates. However, the population is mostly MSS colorectal cancer, where adding PD-1 blockade to chemo plus bevacizumab has given inconsistent results: AtezoTRIBE showed a modest PFS gain, but CheckMate 9X8 failed. The trial must beat an active bevacizumab comparator on BICR-assessed PFS, which is a demanding bar, though Akeso's strong execution record and the 560-patient sample give it a reasonable chance.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ce6bd8a8734e89a1ef6e8dbfd869a85b679254f2ca0f59ab0244b65244ec062d"},{"nct":"NCT07261644","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of 608 in Adult Subjects With Active Ankylosing Spondylitis(AS)","sponsor":"Sunshine Guojian Pharmaceutical (Shanghai) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-14","enrollment":500,"base":0.92,"researched":null,"learned":0.8739879964417623,"rationale":"608 is Sunshine Guojian's anti-IL-17A monoclonal antibody, a mechanism already validated in ankylosing spondylitis. Secukinumab and ixekizumab, and Chinese IL-17A agents such as xeligekimab and gumokimab, have consistently beaten placebo on ASAS40 at week 16, typically by 15–25 percentage points. With about 500 patients randomized against placebo, power to detect an effect of that size is very high, and 608 has already shown efficacy in psoriasis. Primary completion is planned for January 2027, so no result is public yet; the residual risk lies mainly in execution, a high placebo response, or the dose chosen.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0f39a1cd50a03296142a3a90e2730a17e48b4f57cb9bb055790d6cbb7ce35066"},{"nct":"NCT07395687","title":"A Research Study on How Well Different Doses of the Medicine UBT251 Help People Living With Overweight or Obesity","sponsor":"Novo Nordisk A/S","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-14","enrollment":333,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8744164716810177,"rationale":"UBT251 is a GLP-1/GIP/glucagon triple agonist licensed from United Laboratories, and early Chinese studies reportedly showed substantial weight loss. Incretin-class agonists almost always beat placebo on percent body-weight change over 28 weeks, so Part B's efficacy comparison is very likely to be significant. The first-listed primary outcome (Part A TEAEs) is descriptive safety with no hypothesis test, which makes it unclear how the trial will be scored. The main uncertainty is therefore resolution ambiguity rather than drug efficacy, and I know of no public topline result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"569a37d0fcf5b06f1a00c6e12e7d58f2e9a736635909a7e988058fa66e80067c"},{"nct":"NCT04199689","title":"Efficacy Against Oral Persistent Infection, Immunogenicity and Safety of the 9-valent Human Papillomavirus Vaccine (9vHPV) in Men Aged 20-45 Years (V503-049)","sponsor":"Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-15","enrollment":6033,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.6575386906682423,"rationale":"Gardasil 9 and its quadrivalent predecessor are highly effective against persistent HPV infection at genital and anal sites in HPV-naive people, and observational data suggest vaccination cuts oral HPV prevalence by roughly 80-90%. The main risks are a low incidence of persistent oral infection, which could leave the trial with few events even with about 6,000 men and long follow-up, and possibly a prespecified success criterion requiring a vaccine-efficacy lower bound above some threshold. Oral rinse PCR may also pick up transient deposition rather than true infection. I do not recall the primary result being public; primary completion is planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e32d2137142d4bfffb361c31b00c091911be9ca619c699673e26b05aee07e0af"},{"nct":"NCT05608291","title":"A Trial to See if the Combination of Fianlimab With Cemiplimab Works Better Than Pembrolizumab for Preventing or Delaying Melanoma From Coming Back After it Has Been Removed With Surgery","sponsor":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-15","enrollment":1564,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.7810446844975872,"rationale":"The closest precedent, BMS's RELATIVITY-098, tested adjuvant relatlimab plus nivolumab against nivolumab in resected melanoma and failed to improve relapse-free survival, which is a strong negative signal for adding a LAG-3 antibody in this setting. Fianlimab plus cemiplimab produced impressive phase 1 response rates in metastatic melanoma, but beating an active anti-PD-1 comparator in the adjuvant setting is a hard bar. The trial is large and allows two fianlimab dose arms, which modestly raises the chance that one arm succeeds. Overall, I estimate a below-base-rate probability of success.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"612d36c30f8e21e8aeb81312e635267a583cf6fb1ca05f999745389abff52b5a"},{"nct":"NCT05987332","title":"IDE196 (Darovasertib) in Combination With Crizotinib as First-line Therapy in Metastatic Uveal Melanoma","sponsor":"IDEAYA Biosciences","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-01-15","enrollment":420,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.790199903074664,"rationale":"The first comparative efficacy endpoint is Phase 2 PFS by BICR for darovasertib plus crizotinib against investigator's choice of pembrolizumab, ipilimumab plus nivolumab, or dacarbazine, all of which give a median PFS of only about 2–3 months in metastatic uveal melanoma. Single-arm first-line data for the combination showed an objective response rate of about 30–45% and a median PFS of about 7 months, suggesting a large hazard-ratio effect that a trial of this size should detect. Risks include open-label bias being controlled by BICR, possible overestimation from single-arm selection, and the OS endpoint being harder, but the PFS comparison looks highly likely to succeed. I do not reliably recall a public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ef6140e15961ad260cec6b5ae57668767840db01ca2b42956c048f378ad57add"},{"nct":"NCT06764940","title":"A Pivotal Phase II Clinical Trial of Utidelone Injection Plus Capecitabine in HER2-negative Breast Cancer Patients With Brain Metastases","sponsor":"Biostar Pharma, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-15","enrollment":120,"base":0.57,"researched":null,"learned":0.3669377787483469,"rationale":"This is an essentially single-arm pivotal phase II design: stage 1 compares experimental arms only, and stage 2 is single-arm, so success most likely means the IC-ORR confidence bound clearing a prespecified historical threshold rather than beating a control. Earlier Chinese phase II data for utidelone, alone and with capecitabine or bevacizumab, in breast cancer brain metastases reported encouraging intracranial response rates of roughly 30–40%+, which supports a reasonable chance of clearing a modest bar. Against that, the US population is more heavily pretreated, the sponsor is a small company running a 12-site trial, the threshold and power are not disclosed, and enrollment or execution risk is real. On balance this sits slightly above even odds, and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2a5da23b3b41e3f84c86106500521f2e5668f202e923d85de9d07897700f53c9"},{"nct":"NCT06265727","title":"A Phase 1/2 Study to Investigate CRB-701 in Solid Tumors","sponsor":"Corbus Pharmaceuticals Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-16","enrollment":348,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.5144590758218587,"rationale":"This is an open-label, single-arm Phase 1/2 dose-escalation and expansion study with no control arm, so 'success' means defining an MTD/recommended dose and showing meaningful ORR rather than winning a statistical comparison. Corbus has publicly reported interim data for CRB-701 showing a manageable MMAE-type safety profile and encouraging response rates in Nectin-4-expressing tumors such as HNSCC and cervical cancer. Nectin-4 is also a validated ADC target, given enfortumab vedotin's approval. The main uncertainties are how 'meeting the primary endpoint' will be judged for a non-comparative design and whether ORR holds up across the expansion cohorts. Final results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c34c39ab177dbfc837a8a855a053a0652874e3b5495ac3acf408b87edeb1fc36"},{"nct":"NCT07102628","title":"Evaluation of Efficacy and Safety of Early in Hospital Initiation of Inclisiran Treatment in Patients With Acute Coronary Syndromes","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-16","enrollment":305,"base":0.97,"researched":null,"learned":0.8141322570438786,"rationale":"Inclisiran has consistently cut LDL-C by about 50% versus placebo across the ORION trials. In ACS patients started on high-intensity statins, the VICTORION-INCEPTION and AMUNDSEN-type data also showed large placebo-adjusted reductions. With 305 patients and percent change in LDL-C at Day 150 as the primary endpoint, the trial has overwhelming power even though statin up-titration in both arms will lower LDL in the placebo group too. The main risks are operational or analytic quirks, not the drug's effect, and I am not aware of a published result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3d001ec5e82ea3adebc49a3d8f3c817d4e395338a7a6948e3bf24d9b63a54c6c"},{"nct":"NCT05035212","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Immunogenicity, and Safety of RSVpreF in Adults.","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-18","enrollment":38861,"base":0.99,"researched":null,"learned":0.7693815403507014,"rationale":"This is the RENOIR trial of Pfizer's RSVpreF (Abrysvo) in adults aged 60 and older. Its first-season interim analysis, published in NEJM in 2023, showed vaccine efficacy of about 67% against LRTI-RSV with 2 or more symptoms and about 86% with 3 or more symptoms, meeting the prespecified success criteria. Those results supported FDA approval in May 2023. The registry still lists primary completion as 2027 only because of the revaccination substudies, so the first-listed efficacy endpoint has effectively already been met.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"ffe2c9a8b0b201dbaf263cbfe99f86990131f645f09c30d317e93daadb8ff147"},{"nct":"NCT06686654","title":"Study of a Human Metapneumovirus/Respiratory Syncytial Virus mRNA Vaccine Candidate Encapsulated in a Lipid Nanoparticle-based Formulation in Adults Aged 60 Years and Older","sponsor":"Sanofi Pasteur, a Sanofi Company","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-18","enrollment":1530,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.7546527053547184,"rationale":"This Phase 1/2 dose-ranging study's first-listed primary outcomes are descriptive safety counts plus GMT immunogenicity measures, with no prespecified hypothesis test against placebo. Such trials are usually judged successful if the vaccine is tolerable and immunogenic. mRNA RSV vaccines (e.g., Moderna's mRESVIA) and hMPV mRNA candidates have consistently raised neutralizing titers in older adults, so immunogenicity versus placebo is very likely. The main risks are ambiguity in how a descriptive endpoint gets scored, reactogenicity concerns in older adults, and Sanofi's own changing mRNA portfolio priorities.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b6138f22890930948c88b79ce412dc6f473058b027ef40e83b497c1daee96c74"},{"nct":"NCT05170204","title":"A Study Evaluating the Efficacy and Safety of Multiple Therapies in Cohorts of Participants With Locally Advanced, Unresectable, Stage III Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-19","enrollment":68,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.6687854229645646,"rationale":"This is Roche's biomarker-selected stage III NSCLC platform, with cohort A1 comparing alectinib against durvalumab consolidation after chemoradiotherapy in ALK-positive disease. Close analogs strongly favor the targeted drug: LAURA (osimertinib after chemoradiotherapy, EGFR-positive) had a PFS hazard ratio of about 0.16, and ALINA (adjuvant alectinib) about 0.24, while ALK-positive tumors gain little from PD-(L)1 consolidation. The main risk is the small enrollment of 68 with cohort A2 closed, which suggests slow accrual and possibly a reduced or descriptive analysis. Still, a hazard ratio near 0.2 to 0.3 should give a significant result even with few events.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"cedb4423bac56a29992fb9ef1d9c1853bd02a803c4c785393922fb09a5836a25"},{"nct":"NCT06053242","title":"Safety, Tolerability, and Effectiveness of Intramuscular Injection of CELZ-201-DDT for the Treatment of Chronic Lower Back Pain","sponsor":"Creative Medical Technology Holdings Inc","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-20","enrollment":45,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.6708215869492771,"rationale":"The only primary endpoint is safety: the incidence of grade 3/4 or serious adverse events at 6 months in a small (n=45) dose-escalation study of allogeneic cell injections into paraspinal muscle. There is no prespecified efficacy comparison, so a sponsor topline would likely say the endpoint was met if no meaningful safety signal emerged, which is common for local MSC-type cell injections. The main risks are a safety signal at the higher doses, or the microcap sponsor failing to complete or report the trial. I know of no public primary result, and primary completion is planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1707b14f5b06808287a34c90be5693638092f9992c9c45a803e15b37e485add9"},{"nct":"NCT05877963","title":"Study to Evaluate Safety, Efficacy and Pharmacokinetics (PK) of a Modified Regimen of Ublituximab","sponsor":"TG Therapeutics, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-21","enrollment":800,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7522189580076004,"rationale":"The first-listed primary endpoint is a single-arm, descriptive measure in Parts A and C: the percentage of participants with no change or reduction in T1 Gd-enhancing lesions. Ublituximab is an approved anti-CD20 drug that almost completely suppresses these lesions, so nearly all participants should qualify. Part B's PK endpoint compares exposure between two ublituximab regimens, which is likely to show comparable or adequate exposure. The main risks are ambiguity about how a descriptive or PK endpoint would be judged 'met' and somewhat weaker results in the Part C anti-CD20 suboptimal-responder group, while interim Part A data I recall were favorable but the final primary result is not public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5515d295f564090052d55bf20f39ca0a28e6e26351eadd4d2159d3cf05d4dff2"},{"nct":"NCT06858839","title":"Evaluation of Maridebart Cafraglutide in Adult Participants Without Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Who Have Obesity or Are Overweight","sponsor":"Amgen","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-21","enrollment":3853,"base":0.99,"researched":null,"learned":0.9384390176681393,"rationale":"MARITIME-1 is a large Phase 3 trial of a GLP-1 agonist/GIPR antagonist antibody against placebo over 72 weeks. In Phase 2, MariTide produced roughly 16-20% mean weight loss at 52 weeks versus about 2.6% on placebo in people without diabetes. With nearly 4,000 participants and three dose arms, statistical superiority on percent weight change is nearly certain; the main uncertainties are tolerability-driven discontinuation and the size of the effect, neither of which threatens significance. Primary completion is January 2027, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ede01504f727f48ddcd4de7d63e2a5b06bc805fa97cd22f39d976c23ff55a83a"},{"nct":"NCT06858878","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Maridebart Cafraglutide in Adult Participants With Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Who Have Obesity or Are Overweight","sponsor":"Amgen","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-21","enrollment":1105,"base":0.98,"researched":null,"learned":0.9419391891195195,"rationale":"In the Phase 2 T2D cohort, maridebart cafraglutide produced roughly 15-17% mean weight loss at 52 weeks versus about 1-2% on placebo. This trial randomizes about 1,100 participants to three doses against placebo over 72 weeks, so it is heavily powered for a large, well-established incretin-class effect. Tolerability-driven discontinuation could shrink the treatment-policy estimand, but it is very unlikely to erase statistical significance. Primary completion is not until January 2027, so I do not believe results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dff3e3002b6e310f4949c654481e0c3e9a6b42b0d532819a865e18e614744216"},{"nct":"NCT07169695","title":"A Study to Compare the Effectiveness and Safety of T1695 Versus Ciclosporin in Participants With Moderate to Severe Vernal Keratoconjunctivitis","sponsor":"Laboratoires Thea","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-21","enrollment":120,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3332895665793642,"rationale":"This is a 120-patient, investigator-masked phase 2 trial in India comparing T1695, an undisclosed Théa ophthalmic suspension, with active ciclosporin (likely Verkazia, already effective in VKC) on change in corneal staining at week 4. Beating a proven active comparator with statistical significance at this sample size is hard, and phase 2 active-controlled ophthalmology trials are often analysed descriptively or with an estimation focus rather than formally powered for superiority. If the prespecified test is non-inferiority, success would be more likely, but the record does not say so. I put the probability modestly below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4c3f319d147cd390c7e82e50d9c842ea177412b2b335b03edb905cad6051df70"},{"nct":"NCT07097701","title":"An Open-Label, Randomized, Cross-Over Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Mexiletine PR Compared to Mexiletine IR","sponsor":"Lupin Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-22","enrollment":24,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.7976338875324253,"rationale":"The primary outcome is a descriptive safety comparison (TEAEs and ECG intervals) of a prolonged-release reformulation against the same active drug, in a small open-label crossover of 24 patients at a single Belgian site. No efficacy hypothesis or prespecified test is stated, so a significant superiority result is very unlikely, but the sponsor would probably describe comparable safety as a success. How \"meeting the endpoint\" gets adjudicated is therefore ambiguous, which keeps this forecast near the middle. The trial is still recruiting, with primary completion planned for January 2027, and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4f76096559ee2d813d97d7d5c2cf8367cbdc0450f2e11c9c0146b9c6e72db393"},{"nct":"NCT07076199","title":"A Research Study to See How a Weekly Insulin, Insulin Icodec, Helps in Reducing the Blood Sugar Compared to Daily Insulin Glargine, Both in Combination With Insulin Aspart, in Adults With Type 1 Diabetes","sponsor":"Novo Nordisk A/S","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-25","enrollment":877,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.884271254460451,"rationale":"This appears to be Novo Nordisk's new type 1 diabetes trial after the FDA turned down icodec for T1D over hypoglycaemia; the primary endpoint is almost certainly HbA1c non-inferiority versus glargine U100, probably with a 0.3% margin. In ONWARDS 6, icodec met non-inferiority on HbA1c against degludec (estimated difference about 0.05%), and HbA1c non-inferiority with a margin this wide is rarely missed by a comparable basal insulin. The main risk is that a more conservative, hypoglycaemia-focused titration lowers icodec's glycaemic efficacy. With about 877 participants there is ample power, so success is likely; primary completion is January 2027 and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5383922a66301d04870d3c7b789e0d05b73ba05e04a4ea8386eb0e705df43198"},{"nct":"NCT07653100","title":"A Phase 3 Study in India to Describe the Safety and Immunogenicity of RSVpreF","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-25","enrollment":540,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.6963367702560693,"rationale":"This is a descriptive Phase 3 safety and immunogenicity bridging study of Pfizer's already-approved RSVpreF (Abrysvo) in Indian adults, with no formal hypothesis test. RSVpreF has consistently produced robust neutralizing titer rises against both RSV A and B versus placebo, with acceptable reactogenicity, across prior trials. The main uncertainty is how a descriptive safety endpoint gets scored, since local reactions will be higher in the vaccine arm and that is not 'favoring' the vaccine in a superiority sense. Such trials are usually read as successful when they report results in line with the known profile, and primary completion is not until January 2027, so no result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b825db816af8178fc0642fb71e5963d8a7e9341fbdc7e35c51847dcf754c680c"},{"nct":"NCT05757102","title":"A Study to Compare the Efficacy, Safety and Tolerability of FF/UMEC/VI With FF/VI in 12-17-year-olds With Asthma","sponsor":"GlaxoSmithKline","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-26","enrollment":138,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.8827609107093342,"rationale":"In adults, the CAPTAIN trial showed FF/UMEC/VI improved trough FEV1 over FF/VI by about 90–110 mL. Tiotropium add-on trials in adolescents showed similar modest gains, though results were inconsistent. With only about 69 patients per arm, a frequentist test would be underpowered for an effect of about 100 mL, but the Bayesian dynamic-borrowing design pulls in adult data, which makes declaring success much easier unless the adolescent results diverge. Primary completion is not due until 2027 and no results are public, so I put the probability modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7bac801023b030fb9d6594a7238351f1cc66bd953a5d79718abc974c05f2f093"},{"nct":"NCT05038735","title":"Study to Assess the Efficacy and Safety of Alpelisib Plus Fulvestrant in Participants With HR-positive (HR+), HER2-negative, Advanced Breast Cancer After Treatment With a CDK4/6 Inhibitor and an Aromatase Inhibitor.","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-28","enrollment":210,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.7371655789968511,"rationale":"Alpelisib plus fulvestrant already showed a PFS benefit in PIK3CA-mutant disease in SOLAR-1 (HR about 0.65), and the single-arm BYLieve study showed activity after CDK4/6 inhibitors. Other PI3K/AKT-pathway agents (capivasertib in CAPItello-291, inavolisib in INAVO120) succeeded in post-CDK4/6 settings where fulvestrant alone gives a median PFS of only about 2 months, so an HR near 0.5–0.6 is plausible. With 210 patients, power against that effect looks reasonable. The main uncertainties are Protocol Amendment 5, which ends the placebo once participants are unblinded and may signal a truncated or modified study, and toxicity-driven dose reductions or discontinuations diluting the effect.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"381a89616584725f16e0ac278fe853c6fedfc3d8978eb7f042825fdc01b1a3f1"},{"nct":"NCT07496450","title":"A Study of mRNA-1018-H5 Pandemic Influenza Vaccine in Healthy Adults","sponsor":"ModernaTX, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-28","enrollment":4050,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.7987094393014565,"rationale":"Moderna's Phase 1/2 data for mRNA-1018 (H5 clade 2.3.4.4b) reportedly showed strong HAI responses, with large GMT rises and most participants reaching titers ≥1:40 after two doses. Against placebo, the immunogenicity primary endpoints are almost certain to be met. The main risk is if success is judged against CBER accelerated-approval thresholds (e.g., lower 95% CI bound ≥70% seroprotection and ≥40% seroconversion), which unadjuvanted H5 vaccines have historically struggled to reach, particularly in older adults. Given the prior mRNA-1018 data, that risk looks modest, and results are not yet public (primary completion is January 2027).","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"24a1e4ec6b682819c30a607918d235ce78236abf8e62de51bc1d8cf3afaefec4"},{"nct":"NCT04544189","title":"Study Assessing the Efficacy and Safety of Treatment With Alpelisib Plus Fulvestrant Versus Placebo Plus Fulvestrant in Chinese Men and Postmenopausal Women With Advanced Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":69,"base":0.35,"researched":null,"learned":0.3423511449172394,"rationale":"Alpelisib plus fulvestrant has a proven PFS benefit in PIK3CA-mutant HR+/HER2- advanced breast cancer, with SOLAR-1 showing HR about 0.65. This Chinese bridging study, however, enrolled only 69 patients in total, including roughly 15 in the PK cohort, which leaves about 54 randomized against a planned ~105. With perhaps 40 events, formal two-sided significance would need an observed HR of roughly 0.55 or lower, giving power of only about 30–40% even if the true effect is similar to or slightly better than SOLAR-1's. The direction of effect is very likely favorable, but statistical significance is uncertain given the shortfall in enrollment.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ebb7c596313da1acfa3fad1ba795e2770c2d4049779f2dddb00773d48e081145"},{"nct":"NCT04817618","title":"Study of Efficacy and Safety of Iptacopan in Patients With C3 Glomerulopathy.","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":98,"base":0.96,"researched":null,"learned":0.7617740630213449,"rationale":"This is APPEAR-C3G, Novartis's pivotal Phase 3 trial of iptacopan in C3G. The adult cohort, which is the first-listed primary endpoint, reported in 2024 a statistically significant 35.1% placebo-adjusted reduction in 24-hour UPCR at 6 months (p≈0.0014). That result supported FDA approval of Fabhalta for C3G in 2025. The record remains open only for the added adolescent cohort, so the residual risk is mainly in how the outcome gets adjudicated.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"0c43786b95cfa1e6ea2581b6d68720eaef4a7ffd4cd7dd786495c3527308ed17"},{"nct":"NCT05911295","title":"Disitamab Vedotin With Pembrolizumab vs Chemotherapy in Previously Untreated Urothelial Cancer Expressing HER2","sponsor":"Seagen, a wholly owned subsidiary of Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":412,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.8024941592722926,"rationale":"RemeGen's Chinese phase 3 (RC48-C016) of disitamab vedotin plus toripalimab against gemcitabine-platinum in HER2-expressing first-line urothelial cancer showed large PFS and OS benefits (HR roughly 0.36 for PFS). EV-302 also showed that an MMAE ADC plus pembrolizumab beats platinum chemotherapy, with a PFS HR of about 0.45. A HER2-selected population, a chemotherapy comparator and about 412 patients give ample power for BICR-assessed PFS. The main risks are a weaker effect at HER2 IHC 1+ in a global population and toxicity, but success is highly likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ee09c6095233bdf11d258ec7fbc143da606ae55a3b86588f0a13718871d47508"},{"nct":"NCT06118281","title":"ARTEMIS - A Research Study to Look at How Ziltivekimab Works Compared to Placebo in People With a Heart Attack","sponsor":"Novo Nordisk A/S","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":10000,"base":0.37,"researched":null,"learned":0.7196388314459877,"rationale":"ARTEMIS is the first outcomes test of IL-6 inhibition with ziltivekimab, given early after myocardial infarction. Genetic IL-6 receptor data and CANTOS (IL-1β inhibition, HR about 0.85, p of about 0.03 with roughly 1,400 events) support the inflammation hypothesis. However, CLEAR SYNERGY's neutral result with colchicine in a similar post-MI population shows how hard incremental MACE benefit is to demonstrate on top of modern standard of care. With 10,000 patients and only about 2 years of follow-up, the trial likely accrues fewer events than CANTOS, so a modest CANTOS-like effect could easily miss significance, and infection risk could offset some of the benefit.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"61d1aa073f15e9d07c6c51dbafe7a27039b101778e717d7f928f8806168c1308"},{"nct":"NCT06151964","title":"A Trial to Learn How Safe AZD9550 Monotherapy and Combined With AZD6234 is in People With or Without Type 2 Diabetes Who Are Living With Obesity and Overweight","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":166,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8082509384632582,"rationale":"This is a Phase I/II multiple-ascending-dose study whose primary endpoints are descriptive safety, tolerability and PK measures, with no prespecified efficacy comparison, so 'success' effectively means acceptable tolerability and characterised PK. AstraZeneca has already advanced AZD9550 (a GLP-1/glucagon dual agonist) with AZD6234 into a Phase 2b obesity study and keeps adding parts to this trial, which suggests earlier cohorts showed a tolerable profile. The main risks are GI tolerability and glucagon-related effects such as heart rate, or strategic deprioritisation. I don't know of a public topline result for this trial's primary analysis.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c58cc60c02219639689eaa3cb440809ec5fbf5315c345f716a5ed62931453c01"},{"nct":"NCT07207408","title":"Immunogenicity, Safety, and Tolerability of rF1V-1018 Vaccine in Adults 18 to 55 Years of Age","sponsor":"Dynavax Technologies Corporation","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-29","enrollment":148,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7600216470521741,"rationale":"This is a descriptive, dose-finding Phase 2 immunogenicity study with no placebo or active comparator, so 'success' means robust anti-rF1V antibody responses, which Dynavax and DoD would likely report as positive. An earlier Phase 2 trial found that adding the CpG 1018 adjuvant to rF1V produced strong, accelerated antibody responses compared with alum-adjuvanted rF1V. Two Part 1 regimens have already been selected for Part 2, which suggests acceptable early immunogenicity and safety. The main risk is ambiguity in how a single-arm descriptive endpoint is judged, along with possible safety findings.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7f3831aab3ab751f86aae2307ad56ad38f1d9f9981c14e1c9ee32843199a4680"},{"nct":"NCT06474806","title":"Safety and Diagnostic Performance of uPAR PET Imaging in Localised, Untreated Prostate Cancer","sponsor":"Curasight","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-30","enrollment":168,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.4798534889634217,"rationale":"This is a sponsor-run Phase 2 diagnostic trial whose primary endpoint is SUVmax, mainly descriptive, with Part 2 presumably testing whether uptake discriminates ISUP grades. Earlier investigator-led studies of 64Cu-DOTA-AE105 showed uPAR PET uptake correlating with Gleason/ISUP grade, and I believe Curasight reported Part 1 favourably and chose the 200 MBq dose. Descriptive or correlation-type imaging endpoints with an adequate sample (~141) are usually reported as met, but separating low grades (ISUP 1 vs 2–3) is genuinely harder than prior comparisons, so meaningful uncertainty remains. Part 2 topline results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fa0755e8778874b1a758f1b8c2654d928ba2c10d072dbcd84cf255c3cdff9666"},{"nct":"NCT06589986","title":"A Study to Assess the Efficacy and Safety of Afimkibart (Also Known as RO7790121) for Induction and Maintenance Therapy in Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-30","enrollment":400,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.7303806105284507,"rationale":"Afimkibart is an anti-TL1A antibody whose Phase 2 TUSCANY-2 study showed clinical remission rates well above placebo. The mechanism is also supported by positive Phase 2 data for tulisokibart (ARTEMIS-UC) and duvakitug. This 400-patient placebo-controlled Phase 3 should have ample power for week-12 clinical remission, where placebo rates typically run about 10–15% against plausible active rates of 25–35%. Residual risk comes from the usual shrinkage of effects from Phase 2 to Phase 3 and a mixed refractory population, but the class looks well validated.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"35df54198f21bd518dad8934f567923faa8e6c8ccc1409d9ebeb06a50bcfa782"},{"nct":"NCT04241185","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Pembrolizumab (MK-3475) in Combination With Chemoradiotherapy (CRT) Versus CRT Alone in Muscle-invasive Bladder Cancer (MIBC) (MK-3475-992/KEYNOTE-992)","sponsor":"Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":520,"base":0.52,"researched":null,"learned":0.6539320624095939,"rationale":"PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors work in urothelial cancer in the perioperative setting (CheckMate 274 adjuvant DFS, NIAGARA, and EV-303/KEYNOTE-905 were all positive), which supports adding pembrolizumab to bladder-sparing CRT. Against that, checkpoint inhibitors added to definitive CRT have a mixed record: positive in KEYNOTE-A18 and PACIFIC, negative in KEYNOTE-412, JAVELIN H&N, CALLA and KEYNOTE-867. BI-EFS is a composite that includes residual disease after CRT and cystectomy, so it could pick up a local-control or adjuvant-like benefit, but 520 patients is moderate and the effect size is uncertain. I do not recall a public topline result, so I put this near a coin flip, slightly favourable.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"22aa4710c6af83b333a321986315fb16c70836f7319d6cc0165aaff3c18655d3"},{"nct":"NCT05626712","title":"Safety and Efficacy of CELZ-201 in Patients With Recent Onset Type 1 Diabetes","sponsor":"Creative Medical Technology Holdings Inc","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":18,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.48539674366053737,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is safety and tolerability: the incidence of grade 2 or higher adverse events at 6 months in a small open-label, single-site Phase I/IIa trial of 18 patients, with no formal efficacy hypothesis. A microcap sponsor like Creative Medical Technology would very likely describe even modest results as 'safe and well tolerated'. The main risks are slow enrollment (still recruiting, with completion planned for January 2027), possible procedure-related adverse events from intra-arterial pancreatic infusion, and ambiguity about how a descriptive safety endpoint would be judged as met. I recall no public topline result for this trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"e3ca07124fd7f42bb70736546e5fe3081acdbb1766735a6b00d03dab77858317"},{"nct":"NCT06241781","title":"Autologous Tumor Infiltrating Lymphocytes Injection (GT101 Injection) for the Treatment of Recurrent or Metastatic Cervical Cancer","sponsor":"Grit Biotechnology","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":100,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.3108317147650532,"rationale":"Gemcitabine monotherapy is a weak second-line comparator in cervical cancer, with median PFS of about 2–3 months, and TIL therapy (Iovance LN-145, early GT101 data) has shown objective response rates around 40% in this disease. Measuring PFS from first study treatment rather than randomization also helps the TIL arm, because it skips the manufacturing delay. Against that, the trial is a small (n=100) open-label phase II, many Chinese patients will have had prior PD-1/PD-L1 therapy that may blunt TIL efficacy, and it is still recruiting. There is also a real chance of manufacturing failures, dropout or incomplete reporting.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"243dcf379fddc40fe47266869eb646812ecfee4c3727483c87d2b7b9f15fce7f"},{"nct":"NCT06279741","title":"Safety and Efficacy of MSC-EVs in the Prevention of BPD in Extremely Preterm Infants","sponsor":"EXO Biologics S.A.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":265,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3510825397522186,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human Phase 1/2 test of a novel mechanism, umbilical cord MSC-derived extracellular vesicles, in BPD prevention, a field where many pharmacologic and cell-therapy trials have failed. The Phase 2 efficacy comparison has about 80 infants per active arm against only about 40 on placebo, so a statistically significant drop in grade II-III BPD would need a large effect. Supporting evidence for MSC or EV approaches in BPD is mostly preclinical or from small, uncontrolled studies. Recruitment is ongoing with primary completion planned for 2027, so no result is public, and success looks unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c55b70c1a67c82d6e878c9bf579501feacb035fdf8b0dc1401afaddbca671c49"},{"nct":"NCT07009171","title":"Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of KDS2010 in Overweight or Obese Patients","sponsor":"NeuroBiogen Co., Ltd","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":75,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.804291094679514,"rationale":"KDS2010 is a reversible MAO-B inhibitor being tested for obesity on the basis of astrocytic GABA hypothalamic biology and preliminary Phase 1 observations, but MAO-B inhibition has no proven weight-loss efficacy in humans (selegiline was not meaningfully effective). The trial is a small, staged Phase 2a with about 22 active versus 11 placebo patients per dose stage over 12 weeks, so it is powered to detect only large effects of roughly 3–4% placebo-adjusted weight loss. A dose-finding exploratory design and a first-in-mechanism test in obesity point to a low chance of a statistically significant primary result, though pooling the placebo groups or the 240 mg arm could yield a signal.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3600ca6d4f7dd66cb8fcff8f42ec2e411d0331ea565f9484a98480b2b8f399bd"},{"nct":"NCT07940075","title":"SYH2062 Injection in Participants With Mild to Moderate Essential Hypertension .","sponsor":"CSPC Zhongnuo Pharmaceutical (Shijiazhuang) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-01-31","enrollment":360,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.4968335842233527,"rationale":"SYH2062 is most likely CSPC's subcutaneous siRNA against angiotensinogen, a mechanism already validated by zilebesiran, which cut 24-hour ambulatory SBP by about 10–15 mmHg versus placebo in KARDIA-1 and KARDIA-2, including as add-on therapy. With about 360 participants, a placebo comparator and 12 weeks of 24-hour ambulatory monitoring, the trial has ample power for an effect of that size. The main risks are dilution from background antihypertensives, single-blind conduct and a dose-ranging design that may not be fully optimized, but a validated mechanism against placebo usually succeeds. No results are public yet; primary completion is planned for January 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"64eb18423ae6438f6029529e50464413b121e2ebcfb84e85bee25d7796abb6f6"},{"nct":"NCT05219617","title":"Investigate Efficacy and Safety of Carisbamate as Adjunctive Treatment for Seizures Associated With LGS in Children and Adults","sponsor":"SK Life Science, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":252,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.7547193986853481,"rationale":"Placebo-controlled phase 3 LGS trials using percent change in drop seizures have historically succeeded fairly often (rufinamide, clobazam, cannabidiol, fenfluramine), though soticlestat narrowly failed. Carisbamate has mixed prior efficacy: inconsistent phase 3 results in focal epilepsy, and only small open-label phase 2 signals in LGS. Having two dose arms gives two chances to hit, and ~84 patients per arm is reasonably powered for typical LGS effect sizes. The trial is still recruiting with primary completion in 2027, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9f570da36768babe330077f3db08050f4b70388ad69870200d4740d3431f4ba4"},{"nct":"NCT05382286","title":"Study of Sacituzumab Govitecan-hziy and Pembrolizumab Versus Treatment of Physician's Choice and Pembrolizumab in Patients With Previously Untreated, Locally Advanced Inoperable or Metastatic Triple-Negative Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Gilead Sciences","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":443,"base":0.98,"researched":null,"learned":0.7019083682890062,"rationale":"This is ASCENT-04/KEYNOTE-D19. In April 2025 Gilead announced that the trial met its primary endpoint of BICR-assessed PFS. Data presented at ASCO 2025 showed median PFS of 11.2 vs 7.8 months (HR ~0.65, p<0.001) for sacituzumab govitecan plus pembrolizumab versus chemotherapy plus pembrolizumab in PD-L1+ first-line mTNBC.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"243f9b34f3ac1d5eda71a4a2cb8e89fee978d22390f44524cb0ed428b91ce125"},{"nct":"NCT05748873","title":"Promising ROd-cone DYstrophy Gene therapY","sponsor":"SparingVision","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":33,"base":0.83,"researched":null,"learned":0.5564293609396412,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is descriptive safety and tolerability (incidence of AEs/SAEs at 12 months), not a powered efficacy comparison, so 'success' will mean the sponsor reporting an acceptable safety profile. To my knowledge, SparingVision has publicly described Step 1 dose escalation as well tolerated, with DSMB clearance to proceed to the randomized Step 2. Subretinal AAV therapies generally have manageable safety profiles, usually limited to surgery-related events and steroid-responsive inflammation. The main risks are unexpected inflammation or toxicity at higher doses, or this trial being judged on its exploratory efficacy measures, so I keep a modest discount.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"86e806643df852d9a070a965816c00c80bbffc56ab705833f49923cffab12125"},{"nct":"NCT05906992","title":"A Study to Compare Efficacy, Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics and Safety of CT-P53 and Ocrevus in Patients With Relapsing-remitting Multiple Sclerosis","sponsor":"Celltrion","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":512,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.7927749920188025,"rationale":"CT-P53 is a proposed ocrelizumab biosimilar compared against EU- and US-Ocrevus, and the first-listed primary endpoint is PK equivalence (AUC), which biosimilar programs from experienced developers like Celltrion almost always meet. The efficacy co-primary, new GdE lesions to Week 24, sits near a floor because ocrelizumab almost completely suppresses lesion activity, so equivalence there is also likely. The main residual risks are three-way PK equivalence failing on one comparison, manufacturing or analytical differences, and operational problems. Primary completion is not until 2027, and I am not aware of any public results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a3695705bc130fcfc57cc59a0f6c9455390c82768a900d8bad8a107b62c744dc"},{"nct":"NCT06323213","title":"Efficacy and Safety Study of 610 in Patients With Severe Asthma","sponsor":"Sunshine Guojian Pharmaceutical (Shanghai) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":480,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.6779805896106275,"rationale":"610 (SSGJ-610) is an anti-IL-5 monoclonal antibody, a mechanism well validated in severe eosinophilic asthma: mepolizumab and reslizumab consistently cut exacerbation rates by about 50% versus placebo, including in Chinese populations. A 480-patient, 52-week placebo-controlled trial with annualized severe exacerbation rate as the primary endpoint is well powered for an effect of that size. The main risks are a low placebo-arm exacerbation rate in a Chinese cohort and possibly loose eosinophil enrichment criteria. Primary completion is not expected until 2027, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7b3b65f00d37958ef32f8524a586c340eb5597ba580947c7a37c7251b8bcede3"},{"nct":"NCT06365853","title":"A Study of Ocular Toxicity Evaluation and Mitigation During Treatment With Mirvetuximab Soravtansine in Participants With Recurrent Ovarian Cancer With High Folate Receptor-Alpha Expression","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":108,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.3569338327004808,"rationale":"This is a descriptive phase 2 safety study. Its primary endpoint is the incidence of grade 2 or higher MIRV-related corneal adverse events in asymptomatic participants, and neither of its two experimental prophylaxis arms (steroid vs brimonidine drops) is a true control, so no formal superiority test is evident. Prior MIRV experience shows high rates of keratopathy and blurred vision despite prophylaxis. With about 54 patients per arm, a statistically significant difference between the two prophylaxis strategies is unlikely. Success would mainly depend on how a descriptive topline is framed, so I assign a modest probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8c51a110af4ef75057612d80fc93cf8407453cc911ebb233c06a2df4b958b6db"},{"nct":"NCT06413706","title":"A Study Comparing Abemaciclib Plus Temozolomide to Temozolomide Monotherapy in Children and Young Adults With High-grade Glioma Following Radiotherapy","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":45,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3259303364944829,"rationale":"This is a small (about 45 patients), open-label, Lilly-sponsored pediatric phase 2 trial, likely run to meet pediatric regulatory obligations, testing a CDK4/6 inhibitor added to temozolomide in newly diagnosed non-pontine pediatric high-grade glioma. CDK4/6 inhibitors have shown little efficacy in adult or pediatric gliomas, and pediatric HGG adjuvant trials have almost uniformly failed to improve survival endpoints. With this sample size, power to show a two-sided p<0.05 benefit in event-free survival is low, even if the protocol uses a lenient one-sided alpha. Success is therefore unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0273c8fb9fd6efac57a9b8cc81c1dea472fb77cd4884c662b654bbc7686d3c11"},{"nct":"NCT06463665","title":"Efficacy & Safety of Olvimulogene Nanivacirepvec & Platinum-doublet + Physician's Choice of Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Compared to Docetaxel in NSCL Cancer","sponsor":"Genelux Corporation","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":142,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.38543116408217054,"rationale":"The comparator is single-agent docetaxel, which gives only about 3–4 months of PFS after progression on chemo-immunotherapy. The experimental arm combines platinum-doublet rechallenge, a continued checkpoint inhibitor and an oncolytic vaccinia virus, so it could plausibly show a PFS advantage even if the virus adds little. Against that, these patients progressed on platinum plus ICI, and many are likely platinum-refractory; IV oncolytic viruses have a poor track record in randomized solid-tumor trials, and the trial is small (142) and open-label from a small sponsor. Weighing a modest base rate against the weak comparator and multi-agent experimental arm, I estimate roughly a 40% chance of a significant BICR-PFS win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5615d72e4edf5a56df02f705e1d62192efb0f8153437f6086648b7cc7739158b"},{"nct":"NCT06602479","title":"A Study to Investigate the Safety and Efficacy of MEDI0618 Compared to Placebo in Adult Participants With Episodic Migraine","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":309,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.6187894366950993,"rationale":"MEDI0618 is an anti-PACAP monoclonal antibody, a mechanism with partial validation: Lundbeck's anti-PACAP Lu AG09222 beat placebo on monthly migraine days in the phase 2 HOPE trial (about -2 days), whereas Amgen's PAC1 receptor antibody failed. The primary comparison (Dose A vs placebo in about 64 per arm of CGRP-naive patients who failed at least two preventives) has reasonable power if the effect is about 1.5-2 monthly migraine days. That power falls off quickly for smaller effects given episodic migraine's high placebo response. Balancing the mechanism's support against the modest sample and phase 2 uncertainty, I put the chance of success slightly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1a9ce1996f810658448bd908c292812b077d339189beef24b1c9c955ff6c2757"},{"nct":"NCT06680947","title":"A Phase IIb Study of 610 in Participants With Severe Eosinophilic Asthma","sponsor":"Sunshine Guojian Pharmaceutical (Shanghai) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":225,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.5118432124626396,"rationale":"610 (3SBio/Sunshine Guojian) is an anti-IL-5 antibody, a mechanism already validated in severe eosinophilic asthma, which raises the prior for efficacy. However, the primary endpoint is pre-bronchodilator FEV1 at week 52, where anti-IL-5 agents typically give modest placebo-adjusted gains of about 100–150 mL that were not always significant (DREAM, for example). With about 75 patients per arm, a 52-week dropout risk and a fairly lenient entry requirement of one exacerbation, power is only moderate, partly offset by having two dose arms and the larger effects often seen in Chinese trials.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"de2d54d70a46db651ea999f671438868c29f8e55ca238b05df1fb68607bffc70"},{"nct":"NCT06899802","title":"A Phase 2 Trial in Healthy Adult Participants of the Recombinant MVA-BN-WEV Vaccine","sponsor":"Bavarian Nordic","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":411,"base":0.86,"researched":null,"learned":0.5631680617908501,"rationale":"MVA-BN-WEV is built on the licensed MVA-BN vector, and a Phase 1 trial showed it induced neutralizing antibodies against EEEV and VEEV. A placebo-controlled comparison of binding and neutralizing titers in alphavirus-naive adults should therefore almost certainly favor vaccine. The main risk is how 'success' gets defined: the first primary endpoint is dose selection rather than a classic superiority test, and a sponsor could frame results ambiguously or find suboptimal responses for one antigen, such as weaker EEEV neutralization. Primary completion is expected in early 2027, and I am not aware of any topline results.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"47459cb02ded1f17cedfa46ed4afc16901199cca9513953f907a387a78892143"},{"nct":"NCT06905210","title":"Study of New Antiandrogenic Progestogen + Low-dose Estrogen for Moderate Acne Vulgaris","sponsor":"Eurofarma Laboratorios S.A.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":531,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8599742538352797,"rationale":"Combined oral contraceptives, including cyproterone acetate/ethinyl estradiol (Diane-35) and low-dose EE 20 µg regimens such as drospirenone/EE 24+4, have repeatedly beaten placebo on inflammatory lesion counts in acne trials of similar size and duration. This trial uses an established antiandrogenic progestogen at an established dose, with only the estrogen dose reduced, over six cycles against placebo, with about 531 patients randomized 2:1. That gives ample power for the modest but consistent effects COCs typically show. The main risks are the high placebo response in acne, possible slightly lower efficacy with the reduced EE dose, and execution issues at a single-country sponsor. Recruitment started in August 2026 and primary completion is planned for February 2027, so no result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4cdd08fed6edf3cbf93e6727c8817d489685e2514b9c456ed0c29d002680f6f8"},{"nct":"NCT06937203","title":"A First-In-Human Study of ARO-ALK7 in Adults With Obesity With and Without Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus","sponsor":"Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":150,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.7801325681010892,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is a descriptive safety count (number of participants with TEAEs), not a powered efficacy comparison, so 'success' most plausibly means the drug proved generally well tolerated. Arrowhead's siRNA platform has a good tolerability record, and as I recall, interim ARO-ALK7 data showed target knockdown without major safety signals. Final results are not out, with primary completion planned for 2027-02. The main risk is that safety-primary trials can be scored ambiguously or as not meeting a formal endpoint, so I hold at a moderate-high probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a19eb5b69366ff1216d5a8fded1fc1d5c4e46aa9e492a749e2f23f00cbed72f6"},{"nct":"NCT06939595","title":"A Study to Compare Effects and Safety of CT-P51 and Keytruda in Patients With Previously Untreated Metastatic Lung Cancer","sponsor":"Celltrion","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":225,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5757580724805245,"rationale":"CT-P51 is Celltrion's pembrolizumab biosimilar, and this small Georgia-only trial (n=225) has a descriptive safety primary endpoint (TEAE incidence) rather than a formal superiority or equivalence efficacy test. Celltrion's biosimilars have reliably shown comparable safety and efficacy to their reference products. A descriptive safety comparison is very likely to be reported as 'comparable safety,' which a sponsor would announce as meeting the objective. The main uncertainty is how a descriptive endpoint gets scored, plus a small risk of an unexpected imbalance or immunogenicity signal; no results are public yet (primary completion 2027-02).","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4bfe7f292123ed68f9499c3a7cf26f50fd08ec50a5323ba73ec80ef5dc31575e"},{"nct":"NCT06972446","title":"A Study to Evaluate Different Targeted Therapies for Patients With Rheumatoid Arthritis","sponsor":"AbbVie","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":180,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.6654525031622709,"rationale":"This is an exploratory phase 2 platform with about 180 patients split across three placebo-controlled substudies, so roughly 60 per substudy, in a hard-to-treat bDMARD-inadequate-responder population, judged on the demanding ACR50 endpoint at week 12. IL-1 blockade (anakinra) has historically given only modest benefit in RA, and prior anti-CD40 antagonists such as BI 655064 failed to separate from placebo in RA. The combination arm and the three independent chances to win raise the odds of at least one significant result. Still, small arms, a stringent endpoint and weak mechanistic precedent keep the probability below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c6f53d14f67ff9310c8fe80e318e425c69aa91e8f586222ed4871b3d9a76b339"},{"nct":"NCT06996080","title":"A Phase 3 Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Intravitreal KSI-101 in Participants With Macular Edema Secondary to Inflammation (MESI) - PINNACLE","sponsor":"Kodiak Sciences Inc","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":300,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.8134084705839651,"rationale":"KSI-101 is a bispecific IL-6/VEGF-trap fusion. The small open-label Phase 1b APEX study reported large BCVA gains and CST reductions in MESI, and sham-controlled trials of active agents in uveitic macular edema (e.g., PEACHTREE, HURON) have generally succeeded. Uncertainty comes from Roche's anti-IL-6 vamikibart, which gave mixed Phase 3 results (my recollection is that one of two trials missed), and from this trial's restriction to milder edema (CST 320–400 µm), which may limit the room for BCVA improvement over sham. With roughly 100 patients per arm, two doses, and a continuous BCVA primary endpoint, power should be reasonable, so I place the probability modestly above the Phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3d7504d567dd548aec9679ab2fe69ba5b3a3e6fdeb9fea7ccb2e2f77128aa934"},{"nct":"NCT07060456","title":"Efficacy and Safety of HRS9531 in Participants With Type 2 Diabetes Treated With Basal Insulin","sponsor":"Fujian Shengdi Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":300,"base":0.96,"researched":null,"learned":0.9582612513210302,"rationale":"HRS9531 is a GLP-1/GIP dual agonist (Hengrui) that has shown large HbA1c reductions in phase 2 and other phase 3 trials, and the mechanism is well validated (tirzepatide reduced HbA1c by about 2% versus placebo on basal insulin in SURPASS-5). This is a placebo-controlled add-on to basal insulin with baseline HbA1c of 7.5–11% and about 100 per arm, giving very high power. Primary completion is planned for 2027-02, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0057dfdd04eefcc38db85a31ce1074a831b83b728b6dbfce77e776a51d91f0c0"},{"nct":"NCT07118891","title":"Study Evaluating ABCL635 for Vasomotor Symptoms of Menopause","sponsor":"AbCellera Biologics Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":136,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.7703594724463305,"rationale":"This first-in-human Phase 1/2 trial of ABCL635, an NK3R-targeting antibody, has only descriptive safety primary endpoints (AEs, ECG, physical exam, labs), with no formal statistical comparison. A topline announcement would call it met if the drug proved safe and tolerable, which is the usual outcome for a biologic against a validated target (fezolinetant and elinzanetant), especially as a long-acting antibody may avoid the liver signals seen with small molecules. The main risks are unexpected safety or immunogenicity findings, or the sponsor framing a weak Part C efficacy result as a failure, so the estimate is moderately high. I do not recall this trial's own results being public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ffc073a8b644f7f636beac0c421e1e0ae8b55c5df24e82957eea74af7da87aa5"},{"nct":"NCT07223840","title":"A Study of Brenipatide in Adults Who Quit Smoking Cigarettes and Want to Avoid Relapse","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":222,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.3567824815342228,"rationale":"Brenipatide (LY3537031) is a Lilly incretin-class agent being tested in addictions. The human evidence for GLP-1 agonists on smoking abstinence is mixed: an exenatide pilot was positive, a dulaglutide trial was negative on abstinence, and semaglutide data are small. Even proven drugs such as varenicline produce only modest absolute gains in relapse-prevention trials, and about 111 patients per arm can only detect a large effect on continuous abstinence over 24 weeks. Lilly's investment suggests some conviction, but a first test of this mechanism in a hard behavioral endpoint warrants a probability below 50%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"667bcc335788e057aa0815f98ef08ce00073a0169db8547987dd6d55ad6ab1f0"},{"nct":"NCT07245953","title":"A Clinical Study of HT-101 and HT-102 in Patients With Chronic Hepatitis B Virus Infection","sponsor":"Suzhou HepaThera Biotech Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":60,"base":0.15,"researched":null,"learned":0.592929215825646,"rationale":"Both arms receive the active HT-101 + HT-102 combination, which is likely a siRNA plus an antibody or immunomodulator. Cohort B differs only by an 8-week placebo lead-in followed by 16 weeks of treatment, so the primary comparison at W60 is effectively 24 versus 16 weeks of the same regimen. Functional cure rates in low-HBsAg (<3000 IU/mL), NA-suppressed patients can be meaningful with such combinations, but a statistically significant between-arm difference with about 30 patients per arm is unlikely. The design is exploratory, and no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0c3e93d8f37f47b20cf3a63ed8a0ee8b949797663393729c8b63a66f3a56ba41"},{"nct":"NCT07287202","title":"Safety, Tolerability, and Pharmacokinetics of SVG103 (Paxalisib) in Focal Cortical Dysplasia Type II (FCD-II), Tuberous Sclerosis Complex (TSC) or Hemimegalencephaly (HME)","sponsor":"Sovargen","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":12,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.4975663282286559,"rationale":"This is a small (n=12), open-label phase 1b/2a study whose primary endpoint is descriptive safety and tolerability, with no formal hypothesis test, so success usually means the sponsor reports an acceptable safety profile. Paxalisib, a brain-penetrant PI3K/mTOR inhibitor, has known oncology-dose toxicities such as hyperglycemia, rash and mucositis, but low and high doses in a non-cancer epilepsy population with glycemic exclusions should be manageable. The main risks are dose-limiting toxicity at the high dose, discontinuations, or the study stalling. No results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a4d3a27e7a31e55ad375d881cf54d1e8ac20de2429cd9f7e089adc85bd05e305"},{"nct":"NCT07365462","title":"Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of NBI-1065890 Versus Placebo in Adults With Tardive Dyskinesia","sponsor":"Neurocrine Biosciences","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":100,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.3104043265968506,"rationale":"NBI-1065890 appears to be Neurocrine's next-generation VMAT2 inhibitor, a mechanism already proven in tardive dyskinesia. Valbenazine's KINECT 2 and 3 and deutetrabenazine's ARM-TD and AIM-TD trials all met the same AIMS endpoint, scored by blinded central video raters. With about 50 patients per arm and plausible placebo-adjusted effects of 2 to 3 points (SD roughly 3 to 4), power is reasonable, and Neurocrine has deep experience running TD trials. The main risks are phase 2 dose and PK uncertainty for a new molecule and the modest sample size, so the forecast is moderately above base rate rather than near certain.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a8fc16d90b8be72f5f6482cf47e43df82057667d3a73009f65755f8c93510d2f"},{"nct":"NCT07371793","title":"A Study to Evaluate BBI-001 in Healthy Volunteers and in Patients With Hereditary Hemochromatosis","sponsor":"Bond Biosciences","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":34,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.642061853324719,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is incidence and severity of adverse events in a small Phase 1/2a MAD and crossover study, so there is no formal efficacy comparison. Sponsors typically report such trials as having met the endpoint when the drug is 'safe and well tolerated.' BBI-001 is an oral agent meant to reduce dietary iron absorption and is given only briefly here, so a disqualifying safety signal is fairly unlikely. Some probability is held back for tolerability problems, trial discontinuation, or results that are ambiguous or never reported, given primary completion is planned for February 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"847eaac982aeec365d62c70baf4e6db5f29036ed024d20da4c6de85cc0279f9c"},{"nct":"NCT07385287","title":"Field Trial of PfSPZ-LARC2 Vaccine in Burkinabe Adults","sponsor":"Sanaria Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":180,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.42788882460855643,"rationale":"Earlier field trials of Sanaria's radiation-attenuated PfSPZ Vaccine in malaria-exposed adults in Mali and Burkina Faso showed moderate efficacy (about 30–50% by time-to-event), which was statistically significant in at least some analyses. The replication-competent LARC2 parasite is expected to be more potent, and its single-gene predecessor GA2 protected about 90% of volunteers against controlled human malaria infection. Against that, field protection against diverse heterologous strains in semi-immune adults has consistently been much lower than in challenge studies. A high rainy-season attack rate gives roughly 60 participants per arm reasonable power for a moderate effect, and two vaccine arms give two chances, but the effect size remains uncertain, so I put the odds slightly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"eb46d5aea6da6a43871407f0f7f1a1c54a74718a02c5a29c179b7767a116543a"},{"nct":"NCT07393334","title":"Effects of NLS-133, a Potential Non-Hormonal \"On-Demand\" Male Contraceptive","sponsor":"Next Life Sciences","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":10,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.6214835844788728,"rationale":"NLS-133 appears to combine an alpha-1 blocker such as silodosin with a second approved agent. Silodosin and similar uroselective alpha-blockers are known to produce marked, often near-complete, loss of ejaculate volume within hours, so a large effect on semen volume versus placebo is pharmacologically very plausible. With only 10 men the study is small, but the within-subject crossover design, a large expected effect and uncorrected alpha make a significant reduction in semen volume at one or more timepoints likely. Remaining risks are the small sample, the nonparametric test across several arms and timepoints, and uncertainty about how the primary comparison will be defined and reported.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"37000c335048dfa5b9868c8e87f8203ffa7d212119a977fd5c7b4b60cbd5e7d7"},{"nct":"NCT07395986","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Masked, Placebo-Controlled Pilot Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of ZOC2017217 in Subjects With Age-Related Cataract","sponsor":"Ocusun Ophthalmic Pharmaceutical (Guangzhou) Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":8,"base":0.04,"researched":null,"learned":0.39185006724732524,"rationale":"Topical eye drops to reverse age-related cataract (lanosterol/oxysterol-type approaches) have never shown convincing efficacy in humans, so the base rate for this mechanism and indication is very low. Enrollment ended at only 8 subjects, about 4 per arm, against a planned 40, which leaves essentially no power to detect a significant BCDVA difference. This is an exploratory pilot with many descriptive outcomes, and statistical significance on the first-listed BCDVA change is highly unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"14071f3d8ca7f11c2d1ec482eec15f01d57c24429190fcda26b339302d43fd69"},{"nct":"NCT07488897","title":"RIG 101 Trial in Healthy Adults and Adults With Asthma","sponsor":"RIGImmune Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":82,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5657271009793786,"rationale":"This is a first-in-human phase 1/2 trial of RIG-101, an intranasal innate-immune (RIG-I pathway) agent, from a small biotech. The first-listed primaries are safety measures, so the scored efficacy outcome is likely the Part B lower respiratory symptom score AUC after rhinovirus RV-A16 challenge in mild-to-moderate asthmatics. Part B will be small, and challenge-model symptom endpoints are noisy. Antiviral and innate-immune approaches to virus-induced asthma worsening, such as inhaled interferon-beta, have mostly failed to show significant symptom benefit, so a significant LRSS reduction is uncertain, although lenient safety-based interpretations add some upside.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7dbacec1bc21e4150b2ecb1bea8a962cd58dba9d74b07de0a1f6c71d7b227b18"},{"nct":"NCT07491458","title":"A Trial to Investigate Safety, Exposure, and Efficacy of HU6 Compared With Placebo in Adult Participants With Metabolic Dysfunction-associated Steatohepatitis (MASH)","sponsor":"Rivus Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":180,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.6271220193202723,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety, so the relevant efficacy endpoint is percent change in liver fat by MRI-PDFF at 26 weeks. That is a sensitive imaging endpoint on which mitochondrial uncouplers act directly. HU6, a controlled metabolic accelerator and DNP prodrug, previously showed statistically significant liver-fat and weight reductions in Rivus's Phase 2a M-ACCEL and HFpEF trials, as far as I recall. About 45 participants per arm against pooled placebo should be adequately powered for the expected ~25–40% relative fat reduction. The remaining risk lies in tolerability-driven dropout and the modest size of the effect, and the results are not yet public (primary completion is planned for 2027-02).","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a2a3b5c91c5d5935c93043d7aeabdc62d70879d9a176fff72be2bbeced5bcbaa"},{"nct":"NCT07531043","title":"Efficacy and Safety of FID 123472 Ophthalmic Solution for Ocular Redness in Adults","sponsor":"Alcon Research","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":230,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.8469643113856969,"rationale":"Apraclonidine is a potent alpha-adrenergic vasoconstrictor, and low-dose alpha-2 agonists such as brimonidine 0.025% (Lumify) have reliably beaten vehicle on Ora Calibra redness scores. That makes the first-listed 15-minute endpoint close to certain to succeed. The 14-hour co-primary is a more demanding duration claim, but Alcon very likely chose it based on earlier-phase data. The vehicle-controlled design with about 115 subjects per arm gives ample power, so the main residual risk is the long-duration co-primary failing if both endpoints are required.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9c654c383f7c9da35c6c6486a6054522cd74148dc8912592605c501efb4fd720"},{"nct":"NCT07547813","title":"A Proof-of-Concept Study of LAD328 in Adults With Hidradenitis Suppurativa","sponsor":"Almirall, S.A.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":50,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.34258498832844964,"rationale":"LAD328 is an undisclosed-mechanism IV biologic from Almirall in a small (n≈50), single-site Phase 2 proof-of-concept trial in moderate-to-severe HS, with IHS4-55 at week 12 as the primary endpoint. HS trials have substantial placebo response (about 25-35% on IHS4-55/HiSCR50), so with roughly 25 patients per arm a placebo-adjusted difference of about 35-40 points would be needed for p<0.05. Only the most potent mechanisms, such as IL-17 blockade, have achieved that. First-in-indication PoC studies in HS often show numerical trends without reaching significance, so I place the probability below the base rate for a Phase 2 dermatology trial.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"883a12627dc88f73809890e3176b895678898e5be4120ffd5c5a77483fee6b93"},{"nct":"NCT07568730","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Vehicle-Controlled, Double-Masked to Open-Label Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of Lacripep in Subjects With Neurotrophic Keratitis","sponsor":"TearSolutions, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":54,"base":0.27,"researched":null,"learned":0.4921191278555645,"rationale":"Lacripep, a lacritin-derived peptide, missed its primary endpoints in an earlier Phase 2 dry-eye trial in Sjögren's patients, so efficacy evidence for the mechanism is thin. This is a small (n≈54, about 27 per arm) vehicle-controlled Phase 2 trial in Stage 1 NK. Its primary endpoint is change in central corneal fluorescein staining on a coarse 0–3 NEI scale, where vehicle response and regression to the mean can be substantial even after a run-in. Small sponsor, limited power and an unvalidated mechanism in this indication point to below-average odds of a statistically significant win.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"15156f2a28d79ab0b5cba5dddaa87b555324f906b841c2e85eeed0adba49a917"},{"nct":"NCT07580716","title":"Intra-Articular Allocetra in Patients With Primary Knee Osteoarthritis","sponsor":"Enlivex Therapeutics Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":182,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.282680204179561,"rationale":"The prior Phase I/II Allocetra knee OA study appears to have shown benefit mainly in a subgroup of older patients with primary, age-related OA rather than in the overall population, as I recall. This Phase IIb enriches for that subgroup (age ≥64, primary OA), and trials built on post-hoc subgroups often fail to replicate. Intra-articular knee OA trials also face large placebo responses on WOMAC pain, and with about 91 patients per arm only a moderate effect would reach significance. The mechanism is novel and the sponsor small, so a probability somewhat below the Phase 2 base rate seems right.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"671bdc135ea6c5ea8a41c3d051819aa568be1a04e2b5f9042e61ab34b55bdd82"},{"nct":"NCT07645924","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Elismetrep (K-304) in the Acute Treatment of Migraine","sponsor":"TriGemX Bio, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":1800,"base":0.65,"researched":null,"learned":0.8715081008895188,"rationale":"Elismetrep is a first-in-class oral TRPM8 antagonist, licensed from Kallyope to TriGemX. Its Phase 2 acute migraine trial was reported positive on both 2-hour pain freedom and most-bothersome-symptom freedom, and this trial uses the same co-primary endpoints, two doses and a large sample (~600 per arm), so power is high for modest effects. Acute migraine Phase 3s that follow positive Phase 2 results with standard FDA endpoints have historically succeeded often (triptans, gepants, lasmiditan). The main risks are that the mechanism is new, a single Phase 2 may have overstated the effect, both co-primaries must win, and the MBS endpoint carries a high placebo response.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"55019ec6d06d412d42d81c81440a3a5edf09dfb253c234422ab4e24581390b75"},{"nct":"NCT07724340","title":"A Study to Assess the Efficacy, Safety and Tolerability of AT673 Co-administered With Semaglutide in Adult Participants With Type 2 Diabetes (T2D) and Overweight or Obesity","sponsor":"Antag Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":150,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.841283529955786,"rationale":"AT673 appears to be Antag's long-acting GIPR antagonist peptide. Amgen's MariTide gives the mechanism partial validation, and preclinical data suggest GIPR antagonism adds to GLP-1-driven weight loss. However, this is a short 13-week trial in which semaglutide is still being titrated, in T2D patients who typically lose less weight, with about 50 per arm. That makes a statistically significant additive difference of roughly 1.5–2.5% plausible but far from assured. Human efficacy data for this specific molecule are limited, so I place the odds near a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ea70783ca059de009b63d41e86cfad4052a94d84fe67858facf956ddb4d42fd8"},{"nct":"NCT07767513","title":"Study of Oral HRS-5346 in Adult Patients With Elevated Lipoprotein(a) and High Risk of Cardiovascular Events","sponsor":"Shandong Suncadia Medicine Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02","enrollment":60,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.4638059706667675,"rationale":"HRS-5346 is Hengrui's oral small-molecule Lp(a) formation inhibitor, the same mechanism as muvalaplin, which reduced Lp(a) by roughly 70–85% in phase 2, and early HRS-5346 data reportedly showed robust dose-dependent reductions. This 60-patient trial has two dose arms and no placebo, so the primary endpoint is essentially a within-arm percent change from baseline, which will almost certainly be large and statistically significant at week 12. The main risks are ambiguity about how 'success' is judged without a control arm, or an unexpected safety or tolerability issue.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"2e25746c2db176679a0896feee7e7f8f7f27c76901c81ca2013015c12e2f9ae3"},{"nct":"NCT07889284","title":"Combined Metabolic Activator Supplementation in Subjects Diagnosed With Gout","sponsor":"ScandiBio Therapeutics AB","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02","enrollment":336,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.6549381520527681,"rationale":"This tests an untested urate-lowering mechanism: a CMA2 nutraceutical (NAC, L-carnitine, nicotinamide, L-serine) has no established urate-lowering effect, and nicotinic compounds can, if anything, raise uric acid. ScandiBio's Turkish CMA trials have often reported positive results, and a 336-patient Phase 3 suggests the sponsor has some prior signal and powered for a modest effect of about 0.4–0.5 mg/dL. Still, a 4-week change in serum uric acid against placebo is an objective endpoint that resists placebo effects, and the biological rationale is weak. On balance I put the chance of a significant result somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"68bc06df76cb095d76fa569891980e2dfd6ccacf9e789a794767ae8b86dc2bea"},{"nct":"NCT04417621","title":"Study of Efficacy and Safety of LXH254 Combinations in Patients With Previously Treated Unresectable or Metastatic Melanoma","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-02","enrollment":134,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.5720541621919484,"rationale":"This is an uncontrolled, multi-arm Phase II with ORR as the primary endpoint, so 'success' will likely be judged descriptively, by whether any arm shows clinically meaningful activity, rather than by a formal comparison. Interim data I recall from this program showed confirmed responses of roughly 45% for naporafenib (LXH254) plus trametinib in NRAS-mutant melanoma after checkpoint inhibitors. That signal was strong enough for Erasca to start the SEACRAFT-2 Phase 3, while the LTT462 and ribociclib combinations looked weaker. With no control arm and no formal hypothesis test, it is uncertain how a 'met primary endpoint' verdict will be scored, which keeps the probability moderate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9d149129c98007d73550633d04539e5ee9bf6d7af4d7bd668d800abb3a9ccf71"},{"nct":"NCT05217628","title":"An Efficacy and Safety Study of Basimglurant (NOE-101) in Patients With Trigeminal Neuralgia.","sponsor":"Noema Pharma AG","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-02-02","enrollment":166,"base":0.33,"researched":null,"learned":0.6984573986644599,"rationale":"Basimglurant, an mGluR5 negative allosteric modulator, has no proven analgesic efficacy in humans, and Roche's earlier trials of it in depression and fragile X were disappointing, so this is essentially a first efficacy test of the mechanism in trigeminal neuralgia. The enriched randomized-withdrawal design helps by randomizing only open-label responders, but the closest precedent, vixotrigine's randomized-withdrawal phase 2 in TN, missed its time-to-loss-of-efficacy primary endpoint despite a favorable trend. With 166 enrolled, perhaps around 100 will be randomized, which leaves limited power for a time-to-event endpoint in a disease where the placebo response and withdrawal-period noise are substantial. I don't know of any topline result, and primary completion is planned for 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d48313c6e1e26489acd91ed6445360ca898047209ddef3bf5b6ac8a1d9067171"},{"nct":"NCT06185764","title":"A Phase 1/2 Study of VX-670 in Adult Participants With Myotonic Dystrophy 1 (DM1)","sponsor":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-02","enrollment":47,"base":0.73,"researched":null,"learned":0.6259023499377733,"rationale":"The primary endpoint is descriptive safety (number of participants with AEs) in a small Phase 1/2 dose-escalation study, so there is no formal efficacy test. 'Success' here would essentially mean an acceptable safety and tolerability profile, which most such trials report. The main risk is the EEV-PMO platform: Entrada's ENTR-601-44 drew an FDA clinical hold and showed hypomagnesemia/renal signals, so a dose-limiting safety finding or program discontinuation is plausible. I am not aware of topline results for this trial being public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"dbfb05fd2299c17c554b40a6c9ade0b764c3e61ab27844fed89ca9b9f5ad6376"},{"nct":"NCT06636682","title":"FK-PC101 as Adjuvant Therapy for Men With High-Risk Prostate Cancer","sponsor":"Cellvax Therapeutics Inc","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-02","enrollment":100,"base":0.1,"researched":null,"learned":0.2521154364559663,"rationale":"This is a small open-label phase 2 trial (n≈100, 3 sites) from a micro-cap sponsor, testing an autologous irradiated whole-tumor-cell vaccine with BCG as adjuvant therapy after prostatectomy. Earlier cell-based prostate cancer vaccines, such as GVAX, failed in randomized trials, and autologous tumor-cell vaccines have rarely shown significant DFS benefits. With about 22 months of follow-up and a modest event count, the study has little power unless the effect is very large, and enrollment and completion risk is also substantial. An open-label design measuring PSA recurrence could introduce some bias, but a statistically significant DFS win still looks unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"d9b773882670063f464a91fdd4d206f52dd16290cbd14d0fea8913e2689ea00c"},{"nct":"NCT07743008","title":"Phase 2 Trial of a Haemophilus Influenzae Serotype a (Hia) Glycoconjugate Vaccine","sponsor":"InventVacc Biologicals Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-03","enrollment":47,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.40150532224726393,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are descriptive safety measures (solicited, unsolicited and serious adverse events) with no formal hypothesis test, so success effectively means an acceptable safety profile. Hia glycoconjugate vaccines are structurally close to Hib conjugates, which have decades of safety data, and a prior phase 1 presumably supported moving to phase 2. Small alum-adjuvanted conjugate vaccine trials in healthy adults rarely raise safety signals. The main risk is ambiguity in how a descriptive safety-only trial is scored, plus a small chance of an unexpected reactogenicity finding.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"34ffdeb732802ceaaf832fc79332a9cf1385485d5579e76e6006660d3de6b382"},{"nct":"NCT04657289","title":"A Study of the Efficacy, Safety, and Pharmacokinetics of a 36-Week Refill Regimen for the Port Delivery System With Ranibizumab in Patients With Neovascular Age-Related Macular Degeneration (Velodrome)","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-04","enrollment":451,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.6915391027372891,"rationale":"Velodrome is most likely a non-inferiority comparison of the same PDS ranibizumab implant refilled every 36 weeks versus every 24 weeks, with BCVA change as the primary endpoint. My understanding is that supplemental intravitreal ranibizumab is allowed, which tends to protect visual outcomes and makes non-inferiority easier to show. The risk is real, though: pharmacokinetic modeling suggests ranibizumab levels fall substantially by week 36, and the 2022 implant recall and enrollment pause may have added heterogeneity. Weighing the high historical success of anti-VEGF non-inferiority trials against the meaningfully longer interval, I estimate about 70%.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1e3b6131b5b20ab6658e0878e98e1c2a3f183b1261d007e72b000414a67d9b93"},{"nct":"NCT06741969","title":"Nipocalimab in Moderate to Severe Sjogren's Disease","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-04","enrollment":655,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.6600023621266042,"rationale":"In the Phase 2 DAHLIAS trial, nipocalimab 15 mg/kg IV beat placebo on ClinESSDAI change, but the lower dose did not, and Sjögren's has a long record of Phase 3 failures with high placebo responses. Recent successes such as ianalumab's two NEPTUNUS trials on ESSDAI show the endpoint can be met, and 300 patients per study with a 48-week readout gives reasonable power. Risks include the switch to subcutaneous dosing, which may lower IgG less than the effective IV dose, and the modest, variable effect seen on ClinESSDAI. Balancing these, the chance of a positive primary result is a little above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"8108263093a02d71256c96bb055d3aec7485cf8a5f3dcbbab0331a6885342feb"},{"nct":"NCT07521631","title":"Efficacy and Safety of HDM1005 Compared to Tirzepatide in Obese Adults Without Diabetes","sponsor":"Hangzhou Zhongmei Huadong Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-04","enrollment":372,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.7816672470644997,"rationale":"HDM1005 is a GLP-1/GIP dual agonist tested head-to-head against tirzepatide, an approved drug with the same mechanism, in an open-label phase 2 trial with about 93 patients per arm. The record does not say whether the comparison is for superiority or non-inferiority. If superiority is required, beating tirzepatide by a significant margin is unlikely given similar mechanisms and doses. Non-inferiority or just a numerically similar result is more plausible, but whether that would count as success is unclear, so the probability stays modest.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1832717c14d882077d445399bda3be32adc76f88cd5677d40beb87599daa9c78"},{"nct":"NCT07811908","title":"Platform Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Anti-malarial Agents in Participants With Uncomplicated Plasmodium Falciparum Malaria (Cohort C2)","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-04","enrollment":120,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.3297168845338405,"rationale":"This is a small (n≈120), open-label Phase 2 platform cohort comparing a single-dose cipargamin + ganaplacide/lumefantrine combination with Coartem in African children, with PCR-corrected ACPR at Day 29 as the primary endpoint. Coartem cure rates are typically ≥95%, so statistical superiority is essentially impossible, and the cohort is likely descriptive or Bayesian rather than formally powered for non-inferiority. The component drugs have shown strong activity (KALUMA for ganaplacide-lumefantrine, rapid clearance with cipargamin), so high cure rates are plausible, but single-dose regimens in children risk recrudescence and cipargamin carries resistance-emergence concerns. Given uncertainty about how success would be judged, a probability somewhat below even seems appropriate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"52695156ab221be32add325392be09445f15dd8cec1800e87bada2ca914012fb"},{"nct":"NCT06946797","title":"A Study to Evaluate Two Dosing Regimens of Subcutaneous Nivolumab in Combination With Intravenous Ipilimumab and Chemotherapy in Participants With Previously Untreated Metastatic or Recurrent Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-05","enrollment":76,"base":0.9,"researched":null,"learned":0.48371588878413585,"rationale":"This is a descriptive phase 2 pharmacokinetic study (Cmax, Tmax, AUC, Ctrough) of two subcutaneous nivolumab regimens. It has no prespecified efficacy comparison, so \"success\" would mean the sponsor reporting that the PK targets were achieved. Subcutaneous nivolumab (Opdivo Qvantig) already showed noninferior Cavg and Cmin exposure versus IV in CheckMate-67T, which makes adequate exposure with IV ipilimumab and chemotherapy highly likely. The main uncertainty is whether a descriptive PK trial resolves cleanly as \"met,\" or whether exposure on one regimen falls short of the IV benchmark.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"49211d225263eab457e389e2000ed84c171fc19d1efad543dcca392130f8b96a"},{"nct":"NCT07244263","title":"A Study of Zasocitinib in Adults With Hidradenitis Suppurativa","sponsor":"Takeda","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-05","enrollment":91,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5016236761928552,"rationale":"Zasocitinib is a selective TYK2 inhibitor, which acts mainly through IL-23/IL-12 and type I IFN signalling. IL-23 blockade (guselkumab, risankizumab) has failed in HS, whereas broader JAK1 or TYK2/JAK1 inhibitors (upadacitinib, povorcitinib, brepocitinib) have shown activity, so the mechanistic rationale for a pure TYK2 agent is uncertain. The primary endpoint, HiSCR75, is stringent, and HS placebo responses are noisy. With only about 91 patients, the trial needs a large effect to reach significance, so I assign a below-base-rate probability for this first test of a new mechanism in a hard disease.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f67ef23826c95926a8632b7eac19a8ce4acdc5e7e9a508ab1eade3fe21cddb7e"},{"nct":"NCT07397325","title":"Clinical Study of DA-020 for the Treatment of Chemotherapy Induced Alopecia","sponsor":"Applied Biology, Inc.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-05","enrollment":60,"base":0.22,"researched":null,"learned":0.41767697701265666,"rationale":"Topical vasoconstriction with an α1 agonist (oxymetazoline) to prevent chemotherapy-induced alopecia is largely unproven in humans. Taxane and anthracycline regimens cause severe hair loss that even scalp cooling prevents only partially. The trial is small (about 20 per arm), uses a coarse CTCAE grade endpoint and has only two sites, so power to detect a modest effect is limited. Applied Biology often runs small trials that it reports as positive, which nudges the estimate up slightly, but the base rate for a new mechanism in this setting remains low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5b3d29e6dfe828759bce6be47388d0f9ba1fbeb65aa408257ef1c5cab4becd60"},{"nct":"NCT07547228","title":"A Study of PRL3-zumab in Neovascular Age-related Macular Degeneration (nAMD)","sponsor":"Intra-IMMUSG Pte Ltd","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-07","enrollment":15,"base":0.28,"researched":null,"learned":0.48072641568542107,"rationale":"The first-listed primary outcome is safety (CTCAE adverse events), not a powered efficacy comparison, and the trial has only 15 patients randomized 6:6:3 with no formal hypothesis test. A statistically significant BCVA or CST difference versus 3 placebo patients, in anti-VEGF-refractory nAMD treated with a systemic anti-PRL3 antibody (a new mechanism here), is very unlikely. The main route to a 'success' is the small sponsor describing a clean safety profile, possibly alongside favorable descriptive efficacy, as positive topline results, so the probability is held somewhat above the very low chance of a significant efficacy result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"3c4afe3bba4576a7a51b08619c67ced5b8569473683b131f1d2706583fb6a664"},{"nct":"NCT06927739","title":"Focused Orticumab Research for Treating Inflammation in Coronary Arteries","sponsor":"Abcentra","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-08","enrollment":240,"base":0.32,"researched":null,"learned":0.40381190007610657,"rationale":"Orticumab, an anti-oxLDL (ApoB-100 p45) antibody, failed to reduce arterial inflammation on FDG-PET in the earlier GLACIER trial. A later psoriasis phase 2a missed its primary endpoint but hinted at reduced coronary inflammation and plaque on CCTA, which presumably motivated this enriched post-MI trial using a FAI-score primary endpoint. The FAI score is a novel imaging endpoint with untested responsiveness to drug therapy over 24 weeks, and enrolling patients with high baseline FAI invites regression to the mean in both arms. Having two doses and 240 patients helps somewhat, but the weak prior mechanistic evidence and small-biotech phase 2 base rates argue for a below-even probability.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"33f7362c5ca22d65015ca9d737363bfc39280f15af120df515c6727a3245c068"},{"nct":"NCT05771584","title":"Therapeutic Cancer Vaccine (AST-301, pNGVL3-hICD) in Gastric Cancer","sponsor":"Aston Sci. Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-09","enrollment":24,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.2621451211646238,"rationale":"This is a small open-label phase 2 with no control arm, and its primary endpoints are safety and ELISpot immunogenicity, so there is no formal superiority test to pass or fail. The pNGVL3-hICD HER2 ICD plasmid vaccine with GM-CSF has repeatedly induced HER2-specific T-cell responses with good tolerability in earlier breast cancer studies. A sponsor-run proof-of-concept trial like this is likely to be reported as positive on immunogenicity and safety. The main risks are ambiguity in how 'success' is judged without a statistical comparison, and possibly weaker immune responses after gastrectomy and adjuvant chemotherapy.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0e7d219b78f3478a0c2ff6416c8a432018c9efddde7c5bcf3dcb236bf9b133f6"},{"nct":"NCT07170917","title":"Brivekimig for the Treatment of Moderate to Severe Hidradenitis Suppurativa","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-09","enrollment":208,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.4958461473373381,"rationale":"Brivekimig is a TNF/OX40L bispecific nanobody. Its anti-TNF component works through a mechanism already proven in HS (adalimumab), and Sanofi's Phase 2a HS study reportedly showed meaningful improvements over placebo, which prompted this dose-ranging Phase 2b. HiSCR75 is a stringent endpoint, but placebo rates are usually around 15–25%, and with about 52 patients per arm and three doses, a 20-point or larger difference in at least one arm is plausible. The main risks are the HS-typical high placebo response and the inclusion of biologic-experienced patients, who may respond less to a TNF-containing agent.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6926290972368b009563bf1f8d88b089853a8697dbaa13973f25dd3a426e432d"},{"nct":"NCT07175428","title":"Safety in Adult Participants With Atrial Fibrillation Who Are Treated With Anticoagulation","sponsor":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-09","enrollment":1200,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.48521642662967845,"rationale":"Factor XI inhibitors have consistently cut bleeding versus factor Xa inhibitors in AF phase 2 trials: abelacimab against rivaroxaban in AZALEA, and asundexian against apixaban in PACIFIC-AF. A broad 'any bleeding' endpoint with roughly 400 patients per arm should give reasonable power to detect a 40–60% relative reduction over 12 weeks. The main risks are that this phase 2 study may be descriptive rather than formally powered, that the open-label design adds noise to minor bleeding reports, and that event counts over a short 12-week window may be modest. Results are not yet public, since primary completion is planned for February 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"1cb4d869edaaa7ce1c50051f4c08f0a96fd0b038126587172dfb2a78d8916cef"},{"nct":"NCT06260163","title":"A Study of Guselkumab in Pediatric Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-10","enrollment":112,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.8068747081238284,"rationale":"Guselkumab is proven in adult UC: QUASAR showed robust induction and maintenance efficacy, and the mechanism carries over well to pediatric extrapolation studies. This pediatric trial has no placebo arm; both maintenance arms are guselkumab, so the Week 56 remission primary is likely descriptive or compared with a historical or adult placebo benchmark. A sponsor-defined success, such as remission clearly above adult placebo rates of roughly 20%, seems likely. There is still uncertainty from the small sample, the open-ended way 'success' may be judged, and the possibility of no formal hypothesis test.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ba8d0936d0b0735e88b73fe7eb30d270a2af92fcd7af0145e6e850b36ced7beb"},{"nct":"NCT06349980","title":"A Study to Explore the Reasonable Dosage and Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety and Tolerability of HLX10 and HLX04 with or Without HLX53 in Untreated, Locally Advanced or Metastatic Hepatocellular Carcinoma Patients.","sponsor":"Shanghai Henlius Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-10","enrollment":117,"base":0.12,"researched":null,"learned":0.3607276308769644,"rationale":"Anti-TIGIT add-ons to PD-(L)1 backbones have repeatedly failed in randomized trials, including tiragolumab with atezolizumab/bevacizumab in first-line HCC (IMbrave152/SKYSCRAPER-14 was stopped), and HLX53 is an Fc fusion protein with limited clinical data. With about 39 patients per arm in a phase II trial, an ORR comparison has little power unless the effect is very large, and this looks like an exploratory dose-finding study that may not even prespecify formal hypothesis testing. I know of no public topline result, and the low base rate for the TIGIT class makes a statistically significant win unlikely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"0f2bffa840e21187ddd7947fd16121c3e417b4764d47081f189da1a7e46ecca3"},{"nct":"NCT06807424","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Icotrokinra (JNJ-77242113) in Biologic-experienced and Biologic-naive Participants With Active Psoriatic Arthritis","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-10","enrollment":813,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.931356248281534,"rationale":"Icotrokinra is an oral IL-23 receptor antagonist peptide with strongly positive Phase 3 psoriasis results (ICONIC program), and IL-23 pathway blockade (guselkumab, risankizumab) has reliably beaten placebo on ACR20 in PsA, including in biologic-experienced patients. With about 270 patients per arm and ACR20 at Week 16 against placebo, the trial is well powered even for a modest effect. The main risks are that the oral peptide's exposure may be lower than injectable IL-23 blockers, that there was apparently no dedicated PsA Phase 2, and that placebo response could be high in a mixed population. Primary completion is not until 2027, so results are not yet public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c0fe23ad2c0446b4f6144ccf5548a54c7cc97ce0d6a4cdcf0bf4fc9dfeed7faf"},{"nct":"NCT06984627","title":"A Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Rilzabrutinib in Adult Participants With Graves' Disease","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-11","enrollment":33,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.4570923819749527,"rationale":"This is a small open-label, two-dose exploratory Phase 2 with no control arm. Success would most plausibly mean a significant within-arm reduction in FT4 from baseline at week 16, which is a fairly lenient bar if any background antithyroid therapy or spontaneous improvement contributes. BTK inhibition acts indirectly on TRAb-producing B cells and plasma cells, and its effect on thyroid hormone levels within 16 weeks is unproven, unlike FcRn blockers, which lower IgG rapidly. Given the mechanistic uncertainty, the small sample, and the lack of a clear formal hypothesis test, I put this near a coin flip, slightly below.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"fed80125d200289ec2239b7daf781e939cdb1e12556c42295e55d83a1bba1186"},{"nct":"NCT07215702","title":"A Study to Investigate the Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of AZD4144in Participants With Sepsis-associated Acute Kidney Injury.","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-11","enrollment":124,"base":0.2,"researched":null,"learned":0.3881208572828043,"rationale":"AZD4144 appears to be AstraZeneca's NLRP3 inflammasome inhibitor, given the IL-18 and IL-6 biomarker endpoints, and this is likely its first efficacy test in sepsis-associated AKI, a field with a near-uniform record of failed drug trials. The primary endpoint, AUC of 24-hour creatinine clearance during treatment, closely mirrors the STOP-AKI primary for recombinant alkaline phosphatase, which missed despite a mortality signal. Creatinine clearance in septic ICU patients is noisy, and with about 62 patients per arm only a large effect would reach two-sided significance. Base rates for a first-in-disease phase 2a with a new mechanism in a hard critical-care indication support a probability of roughly 20%; primary completion is not expected until February 2027, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"787ba2b38c0066e83c0919e013f71f9cc96d970b27084a8dbefbc801a5bcc30c"},{"nct":"NCT07579741","title":"A Study to Evaluate JL18008 in Subject With HIV Immunological Non-Responders","sponsor":"Jecho Biopharmaceuticals Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-12","enrollment":30,"base":0.75,"researched":null,"learned":0.5798699987401652,"rationale":"The primary outcomes are purely safety and tolerability measures (TEAEs, vitals, labs, ECG) in a small 30-subject Phase Ib add-on study with no powered efficacy comparison, so success will most likely be judged as an acceptable safety profile. Phase Ia data already supported advancing to these doses. JL18008 appears to be a cytokine-type immunomodulator, and comparable agents such as IL-7 and IL-2 have generally been tolerable at studied doses in INRs. The main risks are dose-limiting toxicity at 70 μg/kg or ambiguity in how a safety-only endpoint is scored.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5907997e70e3b0b5849d284a7f9368af7c56927ad17da9b5c31a71df83a87b6d"},{"nct":"NCT04224493","title":"A Study to Assess the Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacodynamics, and Pharmacokinetics of Tazemetostat in Combination With Lenalidomide Plus Rituximab Versus Placebo in Combination With Lenalidomide Plus Rituximab in Adult Patients at Least 18 Years of Age With Relapsed/Refractory Follicular Lymphoma.","sponsor":"Epizyme, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-13","enrollment":599,"base":0.04,"researched":null,"learned":0.7264532874050782,"rationale":"The record says an urgent safety measure, issued after an IDMC review, permanently stopped tazemetostat and placebo, halted enrollment and unblinded the study. Post-measure efficacy analyses are described as descriptive only, so a prespecified, statistically significant PFS win in the ITT-WT population is very unlikely to be declared. A safety-driven stop also suggests the benefit-risk balance did not favour the combination, likely because of the known secondary-malignancy risk of EZH2 inhibition. Some small residual chance remains that a pre-stop analysis showed a significant PFS benefit, but no such topline result is known.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"981d4eb063b13f921e91f969f9b44e0b68b89c736359105d89351bfec1d31b0b"},{"nct":"NCT07415252","title":"SkyVaricella® (NBP608) Vaccine With Lower Potencies in Healthy Children Aged 12 Months to 12 Years","sponsor":"SK Bioscience Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-13","enrollment":780,"base":0.78,"researched":null,"learned":0.8761583410249222,"rationale":"This is a Phase III immunogenicity trial of lower-potency formulations of SKYVaricella, an already licensed Oka/SK vaccine that previously showed non-inferior seroconversion to Varivax. The likely purpose is to support end-of-shelf-life potency specifications, with non-inferiority on seroconversion and GMT against Varivax or full-potency SKYVaricella. Live varicella vaccines usually give very high seroconversion rates (>90–95%), and success by only one of the two test arms, likely the mid-potency one, should suffice. The main risk is that reduced potency lowers GMTs enough to miss a 0.67 GMT-ratio margin, especially for the low-potency arm, and the record does not state the margins.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9b08af024de91d6dfce024d0fed891c8733f8c2d212c3b82d4439103c1816791"},{"nct":"NCT07437547","title":"BPC 157 for Acute Hamstring Muscle Strain Repair","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":120,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5051254226002468,"rationale":"BPC 157's support comes almost entirely from rodent studies, and there is no rigorous human efficacy data, so this is effectively a first test of a new mechanism. In acute hamstring strains, biologic add-ons to standard rehabilitation (e.g., PRP) have generally failed to shorten return-to-play in blinded trials. The trial is modest in size (n=120) against what is likely a small effect, and its registration is of low quality (both arms list both interventions, and the placebo arm is labeled experimental). Single-site trials from small sponsors do report positive results somewhat more often, so I lift the estimate slightly above the low base rate for an unproven peptide.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b1c8e450b78bce685898a006c5ad2718d32ce5f0c4fbc14d55567250139a571c"},{"nct":"NCT07437560","title":"Melanotan II (MT-II) as an Adjunct to NB-UVB Phototherapy for Repigmentation in Stable Nonsegmental Vitiligo","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":60,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.4375775752037431,"rationale":"The mechanism is supported by the afamelanotide plus NB-UVB pilot (Lim et al., JAMA Dermatology 2015), which showed faster and greater repigmentation, especially in darker skin types like most Chinese patients, so MT-II, a potent MC1R agonist, could plausibly add benefit. Against that, this is a single-site, 60-patient phase 2 from an obscure sponsor with a templated-looking record, and the primary endpoint is total VASI change at 24 weeks, a noisy measure where NB-UVB alone produces substantial background repigmentation. Generalized tanning from MT-II may partly unblind assessors but could also confound lesion scoring. Given phase 2 dermatology base rates and the record-quality concerns, I put success somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"002ddd1e043290c9713641889c15139c4f1fd492a47de05a7906dd6e11d6dfdf"},{"nct":"NCT07437586","title":"Topical GHK-Cu Gel for Acute Skin Wound Healing","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":60,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5538700052290167,"rationale":"GHK-Cu has an extensive preclinical and cosmetic literature, but rigorous controlled human wound-healing evidence is sparse and inconsistent, and topical agents rarely speed re-epithelialization of small acute wounds in healthy adults. The paired split-wound design with 60 participants gives decent power. However, assessments only on days 3, 7, 10, 14 and 21 make time-to-healing coarse, and a real difference of a day or two could be missed. A small, obscure sponsor and a sloppy registration slightly raise the chance of a favorable sponsor-reported result, but the base rate for a first test of this mechanism stays low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"5a9121ca77901258be50538be345f13c93eedadd9d43cf556045cbb2aa51ad7c"},{"nct":"NCT07481734","title":"Tesamorelin for Reduction of Liver Fat in Adults With Fatty Liver Disease","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":120,"base":0.7,"researched":null,"learned":0.4031830198263617,"rationale":"In earlier randomized trials, tesamorelin reduced MRI-measured hepatic fat in people with HIV and NAFLD, with an absolute reduction of about 4 points versus placebo in the 2019 Lancet HIV trial, and growth hormone axis stimulation has reduced liver fat in obese non-HIV adults too, so the mechanism has proof of concept. With 120 participants randomized 1:1, baseline PDFF of at least 10%, 52 weeks of treatment and a placebo comparator, MRI-PDFF should have adequate power for a plausible effect. Risks include a weaker effect in general MASLD than in HIV-associated visceral adiposity, a placebo response from lifestyle counseling, dose reductions for high IGF-1, and an unusual single-site record from a small sponsor (only participants masked, both arms labeled experimental). The trial is still recruiting, with primary completion planned for February 2027, so no result is public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"55a140c8780f6ce4db521ec725f18d5ffadc9c3a3bded0da2bf5a06bc63b241f"},{"nct":"NCT07481747","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Tirzepatide Once Weekly Versus Placebo in Participants Who Are Either Obese or Overweight With Weight-Related Comorbidities (SURMOUNT-1)","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":2539,"base":0.96,"researched":null,"learned":0.9413536269805848,"rationale":"This registration largely copies the original SURMOUNT-1 design: tirzepatide 5, 10 and 15 mg against placebo, with percent weight change at 72 weeks as the primary endpoint. The original Lilly trial showed placebo-adjusted weight loss of roughly 13–18% with p<0.001, an effect that is very hard to miss. The odd features (an unfamiliar sponsor, a single site in China, a timeline inconsistent with a 72-week endpoint) raise some risk around trial conduct and reporting, but not the drug's efficacy against placebo. A placebo-controlled trial of a proven drug like this succeeds almost every time, so a high probability is warranted.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"b394163096af48be766e772f64a3f2c95bb85fddc901a2b793fa7feea91d3534"},{"nct":"NCT07487363","title":"TB-500 (Thymosin Beta 4 17-23 Fragment) for Cardiovascular Biomarkers in Stable ASCVD","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":80,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.4374647128647196,"rationale":"The primary endpoints are safety measures (TEAE and SAE incidence), not efficacy comparisons, so 'success' most plausibly means the drug proves acceptably tolerated. Small phase 1/2 peptide trials with safety primaries usually report acceptable tolerability. Several features lower confidence: the registration looks template-like ('not provided in this public example'), the sponsor is little-known, TB-500 is a gray-market peptide with no prior regulated clinical record, and it is a single-site study, so it may never report clearly. It is also ambiguous how a safety primary would be scored against a superiority-style definition.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c78fde9e2d9ca34752427e978dd068ef2f61eadf902a4fc312980ac443bb15e3"},{"nct":"NCT07493265","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of E2086 in Adults With Narcolepsy","sponsor":"Eisai Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":64,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5823296989213895,"rationale":"E2086 is Eisai's oral orexin-2 receptor agonist. Other drugs in this class (oveporexton/TAK-861, alixorexton/ALKS 2680, ORX750) have produced very large, highly significant MWT gains over placebo in NT1, and alixorexton also reached significance in NT2. Eisai's own early E2086 data in NT1 pointed to wakefulness benefits, and a small sample is enough given these effect sizes, especially in the NT1 cohort with a sequential three-dose design. The main risks are a weaker NT2 effect, ambiguity in how the cohorts are combined for the primary analysis, and tolerability limiting the doses, but success remains likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a096d62cf60aa677145df2a9534ab1261cc5b0e39cbf31800288ba2788196729"},{"nct":"NCT07505745","title":"MOTS-c for Improving Insulin Sensitivity in Adults With Prediabetes and Overweight/Obesity","sponsor":"Hudson Biotech","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-14","enrollment":120,"base":0.25,"researched":null,"learned":0.4081025337338888,"rationale":"MOTS-c is a first-in-class mitochondrial-derived peptide whose insulin-sensitizing effects come from rodent studies, and the only related human data (CohBar's analog CB4211) showed modest, inconsistent metabolic effects. A small unknown sponsor running a single-site Phase 2a with 120 participants and a noisy OGTT-derived Matsuda index makes a significant result against a lifestyle-counseled placebo arm unlikely. Small Chinese single-site trials sometimes report positive results, so I nudge slightly above the base rate for a novel mechanism. Primary completion is planned for 2027, so no result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"31d7e47c87e0e5e3e2291e67dd012ed11814cabae883b5ea830df8718633e677"},{"nct":"NCT02972840","title":"A Study of BR Alone Versus in Combination With Acalabrutinib in Subjects With Previously Untreated MCL","sponsor":"Acerta Pharma BV","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-15","enrollment":635,"base":0.97,"researched":null,"learned":0.7331430423516863,"rationale":"This is the ECHO trial (ACE-LY-308). AstraZeneca announced in 2024 that it met its primary endpoint of IRC-assessed PFS. The reported result was HR about 0.73, p≈0.016, with median PFS 66.4 vs 49.6 months; it was presented at EHA 2024 and led to FDA approval of acalabrutinib plus BR in untreated MCL in early 2025. The registry's later primary completion date likely reflects continued follow-up rather than a pending primary analysis.","sources":0,"state":"public","leaf":"26b216a690dd75ac90f9ffca07072aad511acd34de4e7f85f27b8141315c6a50"},{"nct":"NCT06592794","title":"A Study to Investigate the Safety and Efficacy of mRNA-1403 in Participants ≥18 Years of Age for the Prevention of Acute Gastroenteritis","sponsor":"ModernaTX, Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-15","enrollment":37864,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.6615482782941234,"rationale":"Norovirus vaccines have a poor efficacy record: Takeda's bivalent VLP showed weak or non-significant protection in adult field and challenge studies, and HilleVax's infant trial failed in 2024. mRNA-1403 produced robust HBGA-blocking antibody responses in Phase 1/2, the trial is large (about 38,000 participants) and event-driven, and the primary endpoint is restricted to vaccine-matched genotypes, all of which improve the odds. Against that are shifting circulating strains (the GII.17 surge), the clinical hold over a Guillain-Barré case, and an untested correlate of protection, so the outcome looks close to a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"90691b184bf7885bec0759188ca35e861a90b33267405f2415d3d2b4b301391a"},{"nct":"NCT07017777","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Immunogenicity and Safety of 13-valent Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccine (PCV13i) in Healthy Infants Aged 2 Months (Minimum 6 Weeks)","sponsor":"CanSino Biologics Inc.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-15","enrollment":600,"base":0.88,"researched":null,"learned":0.8511777731123511,"rationale":"This is a non-inferiority immunogenicity trial comparing CanSino's PCV13i, a 13-valent conjugate on CRM197/TT carriers, with Prevnar 13 in Thai infants, using IgG ≥0.35 µg/mL seroresponse 30 days after the booster as the primary measure. PCV13i has already shown non-inferiority to Prevnar 13 in Chinese pivotal trials, and post-booster seroresponse rates for most serotypes approach 100%, which makes typical -10% margins easy to meet. The main risk is that non-inferiority probably has to hold for every serotype, with serotype 3 or a carrier-specific serotype (TT-conjugated) as the likeliest problems, plus some regulatory or operational uncertainty. Primary completion is expected in 2027, so no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ff1d201f85dbc0f9b73f8b70d09aa9f429d891abeaf846448458bae66995ddb9"},{"nct":"NCT07245771","title":"Phase 1/2a Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics and Effect on Body Weight of RN3161 as Monotherapy and in Combination With Tirzepatide in Adults With Overweight and Obesity","sponsor":"Ikaria Bioscience Pty Ltd","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-15","enrollment":104,"base":0.77,"researched":null,"learned":0.8205614028893694,"rationale":"This is a Phase 1/2a first-in-human study of RN3161, an siRNA from Rona Therapeutics, and every primary outcome is a descriptive safety or tolerability measure (AEs, vitals, ECG, labs). There is no prespecified superiority test, so a sponsor would most likely call the primary endpoint met if the drug proves acceptably safe and tolerable. Most siRNA programs clear early safety readily. The main risks are an unexpected safety signal or an ambiguous judgment on whether a descriptive safety endpoint was met. Primary completion is planned for 2027, and I don't believe any results are public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a8fc715d568664ece9ed540310e41c53ce9fbcf0fc8a0565ddf9106634f90cfe"},{"nct":"NCT06140836","title":"A Study of Repotrectinib Versus Crizotinib in Participants With Locally Advanced or Metastatic Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitor (TKI)-naïve ROS1-positive Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) (TRIDENT-3)","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-16","enrollment":190,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7310087218602224,"rationale":"In TRIDENT-1, repotrectinib produced a 79% response rate and a median PFS of about 35.7 months in TKI-naïve ROS1+ NSCLC. Crizotinib's historical PFS in this setting is roughly 16–19 months, and it penetrates the CNS poorly, so intracranial progression is common on the control arm. A randomized comparison of about 190 patients should be powered to detect a plausible hazard ratio near 0.5, and next-generation ROS1/ALK TKIs have consistently beaten crizotinib on PFS in head-to-head trials. The main risks are an immature event count at the analysis and crizotinib doing better than expected, but success looks likely; I don't recall any public topline result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"bd830b2c47be7782b32833bcbda8c7c9bc9710efba04a7fa36232304ca90a61d"},{"nct":"NCT07082114","title":"A Phase 3 Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of HDM1002 Tablets in Adults With Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus","sponsor":"Hangzhou Zhongmei Huadong Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-16","enrollment":800,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.9373609762664485,"rationale":"HDM1002 is Huadong's oral small-molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist. In this Chinese metformin add-on trial its HbA1c change is compared with dapagliflozin, an SGLT2 inhibitor that typically lowers HbA1c only about 0.8–1.0%. Oral small-molecule GLP-1 agonists such as orforglipron have beaten dapagliflozin on HbA1c (ACHIEVE-2), and earlier-phase HDM1002 data reportedly showed meaningful glucose lowering, so 200 patients per arm gives ample power for one of three doses to succeed. The main risks are an unexpected safety problem (e.g., liver signals seen in the class), high dropout from GI tolerability, or a weaker-than-expected effect, so I discount from near-certainty.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"70c98c5032826522e4781047235ec9005785d7d487e4c8790907f6d9c77dbcf5"},{"nct":"NCT06233461","title":"A Study on the Safety of TAK-279 and Whether it Can Reduce Inflammation in the Bowel of Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Crohn's Disease","sponsor":"Takeda","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-17","enrollment":268,"base":0.4,"researched":null,"learned":0.4282670082089923,"rationale":"Zasocitinib is a highly selective, potent TYK2 inhibitor. It blocks IL-23/IL-12 signalling, a pathway validated in Crohn's disease by ustekinumab and risankizumab, and it reaches higher target coverage than deucravacitinib. Against that, deucravacitinib failed its phase 2 trials in both Crohn's disease (LATTICE-CD) and UC, Phase 2 Crohn's trials of new oral mechanisms often fail, and the endoscopic response endpoint with about 67 patients per arm needs a real effect of roughly 15+ percentage points over a 10–15% placebo rate. One of three doses succeeding counts, and dose selection is informed by psoriasis data, so I put the chance of success somewhat below even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ade14f0fc6aa94b96fbae807748b9807f45f520af509eacf6508bf5cb2e80b82"},{"nct":"NCT07424144","title":"An Extension Study to Investigate the Long-term Safety and Tolerability of Itepekimab in Adult Participants With Inadequately Controlled Chronic Rhinosinusitis With Nasal Polyps","sponsor":"Sanofi","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-17","enrollment":59,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.7218441173693319,"rationale":"This is a double-blind extension in which both arms receive itepekimab, and the only primary endpoint is descriptive safety (AE incidence). There is no prespecified efficacy comparison against a control, so 'success' mostly means completing the study without an unexpected safety signal; itepekimab's safety profile has been benign across asthma, COPD and CRSwNP trials. Uncertainty remains because enrollment was small (59, possibly signalling a curtailed program) and it is ambiguous how a safety-only endpoint will be scored.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"576afe4c092f95d2e8ada15e8e31f6c636b4721f73da6494a47a24c5ccbbf78e"},{"nct":"NCT07486960","title":"Study to Evaluate Tulisokibart in Adults With Psoriatic Arthritis (MK-7240-015)","sponsor":"Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-17","enrollment":140,"base":0.42,"researched":null,"learned":0.893388609434985,"rationale":"Tulisokibart is an anti-TL1A antibody with positive Phase 2 data in ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease, but TL1A blockade has no proven efficacy in psoriatic arthritis or any rheumatologic indication. There is some biologic rationale, since TL1A drives Th17/IL-17 and ILC3 pathways, and ACR20 at week 16 against placebo is a comparatively easy endpoint, with three doses each getting a shot at significance. Still, about 35 patients per arm and a 25–30% placebo ACR20 rate need a delta near 30 points to reach significance, which only well-established mechanisms reliably deliver. With no public result yet (primary completion is planned for February 2027), I sit near the base rate for a first test of a new mechanism in this disease.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"873f557ef8bc90043c075a0afd743eefa4c4460bc83b999fa6163936bca6607a"},{"nct":"NCT06087835","title":"Study to Investigate Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of Zibotentan/Dapagliflozin Compared to Dapagliflozin in Participants With Chronic Kidney Disease and High Proteinuria (ZENITH High Proteinuria)","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-18","enrollment":1835,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.7689612216531118,"rationale":"Endothelin antagonists have clear evidence of kidney benefit: SONAR (atrasentan) reduced hard renal outcomes, PROTECT (sparsentan) improved eGFR slope, and the ZENITH-CKD phase 2b showed meaningful extra albuminuria lowering from zibotentan on top of dapagliflozin. The risk is that a 24-month change-in-eGFR primary absorbs the acute hemodynamic eGFR dip these drugs cause, and fluid retention may force discontinuations. Sparsentan's total-slope results were borderline in PROTECT, and DUPLEX missed its eGFR endpoint. The large, rapidly progressing high-proteinuria population (n≈1835) gives reasonable power, so I put success modestly above even odds.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"26af48715f0c801b8432432a711f3b30e08f8ccde1fe22f7b31dff6a16ed0fee"},{"nct":"NCT07015905","title":"REGN7508 Versus Apixaban and Enoxaparin for Thromboprophylaxis After Total Knee Arthroplasty in Adults","sponsor":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-20","enrollment":2000,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.8174214355091903,"rationale":"REGN7508 (cenvacibart) is a factor XI catalytic-domain antibody. As I recall, Regeneron's Phase 2 ROXI-VTE TKA studies showed markedly lower VTE rates than enoxaparin and numerically lower rates than apixaban. Across the class (abelacimab, osocimab, FXI-ASO, milvexian), FXI inhibition has consistently beaten enoxaparin in knee arthroplasty on venographic VTE endpoints. The primary comparison is probably non-inferiority or superiority versus enoxaparin and/or apixaban, and with about 2000 patients and high event rates the trial is well powered, though superiority over apixaban would be the harder bar. Primary completion is not expected until February 2027, so no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"7e7f5a89539a6d3354adfcd52612530b79368a203ade7a873d296e73212f055e"},{"nct":"NCT07019675","title":"A Study of SKB518 in Patients With Lung Cancer","sponsor":"Sichuan Kelun-Biotech Biopharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-20","enrollment":192,"base":0.58,"researched":null,"learned":0.3765748754906344,"rationale":"This is an exploratory, open-label phase II study of Kelun's SKB518 ADC. The first-listed primary outcome is AE incidence, and the efficacy endpoints (ORR, PFS) are mostly single-arm, with no clear prespecified statistical comparison. Kelun's ADCs have generally shown good activity in lung cancer, and SCLC responds well to novel ADCs, so a positive-sounding readout is plausible. Still, the lack of a formal hypothesis test and the uncertainty about how success would be judged keep this forecast moderate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a977a62735bb27688304f1697f3114e05d70d37b188881fcbe66ab6d90fed942"},{"nct":"NCT07494409","title":"A Study of AND017 to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety in Dialysis-Dependent Chronic Kidney Disease (DD-CKD) Patients With Anemia","sponsor":"Kind Pharmaceuticals LLC","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-20","enrollment":300,"base":0.87,"researched":null,"learned":0.731919033604105,"rationale":"AND017 is an oral HIF-PHI, and essentially every HIF-PHI phase 3 non-inferiority trial against ESA in dialysis patients (roxadustat, daprodustat, vadadustat, enarodustat, desidustat) met its hemoglobin efficacy margin. The record is framed as maintenance of mean Hb over weeks 23–27 versus ESA in ESA-converted dialysis patients, which implies a non-inferiority design with a dose-titratable drug, an easy setting to win. The open-label design, 300 patients in China and earlier phase 2 data showing Hb effects support a high probability, tempered slightly by the small sponsor and limited published data.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"9e94e1d6c98e7ba4596bb2717842cde124ec61c8e087bef424243fc9ca8e6d1d"},{"nct":"NCT04529772","title":"A Combination of Acalabrutinib With R-CHOP in Subjects With Previously Untreated Non-GCB DLBCL (ACE-LY-312)","sponsor":"Acerta Pharma BV","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-22","enrollment":611,"base":0.36,"researched":null,"learned":0.6593503538178418,"rationale":"PHOENIX (ibrutinib + R-CHOP in non-GCB DLBCL) missed its primary endpoint. Its signal was limited to patients under 60, and R-CHOP intensity suffered from toxicity in older patients. ESCALADE uses the better-tolerated acalabrutinib, caps age at 75 and enrolls about 611 patients, which plausibly gives it a better chance than PHOENIX. Even so, frontline DLBCL add-on trials have a poor track record (POLARIX is the main exception), and the inclusion of IPI 1 and unclassified patients dilutes the ABC-specific effect, so modest odds seem right.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"20bed1bc528afb8893b4768cb912080795a5f7a71e8f23a284dc7a68993222bd"},{"nct":"NCT06834932","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Safety, and Pharmacokinetics of AZD0780 in Participants With Dyslipidaemia","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 2/3","due":"2027-02-22","enrollment":432,"base":0.95,"researched":null,"learned":0.9038198917353476,"rationale":"AZD0780 is an oral small-molecule PCSK9 inhibitor. In the Phase IIb PURSUIT trial it lowered LDL-C by roughly 50% versus placebo on top of statins. The first-listed primary outcomes are descriptive Part A PK measures, so the relevant efficacy test is Part B's placebo-controlled LDL-C change at 12 weeks. With about 320 participants and an expected placebo-adjusted reduction near 50%, statistical significance is close to certain; the main residual risk is ambiguity about how a PK-first primary endpoint gets scored.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"06f324c2ab7f8b35d2481d1a67d7829293cf37b4b7a0c8428a98e72b5b696ceb"},{"nct":"NCT06868212","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy of Remibrutinib Compared to Dupilumab at Early Timepoints in Adults With Chronic Spontaneous Urticaria Inadequately Controlled by Second Generation H1-antihistamines","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-22","enrollment":409,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.8078461655324068,"rationale":"In REMIX-1/2, remibrutinib separated from placebo on UAS7 as early as Week 1, with roughly a 7–9 point placebo-adjusted change by Week 2–4. In CUPID, dupilumab's benefit built slowly and was only modestly above placebo at early timepoints. Novartis chose the Week 4 endpoint to exploit that onset-speed difference, and with ~400 patients randomized 1:1 a plausible 4–6 point advantage (SD ~11–12) gives very high power. The main risks are a faster-than-expected dupilumab response with the 600 mg loading dose, high US placebo-like improvement in both arms shrinking the gap, and the inherent unpredictability of head-to-head trials.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"92dc565d8323cb02f7844d81f7de759d310ca21adf79ae64c9b10b1c7c14e818"},{"nct":"NCT07598383","title":"A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-blind, Vehicle Controlled Phase II Clinical Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of VC005 Gel in Adult Subjects With Mild to Moderate Atopic Dermatitis","sponsor":"Jiangsu vcare pharmaceutical technology co., LTD","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-22","enrollment":120,"base":0.72,"researched":null,"learned":0.7372206062797401,"rationale":"VC005 is, as far as I recall, Vcare's JAK inhibitor, here as a topical gel. Topical JAK inhibitors such as ruxolitinib cream and delgocitinib have shown large, rapid EASI improvements over vehicle in mild-to-moderate atopic dermatitis, often clearly significant by week 4 even in modest phase 2 samples. With three dose arms of about 30 patients each, a continuous EASI-change endpoint, and the need for only one dose to win, power should be adequate despite the meaningful vehicle response typical in AD. Uncertainty about the formulation's skin penetration and the small single-site design temper confidence.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"382fb763806e343dcd1d8b267678d702720d104dce7140ac9583f9d7d1694c4c"},{"nct":"NCT05138133","title":"Phase 3 Study of Anifrolumab in Adult Patients With Active Proliferative Lupus Nephritis","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-23","enrollment":363,"base":0.45,"researched":null,"learned":0.6084947132764265,"rationale":"IRIS uses the intensified anifrolumab regimen that, in the Phase 2 TULIP-LN trial, showed a numerically higher complete renal response rate (about 45% vs 31%) even though that trial missed its proteinuria primary endpoint. Lupus nephritis add-on trials have a mixed record: belimumab, voclosporin and obinutuzumab succeeded, while rituximab, abatacept and ocrelizumab failed, and a TYK2/interferon-pathway drug (deucravacitinib) also failed in this disease. With about 180 patients per arm, a strict week-52 complete renal response endpoint and a Phase 2 signal of roughly 14 points, power is moderate, and Phase 2 effect estimates often shrink in Phase 3. Primary completion is February 2027, so no topline result is public yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"470e5c2648f30b6b0cac7af33f07a7be061b6eac92dc9903e08f5b86184f7e86"},{"nct":"NCT07873463","title":"Flutemetamol F 18 Injection Formulation Comparison","sponsor":"GE Healthcare","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-25","enrollment":20,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.5077946569927231,"rationale":"This is a small crossover bridging study by GE Healthcare comparing a reformulation (GE-287) of the approved amyloid PET tracer Vizamyl, where success means showing comparable SUVr and biodistribution rather than superiority. The active moiety is unchanged and the excipients were changed for tolerability and manufacturing, so regional SUVr values should be highly concordant, and sponsors in these studies typically declare equivalence or comparability. The main risks are an undefined equivalence margin with only 20 participants, and possible biodistribution differences from the excipient change (e.g., PS80), which could alter early organ SUV in the heart, liver or kidneys. Overall, success is likely.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"54eb65429592949ab4de1b646ba10cb08900d5a33aeca51cf1c18d5589fe60e6"},{"nct":"NCT01872260","title":"Study of LEE011, BYL719 and Letrozole in Advanced ER+ Breast Cancer","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 1/2","due":"2027-02-26","enrollment":259,"base":0.6,"researched":null,"learned":0.3919599150916524,"rationale":"This is an uncontrolled Phase Ib dose-escalation and expansion study whose primary outcomes are DLT incidence, safety and PK, so there is no superiority comparison; 'success' can only mean defining an MTD/RP2D and characterizing tolerability. Conference reports have described the ribociclib+letrozole doublet and the triple combination with alpelisib, with RP2Ds identified but notable hyperglycemia and other toxicity in the triplet. Ribociclib+letrozole later went on to approval, which suggests the doublet objectives were met. Because success is ambiguous for a safety-only primary endpoint and the final results are not formally posted, I put the probability moderately above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"33d2404861b07ed31251660d57b02302d209e1f5b3fb044676f052b53cbf2906"},{"nct":"NCT04208178","title":"Study of Alpelisib (BYL719) in Combination With Trastuzumab and Pertuzumab as Maintenance Therapy in Patients With HER2-positive Advanced Breast Cancer With a PIK3CA Mutation","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-26","enrollment":19,"base":0.03,"researched":null,"learned":0.6143014651693809,"rationale":"Novartis permanently halted recruitment in December 2022 because the HER2+ treatment landscape had changed. Only 19 patients were enrolled in total, most of them probably in the Part 1 safety run-in, so very few were randomized in Part 2. Part 2 participants are being unblinded, which means any PFS comparison will be descriptive and hugely underpowered, and a statistically significant PFS benefit is very unlikely. Part 1's DLT endpoint involves no comparison and cannot count as efficacy success, so the chance of meeting the primary endpoint is very low.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"6c9cf443e34606808f985d1d4352e53b369e95ab3b6c798800e98be73fecc26c"},{"nct":"NCT07382167","title":"A 26-Wk Study to Assess Safety & Efficacy of Tenapanor for T/t of Chronic Idiopathic Constipation in Adults","sponsor":"Ardelyx","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-26","enrollment":692,"base":0.8,"researched":null,"learned":0.874671769750483,"rationale":"Tenapanor is already approved for IBS-C after two positive Phase 3 trials with clear gains in CSBM frequency. Other secretagogue-type drugs (linaclotide, plecanatide, lubiprostone) have reliably succeeded against placebo in chronic idiopathic constipation, including on this same stringent durable 9/12-week CSBM responder endpoint. With about 170 patients per arm, three doses, and placebo durable-response rates typically in the single digits to low teens, the trial looks well powered. The main risks are the stringent endpoint, a possibly modest effect in a non-IBS population, and the absence of a known Phase 2 CIC dataset.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"16587ae9229680dbb3b313ada4a9b4d0f1b3181627aca94186492f39f59bd732"},{"nct":"NCT07073417","title":"A Study to Compare XW003 Injection and Semaglutide Injection in Chinese Adults With Obesity (SLIMMER-UP-SWITCH)","sponsor":"Hangzhou Sciwind Biosciences Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-27","enrollment":163,"base":0.42,"researched":null,"learned":0.7392197734302348,"rationale":"Ecnoglutide (XW003) gave about 15% mean weight loss at 48 weeks in the Chinese phase 3 SLIMMER trial, while semaglutide 2.4 mg gave about 12–13% in Chinese/East Asian populations (STEP 7), so any true advantage is probably modest, around 1–3 percentage points. With roughly 80 participants per arm and an SD near 7%, a difference of that size is only borderline detectable, and the small open-label 'switching' phase 2 may not even be powered for formal superiority. Sponsor confidence in running a head-to-head and possible higher dosing push the estimate up slightly, but a statistically significant superiority result is roughly a coin flip or a bit less.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f76b825142fb570cb796d9c7f5c63df3de2fb94507c939d767cdd9bc4b4cab39"},{"nct":"NCT04587830","title":"ADI-PEG 20 Plus Radiotherapy and Temozolomide in Subjects With Glioblastoma Multiforme","sponsor":"Polaris Group","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":100,"base":0.13,"researched":null,"learned":0.20196819345950198,"rationale":"Randomized add-on trials to Stupp radiotherapy plus temozolomide in newly diagnosed GBM have an extremely poor track record, and a 100-patient trial powered on overall survival needs a large hazard-ratio improvement to reach p<0.05. The rationale is mechanistic (GBM is often ASS1-deficient) and a small phase 1b cohort reported an encouraging median OS of about 29 months, but single-arm GBM survival data are notoriously unreliable. ADI-PEG 20 has been mixed elsewhere, failing in phase 3 HCC and succeeding modestly in mesothelioma with chemotherapy. The primary outcome also leans on subgroup and biomarker exploration, suggesting limited confidence in an all-comers OS win, though a small chance of success remains.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"f8f17b9bd68fa6953b357b2d3f311f45b238839a2a17e551ea552df8bf35bcb0"},{"nct":"NCT05821478","title":"Efficacy of an Adapted Antibiotherapy in Hurley Stage 2 Hidradenitis Suppurativa Patients","sponsor":"Institut Pasteur","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":92,"base":0.62,"researched":null,"learned":0.6545816021692766,"rationale":"This is an investigator-driven trial from the Necker/Pasteur group, whose earlier open-label and retrospective series of ceftriaxone plus metronidazole followed by rifampicin, moxifloxacin and metronidazole reported high remission rates in Hurley 1–2 hidradenitis suppurativa. Lymecycline is a weak comparator, so IHS4-90 remission at week 12 in the control arm should be low, perhaps 10–15%. With 92 patients, a true difference of about 25–30 points would be well powered. Risks include effect shrinkage under double-blind conditions, the stringent IHS4-90 endpoint, and dropouts from poor tolerance of the intensive regimen.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"79a7e07f1c9aa4585b1fcd9f043c9203722b9809c3977f28ff4fb1b370eb2532"},{"nct":"NCT05972473","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of IBI302 in Subjects With nAMD","sponsor":"Innovent Biologics (Suzhou) Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":600,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.7382082769831333,"rationale":"This is a Phase 3 trial of efdamrofusp alfa (a VEGF/complement bispecific) against aflibercept 2 mg Q8W in treatment-naive nAMD, with mean BCVA change averaged over weeks 44–52 as the primary endpoint, and it is almost certainly a non-inferiority design. Non-inferiority BCVA trials of potent anti-VEGF agents against aflibercept (faricimab, brolucizumab, aflibercept 8 mg) have nearly all met their margins. The Phase 2 STAR data for the 8 mg dose showed BCVA gains numerically comparable to or better than aflibercept. The main residual risks are a possible superiority hypothesis, extended-interval dosing underperforming, or execution issues, and I do not know of any topline result yet.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4358cc455ad30070a43ef4b41b0b172021f07e51903f87b8e74090621e849a78"},{"nct":"NCT06551324","title":"A Study to Learn About the Investigational Medicine Called PF-06821497 (Mevrometostat) in Men With mCRPC Who Were Previously Treated With Abiraterone Acetate for Prostate Cancer (MEVPRO-1).","sponsor":"Pfizer","phase":"Phase 3","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":609,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.7230888388701008,"rationale":"In the randomized phase 1 expansion in post-abiraterone mCRPC, mevrometostat plus enzalutamide roughly doubled rPFS versus enzalutamide alone (about 14 vs 6 months, HR about 0.5), and Pfizer moved straight to this phase 3. The control arm is physician's choice: enzalutamide after abiraterone performs poorly, but docetaxel is a stronger comparator and makes success somewhat harder. Other EZH2 agents have shown mixed results in prostate cancer, and the phase 1 signal came from a small sample, so some regression toward a smaller effect is likely. With 609 patients and a BICR-assessed rPFS endpoint, the trial should be well powered for a moderate effect, so I put success above the oncology phase 3 base rate.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"ad0c556ce716a5871891cbbb87e06d14c1ad045731ee463cb97d8095763b2817"},{"nct":"NCT06712654","title":"A Study to Evaluate Safety, Tolerability and Efficacy of AP306 at Fixed Doses in Dialysis Participants With Hyperphosphatemia","sponsor":"R1 Therapeutics","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":168,"base":0.82,"researched":null,"learned":0.8759335325913694,"rationale":"AP306 (EOS789) is a pan-phosphate transporter inhibitor, and Alebund's earlier Chinese Phase 2 in hemodialysis patients reported clinically meaningful serum phosphate reductions versus placebo, so mechanism and drug-level proof of concept exist. This Phase 2b compares six fixed-dose arms against placebo on change in serum phosphate over 8 weeks, a responsive surrogate where binders and tenapanor typically separate from placebo by roughly 1 mg/dL or more, especially after binder washout. With about 24 patients per arm, power for at least one dose to reach significance is reasonable. Remaining risks are small arms, GI tolerability causing dropouts, and a possibly modest effect at fixed doses.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c092889656f981987949630ecf19de9bfc248827d60faf623513a8a51b00cb2e"},{"nct":"NCT06800651","title":"Trial of JMKX003142 in Participants With Rapidly Progressive Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease (ADPKD)","sponsor":"Jemincare","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":135,"base":0.68,"researched":null,"learned":0.45764338914035435,"rationale":"JMKX003142 appears to be an aquaretic, likely a vasopressin V2 antagonist: the record excludes patients who cannot sense thirst and those likely to need diuretics. That mechanism was validated for slowing total kidney volume growth by tolvaptan, whose year-1 TKV effects were large relative to variability. With about 67 patients per arm in a rapidly progressive population, a 52-week percentage change in TKV against placebo should be well powered if the drug reaches adequate V2 blockade. The main risks are uncertainty about the mechanism and dose, a small single-site Chinese phase 2, and primary completion not due until 2027, so no results are public.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"15e778e0365f958dec7d8d7d6d543c496419c80af602b9377c9da315840af30a"},{"nct":"NCT06982963","title":"Randomized, Double Blind, Placebo-controlled Phase 2 Study in Adults With Celiac Disease","sponsor":"Forte Biosciences, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":100,"base":0.55,"researched":null,"learned":0.3288287983668501,"rationale":"FB102 is an anti-CD122 antibody that blocks IL-2/IL-15 signaling. Forte's small phase 1b gluten-challenge study reportedly showed protection of villous height to crypt depth ratio and of intraepithelial lymphocyte counts versus placebo. Gluten challenge with a histologic composite endpoint (VCIEL) is a sensitive, objective design, and an earlier TG2 inhibitor (ZED1227) succeeded with a similar setup. However, the related anti-IL-15 antibody AMG 714 missed its primary Vh:Cd endpoint, the placebo arm is small (about 20 patients), and phase 2 celiac programs have a mixed record, so I put the chance modestly above even.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"a4200b00197468d0dbf3d24d331055941ad8cf3bd23107801cc69bc97a2e1fd8"},{"nct":"NCT07105488","title":"A Study Evaluating BFB759 in Moderate to Severe Atopic Dermatitis","sponsor":"Bluefin Biomedicine, Inc.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":225,"base":0.5,"researched":null,"learned":0.570884751068428,"rationale":"BFB759 is a first-in-class multi-cytokine-inhibiting mAb from a small biotech. A Phase 2 placebo-controlled AD trial with roughly 75 patients per arm and EASI percent change at week 16 is reasonably powered for a moderate effect, and placebo responses in AD are modest. However, many novel mechanisms in AD Phase 2 have failed or been marginal (IL-33, IL-18, TSLP, IL-22), and public data on this drug are limited. Two dose arms add some chance that one succeeds, so I put this close to a coin flip.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"53a80f176a8f4e89a88ddce080f913e29cbe699c4df8bc4b2cadcf12d4c4e574"},{"nct":"NCT07552012","title":"A Phase II Clinical Trial to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of FXS5626 in Patients With NIU","sponsor":"Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Industrial Development Co. Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":40,"base":0.3,"researched":null,"learned":0.5457010485059177,"rationale":"FXS5626 is likely an oral JAK/TYK2-type immunomodulator, and drugs with that mechanism, such as adalimumab and brepocitinib, have shown efficacy against treatment failure in non-anterior non-infectious uveitis, so the biology is plausible. However, this is a tiny 40-patient trial randomized 2:1:1, leaving only about 10 placebo patients. Even a large effect (for example 40% vs 80% treatment failure) would hover around p≈0.05, and small Chinese phase 2 dose-finding studies are often descriptive rather than powered for formal significance. Results are not yet public (primary completion is February 2027), so I estimate a modest probability of a statistically significant primary result.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"c2efe80cc3e77bda994278f8880448b94e290f7c4682a2c807c6629c7f273d8c"},{"nct":"NCT07658560","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of BGM0504 Tablets in Overweight or Obese Participants Without Diabetes","sponsor":"BrightGene Bio-Medical Technology Co., Ltd.","phase":"Phase 2","due":"2027-02-28","enrollment":200,"base":0.85,"researched":null,"learned":0.872951431285284,"rationale":"BGM0504 is BrightGene's GLP-1/GIP dual agonist, and the injectable form has already produced substantial weight loss in Chinese phase 2 studies. The mechanism is well validated against placebo on body weight. The main risk is oral peptide bioavailability, but four dose arms of about 40 participants each over 20 weeks leave ample power if exposure is even modest, and only one dose needs to succeed. The primary result is not yet public, with primary completion planned for February 2027.","sources":0,"state":"unscreened","leaf":"4e8150be4247ae733cbf18d045b579d5a2a6c7da479e369cf46cc9e9d51ac8ec"}]};
